x. 1 root root 558 Aug  1 00:43 timer.sh\ntotal 0\ndrwxr-xr-x. 2 root root  6 Aug 21 23:39 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 1 root root 18 Aug 22 22:15 ..\n/app\ntotal 8\ndrwxr-xr-x. 2 root root  34 Aug 22 22:15 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 6 root root  63 Aug 22 22:15 ..\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root  32 Aug 22 22:15 .git\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 root root 558 Aug 22 22:15 timer.sh\ngitdir: /app/.git/worktrees/app-architect-1\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'fastapi'\nPackage           Version\n----------------- -------\ngreenlet          3.5.5\npip               26.2.1\nplaywright        1.62.0\npyee              13.0.1\ntyping_extensions 4.16.0\n/opt/venv/bin/pip\n/usr/bin/npm\n==== MARATHON-3 ====\nAuth API: register, login, me, bearer tokens\nImplement POST /api/auth/register, POST /api/auth/login, GET /api/auth/me per contract. Username URL-safe slug; password >=8; 201 {user,token} with token length >=16; duplicate username 409; invalid username/short password 400; wrong password 401; missing/invalid bearer 401. No email field. Persist users and tokens cluster-wide so any node accepts the same token.\ndeps: [{'issue_id': 'MARATHON-3', 'depends_on_id': 'MARATHON-2', 'type': 'blocks', 'title': 'Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis', 'status': 'in_progress', 'issue_type': 'task', 'created_at': '2026-08-22T22:17:01.484557004Z', 'created_by': 'marathon-harness'}] None\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\n==== MARATHON-13 ====\nWebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\nws://host/api/ws?token= bearer. Client: subscribe, resume with since_seq. Server: subscribed/resumed with head_seq; resume.gap if since_seq older than retained tail. Durable per-channel frames {type, seq, channel_id, ...} for message/reply/reaction/membership/channel mutations. seq dense per-channel (+1 per durable event, no gaps/duplicates). Profile updates: {type:user.updated,user} globally without channel_id/seq. Same seq visible across all HTTP nodes (fan-out task will complete cross-node).\ndeps: [{'issue_id': 'MARATHON-13', 'depends_on_id': 'MARATHON-8', 'type': 'blocks', 'title': 'Messages, threads, reactions REST API', 'status': 'open', 'issue_type': 'task', 'created_at': '2026-08-22T22:17:29.97263884Z', 'created_by': 'marathon-harness'}] None\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\n==== MARATHON-14 ====\nCross-node fan-out and Redis-outage resilience\nDurable channel events from any HTTP node share one dense seq, replay after reconnecting to a different node, and fan out across the cluster. Use local Redis pub/sub on 127.0.0.1:6379 when available. When Redis is SIGKILLed, within 5s writes must still succeed, cross-node WS subscribers still receive events, and seq stays dense; start.sh respawns Redis and normal pub/sub resumes. Killing one HTTP node must not stop reads/writes/WS/replay on the other two. Meet latency: message.new median ≤300ms, p95 ≤800ms, ≤1% missing observer events under concurrent multi-node writes.\ndeps: [{'issue_id': 'MARATHON-14', 'depends_on_id': 'MARATHON-13', 'type': 'blocks', 'title': 'WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq', 'status': 'open', 'issue_type': 'task', 'created_at': '2026-08-22T22:17:29.991315274Z', 'created_by': 'marathon-harness'}] None\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\n==== MARATHON-15 ====\nIRC gateway on :6667 with bidirectional bridge\nListen 0.0.0.0:6667. PASS token before NICK/USER; bad → 464. Registration 001-005 then 422 NOMOTD. JOIN unknown → 403; nick collision → 433 keep connection; unknown cmd → 421. Map web channels to #{workspace-slug}-{channel-name}. JOIN → JOIN prefix, 353, 366; topic 332/331. PRIVMSG commits into same dense per-channel seq as HTTP messages; web messages fan out to IRC as PRIVMSG. Support PING/PONG/QUIT/NAMES/WHO/LIST/TOPIC/MODE; QUIT closes without error reply. Survives HTTP node kill via remaining cluster.\ndeps: [{'issue_id': 'MARATHON-15', 'depends_on_id': 'MARATHON-13', 'type': 'blocks', 'title': 'WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq', 'status': 'open', 'issue_type': 'task', 'created_at': '2026-08-22T22:17:47.161Z', 'created_by': 'marathon-harness'}, {'issue_id': 'MARATHON-15', 'depends_on_id': 'MARATHON-14', 'type': 'blocks', 'title': 'Cross-node fan-out and Redis-outage resilience', 'status': 'open', 'issue_type': 'task', 'created_at': '2026-08-22T22:17:56.337822522Z', 'created_by': 'marathon-harness'}] None\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\n==== MARATHON-16 ====\nSPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\nServe SPA from GET / on any node. Sign-up form with visible error on invalid input; auto-login on success. Logout/login restores same workspace. Store bearer in localStorage huddle.token (or accepted fallbacks). Three-pane layout shell: coloured sidebar + message pane + on-demand thread panel. Workspace identity in sidebar. Stable selectors: auth-form, auth-submit, auth-toggle, auth-modal, workspace-create-form, empty-state-create-workspace, join-workspace-*, current-user, logout-btn, workspace-header, channel-list, dms-list. Drivable at 1280x900.\ndeps: [{'issue_id': 'MARATHON-16', 'depends_on_id': 'MARATHON-3', 'type': 'blocks', 'title': 'Auth API: register, login, me, bearer tokens', 'status': 'open', 'issue_type': 'task', 'created_at': '2026-08-22T22:17:47.182147122Z', 'created_by': 'marathon-harness'}, {'issue_id': 'MARATHON-16', 'depends_on_id': 'MARATHON-5', 'type': 'blocks', 'title': 'Workspaces: create, list, detail, auto #general', 'status': 'open', 'issue_type': 'task', 'created_at': '2026-08-22T22:17:47.186156468Z', 'created_by': 'marathon-harness'}] None\nlabels: ['architect', 'frontend']\nUpdate issue fields\n\nUsage:\n  loom data update <issue-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --add-label stringArray           Add label (repeatable); other labels are preserved\n      --assignee string                 Set assignee\n      --depends-on stringArray          Add dependency on issue ID (repeatable)\n      --description string              Set description\n      --description-from-file string    Read description from file (use - for stdin)\n      --design string                   Set design\n      --design-format string            Set design format (markdown or html)\n  -h, --help                            help for update\n      --notes string                    Set notes\n      --priority int                    Set priority\n      --remove-depends-on stringArray   Remove dependency on issue ID (repeatable)\n      --remove-label stringArray        Remove label (repeatable); other labels are preserved\n      --status string                   Set status\n      --title string                    Set title\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n  -o, --output string       Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string       Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\nAdd a comment to an issue (HTTP)\n\nUsage:\n  loom data comment <issue-id> <text> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --author string   Comment author (defaults to server-side session user)\n  -h, --help            help for comment\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n  -o, --output string       Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string       Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\n['id', 'title', 'status', 'priority', 'issue_type', 'owner', 'has_design', 'created_at', 'updated_at', 'created_by', 'description', 'de