{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-20c38e59-8191-4312-9cf7-efd810fcb317-8\nfc_7e5d4971-6bfc-94b8-9bd5-8105cdcdda8d_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cat > /tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n# MARATHON-2 — Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task boots the Huddle cluster so the verifier (and every later feature task) has a live, self-contained process tree: `/app/start.sh` stays in the foreground, supervises a local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, and respawns any of those children after `SIGKILL`. Each node exposes a stub `GET /` and the contracted `GET /api/health`. The design also locks language/framework and the shared durable storage layout that Auth, messages, fan-out, IRC, and the SPA will all assume.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Language / HTTP framework | **Python 3.12 + FastAPI + Uvicorn** |\n| Shared durable store | **SQLite file** at `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` with **WAL** + busy timeout (shared by all nodes) |\n| Cross-node transport | **Local Redis** on `127.0.0.1:6379` (pub/sub / coordination only — **not** source of truth) |\n| Process supervisor | **`/app/start.sh`** (bash): create dirs, ensure venv+deps, start Redis + 3 Uvicorn workers, foreground wait loop with respawn |\n| Runtime root | Repo root **is** `/app` when the verifier runs |\n\n### Why this stack\n\n- Epic/instruction leave language open; Python 3.12, `sqlite3`, and `redis-server` are already on the image. FastAPI covers REST + future WebSockets (Starlette) without a second runtime for the backend/IRC path.\n- Redis outage requirements (MARATHON-14: writes and dense `seq` continue while Redis is dead) **forbid** using Redis as the durable store. SQLite on a shared filesystem path is the simplest self-contained SoT that all three processes can open.\n- A shell supervisor matches the verifier contract (`./start.sh` foreground) and can respawn both HTTP and Redis without DinD or external orchestrators.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Node.js + Express/Fastify | Equally viable for HTTP/WS; would split backend (IRC later) across languages or force Node for IRC too. Python keeps one backend language. |\n| Redis as primary DB | Contradicts Redis-`SIGKILL` resilience (writes must succeed without Redis). |\n| Postgres / Docker services | Remote/DinD-ish; not self-contained on this image. |\n| One process binding three ports | Harder crash isolation; grader kills **one** node and expects the other two to keep serving — three OS processes are required. |\n| Systemd / supervisord | Extra dependency; bash loop is enough and stays in-repo. |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nSQLite WAL under concurrent writers is correct for this density but needs disciplined `busy_timeout` / short transactions in later tasks. We accept that complexity over introducing another datastore. Dependency install on first boot (`pip install -r requirements.txt` into `/app/.venv`) adds a few seconds to cold start — acceptable vs baking undeclared global packages into the image.\n\n### Conventions fixed for sibling tasks (no sibling designs exist yet)\n\n1. Product name: **Huddle**.\n2. API prefix: `/api/...`; JSON; REST status codes per epic instruction.\n3. `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` ↔ ports `{8000,8001,8002}` (never swap).\n4. Durable SoT: SQLite under `/app/data/`; Redis is ephemeral fan-out only.\n5. Health response is **not** resource-enveloped (explicit epic exception): `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"node_id\":N}`.\n6. Env per process: `HUDDLE_NODE_ID`, `HUDDLE_PORT`, `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR` (default `/app/data`), `HUDDLE_REDIS_URL` (default `redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0`).\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Seam: Verifier / browser ↔ HTTP nodes\n\n#### `GET /api/health`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Server (each node)** | Return `200` with `Content-Type: application/json` body exactly shaped as below. Does **not** require auth. Does **not** need to probe Redis or SQLite for this task (liveness of the HTTP process is enough). |\n| **Client / grader** | `GET http://127.0.0.1:800{N}/api/health` and assert status + `node_id`. |\n\n**Response (200):**\n```json\n{\"status\": \"ok\", \"node_id\": 0}\n```\n- `status`: string, always `\"ok\"` when the process is serving this route.\n- `node_id`: integer `0` | `1` | `2` matching the process’s configured node (port 8000→0, 8001→1, 8002→2).\n\n**Failure / slow behavior:**\n- If the node process is dead (pre-respawn): TCP connection refused / reset. Clients retry; supervisor must restore the listener within **60s** of `SIGKILL`.\n- If the node is overloaded: may delay; no special health degradation payload in this task.\n- Wrong `node_id` for a port is a **hard fail** (misconfiguration), not a soft warning.\n\n#### `GET /`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Server** | `200` with an HTML document (text/html). Minimal stub page titled or branded “Huddle” so a browser fetch succeeds on every node. No SPA, no auth UI yet (MARATHON-16 owns that). |\n| **Client** | Expects HTML 200; must not depend on specific `data-testid`s until the SPA task. |\n\n**Failure:** same as health — connection errors until respawn.\n\n### Seam: `start.sh` ↔ child processes\n\n| Child | Bind | Identity | Restart |\n|-------|------|----------|---------|\n| `redis-server` | `127.0.0.1:6379` | pidfile under `/app/data/run/redis.pid` | Respawning required after `SIGKILL` |\n| Uvicorn node 0 | `127.0.0.1:8000` | `HUDDLE_NODE_ID=0` | Respawning within 60s |\n| Uvicorn node 1 | `127.0.0.1:8001` | `HUDDLE_NODE_ID=1` | Respawning within 60s |\n| Uvicorn node 2 | `127.0.0.1:8002` | `HUDDLE_NODE_ID=2` | Respawning within 60s |\n\n- `start.sh` remains the foreground PID the verifier tracks. It must not daemonize itself (`exit` only when shutting down).\n- On `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM` to `start.sh`: stop children (TERM then KILL), then exit non-zero or zero consistently; do not leave orphans listening on the fixed ports.\n- **No IRC listener in this task** (MARATHON-15). Port `6667` stays free.\n\n### Seam: HTTP nodes ↔ durable storage / Redis (layout only)\n\n- Nodes **may** open the SQLite file read/write in this task only to apply WAL pragmas / ensure the file exists; no product schema required yet beyond optional `schema_migrations` bootstrap (see Data Model).\n- Nodes **need not** connect to Redis for health/stub routes. Redis must still be **running** (and respawned) so later fan-out tasks find it at the fixed address.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Filesystem layout (authoritative)\n\n```\n/app/\n  start.sh                 # foreground supervisor (executable)\n  requirements.txt         # fastapi, uvicorn[standard], ...\n  .venv/                   # created at runtime by start.sh (gitignored)\n  server/\n    __init__.py\n    settings.py            # reads HUDDLE_* env; paths; node_id/port validation\n    app.py                 # FastAPI factory: GET /, GET /api/health\n  data/                    # durable root (survives process restarts)\n    huddle.sqlite          # shared DB (created on first start if missing)\n    huddle.sqlite-wal      # WAL sidecar (runtime)\n    huddle.sqlite-shm      # SHM sidecar (runtime)\n    redis/\n      redis.conf           # generated or checked-in local config\n      dump.rdb             # optional RDB (runtime)\n    files/                 # reserved for MARATHON-10 uploads (empty dir ok)\n    run/                   # pidfiles, redis pid (runtime; gitignored contents)\n  timer.sh                 # pre-existing harness helper — DO NOT MODIFY\n```\n\n### SQLite\n\n- **Path:** `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` (override only via `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`).\n- **Pragmas (every node on connect):** `journal_mode=WAL`, `busy_timeout=5000` (or ≥5s), `foreign_keys=ON`, `synchronous=NORMAL`.\n- **Schema in this task:** either (a) create an empty DB file with pragmas only, or (b) create a single bootstrap table:\n  - `schema_migrations(version INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, applied_at TEXT NOT NULL)` with no product rows.\n- **Product tables** (users, tokens, workspaces, …): **out of scope** — owned by MARATHON-3+.\n- **Backward compatibility:** greenfield; no migration from a prior schema.\n\n### Redis\n\n- Bind **only** `127.0.0.1:6379` (no external interfaces).\n- `dir` = `/app/data/redis`, `pidfile` = `/app/data/run/redis.pid`, `daemonize no` (supervised by `start.sh` as a background job via `&` + wait loop — Redis itself stays non-daemonized under the supervisor’s process group, or uses `daemonize no` and is backgrounded by the shell).\n- **No application key schema** in this task. Persistence (RDB) may be enabled for convenience but must not be treated as SoT by later designs.\n- AOF: optional; default off to keep boot simple unless implementer prefers AOF for local debugging.\n\n### Identity types (cluster-wide conventions for later tasks)\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `node_id` | `int` 0..2 | Process-local, not stored in SQLite |\n| Future resource `id` | stable string (ULID/UUID) | Not created here; document expectation only |\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `start.sh` | Executable supervisor: resolve `APP_ROOT`, `mkdir -p` data dirs, create `/app/.venv` if missing, `pip install -r requirements.txt`, write/ensure `data/redis/redis.conf`, start `redis-server`, start three `uvicorn server.app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port ...`, foreground respawn loop, signal cleanup. |\n| `requirements.txt` | Pin flexible-but-declared deps: `fastapi`, `uvicorn[standard]`; optionally `redis` package now so MARATHON-14 does not re-litigate install (unused in stub routes is fine). |\n| `server/__init__.py` | Empty or package marker. |\n| `server/settings.py` | Load `HUDDLE_NODE_ID`, `HUDDLE_PORT`, `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`; validate `node_id`∈{0,1,2} and port matches mapping; expose Redis URL and sqlite path helpers. |\n| `server/app.py` | FastAPI app: `GET /api/health` → JSON contract; `GET /` → minimal HTML stub. |\n| `data/redis/.gitkeep` | Ensure redis data dir exists in git. |\n| `data/files/.gitkeep` | Reserve upload root for MARATHON-10. |\n| `data/run/.gitkeep` | Runtime pid dir placeholder. |\n| `data/redis/redis.conf` | **Either** commit a static conf **or** generate from `start.sh`; must bind 127.0.0.1:6379 and set `dir`/`pidfile` under `/app/data`. |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `.gitignore` | Ignore `/app/.venv/`, `data/**/*.sqlite*`, `data/redis/dump.rdb`, `data/redis/appendonly.aof`, `data/run/*.pid`, keep ignoring existing harness paths (`loom-prompts/`, etc.). Do **not** ignore `data/**/.gitkeep` or a committed `redis.conf` if checked in. |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `timer.sh` | Harness time helper |\n| `loom-prompts/**` | Agent prompts |\n| IRC / SPA / Auth modules | Later tasks |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order for this task (single implementer)\n\n1. `requirements.txt` + `server/settings.py` + `server/app.py` (health + stub `/`).\n2. `.gitignore` + `data/**/.gitkeep` (+ optional `redis.conf`).\n3. `start.sh` supervisor last (wires everything).\n4. Manual verify: boot, health on three ports, kill one uvicorn + redis, confirm respawn.\n\nParallelism inside the task: server package vs ignore/data layout can proceed in parallel; `start.sh` depends on both.\n\n### Downstream seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumed by |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `start.sh` boots Redis + 3 nodes; health contract | Verifier, all backend tasks, QA |\n| `HUDDLE_NODE_ID` / port mapping | Logging, future debugging; MARATHON-14 |\n| `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` + WAL pragmas | MARATHON-3 (users/tokens), then all persistence tasks |\n| Redis at `127.0.0.1:6379` supervised/respawned | MARATHON-13/14 (pub/sub); must already be up |\n| Stub `GET /` | Replaced by MARATHON-16 SPA (same route) |\n| FastAPI app factory in `server.app:app` | All later route modules mount on same app |\n\n### Must land before\n\n- **MARATHON-3** (Auth) is blocked on this task — needs live nodes + shared DB path.\n- No other task should invent a second supervisor or a different port/node map.\n\n### Suggested follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n\n- Product schema migrations framework details → first persistence task (MARATHON-3) can add Alembic/raw SQL migrations on the shared file.\n- WebSocket / fan-out / IRC → MARATHON-13/14/15.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|\n| Auth register/login/me (MARATHON-3) | Separate task; only needs our DB path + live nodes |\n| Profiles, workspaces, channels, messages, DMs, files, search, groups | MARATHON-4…12 |\n| WebSocket subscribe/resume + dense seq (MARATHON-13) | Depends on messages |\n| Cross-node fan-out + Redis-outage behavior beyond respawn (MARATHON-14) | Needs events; this task only respawns Redis |\n| IRC `:6667` (MARATHON-15) | Explicit later task; neighborhood/harness ports list includes 6667 but we must not bind it yet |\n| SPA + `data-testid`s (MARATHON-16+) | Replaces stub `GET /` |\n| `timer.sh` behavior | Harness-owned |\n| Enveloped error JSON conventions beyond health | Defined in epic; apply starting with Auth |\n| Neighborhood scan of repo code for `start.sh` / `redis` / `/api/health` | **No hits** in the empty baseline beyond `timer.sh` and empty `data/` — nothing else to exclude |\n\n**Neighborhood scan result:** baseline repo contains only `timer.sh`, empty `data/`, `.gitignore`, and `loom-prompts/`. No pre-existing HTTP server, Redis config, or health route to reconcile. Harness utilities `marathon-freeports` / `marathon-portlock` clear ports `{8000,8001,8002,6667,6379}` before verify — implementers must not rely on stale listeners.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Cold start, empty `data/` | `start.sh` creates dirs + sqlite file; starts Redis; starts 3 nodes; then blocks in wait/respawn loop. |\n| Port 800x already busy at start | Fail fast: log which port, exit non-zero. Do not partially serve “whatever’s free.” (Verifier runs `marathon-freeports` first; residual busy = real error.) |\n| Port 6379 busy at start with foreign process | Fail fast after brief retry; do not attach to unknown Redis. |\n| HTTP child `SIGKILL` | Supervisor detects exit (wait/`SIGCHLD`/poll ≤2s); restart that node only with same `HUDDLE_NODE_ID`/port; listener restored in **&lt; 60s**. Other nodes uninterrupted. |\n| Redis `SIGKILL` | Supervisor restarts `redis-server` with same conf. (Fan-out degradation during gap is MARATHON-14; here only respawn is required.) |\n| Repeated crash loop | Keep respawning (with optional short backoff ≤2s) so the 60s window is met; log each restart to stdout/stderr (captured by verifier logs). |\n| `start.sh` receives `SIGTERM`/`SIGINT` | Propagate shutdown to Redis + all nodes; wait briefly; `_exit`. No orphaned listeners. |\n| `HUDDLE_NODE_ID` missing when launching uvicorn manually | `settings.py` aborts process startup with clear error (non-zero). `start.sh` always sets the env. |\n| `node_id`/port mismatch (e.g. id=0 on 8001) | Refuse to start that process. |\n| pip / venv failure | Exit non-zero before binding ports; do not hang silently. |\n| SQLite locked during bootstrap | Retry within busy_timeout; if still failing, log and exit that node (supervisor will respawn). |\n| Health called during startup race | Until bind completes, connection refused — acceptable. After bind, health must be correct. |\n| Partial cluster (only 2 nodes up) | Allowed transiently during respawn; steady state is 3. |\n| Writing product data | Not in this task; stub routes are read-only. |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `test -x /app/start.sh` (or repo-root `start.sh` executable bit set).\n2. Running `./start.sh` from `/app` does not exit on its own while children are healthy (foreground supervisor).\n3. Within a short boot window (e.g. ≤30s cold including pip), all of the following succeed:\n   - `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health` → `200` JSON `status==\"ok\"` and `node_id==0`\n   - same for `:8001` → `node_id==1`\n   - same for `:8002` → `node_id==2`\n4. `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8000/` (and 8001/8002) → `200` with `Content-Type` HTML (or text/html).\n5. `redis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 -p 6379 PING` → `PONG` while `start.sh` is alive.\n6. **HTTP respawn:** `SIGKILL` one uvicorn/node PID; without rerunning `start.sh`, within **60s** that port’s `/api/health` returns 200 with the **same** `node_id` as before. The other two ports remain healthy throughout.\n7. **Redis respawn:** `SIGKILL` the redis-server PID; without rerunning `start.sh`, `PING` succeeds again after respawn (implementer should target well under 60s; epic’s 5s write continuity is **not** required until MARATHON-14).\n8. **Negative:** `node_id` values must **not** be swapped across ports; health must **not** require `Authorization`.\n9. **Negative:** `start.sh` must **not** depend on Docker, remote Redis, or network services outside localhost.\n10. **Negative:** this task must **not** bind `:6667`.\n11. Durable path `/app/data/` exists after boot; sqlite file present if bootstrap creates it.\n12. No modifications to `timer.sh`.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated / scriptable checks (implementer or QA)\n\n```bash\ncd /app && ./start.sh &\n# wait for health on 8000/8001/8002\nfor p in 0 1 2; do\n  curl -sf \"http://127.0.0.1:800${p}/api/health\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); assert d=={'status':'ok','node_id':$p}\"\ndone\nredis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 -p 6379 PING | grep PONG\n# kill one node\nkill -9 \"$(pgrep -f 'uvicorn.*8001' | head -1)\"\n# poll until 8001 health returns node_id 1 within 60s\n# kill redis and poll PING\n```\n\n### Manual verification\n\n1. Boot `./start.sh`; watch logs for three “Uvicorn running” lines and Redis ready.\n2. Browser or curl `GET /` on each port — stub HTML loads.\n3. `kill -9` a node; confirm curl failures then recovery &lt;60s.\n4. `kill -9` redis; confirm `redis-cli PING` recovers via supervisor.\n5. `kill` the `start.sh` process group; confirm ports are free (`marathon-freeports` / `ss`).\n\n### Out of scope for this task’s tests\n\nAuth flows, WS fan-out during Redis outage, IRC, SPA selectors — covered by later tasks/QA once those land.\nDESIGN_EOF\n# Save design via loom\nloom data update MARATHON-2 --design=\"$(cat /tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md)\" --design-format=markdown --notes=\"New design (no needs-revision). No sibling designs existed; conventions established here for Python/FastAPI+Uvicorn, SQLite WAL at /app/data/huddle.sqlite, Redis pub/sub-only on :6379, node_id↔port map. Keep label backend for implementer routing after architect approval removes architect.\"\n","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-20c38e59-8191-4312-9cf7-efd810fcb317-8\nfc_7e5d4971-6bfc-94b8-9bd5-8105cdcdda8d_0","simpleCommands":["cat","loom","cat"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cat","args":[],"fullText":"cat"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"update"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-2"},{"type":"concatenation","value":"--design=\"$(cat /tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md)\""},{"type":"word","value":"--design-format=markdown"},{"type":"concatenation","value":"--notes=\"New design (no needs-revision). No sibling designs existed; conventions established here for Python/FastAPI+Uvicorn, SQLite WAL at /app/data/huddle.sqlite, Redis pub/sub-only on :6379, node_id↔port map. Keep label backend for implementer routing after architect approval removes architect.\""}],"fullText":"loom data update MARATHON-2 --design=\"$(cat /tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md)\" --design-format=markdown --notes=\"New design (no needs-revision). No sibling designs existed; conventions established here for Python/FastAPI+Uvicorn, SQLite WAL at /app/data/huddle.sqlite, Redis pub/sub-only on :6379, node_id↔port map. Keep label backend for implementer routing after architect approval removes architect.\""},{"name":"cat","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md"}],"fullText":"cat /tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":true,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":false,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"cat"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Write and save MARATHON-2 design","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"75e8a5ba-5b3e-48bc-a76f-1e5b5bfde32d","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"description":"Write and save MARATHON-2 design"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-20c38e59-8191-4312-9cf7-efd810fcb317-8\nfc_7e5d4971-6bfc-94b8-9bd5-8105cdcdda8d_0","startedAtMs":"1787437240231"},"model_call_id":"3487d7ee-7391-4e0b-a56e-b1f7a484b8fa-8-79uv","session_id":"75e8a5ba-5b3e-48bc-a76f-1e5b5bfde32d","timestamp_ms":1787437240278}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-20c38e59-8191-4312-9cf7-efd810fcb317-8\nfc_7e5d4971-6bfc-94b8-9bd5-8105cdcdda8d_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cat > /tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n# MARATHON-2 — Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task boots the Huddle cluster so the verifier (and every later feature task) has a live, self-contained process tree: `/app/start.sh` stays in the foreground, supervises a local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, and respawns any of those children after `SIGKILL`. Each node exposes a stub `GET /` and the contracted `GET /api/health`. The design also locks language/framework and the shared durable storage layout that Auth, messages, fan-out, IRC, and the SPA will all assume.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Language / HTTP framework | **Python 3.12 + FastAPI + Uvicorn** |\n| Shared durable store | **SQLite file** at `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` with **WAL** + busy timeout (shared by all nodes) |\n| Cross-node transport | **Local Redis** on `127.0.0.1:6379` (pub/sub / coordination only — **not** source of truth) |\n| Process supervisor | **`/app/start.sh`** (bash): create dirs, ensure venv+deps, start Redis + 3 Uvicorn workers, foreground wait loop with respawn |\n| Runtime root | Repo root **is** `/app` when the verifier runs |\n\n### Why this stack\n\n- Epic/instruction leave language open; Python 3.12, `sqlite3`, and `redis-server` are already on the image. FastAPI covers REST + future WebSockets (Starlette) without a second runtime for the backend/IRC path.\n- Redis outage requirements (MARATHON-14: writes and dense `seq` continue while Redis is dead) **forbid** using Redis as the durable store. SQLite on a shared filesystem path is the simplest self-contained SoT that all three processes can open.\n- A shell supervisor matches the verifier contract (`./start.sh` foreground) and can respawn both HTTP and Redis without DinD or external orchestrators.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Node.js + Express/Fastify | Equally viable for HTTP/WS; would split backend (IRC later) across languages or force Node for IRC too. Python keeps one backend language. |\n| Redis as primary DB | Contradicts Redis-`SIGKILL` resilience (writes must succeed without Redis). |\n| Postgres / Docker services | Remote/DinD-ish; not self-contained on this image. |\n| One process binding three ports | Harder crash isolation; grader kills **one** node and expects the other two to keep serving — three OS processes are required. |\n| Systemd / supervisord | Extra dependency; bash loop is enough and stays in-repo. |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nSQLite WAL under concurrent writers is correct for this density but needs disciplined `busy_timeout` / short transactions in later tasks. We accept that complexity over introducing another datastore. Dependency install on first boot (`pip install -r requirements.txt` into `/app/.venv`) adds a few seconds to cold start — acceptable vs baking undeclared global packages into the image.\n\n### Conventions fixed for sibling tasks (no sibling designs exist yet)\n\n1. Product name: **Huddle**.\n2. API prefix: `/api/...`; JSON; REST status codes per epic instruction.\n3. `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` ↔ ports `{8000,8001,8002}` (never swap).\n4. Durable SoT: SQLite under `/app/data/`; Redis is ephemeral fan-out only.\n5. Health response is **not** resource-enveloped (explicit epic exception): `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"node_id\":N}`.\n6. Env per process: `HUDDLE_NODE_ID`, `HUDDLE_PORT`, `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR` (default `/app/data`), `HUDDLE_REDIS_URL` (default `redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0`).\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Seam: Verifier / browser ↔ HTTP nodes\n\n#### `GET /api/health`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Server (each node)** | Return `200` with `Content-Type: application/json` body exactly shaped as below. Does **not** require auth. Does **not** need to probe Redis or SQLite for this task (liveness of the HTTP process is enough). |\n| **Client / grader** | `GET http://127.0.0.1:800{N}/api/health` and assert status + `node_id`. |\n\n**Response (200):**\n```json\n{\"status\": \"ok\", \"node_id\": 0}\n```\n- `status`: string, always `\"ok\"` when the process is serving this route.\n- `node_id`: integer `0` | `1` | `2` matching the process’s configured node (port 8000→0, 8001→1, 8002→2).\n\n**Failure / slow behavior:**\n- If the node process is dead (pre-respawn): TCP connection refused / reset. Clients retry; supervisor must restore the listener within **60s** of `SIGKILL`.\n- If the node is overloaded: may delay; no special health degradation payload in this task.\n- Wrong `node_id` for a port is a **hard fail** (misconfiguration), not a soft warning.\n\n#### `GET /`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Server** | `200` with an HTML document (text/html). Minimal stub page titled or branded “Huddle” so a browser fetch succeeds on every node. No SPA, no auth UI yet (MARATHON-16 owns that). |\n| **Client** | Expects HTML 200; must not depend on specific `data-testid`s until the SPA task. |\n\n**Failure:** same as health — connection errors until respawn.\n\n### Seam: `start.sh` ↔ child processes\n\n| Child | Bind | Identity | Restart |\n|-------|------|----------|---------|\n| `redis-server` | `127.0.0.1:6379` | pidfile under `/app/data/run/redis.pid` | Respawning required after `SIGKILL` |\n| Uvicorn node 0 | `127.0.0.1:8000` | `HUDDLE_NODE_ID=0` | Respawning within 60s |\n| Uvicorn node 1 | `127.0.0.1:8001` | `HUDDLE_NODE_ID=1` | Respawning within 60s |\n| Uvicorn node 2 | `127.0.0.1:8002` | `HUDDLE_NODE_ID=2` | Respawning within 60s |\n\n- `start.sh` remains the foreground PID the verifier tracks. It must not daemonize itself (`exit` only when shutting down).\n- On `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM` to `start.sh`: stop children (TERM then KILL), then exit non-zero or zero consistently; do not leave orphans listening on the fixed ports.\n- **No IRC listener in this task** (MARATHON-15). Port `6667` stays free.\n\n### Seam: HTTP nodes ↔ durable storage / Redis (layout only)\n\n- Nodes **may** open the SQLite file read/write in this task only to apply WAL pragmas / ensure the file exists; no product schema required yet beyond optional `schema_migrations` bootstrap (see Data Model).\n- Nodes **need not** connect to Redis for health/stub routes. Redis must still be **running** (and respawned) so later fan-out tasks find it at the fixed address.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Filesystem layout (authoritative)\n\n```\n/app/\n  start.sh                 # foreground supervisor (executable)\n  requirements.txt         # fastapi, uvicorn[standard], ...\n  .venv/                   # created at runtime by start.sh (gitignored)\n  server/\n    __init__.py\n    settings.py            # reads HUDDLE_* env; paths; node_id/port validation\n    app.py                 # FastAPI factory: GET /, GET /api/health\n  data/                    # durable root (survives process restarts)\n    huddle.sqlite          # shared DB (created on first start if missing)\n    huddle.sqlite-wal      # WAL sidecar (runtime)\n    huddle.sqlite-shm      # SHM sidecar (runtime)\n    redis/\n      redis.conf           # generated or checked-in local config\n      dump.rdb             # optional RDB (runtime)\n    files/                 # reserved for MARATHON-10 uploads (empty dir ok)\n    run/                   # pidfiles, redis pid (runtime; gitignored contents)\n  timer.sh                 # pre-existing harness helper — DO NOT MODIFY\n```\n\n### SQLite\n\n- **Path:** `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` (override only via `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`).\n- **Pragmas (every node on connect):** `journal_mode=WAL`, `busy_timeout=5000` (or ≥5s), `foreign_keys=ON`, `synchronous=NORMAL`.\n- **Schema in this task:** either (a) create an empty DB file with pragmas only, or (b) create a single bootstrap table:\n  - `schema_migrations(version INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, applied_at TEXT NOT NULL)` with no product rows.\n- **Product tables** (users, tokens, workspaces, …): **out of scope** — owned by MARATHON-3+.\n- **Backward compatibility:** greenfield; no migration from a prior schema.\n\n### Redis\n\n- Bind **only** `127.0.0.1:6379` (no external interfaces).\n- `dir` = `/app/data/redis`, `pidfile` = `/app/data/run/redis.pid`, `daemonize no` (supervised by `start.sh` as a background job via `&` + wait loop — Redis itself stays non-daemonized under the supervisor’s process group, or uses `daemonize no` and is backgrounded by the shell).\n- **No application key schema** in this task. Persistence (RDB) may be enabled for convenience but must not be treated as SoT by later designs.\n- AOF: optional; default off to keep boot simple unless implementer prefers AOF for local debugging.\n\n### Identity types (cluster-wide conventions for later tasks)\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `node_id` | `int` 0..2 | Process-local, not stored in SQLite |\n| Future resource `id` | stable string (ULID/UUID) | Not created here; document expectation only |\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `start.sh` | Executable supervisor: resolve `APP_ROOT`, `mkdir -p` data dirs, create `/app/.venv` if missing, `pip install -r requirements.txt`, write/ensure `data/redis/redis.conf`, start `redis-server`, start three `uvicorn server.app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port ...`, foreground respawn loop, signal cleanup. |\n| `requirements.txt` | Pin flexible-but-declared deps: `fastapi`, `uvicorn[standard]`; optionally `redis` package now so MARATHON-14 does not re-litigate install (unused in stub routes is fine). |\n| `server/__init__.py` | Empty or package marker. |\n| `server/settings.py` | Load `HUDDLE_NODE_ID`, `HUDDLE_PORT`, `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`; validate `node_id`∈{0,1,2} and port matches mapping; expose Redis URL and sqlite path helpers. |\n| `server/app.py` | FastAPI app: `GET /api/health` → JSON contract; `GET /` → minimal HTML stub. |\n| `data/redis/.gitkeep` | Ensure redis data dir exists in git. |\n| `data/files/.gitkeep` | Reserve upload root for MARATHON-10. |\n| `data/run/.gitkeep` | Runtime pid dir placeholder. |\n| `data/redis/redis.conf` | **Either** commit a static conf **or** generate from `start.sh`; must bind 127.0.0.1:6379 and set `dir`/`pidfile` under `/app/data`. |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `.gitignore` | Ignore `/app/.venv/`, `data/**/*.sqlite*`, `data/redis/dump.rdb`, `data/redis/appendonly.aof`, `data/run/*.pid`, keep ignoring existing harness paths (`loom-prompts/`, etc.). Do **not** ignore `data/**/.gitkeep` or a committed `redis.conf` if checked in. |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `timer.sh` | Harness time helper |\n| `loom-prompts/**` | Agent prompts |\n| IRC / SPA / Auth modules | Later tasks |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order for this task (single implementer)\n\n1. `requirements.txt` + `server/settings.py` + `server/app.py` (health + stub `/`).\n2. `.gitignore` + `data/**/.gitkeep` (+ optional `redis.conf`).\n3. `start.sh` supervisor last (wires everything).\n4. Manual verify: boot, health on three ports, kill one uvicorn + redis, confirm respawn.\n\nParallelism inside the task: server package vs ignore/data layout can proceed in parallel; `start.sh` depends on both.\n\n### Downstream seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumed by |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `start.sh` boots Redis + 3 nodes; health contract | Verifier, all backend tasks, QA |\n| `HUDDLE_NODE_ID` / port mapping | Logging, future debugging; MARATHON-14 |\n| `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` + WAL pragmas | MARATHON-3 (users/tokens), then all persistence tasks |\n| Redis at `127.0.0.1:6379` supervised/respawned | MARATHON-13/14 (pub/sub); must already be up |\n| Stub `GET /` | Replaced by MARATHON-16 SPA (same route) |\n| FastAPI app factory in `server.app:app` | All later route modules mount on same app |\n\n### Must land before\n\n- **MARATHON-3** (Auth) is blocked on this task — needs live nodes + shared DB path.\n- No other task should invent a second supervisor or a different port/node map.\n\n### Suggested follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n\n- Product schema migrations framework details → first persistence task (MARATHON-3) can add Alembic/raw SQL migrations on the shared file.\n- WebSocket / fan-out / IRC → MARATHON-13/14/15.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|\n| Auth register/login/me (MARATHON-3) | Separate task; only needs our DB path + live nodes |\n| Profiles, workspaces, channels, messages, DMs, files, search, groups | MARATHON-4…12 |\n| WebSocket subscribe/resume + dense seq (MARATHON-13) | Depends on messages |\n| Cross-node fan-out + Redis-outage behavior beyond respawn (MARATHON-14) | Needs events; this task only respawns Redis |\n| IRC `:6667` (MARATHON-15) | Explicit later task; neighborhood/harness ports list includes 6667 but we must not bind it yet |\n| SPA + `data-testid`s (MARATHON-16+) | Replaces stub `GET /` |\n| `timer.sh` behavior | Harness-owned |\n| Enveloped error JSON conventions beyond health | Defined in epic; apply starting with Auth |\n| Neighborhood scan of repo code for `start.sh` / `redis` / `/api/health` | **No hits** in the empty baseline beyond `timer.sh` and empty `data/` — nothing else to exclude |\n\n**Neighborhood scan result:** baseline repo contains only `timer.sh`, empty `data/`, `.gitignore`, and `loom-prompts/`. No pre-existing HTTP server, Redis config, or health route to reconcile. Harness utilities `marathon-freeports` / `marathon-portlock` clear ports `{8000,8001,8002,6667,6379}` before verify — implementers must not rely on stale listeners.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Cold start, empty `data/` | `start.sh` creates dirs + sqlite file; starts Redis; starts 3 nodes; then blocks in wait/respawn loop. |\n| Port 800x already busy at start | Fail fast: log which port, exit non-zero. Do not partially serve “whatever’s free.” (Verifier runs `marathon-freeports` first; residual busy = real error.) |\n| Port 6379 busy at start with foreign process | Fail fast after brief retry; do not attach to unknown Redis. |\n| HTTP child `SIGKILL` | Supervisor detects exit (wait/`SIGCHLD`/poll ≤2s); restart that node only with same `HUDDLE_NODE_ID`/port; listener restored in **&lt; 60s**. Other nodes uninterrupted. |\n| Redis `SIGKILL` | Supervisor restarts `redis-server` with same conf. (Fan-out degradation during gap is MARATHON-14; here only respawn is required.) |\n| Repeated crash loop | Keep respawning (with optional short backoff ≤2s) so the 60s window is met; log each restart to stdout/stderr (captured by verifier logs). |\n| `start.sh` receives `SIGTERM`/`SIGINT` | Propagate shutdown to Redis + all nodes; wait briefly; `_exit`. No orphaned listeners. |\n| `HUDDLE_NODE_ID` missing when launching uvicorn manually | `settings.py` aborts process startup with clear error (non-zero). `start.sh` always sets the env. |\n| `node_id`/port mismatch (e.g. id=0 on 8001) | Refuse to start that process. |\n| pip / venv failure | Exit non-zero before binding ports; do not hang silently. |\n| SQLite locked during bootstrap | Retry within busy_timeout; if still failing, log and exit that node (supervisor will respawn). |\n| Health called during startup race | Until bind completes, connection refused — acceptable. After bind, health must be correct. |\n| Partial cluster (only 2 nodes up) | Allowed transiently during respawn; steady state is 3. |\n| Writing product data | Not in this task; stub routes are read-only. |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `test -x /app/start.sh` (or repo-root `start.sh` executable bit set).\n2. Running `./start.sh` from `/app` does not exit on its own while children are healthy (foreground supervisor).\n3. Within a short boot window (e.g. ≤30s cold including pip), all of the following succeed:\n   - `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health` → `200` JSON `status==\"ok\"` and `node_id==0`\n   - same for `:8001` → `node_id==1`\n   - same for `:8002` → `node_id==2`\n4. `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8000/` (and 8001/8002) → `200` with `Content-Type` HTML (or text/html).\n5. `redis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 -p 6379 PING` → `PONG` while `start.sh` is alive.\n6. **HTTP respawn:** `SIGKILL` one uvicorn/node PID; without rerunning `start.sh`, within **60s** that port’s `/api/health` returns 200 with the **same** `node_id` as before. The other two ports remain healthy throughout.\n7. **Redis respawn:** `SIGKILL` the redis-server PID; without rerunning `start.sh`, `PING` succeeds again after respawn (implementer should target well under 60s; epic’s 5s write continuity is **not** required until MARATHON-14).\n8. **Negative:** `node_id` values must **not** be swapped across ports; health must **not** require `Authorization`.\n9. **Negative:** `start.sh` must **not** depend on Docker, remote Redis, or network services outside localhost.\n10. **Negative:** this task must **not** bind `:6667`.\n11. Durable path `/app/data/` exists after boot; sqlite file present if bootstrap creates it.\n12. No modifications to `timer.sh`.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated / scriptable checks (implementer or QA)\n\n```bash\ncd /app && ./start.sh &\n# wait for health on 8000/8001/8002\nfor p in 0 1 2; do\n  curl -sf \"http://127.0.0.1:800${p}/api/health\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); assert d=={'status':'ok','node_id':$p}\"\ndone\nredis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 -p 6379 PING | grep PONG\n# kill one node\nkill -9 \"$(pgrep -f 'uvicorn.*8001' | head -1)\"\n# poll until 8001 health returns node_id 1 within 60s\n# kill redis and poll PING\n```\n\n### Manual verification\n\n1. Boot `./start.sh`; watch logs for three “Uvicorn running” lines and Redis ready.\n2. Browser or curl `GET /` on each port — stub HTML loads.\n3. `kill -9` a node; confirm curl failures then recovery &lt;60s.\n4. `kill -9` redis; confirm `redis-cli PING` recovers via supervisor.\n5. `kill` the `start.sh` process group; confirm ports are free (`marathon-freeports` / `ss`).\n\n### Out of scope for this task’s tests\n\nAuth flows, WS fan-out during Redis outage, IRC, SPA selectors — covered by later tasks/QA once those land.\nDESIGN_EOF\n# Save design via loom\nloom data update MARATHON-2 --design=\"$(cat /tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md)\" --design-format=markdown --notes=\"New design (no needs-revision). No sibling designs existed; conventions established here for Python/FastAPI+Uvicorn, SQLite WAL at /app/data/huddle.sqlite, Redis pub/sub-only on :6379, node_id↔port map. Keep label backend for implementer routing after architect approval removes architect.\"\n","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-20c38e59-8191-4312-9cf7-efd810fcb317-8\nfc_7e5d4971-6bfc-94b8-9bd5-8105cdcdda8d_0","simpleCommands":["cat","loom","cat"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cat","args":[],"fullText":"cat"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"update"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-2"},{"type":"concatenation","value":"--design=\"$(cat /tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md)\""},{"type":"word","value":"--design-format=markdown"},{"type":"concatenation","value":"--notes=\"New design (no needs-revision). No sibling designs existed; conventions established here for Python/FastAPI+Uvicorn, SQLite WAL at /app/data/huddle.sqlite, Redis pub/sub-only on :6379, node_id↔port map. Keep label backend for implementer routing after architect approval removes architect.\""}],"fullText":"loom data update MARATHON-2 --design=\"$(cat /tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md)\" --design-format=markdown --notes=\"New design (no needs-revision). No sibling designs existed; conventions established here for Python/FastAPI+Uvicorn, SQLite WAL at /app/data/huddle.sqlite, Redis pub/sub-only on :6379, node_id↔port map. Keep label backend for implementer routing after architect approval removes architect.\""},{"name":"cat","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md"}],"fullText":"cat /tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":true,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":false,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"cat"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Write and save MARATHON-2 design","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"75e8a5ba-5b3e-48bc-a76f-1e5b5bfde32d","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"cat > /tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n# MARATHON-2 — Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task boots the Huddle cluster so the verifier (and every later feature task) has a live, self-contained process tree: `/app/start.sh` stays in the foreground, supervises a local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, and respawns any of those children after `SIGKILL`. Each node exposes a stub `GET /` and the contracted `GET /api/health`. The design also locks language/framework and the shared durable storage layout that Auth, messages, fan-out, IRC, and the SPA will all assume.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Language / HTTP framework | **Python 3.12 + FastAPI + Uvicorn** |\n| Shared durable store | **SQLite file** at `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` with **WAL** + busy timeout (shared by all nodes) |\n| Cross-node transport | **Local Redis** on `127.0.0.1:6379` (pub/sub / coordination only — **not** source of truth) |\n| Process supervisor | **`/app/start.sh`** (bash): create dirs, ensure venv+deps, start Redis + 3 Uvicorn workers, foreground wait loop with respawn |\n| Runtime root | Repo root **is** `/app` when the verifier runs |\n\n### Why this stack\n\n- Epic/instruction leave language open; Python 3.12, `sqlite3`, and `redis-server` are already on the image. FastAPI covers REST + future WebSockets (Starlette) without a second runtime for the backend/IRC path.\n- Redis outage requirements (MARATHON-14: writes and dense `seq` continue while Redis is dead) **forbid** using Redis as the durable store. SQLite on a shared filesystem path is the simplest self-contained SoT that all three processes can open.\n- A shell supervisor matches the verifier contract (`./start.sh` foreground) and can respawn both HTTP and Redis without DinD or external orchestrators.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Node.js + Express/Fastify | Equally viable for HTTP/WS; would split backend (IRC later) across languages or force Node for IRC too. Python keeps one backend language. |\n| Redis as primary DB | Contradicts Redis-`SIGKILL` resilience (writes must succeed without Redis). |\n| Postgres / Docker services | Remote/DinD-ish; not self-contained on this image. |\n| One process binding three ports | Harder crash isolation; grader kills **one** node and expects the other two to keep serving — three OS processes are required. |\n| Systemd / supervisord | Extra dependency; bash loop is enough and stays in-repo. |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nSQLite WAL under concurrent writers is correct for this density but needs disciplined `busy_timeout` / short transactions in later tasks. We accept that complexity over introducing another datastore. Dependency install on first boot (`pip install -r requirements.txt` into `/app/.venv`) adds a few seconds to cold start — acceptable vs baking undeclared global packages into the image.\n\n### Conventions fixed for sibling tasks (no sibling designs exist yet)\n\n1. Product name: **Huddle**.\n2. API prefix: `/api/...`; JSON; REST status codes per epic instruction.\n3. `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` ↔ ports `{8000,8001,8002}` (never swap).\n4. Durable SoT: SQLite under `/app/data/`; Redis is ephemeral fan-out only.\n5. Health response is **not** resource-enveloped (explicit epic exception): `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"node_id\":N}`.\n6. Env per process: `HUDDLE_NODE_ID`, `HUDDLE_PORT`, `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR` (default `/app/data`), `HUDDLE_REDIS_URL` (default `redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0`).\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Seam: Verifier / browser ↔ HTTP nodes\n\n#### `GET /api/health`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Server (each node)** | Return `200` with `Content-Type: application/json` body exactly shaped as below. Does **not** require auth. Does **not** need to probe Redis or SQLite for this task (liveness of the HTTP process is enough). |\n| **Client / grader** | `GET http://127.0.0.1:800{N}/api/health` and assert status + `node_id`. |\n\n**Response (200):**\n```json\n{\"status\": \"ok\", \"node_id\": 0}\n```\n- `status`: string, always `\"ok\"` when the process is serving this route.\n- `node_id`: integer `0` | `1` | `2` matching the process’s configured node (port 8000→0, 8001→1, 8002→2).\n\n**Failure / slow behavior:**\n- If the node process is dead (pre-respawn): TCP connection refused / reset. Clients retry; supervisor must restore the listener within **60s** of `SIGKILL`.\n- If the node is overloaded: may delay; no special health degradation payload in this task.\n- Wrong `node_id` for a port is a **hard fail** (misconfiguration), not a soft warning.\n\n#### `GET /`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Server** | `200` with an HTML document (text/html). Minimal stub page titled or branded “Huddle” so a browser fetch succeeds on every node. No SPA, no auth UI yet (MARATHON-16 owns that). |\n| **Client** | Expects HTML 200; must not depend on specific `data-testid`s until the SPA task. |\n\n**Failure:** same as health — connection errors until respawn.\n\n### Seam: `start.sh` ↔ child processes\n\n| Child | Bind | Identity | Restart |\n|-------|------|----------|---------|\n| `redis-server` | `127.0.0.1:6379` | pidfile under `/app/data/run/redis.pid` | Respawning required after `SIGKILL` |\n| Uvicorn node 0 | `127.0.0.1:8000` | `HUDDLE_NODE_ID=0` | Respawning within 60s |\n| Uvicorn node 1 | `127.0.0.1:8001` | `HUDDLE_NODE_ID=1` | Respawning within 60s |\n| Uvicorn node 2 | `127.0.0.1:8002` | `HUDDLE_NODE_ID=2` | Respawning within 60s |\n\n- `start.sh` remains the foreground PID the verifier tracks. It must not daemonize itself (`exit` only when shutting down).\n- On `SIGINT`/`SIGTERM` to `start.sh`: stop children (TERM then KILL), then exit non-zero or zero consistently; do not leave orphans listening on the fixed ports.\n- **No IRC listener in this task** (MARATHON-15). Port `6667` stays free.\n\n### Seam: HTTP nodes ↔ durable storage / Redis (layout only)\n\n- Nodes **may** open the SQLite file read/write in this task only to apply WAL pragmas / ensure the file exists; no product schema required yet beyond optional `schema_migrations` bootstrap (see Data Model).\n- Nodes **need not** connect to Redis for health/stub routes. Redis must still be **running** (and respawned) so later fan-out tasks find it at the fixed address.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Filesystem layout (authoritative)\n\n```\n/app/\n  start.sh                 # foreground supervisor (executable)\n  requirements.txt         # fastapi, uvicorn[standard], ...\n  .venv/                   # created at runtime by start.sh (gitignored)\n  server/\n    __init__.py\n    settings.py            # reads HUDDLE_* env; paths; node_id/port validation\n    app.py                 # FastAPI factory: GET /, GET /api/health\n  data/                    # durable root (survives process restarts)\n    huddle.sqlite          # shared DB (created on first start if missing)\n    huddle.sqlite-wal      # WAL sidecar (runtime)\n    huddle.sqlite-shm      # SHM sidecar (runtime)\n    redis/\n      redis.conf           # generated or checked-in local config\n      dump.rdb             # optional RDB (runtime)\n    files/                 # reserved for MARATHON-10 uploads (empty dir ok)\n    run/                   # pidfiles, redis pid (runtime; gitignored contents)\n  timer.sh                 # pre-existing harness helper — DO NOT MODIFY\n```\n\n### SQLite\n\n- **Path:** `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` (override only via `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`).\n- **Pragmas (every node on connect):** `journal_mode=WAL`, `busy_timeout=5000` (or ≥5s), `foreign_keys=ON`, `synchronous=NORMAL`.\n- **Schema in this task:** either (a) create an empty DB file with pragmas only, or (b) create a single bootstrap table:\n  - `schema_migrations(version INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, applied_at TEXT NOT NULL)` with no product rows.\n- **Product tables** (users, tokens, workspaces, …): **out of scope** — owned by MARATHON-3+.\n- **Backward compatibility:** greenfield; no migration from a prior schema.\n\n### Redis\n\n- Bind **only** `127.0.0.1:6379` (no external interfaces).\n- `dir` = `/app/data/redis`, `pidfile` = `/app/data/run/redis.pid`, `daemonize no` (supervised by `start.sh` as a background job via `&` + wait loop — Redis itself stays non-daemonized under the supervisor’s process group, or uses `daemonize no` and is backgrounded by the shell).\n- **No application key schema** in this task. Persistence (RDB) may be enabled for convenience but must not be treated as SoT by later designs.\n- AOF: optional; default off to keep boot simple unless implementer prefers AOF for local debugging.\n\n### Identity types (cluster-wide conventions for later tasks)\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `node_id` | `int` 0..2 | Process-local, not stored in SQLite |\n| Future resource `id` | stable string (ULID/UUID) | Not created here; document expectation only |\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `start.sh` | Executable supervisor: resolve `APP_ROOT`, `mkdir -p` data dirs, create `/app/.venv` if missing, `pip install -r requirements.txt`, write/ensure `data/redis/redis.conf`, start `redis-server`, start three `uvicorn server.app:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port ...`, foreground respawn loop, signal cleanup. |\n| `requirements.txt` | Pin flexible-but-declared deps: `fastapi`, `uvicorn[standard]`; optionally `redis` package now so MARATHON-14 does not re-litigate install (unused in stub routes is fine). |\n| `server/__init__.py` | Empty or package marker. |\n| `server/settings.py` | Load `HUDDLE_NODE_ID`, `HUDDLE_PORT`, `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`; validate `node_id`∈{0,1,2} and port matches mapping; expose Redis URL and sqlite path helpers. |\n| `server/app.py` | FastAPI app: `GET /api/health` → JSON contract; `GET /` → minimal HTML stub. |\n| `data/redis/.gitkeep` | Ensure redis data dir exists in git. |\n| `data/files/.gitkeep` | Reserve upload root for MARATHON-10. |\n| `data/run/.gitkeep` | Runtime pid dir placeholder. |\n| `data/redis/redis.conf` | **Either** commit a static conf **or** generate from `start.sh`; must bind 127.0.0.1:6379 and set `dir`/`pidfile` under `/app/data`. |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `.gitignore` | Ignore `/app/.venv/`, `data/**/*.sqlite*`, `data/redis/dump.rdb`, `data/redis/appendonly.aof`, `data/run/*.pid`, keep ignoring existing harness paths (`loom-prompts/`, etc.). Do **not** ignore `data/**/.gitkeep` or a committed `redis.conf` if checked in. |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `timer.sh` | Harness time helper |\n| `loom-prompts/**` | Agent prompts |\n| IRC / SPA / Auth modules | Later tasks |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order for this task (single implementer)\n\n1. `requirements.txt` + `server/settings.py` + `server/app.py` (health + stub `/`).\n2. `.gitignore` + `data/**/.gitkeep` (+ optional `redis.conf`).\n3. `start.sh` supervisor last (wires everything).\n4. Manual verify: boot, health on three ports, kill one uvicorn + redis, confirm respawn.\n\nParallelism inside the task: server package vs ignore/data layout can proceed in parallel; `start.sh` depends on both.\n\n### Downstream seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumed by |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `start.sh` boots Redis + 3 nodes; health contract | Verifier, all backend tasks, QA |\n| `HUDDLE_NODE_ID` / port mapping | Logging, future debugging; MARATHON-14 |\n| `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` + WAL pragmas | MARATHON-3 (users/tokens), then all persistence tasks |\n| Redis at `127.0.0.1:6379` supervised/respawned | MARATHON-13/14 (pub/sub); must already be up |\n| Stub `GET /` | Replaced by MARATHON-16 SPA (same route) |\n| FastAPI app factory in `server.app:app` | All later route modules mount on same app |\n\n### Must land before\n\n- **MARATHON-3** (Auth) is blocked on this task — needs live nodes + shared DB path.\n- No other task should invent a second supervisor or a different port/node map.\n\n### Suggested follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n\n- Product schema migrations framework details → first persistence task (MARATHON-3) can add Alembic/raw SQL migrations on the shared file.\n- WebSocket / fan-out / IRC → MARATHON-13/14/15.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|\n| Auth register/login/me (MARATHON-3) | Separate task; only needs our DB path + live nodes |\n| Profiles, workspaces, channels, messages, DMs, files, search, groups | MARATHON-4…12 |\n| WebSocket subscribe/resume + dense seq (MARATHON-13) | Depends on messages |\n| Cross-node fan-out + Redis-outage behavior beyond respawn (MARATHON-14) | Needs events; this task only respawns Redis |\n| IRC `:6667` (MARATHON-15) | Explicit later task; neighborhood/harness ports list includes 6667 but we must not bind it yet |\n| SPA + `data-testid`s (MARATHON-16+) | Replaces stub `GET /` |\n| `timer.sh` behavior | Harness-owned |\n| Enveloped error JSON conventions beyond health | Defined in epic; apply starting with Auth |\n| Neighborhood scan of repo code for `start.sh` / `redis` / `/api/health` | **No hits** in the empty baseline beyond `timer.sh` and empty `data/` — nothing else to exclude |\n\n**Neighborhood scan result:** baseline repo contains only `timer.sh`, empty `data/`, `.gitignore`, and `loom-prompts/`. No pre-existing HTTP server, Redis config, or health route to reconcile. Harness utilities `marathon-freeports` / `marathon-portlock` clear ports `{8000,8001,8002,6667,6379}` before verify — implementers must not rely on stale listeners.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Cold start, empty `data/` | `start.sh` creates dirs + sqlite file; starts Redis; starts 3 nodes; then blocks in wait/respawn loop. |\n| Port 800x already busy at start | Fail fast: log which port, exit non-zero. Do not partially serve “whatever’s free.” (Verifier runs `marathon-freeports` first; residual busy = real error.) |\n| Port 6379 busy at start with foreign process | Fail fast after brief retry; do not attach to unknown Redis. |\n| HTTP child `SIGKILL` | Supervisor detects exit (wait/`SIGCHLD`/poll ≤2s); restart that node only with same `HUDDLE_NODE_ID`/port; listener restored in **&lt; 60s**. Other nodes uninterrupted. |\n| Redis `SIGKILL` | Supervisor restarts `redis-server` with same conf. (Fan-out degradation during gap is MARATHON-14; here only respawn is required.) |\n| Repeated crash loop | Keep respawning (with optional short backoff ≤2s) so the 60s window is met; log each restart to stdout/stderr (captured by verifier logs). |\n| `start.sh` receives `SIGTERM`/`SIGINT` | Propagate shutdown to Redis + all nodes; wait briefly; `_exit`. No orphaned listeners. |\n| `HUDDLE_NODE_ID` missing when launching uvicorn manually | `settings.py` aborts process startup with clear error (non-zero). `start.sh` always sets the env. |\n| `node_id`/port mismatch (e.g. id=0 on 8001) | Refuse to start that process. |\n| pip / venv failure | Exit non-zero before binding ports; do not hang silently. |\n| SQLite locked during bootstrap | Retry within busy_timeout; if still failing, log and exit that node (supervisor will respawn). |\n| Health called during startup race | Until bind completes, connection refused — acceptable. After bind, health must be correct. |\n| Partial cluster (only 2 nodes up) | Allowed transiently during respawn; steady state is 3. |\n| Writing product data | Not in this task; stub routes are read-only. |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `test -x /app/start.sh` (or repo-root `start.sh` executable bit set).\n2. Running `./start.sh` from `/app` does not exit on its own while children are healthy (foreground supervisor).\n3. Within a short boot window (e.g. ≤30s cold including pip), all of the following succeed:\n   - `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health` → `200` JSON `status==\"ok\"` and `node_id==0`\n   - same for `:8001` → `node_id==1`\n   - same for `:8002` → `node_id==2`\n4. `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8000/` (and 8001/8002) → `200` with `Content-Type` HTML (or text/html).\n5. `redis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 -p 6379 PING` → `PONG` while `start.sh` is alive.\n6. **HTTP respawn:** `SIGKILL` one uvicorn/node PID; without rerunning `start.sh`, within **60s** that port’s `/api/health` returns 200 with the **same** `node_id` as before. The other two ports remain healthy throughout.\n7. **Redis respawn:** `SIGKILL` the redis-server PID; without rerunning `start.sh`, `PING` succeeds again after respawn (implementer should target well under 60s; epic’s 5s write continuity is **not** required until MARATHON-14).\n8. **Negative:** `node_id` values must **not** be swapped across ports; health must **not** require `Authorization`.\n9. **Negative:** `start.sh` must **not** depend on Docker, remote Redis, or network services outside localhost.\n10. **Negative:** this task must **not** bind `:6667`.\n11. Durable path `/app/data/` exists after boot; sqlite file present if bootstrap creates it.\n12. No modifications to `timer.sh`.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated / scriptable checks (implementer or QA)\n\n```bash\ncd /app && ./start.sh &\n# wait for health on 8000/8001/8002\nfor p in 0 1 2; do\n  curl -sf \"http://127.0.0.1:800${p}/api/health\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); assert d=={'status':'ok','node_id':$p}\"\ndone\nredis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 -p 6379 PING | grep PONG\n# kill one node\nkill -9 \"$(pgrep -f 'uvicorn.*8001' | head -1)\"\n# poll until 8001 health returns node_id 1 within 60s\n# kill redis and poll PING\n```\n\n### Manual verification\n\n1. Boot `./start.sh`; watch logs for three “Uvicorn running” lines and Redis ready.\n2. Browser or curl `GET /` on each port — stub HTML loads.\n3. `kill -9` a node; confirm curl failures then recovery &lt;60s.\n4. `kill -9` redis; confirm `redis-cli PING` recovers via supervisor.\n5. `kill` the `start.sh` process group; confirm ports are free (`marathon-freeports` / `ss`).\n\n### Out of scope for this task’s tests\n\nAuth flows, WS fan-out during Redis outage, IRC, SPA selectors — covered by later tasks/QA once those land.\nDESIGN_EOF\n# Save design via loom\nloom data update MARATHON-2 --design=\"$(cat /tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md)\" --design-format=markdown --notes=\"New design (no needs-revision). No sibling designs existed; conventions established here for Python/FastAPI+Uvicorn, SQLite WAL at /app/data/huddle.sqlite, Redis pub/sub-only on :6379, node_id↔port map. Keep label backend for implementer routing after architect approval removes architect.\"\n","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"updated MARATHON-2\n","stderr":"","executionTime":176,"interleavedOutput":"updated MARATHON-2\n","localExecutionTimeMs":66},"isBackground":false},"description":"Write and save MARATHON-2 design"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-20c38e59-8191-4312-9cf7-efd810fcb317-8\nfc_7e5d4971-6bfc-94b8-9bd5-8105cdcdda8d_0","startedAtMs":"1787437240231","completedAtMs":"1787437240407"},"model_call_id":"3487d7ee-7391-4e0b-a56e-b1f7a484b8fa-8-79uv","session_id":"75e8a5ba-5b3e-48bc-a76f-1e5b5bfde32d","timestamp_ms":1787437240437}
