| head -5\nwhich loom; loom data update --help 2>&1 | head -80","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"================================================================================\nMARATHON-2 Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis status= closed labels= ['backend']\nNOTES LEN 284\nImplemented Python/FastAPI+Uvicorn cluster scaffold per design. start.sh supervises Redis :6379 + nodes 8000/8001/8002 with SIGKILL respawn. GET /api/health and stub GET / verified; unit tests in tests/test_health.py. SQLite WAL bootstrap at data/huddle.sqlite with schema_migrations.\nDESIGN LEN 18024\nwrote /tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md\n================================================================================\nMARATHON-3 Auth API: register, login, me, bearer tokens status= closed labels= ['backend']\nNOTES LEN 335\nAuth API implemented: POST /api/auth/register|login, GET /api/auth/me; SQLite users+auth_tokens (migration v1); scrypt passwords; SHA-256 bearer tokens; error envelope; get_current_user dependency. Tests: tests/test_auth.py (33 suite total green). Cluster verified token across :8000/:8001/:8002. Logout/revoke out of scope per design.\nDESIGN LEN 20666\nwrote /tmp/MARATHON-3-design.md\n================================================================================\nMARATHON-5 Workspaces: create, list, detail, auto #general status= review labels= ['architect', 'backend']\nNOTES LEN 250\nDesign complete for Workspaces create/list/detail + auto #general. Keeps backend label for implementer after architect approval. Establishes WorkspaceObj, ChannelObj seed, migration v2 (workspaces/members/channels/read_state). Blocks MARATHON-6/7/16.\nDESIGN LEN 23608\nwrote /tmp/MARATHON-5-design.md\ntime=2026-08-22T22:48:33.907Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\nError: backend [not_found] AddComment: issue not found\nUsage:\n  loom data comment <issue-id> <text> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --author string   Comment author (defaults to server-side session user)\n  -h, --help            help for comment\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n  -o, --output string       Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string       Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\n\nbackend [not_found] AddComment: issue not found\nThe 'loom data' subtree contains thin CLI commands that interact\nwith the configured loom issue backend. When --server or LOOM_SERVER_URL is\nset, commands talk to that loom server over HTTP. Without a server, issue\ncommands use the local backend selected by the workspace configuration and\ndaemon IPC environment.\n/installed-agent/loom-marathon/bin/loom\nUpdate issue fields\n\nUsage:\n  loom data update <issue-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --add-label stringArray           Add label (repeatable); other labels are preserved\n      --assignee string                 Set assignee\n      --depends-on stringArray          Add dependency on issue ID (repeatable)\n      --description string              Set description\n      --description-from-file string    Read description from file (use - for stdin)\n      --design string                   Set design\n      --design-format string            Set design format (markdown or html)\n  -h, --help                            help for update\n      --notes string                    Set notes\n      --priority int                    Set priority\n      --remove-depends-on stringArray   Remove dependency on issue ID (repeatable)\n      --remove-label stringArray        Remove label (repeatable); other labels are preserved\n      --status string                   Set status\n      --title string         