tion.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":145,"content":"- 400 `validation_error` — invalid username or password length.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":161,"content":"- 400 — missing/invalid body field types (empty username string, etc.) as `validation_error`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":192,"content":"MARATHON-4/5/10/16 must not reimplement bearer parsing.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":281,"content":"| Profile PATCH routes | MARATHON-4 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":299,"content":"| `UserObj` JSON shape | MARATHON-4 (Profiles), MARATHON-5+ (owner/member displays), MARATHON-16 (SPA session user) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":300,"content":"| Bearer + `get_current_user` | MARATHON-4, 5, 10, and all authenticated APIs |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":302,"content":"| `users` / `auth_tokens` tables | Profiles (updates same row); no second users table |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":311,"content":"- MARATHON-4, 5, 10, 16 (declared blockers).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":316,"content":"- Profile field validation / PATCH — MARATHON-4.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":317,"content":"- `user.updated` WebSocket broadcast — MARATHON-4/13.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":323,"content":"| Profile GET/PATCH `/api/users/...` | future `server/users/routes.py` | MARATHON-4 owns UserObj mutation + timezone validation |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":352,"content":"| Password length 7 | **400** `validation_error` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":377,"content":"3. Invalid username or password &lt; 8 → **400** with `code=validation_error`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../../../../../tmp/m3.json","matches":[{"lineNumber":13,"content":"  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-3 — Auth API: register, login, me, bearer tokens\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task adds the first product API surface for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, backed by durable users and bearer tokens in the shared SQLite database so any of the three HTTP nodes accepts the same credential. It locks the canonical `UserObj` JSON shape (consumed by Profiles, Workspaces, and the SPA), the error envelope convention for all later REST routes, and a reusable FastAPI auth dependency that every authenticated endpoint will import.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Durable auth store | **SQLite** at `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` (shared by all nodes) — tables `users` + `auth_tokens` |\\n| Token transport | Opaque bearer string in `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` |\\n| Token persistence | Store **SHA-256 hex** of the token; return plaintext only in register/login responses |\\n|  [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":23,"content":"      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-4\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":26,"content":"      \"title\": \"Profiles API: UserObj get and patch me\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../../../../../tmp/loom-list.json","matches":[{"lineNumber":14,"content":"    \"design\": \"# MARATHON-2 — Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task boots the Huddle cluster so the verifier (and every later feature task) has a live, self-contained process tree: `/app/start.sh` stays in the foreground, supervises a local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, and respawns any of those children after `SIGKILL`. Each node exposes a stub `GET /` and the contracted `GET /api/health`. The design also locks language/framework and the shared durable storage layout that Auth, messages, fan-out, IRC, and the SPA will all assume.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Language / HTTP framework | **Python 3.12 + FastAPI + Uvicorn** |\\n| Shared durable store | **SQLite file** at `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` with **WAL** + busy timeout (shared by all nodes) |\\n| Cross-node transport | **Local Redis** on `127.0.0.1:6379` (pub/sub / coordination only [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":36,"content":"    \"design\": \"# MARATHON-3 — Auth API: register, login, me, bearer tokens\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task adds the first product API surface for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, backed by durable users and bearer tokens in the shared SQLite database so any of the three HTTP nodes accepts the same credential. It locks the canonical `UserObj` JSON shape (consumed by Profiles, Workspaces, and the SPA), the error envelope convention for all later REST routes, and a reusable FastAPI auth dependency that every authenticated endpoint will import.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Durable auth store | **SQLite** at `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` (shared by all nodes) — tables `users` + `auth_tokens` |\\n| Token transport | Opaque bearer string in `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` |\\n| Token persistence | Store **SHA-256 hex** of the token; return plaintext only in register/login responses |\\n [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":135,"content":"    \"id\": \"MARATHON-4\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":136,"content":"    \"title\": \"Profiles API: UserObj get and patch me\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../../../../../tmp/m2.json","matches":[{"lineNumber":14,"content":"  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-2 — Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThis task boots the Huddle cluster so the verifier (and every later feature task) has a live, self-contained process tree: `/app/start.sh` stays in the foreground, supervises a local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, and respawns any of those children after `SIGKILL`. Each node exposes a stub `GET /` and the contracted `GET /api/health`. The design also locks language/framework and the shared durable storage layout that Auth, messages, fan-out, IRC, and the SPA will all assume.\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Language / HTTP framework | **Python 3.12 + FastAPI + Uvicorn** |\\n| Shared durable store | **SQLite file** at `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` with **WAL** + busy timeout (shared by all nodes) |\\n| Cross-node transport | **Local Redis** on `127.0.0.1:6379` (pub/sub / coordination only — [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":79,"totalMatchedLines":79,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-780f2f2d-163f-4c01-b90e-843fe058d210-15\nfc_704b05be-ef1b-961e-8ebe-f6b69b9c647b_1","startedAtMs":"1787438913806","completedAtMs":"1787438914004"},"model_call_id":"52c7e569-f580-424e-9bd3-33cce841899c-4-gz89","session_id":"a3bad295-2ca9-4573-bf75-ec471b6d0b93","timestamp_ms":1787438914031}
