{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-ae4d8276-d1f2-445b-8ca1-913ced2184c6-18\nfc_d6ba5dfb-bf6f-9027-92b8-bf8b2b9773b0_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/MARATHON-3-design.md","offset":250,"limit":150},"result":{"success":{"content":"\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/__init__.py` | Package marker; optionally re-export router + `get_current_user`. |\n| `server/auth/passwords.py` | Hash / verify helpers (`scrypt`). |\n| `server/auth/tokens.py` | Mint raw token; hash; insert row; resolve hash → `user_id`. |\n| `server/auth/users.py` | Create user; fetch by id/username; map row → `UserObj` dict. |\n| `server/auth/deps.py` | `get_current_user` FastAPI dependency; 401 envelope helper. |\n| `server/auth/routes.py` | `APIRouter` with register / login / me. |\n| `server/errors.py` | Small helper to build `JSONResponse` error envelopes (shared). |\n| `tests/test_auth.py` | Contract tests: register 201, duplicate 409, validation 400, login 200/401, me 200/401, cross-DB identity (same sqlite path / TestClient). |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/db.py` | Add `migrate(conn)` / `ensure_schema(sqlite_path)` applying version 1 DDL; keep existing bootstrap. Prefer a list of `(version, sql_callable)` migrations. Expose `connect(sqlite_path) -> Connection` used by auth (WAL pragmas every time). |\n| `server/app.py` | Call full schema ensure on lifespan (not only bootstrap); `include_router` auth routes; leave `/api/health` and stub `GET /` unchanged. |\n| `requirements.txt` | **No new dependencies required** if using stdlib crypto + uuid. Do not add Redis usage for auth. |\n| `tests/test_health.py` | Only if lifespan/migration changes break bootstrap assertions — keep health unauthenticated; do not weaken existing checks. |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `start.sh` | Supervisor already shares `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`; no auth-specific change |\n| `server/settings.py` | Already exposes sqlite path |\n| `timer.sh`, `loom-prompts/**` | Harness |\n| SPA / `GET /` HTML | MARATHON-16 |\n| Profile PATCH routes | MARATHON-4 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order (single implementer)\n\n1. `server/errors.py` + `db.py` migration v1.\n2. `passwords.py` / `tokens.py` / `users.py`.\n3. `deps.py` + `routes.py`.\n4. Wire `app.py`.\n5. `tests/test_auth.py` + manual three-port check.\n\nParallelism: password helpers and error helper can proceed in parallel; routes depend on both + migration.\n\n### Downstream seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumed by |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `UserObj` JSON shape | MARATHON-4 (Profiles), MARATHON-5+ (owner/member displays), MARATHON-16 (SPA session user) |\n| Bearer + `get_current_user` | MARATHON-4, 5, 10, and all authenticated APIs |\n| Error envelope `{error:{code,message}}` | All subsequent REST tasks + SPA error rendering |\n| `users` / `auth_tokens` tables | Profiles (updates same row); no second users table |\n| Register/login `{user,token}` | MARATHON-16 token storage (`huddle.token`) |\n\n### Upstream dependency\n\n- **MARATHON-2** (closed): shared SQLite path, app factory, cluster boot — required and present.\n\n### Must land before\n\n- MARATHON-4, 5, 10, 16 (declared blockers).\n\n### Suggested follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n\n- `POST /api/auth/logout` / token revoke — separate task if needed.\n- Profile field validation / PATCH — MARATHON-4.\n- `user.updated` WebSocket broadcast — MARATHON-4/13.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| Profile GET/PATCH `/api/users/...` | future `server/users/routes.py` | MARATHON-4 owns UserObj mutation + timezone validation |\n| SPA auth forms, `huddle.token`, selectors | `GET /` stub in `server/app.py` | MARATHON-16; do not replace stub HTML here |\n| Workspace/member authz | — | MARATHON-5/6 |\n| Redis token cache / pubsub auth events | Redis | Wrong SoT; fan-out is MARATHON-14 |\n| IRC PASS/NickServ-style auth | — | MARATHON-15 |\n| Logout / revoke / token TTL | `auth_tokens` rows live forever in this task | No logout in contract |\n| Email verification / OAuth | — | Forbidden / not in product scope |\n| Changing `/api/health` auth or envelope | `server/app.py` health handler | MARATHON-2 contract |\n| `timer.sh` / harness port helpers | — | Harness-owned |\n\nNeighborhood scan (repo after MARATHON-2 merge):\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `server/app.py` — FastAPI factory, health, stub `/` | **In scope** — mount auth router; leave health/stub behavior |\n| `server/db.py` — WAL bootstrap + `schema_migrations` | **In scope** — add migration v1 |\n| `server/settings.py` — paths/env | Out of scope (no change needed) |\n| `tests/test_health.py` — asserts health JSON; mentions Authorization absence | Keep green; auth tests are separate file |\n| `start.sh` — venv, redis, three uvicorn | Out of scope |\n| `requirements.txt` — fastapi/uvicorn/redis/httpx/pytest | Out of scope unless a dep is unavoidable (prefer none) |\n| Grep `auth`/`bearer`/`token`/`register` | Only incidental Authorization note in health test — not a second auth system |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Duplicate username (UNIQUE race) | Catch integrity error → **409** `conflict`; do not 500 |\n| Login unknown user | **401** same message as wrong password |\n| Login wrong password | **401**; do not mint token |\n| Password length 7 | **400** `validation_error` |\n| Password length 8 | Accepted (if username valid) |\n| Username `Ada` (uppercase) | **400** (pattern requires lowercase) |\n| Username `ab` | Allowed (length 2) |\n| Username `a` | **400** |\n| Username `user@x.com` | **400** |\n| Body missing `password` | **400** |\n| Extra JSON fields on register | Ignore |\n| `Content-Type` not JSON / invalid JSON | **400** (or framework 422 normalized to envelope 400 — implementer must expose envelope, not raw Starlette HTML) |\n| `Authorization: bearer <token>` (lowercase scheme) | Accept |\n| `Authorization: Bearer` with no token | **401** |\n| Token valid on node 0, used on node 2 | **200** `/me` (shared DB) |\n| User deleted (future) with orphan tokens | FK CASCADE removes tokens; for now no delete API |\n| SQLite locked under concurrent registers | Wait `busy_timeout`; on failure log and return 500/503 — do not corrupt partial user-without-token (single transaction) |\n| Register succeeds but response lost | Client may retry → **409**; client should login instead (SPA concern) |\n| Empty DB / first boot | Migration 1 runs; register works |\n| Health during auth work | Still 200 without auth |\n| Token string with spaces / newlines | Treat as invalid → **401** |\n| Display name only spaces | Treat as empty → default to username |\n| Concurrent logins | Each gets distinct token; both remain valid |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `POST /api/auth/register` with valid `{username,password}` → **201**, JSON body has `user` (`UserObj` keys exactly as specified, no `email`) and `token` with **len(token) ≥ 16**.\n2. Duplicate username → **409** with error envelope `code=conflict`.\n3. Invalid username or password &lt; 8 → **400** with `code=validation_error`.\n4. `POST /api/auth/login` with correct credentials → **200** and `{user,token}` (new token).\n5. Login with wrong password or unknown user → **401** `unauthorized` (same handling for both; **must not** 404).\n6. `GET /api/auth/me` with `Authorization: Bearer <token>` from register or login → **200** `{user}` matching the registered user.\n7. `/me` without header, with bad token, or with non-Bearer scheme → **401**.\n8. **Cluster:** token minted via `:8000` is accepted by `/api/auth/me` on `:8001` and `:8002` while `./start.sh` is running (shared SQLite).\n9. **Negative:** responses must **not** include `email`; passwords must **not** appear in any response body.\n10. **Negative:** `/api/health` must still return unenveloped `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"node_id\":N}` without auth.\n11. **Negative:** auth data must **not** be stored only in process memory or only in Redis.\n12. Users and tokens survive node process restart (SQLite file under `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated (implementer)\n\n`tests/test_auth.py` using `TestClient(create_app(Settings(...)))` with per-test `tmp_path` sqlite:\n\n- register happy path + token length.\n- duplicate → 409.\n- short password / bad username → 400.\n- login success + wrong password → 401.\n- me success + missing/invalid bearer → 401.\n- UserObj keys set equality (include null profile fields).","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":422,"fileSize":20824,"path":"/tmp/MARATHON-3-design.md","readRange":{"startLine":250,"endLine":399},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-ae4d8276-d1f2-445b-8ca1-913ced2184c6-18\nfc_d6ba5dfb-bf6f-9027-92b8-bf8b2b9773b0_0","startedAtMs":"1787438917589","completedAtMs":"1787438918094"},"model_call_id":"52c7e569-f580-424e-9bd3-33cce841899c-5-a6qx","session_id":"a3bad295-2ca9-4573-bf75-ec471b6d0b93","timestamp_ms":1787438918121}
