{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-12\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_0","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"^## |UserObj|token|localStorage|SPA|huddle\\.token|data-testid|selector","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-3-design.md","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-12\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_0","offset":0}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-12\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_0","startedAtMs":"1787440331597"},"model_call_id":"a74d7e62-a08d-4d88-aaf5-b4d85b65652b-4-7uuv","session_id":"ce65663b-c70a-428f-a8bb-f87b51fd396c","timestamp_ms":1787440332039}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-12\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_0","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"^## |UserObj|token|localStorage|SPA|huddle\\.token|data-testid|selector","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-3-design.md","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-12\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_0","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"^## |UserObj|token|localStorage|SPA|huddle\\.token|data-testid|selector","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-3-design.md","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"../../../../../tmp/MARATHON-3-design.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":1,"content":"# MARATHON-3 — Auth API: register, login, me, bearer tokens","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3,"content":"## Summary","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":5,"content":"This task adds the first product API surface for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, backed by durable users and bearer tokens in the shared SQLite database so any of the three HTTP nodes accepts the same credential. It locks the canonical `UserObj` JSON shape (consumed by Profiles, Workspaces, and the SPA), the error envelope convention for all later REST routes, and a reusable FastAPI auth dependency that every authenticated endpoint will import.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":7,"content":"## Technical Approach","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":13,"content":"| Durable auth store | **SQLite** at `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` (shared by all nodes) — tables `users` + `auth_tokens` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":14,"content":"| Token transport | Opaque bearer string in `Authorization: Bearer <token>` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":15,"content":"| Token persistence | Store **SHA-256 hex** of the token; return plaintext only in register/login responses |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":17,"content":"| User / token ids | Stable strings: **UUID4** hex/`str` for `users.id`; tokens identified by hash (no separate public token id) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":20,"content":"| Schema evolution | Extend MARATHON-2 `schema_migrations`: apply version **1** (users + auth_tokens) idempotently on node lifespan |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":24,"content":"- MARATHON-2 fixed SQLite as SoT and Redis as ephemeral fan-out only. Storing tokens in Redis would break “any node accepts the same token” after Redis `SIGKILL` and contradicts MARATHON-14. Shared SQLite is the only persistence already wired on every node.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":25,"content":"- Opaque bearer tokens match the epic (“REST + bearer auth”) and the SPA task (`localStorage` `huddle.token`) without JWT clock skew or shared signing secrets across processes.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":26,"content":"- Hashing stored tokens limits damage from a DB file read while still allowing constant-time lookup by hashing the presented bearer.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":28,"content":"- Establishing `UserObj` and the `{ \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\" } }` envelope here prevents Profiles/SPA from inventing competing shapes (MARATHON-2 deferred error envelopes to Auth).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":34,"content":"| JWT / signed tokens | Needs shared secret rotation; harder to revoke; not required by contract |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":36,"content":"| Per-node in-memory tokens | Violates “cluster-wide / any node accepts the same token” |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":42,"content":"Multiple live tokens per user (each register/login mints a new row) simplifies SPA “login again” without a logout API, at the cost of unbounded token rows until a later revoke/logout task cleans them up. Acceptable for marathon scope; document logout/revoke as out of scope.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":52,"content":"## Interface Contracts","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":56,"content":"#### `UserObj`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":99,"content":"**Do not** return FastAPI’s default `{\"detail\": ...}` for these routes — normalize to the envelope above so SPA and graders have one shape. (`GET /api/health` remains the documented exception.)","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":117,"content":"- Header: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":118,"content":"- Scheme is case-insensitive `Bearer`; exactly one space; token is the opaque string from register/login.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":119,"content":"- Missing header, non-Bearer scheme, empty token, or unknown/revoked token → **401** `unauthorized`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":127,"content":"| **Client (SPA / grader)** | JSON body `{ \"username\": string, \"password\": string }`. Optional `display_name` allowed; ignore unknown fields or reject — **server must ignore unknown fields** (forward-compatible). While waiting: disable submit / show pending. On 400/409: show `error.message`. On 201: store `token` (SPA: `localStorage` key `huddle.token` — owned by MARATHON-16) and treat `user` as session user. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":128,"content":"| **Server** | Validate username/password; hash password; insert user + token in one transaction; return 201. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":139,"content":"  \"user\": { /* UserObj */ },","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":140,"content":"  \"token\": \"<opaque string length >= 16>\"","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":155,"content":"| **Client** | Body `{ \"username\", \"password\" }`. On success store token same as register. Do not distinguish “unknown user” vs “bad password” in UI copy if using server message (both 401). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":156,"content":"| **Server** | Lookup by username; verify password; mint **new** token row; return 200 `{ user, token }`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":158,"content":"**Response 200:** same shape as register’s 201 body (`user` + `token`).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":171,"content":"| **Client** | Send stored bearer. On 401: clear token and show auth form (SPA). While loading: show shell placeholder / spinner without flashing logged-out if token present. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":172,"content":"| **Server** | Resolve bearer → user; return 200 `{ \"user\": UserObj }`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":176,"content":"{ \"user\": { /* UserObj */ } }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":190,"content":"3. On success yields the full `UserObj` (or internal user row mapped to `UserObj`).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":196,"content":"Register on `:8000`, then `GET /api/auth/me` on `:8001` / `:8002` with the same token **must** succeed. Implementer verifies this; design requires single shared SQLite SoT (already true via `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":198,"content":"## Data Model","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":221,"content":"#### Table `auth_tokens`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":225,"content":"| `token_hash` | TEXT | NOT NULL | PK; hex SHA-256 of raw token |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":239,"content":"- Raw token: `secrets.token_urlsafe(32)` (always length ≥ 16).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":240,"content":"- Persist only `hashlib.sha256(raw_token.encode(\"ascii\")).hexdigest()`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":241,"content":"- Compare presented token by hashing then PK lookup (constant-time compare optional once looked up by hash).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":247,"content":"| Add `users`, `auth_tokens`; insert migration version 1 | Yes — additive on greenfield / version 0 DBs |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":249,"content":"## Files to Create / Files to Modify","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":257,"content":"| `server/auth/tokens.py` | Mint raw token; hash; insert row; resolve hash → `user_id`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":258,"content":"| `server/auth/users.py` | Create user; fetch by id/username; map row → `UserObj` dict. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":280,"content":"| SPA / `GET /` HTML | MARATHON-16 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":283,"content":"## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":288,"content":"2. `passwords.py` / `tokens.py` / `users.py`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":299,"content":"| `UserObj` JSON shape | MARATHON-4 (Profiles), MARATHON-5+ (owner/member displays), MARATHON-16 (SPA session user) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":301,"content":"| Error envelope `{error:{code,message}}` | All subsequent REST tasks + SPA error rendering |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":302,"content":"| `users` / `auth_tokens` tables | Profiles (updates same row); no second users table |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":303,"content":"| Register/login `{user,token}` | MARATHON-16 token storage (`huddle.token`) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":315,"content":"- `POST /api/auth/logout` / token revoke — separate task if needed.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":319,"content":"## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":323,"content":"| Profile GET/PATCH `/api/users/...` | future `server/users/routes.py` | MARATHON-4 owns UserObj mutation + timezone validation |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":324,"content":"| SPA auth forms, `huddle.token`, selectors | `GET /` stub in `server/app.py` | MARATHON-16; do not replace stub HTML here |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":326,"content":"| Redis token cache / pubsub auth events | Redis | Wrong SoT; fan-out is MARATHON-14 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":328,"content":"| Logout / revoke / token TTL | `auth_tokens` rows live forever in this task | No logout in contract |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":343,"content":"| Grep `auth`/`bearer`/`token`/`register` | Only incidental Authorization note in health test — not a second auth system |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":345,"content":"## Edge Cases & Error Handling","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":351,"content":"| Login wrong password | **401**; do not mint token |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":361,"content":"| `Authorization: bearer <token>` (lowercase scheme) | Accept |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":362,"content":"| `Authorization: Bearer` with no token | **401** |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":364,"content":"| User deleted (future) with orphan tokens | FK CASCADE removes tokens; for now no delete API |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":365,"content":"| SQLite locked under concurrent registers | Wait `busy_timeout`; on failure log and return 500/503 — do not corrupt partial user-without-token (single transaction) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":366,"content":"| Register succeeds but response lost | Client may retry → **409**; client should login instead (SPA concern) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":371,"content":"| Concurrent logins | Each gets distinct token; both remain valid |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":373,"content":"## Acceptance Criteria","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":375,"content":"1. `POST /api/auth/register` with valid `{username,password}` → **201**, JSON body has `user` (`UserObj` keys exactly as specified, no `email`) and `token` with **len(token) ≥ 16**.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":378,"content":"4. `POST /api/auth/login` with correct credentials → **200** and `{user,token}` (new token).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":380,"content":"6. `GET /api/auth/me` with `Authorization: Bearer <token>` from register or login → **200** `{user}` matching the registered user.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":381,"content":"7. `/me` without header, with bad token, or with non-Bearer scheme → **401**.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":382,"content":"8. **Cluster:** token minted via `:8000` is accepted by `/api/auth/me` on `:8001` and `:8002` while `./start.sh` is running (shared SQLite).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":386,"content":"12. Users and tokens survive node process restart (SQLite file under `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":388,"content":"## Testing Strategy","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":394,"content":"- register happy path + token length.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":399,"content":"- UserObj keys set equality (include null profile fields).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":410,"content":"# capture token; then:","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":421,"content":"3. Confirm `data/huddle.sqlite` contains `users` / `auth_tokens` rows (no plaintext passwords).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":422,"content":"4. Kill one HTTP node; after respawn, same token still works on that port.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":79,"totalMatchedLines":79,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-12\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_0","startedAtMs":"1787440331597","completedAtMs":"1787440332084"},"model_call_id":"a74d7e62-a08d-4d88-aaf5-b4d85b65652b-4-7uuv","session_id":"ce65663b-c70a-428f-a8bb-f87b51fd396c","timestamp_ms":1787440332107}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-13\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_1","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"^## |SPA|join|WorkspaceObj|slug|Interface","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-5-design.md","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-13\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_1","offset":0}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-13\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_1","startedAtMs":"1787440332021"},"model_call_id":"a74d7e62-a08d-4d88-aaf5-b4d85b65652b-4-7uuv","session_id":"ce65663b-c70a-428f-a8bb-f87b51fd396c","timestamp_ms":1787440332311}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-13\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_1","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"^## |SPA|join|WorkspaceObj|slug|Interface","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-5-design.md","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-13\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_1","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"^## |SPA|join|WorkspaceObj|slug|Interface","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-5-design.md","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"../../../../../tmp/MARATHON-5-design.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":3,"content":"## Summary","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":5,"content":"This task adds the workspace tenancy root for Huddle: authenticated callers can create a workspace (unique kebab `slug`, display `name`, creator as `owner`, default `join_mode=open`), which atomically provisions the public `#general` channel and membership rows; list workspaces they own or belong to; and load a workspace by slug with the visible channel list plus embedded `read_state`. It locks `WorkspaceObj`, the initial `ChannelObj` shape used by later channel APIs, the SQLite schema for workspaces/members/channels, and the REST contracts the SPA shell (MARATHON-16) and members/channels tasks (MARATHON-6/7) consume.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":9,"content":"## Technical Approach","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":28,"content":"- Epic requires workspaces before channels, invitations, and the SPA shell. Without durable membership + `#general`, MARATHON-6/7/16 have no seam.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":32,"content":"- Embedding the **full** `read_state` entry shape now (not a truncated `{channel_id, last_read_seq}`) prevents SPA/MARATHON-11 divergence on badge fields.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":40,"content":"| Soft-create `#general` only as a name string without a channel row | Downstream channel APIs and SPA channel list need a real `id` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":41,"content":"| Allow unauthenticated workspace list/detail | Contradicts bearer-auth epic convention; SPA always has a session user |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":43,"content":"| Include `join_mode` in POST body | Task body is `{slug,name}` only; `join_mode` changes are MARATHON-6 PATCH |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":49,"content":"This task introduces **minimal** channel + membership schema ahead of MARATHON-6/7 so create/list/detail work end-to-end. Full join/leave/role/archive/pin behavior stays out of scope; implementers must not invent those routes here. We accept a slightly larger migration v2 (including `unread_count` / `mention_count` columns on `channel_read_state`) in exchange for a single coherent create transaction and stable JSON types shared with MARATHON-11.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":59,"content":"## Interface Contracts","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":63,"content":"#### `WorkspaceObj`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":68,"content":"  \"slug\": \"acme\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":71,"content":"  \"join_mode\": \"open\"","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":78,"content":"| `slug` | string | required | Unique cluster-wide; kebab per regex below; immutable in this task (no rename API) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":81,"content":"| `join_mode` | string | required | Exactly `\"open\"` or `\"invite_only\"`; create always `\"open\"` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":85,"content":"#### `ChannelObj` (initial; owned jointly — this task creates rows + JSON; MARATHON-7 extends behavior)","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":132,"content":"- **Negative:** must **not** return truncated entries like `{channel_id, last_read_seq}` only; SPA and MARATHON-11 depend on `unread_count` / `mention_count` always being present on each entry.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":144,"content":"| `validation_error` | 400 | Bad slug/name |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":147,"content":"| `conflict` | 409 | Duplicate workspace slug |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":148,"content":"| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown slug **or** caller not a workspace member |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":154,"content":"| **Client (SPA / grader)** | `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; JSON `{ \"slug\", \"name\" }`. While slow: disable create submit / show pending (`workspace-create-form` lives in MARATHON-16). On 201: store returned workspace as current; navigate shell to its channels. On 400/409: show `error.message`. On 401: re-auth. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":160,"content":"{ \"slug\": \"acme\", \"name\": \"Acme Corp\" }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":163,"content":"- Required: `slug`, `name` (strings).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":165,"content":"- Do **not** accept `join_mode` as authoritative; always persist `\"open\"` (ignore if present).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":182,"content":"  \"workspace\": { \"id\": \"...\", \"slug\": \"acme\", \"name\": \"Acme Corp\", \"owner_id\": \"<creator>\", \"join_mode\": \"open\" },","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":187,"content":"**Errors:** 401; 400 validation; 409 `conflict` message e.g. `\"slug already taken\"`; SQLite integrity race → same 409.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":199,"content":"{ \"workspaces\": [ /* WorkspaceObj, ... */ ] }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":202,"content":"- Order: `name ASC` (case-insensitive), tie-break `slug ASC`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":205,"content":"### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":210,"content":"| **Server** | Resolve by slug; require membership; build filtered `channels` + `read_state`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":225,"content":"  \"workspace\": { /* WorkspaceObj */ },","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":235,"content":"  \"workspace\": { \"id\": \"...\", \"slug\": \"acme\", \"name\": \"Acme Corp\", \"owner_id\": \"...\", \"join_mode\": \"open\" },","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":255,"content":"**Errors:** 401; 404 `not_found` if slug missing **or** caller not a member (same message, e.g. `\"workspace not found\"` — do not leak invite-only existence).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":259,"content":"`RequestValidationError` → 400 envelope for **any** path starting with `/api/` except exact `/api/health`. Keeps SPA/grader on one error shape for workspaces and future routes. MARATHON-4 design adopts the same rule — apply once; either task may land the change first.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":261,"content":"## Data Model","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":272,"content":"| `slug` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UNIQUE |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":275,"content":"| `join_mode` | TEXT | NOT NULL | CHECK IN (`open`,`invite_only`); default `open` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":337,"content":"1. INSERT `workspaces` (`join_mode='open'`, `owner_id=creator`).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":343,"content":"On any failure: rollback; map UNIQUE(slug) → 409; unexpected → 500 (log).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":345,"content":"## Files to Create / Files to Modify","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":352,"content":"| `server/workspaces/store.py` | Slug/name validation; insert workspace; list for user; get by slug; membership check; row→`WorkspaceObj`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":353,"content":"| `server/workspaces/routes.py` | `POST \"\"`, `GET \"\"`, `GET \"/{slug}\"` under prefix `/api/workspaces`; Depend `get_current_user`; parse `include_archived` (`1` \\| case-insensitive `true`). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":356,"content":"| `tests/test_workspaces.py` | Contract tests for create/list/detail, authz, slug conflict, archive query (`1` and `true`), full `read_state` keys, envelope errors. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":373,"content":"| SPA / replace `GET /` | MARATHON-16 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":375,"content":"| Channel create/join/leave/archive/pins routes | MARATHON-7 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":378,"content":"## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":397,"content":"| `WorkspaceObj` + `/api/workspaces` create/list/detail | MARATHON-6, 7, 12, 16, 18 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":399,"content":"| Auto `#general` with `name=\"general\"` | SPA default channel; IRC/bridge later |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":400,"content":"| `join_mode` column default `open` | MARATHON-6 PATCH; MARATHON-7 join rules |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":403,"content":"| `include_archived` ∈ {`1`,`true`} | SPA / channel settings UI |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":404,"content":"| 404-for-non-members detail policy | SPA routing |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":418,"content":"- Extra channels, join/leave, archive, pins → MARATHON-7.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":420,"content":"- SPA forms/selectors → MARATHON-16.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":422,"content":"## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":426,"content":"| `GET/PATCH` members, transfer ownership | future `/api/workspaces/{slug}/members` | MARATHON-6 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":427,"content":"| `PATCH` workspace `name`/`join_mode` | — | MARATHON-6 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":428,"content":"| `POST .../channels`, join/leave, topic, archive, pins | — | MARATHON-7 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":429,"content":"| Open-workspace auto-onboard of non-members | join rules in MARATHON-7 | Non-members get 404 on detail until they become members via later APIs |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":434,"content":"| SPA workspace shell / `workspace-create-form` | stub `GET /` | MARATHON-16 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":453,"content":"## Edge Cases & Error Handling","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":460,"content":"| Duplicate slug | **409** `conflict` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":461,"content":"| Concurrent duplicate slug inserts | IntegrityError → **409** (no 500) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":466,"content":"| Second create by same user different slug | Allowed (multi-workspace) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":468,"content":"| Detail unknown slug | **404** |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":469,"content":"| Detail existing slug, non-member | **404** (same body as unknown) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":482,"content":"| `join_mode` column somehow not `open`/`invite_only` | Prevented by CHECK; API never emits other values |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":484,"content":"## Acceptance Criteria","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":486,"content":"1. `POST /api/workspaces` with valid Bearer + `{slug,name}` → **201** with `workspace` (`WorkspaceObj` keys exactly) and `general_channel` (`ChannelObj` keys exactly); `workspace.join_mode==\"open\"`; `workspace.owner_id` equals caller; `general_channel.name==\"general\"`; `is_private/is_dm/is_archived` are JSON `false`; `topic==\"\"`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":487,"content":"2. Duplicate `slug` → **409** envelope `code=conflict`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":488,"content":"3. Invalid slug (fails `^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`) or empty/whitespace name → **400** `validation_error`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":490,"content":"5. After create, `GET /api/workspaces` includes that workspace for the creator and does **not** require a second join call.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":491,"content":"6. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as member → **200** with `workspace`, `channels` containing `#general`, and `read_state` (array; may be empty). When non-empty, **every** entry has exactly the keys `channel_id`, `last_read_seq`, `unread_count`, `mention_count` (integers ≥ 0 for the three numeric fields).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":492,"content":"7. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as different user with no membership → **404** (must **not** return 200).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":500,"content":"## Testing Strategy","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":507,"content":"- Duplicate slug → 409.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":508,"content":"- Bad slug / blank name → 400 envelope.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":530,"content":"2. Second account cannot open the slug (404).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":77,"totalMatchedLines":77,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-13\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_1","startedAtMs":"1787440332021","completedAtMs":"1787440332349"},"model_call_id":"a74d7e62-a08d-4d88-aaf5-b4d85b65652b-4-7uuv","session_id":"ce65663b-c70a-428f-a8bb-f87b51fd396c","timestamp_ms":1787440332372}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-14\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_2","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"^## |UserObj|SPA","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-14\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_2","offset":0}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-14\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_2","startedAtMs":"1787440332293"},"model_call_id":"a74d7e62-a08d-4d88-aaf5-b4d85b65652b-4-7uuv","session_id":"ce65663b-c70a-428f-a8bb-f87b51fd396c","timestamp_ms":1787440332838}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-14\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_2","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"^## |UserObj|SPA","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-14\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_2","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"^## |UserObj|SPA","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"../../../../../tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":1,"content":"# MARATHON-4 — Profiles API: UserObj get and patch me","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3,"content":"## Summary","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":5,"content":"This task adds the Profiles REST surface on top of the Auth-owned `users` table: authenticated `GET /api/users/{id}` returns a canonical `UserObj` (or 404), and authenticated `PATCH /api/users/me` applies any subset of mutable profile fields with IANA timezone and length validation (400 on failure). It does **not** change the `UserObj` shape locked by MARATHON-3; it only mutates profile columns already present in migration v1 and leaves a clear, channel-less `user.updated` event contract so MARATHON-13/14 can fan profile changes over WebSocket later.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":7,"content":"## Technical Approach","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":16,"content":"| `UserObj` mapping | Keep sole mapper in `server/auth/users.py` (`row_to_user_obj` / `USER_OBJ_KEYS`); Profiles calls into that module for reads/updates — **no second users table or second JSON shape** |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":25,"content":"- MARATHON-3 already created nullable profile columns and the exact `UserObj` keys; inventing a parallel profile store would diverge sibling contracts and break SPA/`/api/auth/me` consistency.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":43,"content":"Any authenticated user may `GET` any other user’s public `UserObj` (no workspace membership gate). That unlocks mentions/DMs/member lists later at the cost of a cluster-global user directory. Acceptable for marathon scope; workspace-scoped visibility can be a later task if needed.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":49,"content":"From **MARATHON-3**: `UserObj` keys exactly `{id,username,display_name,timezone,avatar_url,status_text,status_emoji}`; UUID4 string ids; UTC `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ` for `updated_at`; `ApiError` envelope; `get_current_user`; ignore unknown JSON body fields; `400`/`validation_error`; `401`/`unauthorized`; no `email` ever.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":53,"content":"## Interface Contracts","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":57,"content":"#### `UserObj` (unchanged from MARATHON-3)","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":97,"content":"| **Client (SPA / grader)** | `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. While slow: keep prior profile cache / show lightweight loading on profile popover. On 200: render `user` fields (avatar, display name, status). On 404: treat as unknown user (do not retry forever). On 401: re-auth. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":98,"content":"| **Server** | Require auth; load user by path `id`; return 200 `{ \"user\": UserObj }` or 404. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":103,"content":"{ \"user\": { /* UserObj */ } }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":110,"content":"- **Negative:** must **not** return password hashes, tokens, `email`, or internal columns (`created_at`/`updated_at`/`password_hash` are not part of `UserObj`).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":115,"content":"- Caller may fetch **their own** id or **another** user’s id; both return the same public `UserObj` shape.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":121,"content":"| **Client** | Bearer; JSON object with **any subset** of mutable fields. While slow: disable save / keep form dirty state; do not clear local fields until 200. On 200: replace session/profile user with returned `user` (SPA: same object shape as auth). On 400: show `error.message` next to the offending field. On 401: re-auth. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":122,"content":"| **Server** | Auth → validate provided fields → UPDATE row → bump `updated_at` → return full `UserObj` → invoke `publish_user_updated`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":138,"content":"- Empty object `{}`: **200**, unchanged `UserObj` (no publish call).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":144,"content":"| `display_name` | Must be `string` if present (JSON `null` allowed → treat as reset). Strip leading/trailing whitespace. If empty after strip **or** JSON `null` → persist `username` (never store NULL; `UserObj.display_name` stays a string). Max length **80** Unicode code points after strip (reject longer). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":155,"content":"{ \"user\": { /* full UserObj after update */ } }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":169,"content":"  \"user\": { /* UserObj */ }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":185,"content":"## Data Model","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":212,"content":"## Files to Create / Files to Modify","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":221,"content":"| `tests/test_profiles.py` | Contract tests for GET/PATCH, auth, 404, validation lengths/timezone, UserObj key set, no-op PATCH, ignore immutable keys. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":227,"content":"| `server/auth/users.py` | Add profile validators + `update_user_profile(conn, user_id, patch) -> dict` (or equivalent) that UPDATEs columns and returns `UserObj`. Reuse `normalize_display_name` semantics for PATCH resets. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":239,"content":"| SPA / `GET /` HTML | MARATHON-16 / settings UI MARATHON-18 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":243,"content":"## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":264,"content":"| Profile length + IANA rules | SPA client-side hints (optional); graders |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":270,"content":"- **MARATHON-3** (closed): `users` table, `UserObj`, bearer, envelope — required and present.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":275,"content":"- Profile UI in SPA settings (MARATHON-16/18) and any feature that assumes GET-by-id directory.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":284,"content":"## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":290,"content":"| SPA profile/settings forms + `data-testid` | frontend | MARATHON-16/18 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":303,"content":"| `server/auth/users.py` — `UserObj` map, create, get_by_id | **In scope** — add update/validators; do not change register defaults |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":305,"content":"| `server/auth/deps.py` — bearer → UserObj | **Consume only** |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":309,"content":"| `tests/test_auth.py` — UserObj null profile fields | Keep green; profiles tests are a new file |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":313,"content":"## Edge Cases & Error Handling","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":343,"content":"## Acceptance Criteria","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":345,"content":"1. `GET /api/users/{id}` with valid bearer and existing id → **200** `{ \"user\": UserObj }` with exact key set and no `email`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":360,"content":"## Testing Strategy","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":390,"content":"- SPA form selectors (MARATHON-16/18).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":40,"totalMatchedLines":40,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-c7660d33-ae11-4ab6-9b2e-8a3f6df0d58a-14\nfc_e3d3bd39-7676-9773-aa6b-20257f207788_2","startedAtMs":"1787440332293","completedAtMs":"1787440332875"},"model_call_id":"a74d7e62-a08d-4d88-aaf5-b4d85b65652b-4-7uuv","session_id":"ce65663b-c70a-428f-a8bb-f87b51fd396c","timestamp_ms":1787440332899}
