{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-5e37ec1f-d2f3-4de0-8f11-53f80bd94776-27\nfc_17012780-636c-9b9b-899c-7d2bbc5fb7c2_3","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"slug|SLUG_RE|validate","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-5-design.md","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-5e37ec1f-d2f3-4de0-8f11-53f80bd94776-27\nfc_17012780-636c-9b9b-899c-7d2bbc5fb7c2_3","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"slug|SLUG_RE|validate","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-5-design.md","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"../../../../../tmp/MARATHON-5-design.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":5,"content":"This task adds the workspace tenancy root for Huddle: authenticated callers can create a workspace (unique kebab `slug`, display `name`, creator as `owner`, default `join_mode=open`), which atomically provisions the public `#general` channel and membership rows; list workspaces they own or belong to; and load a workspace by slug with the visible channel list plus embedded `read_state`. It locks `WorkspaceObj`, the initial `ChannelObj` shape used by later channel APIs, the SQLite schema for workspaces/members/channels, and the REST contracts the SPA shell (MARATHON-16) and members/channels tasks (MARATHON-6/7) consume.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":43,"content":"| Include `join_mode` in POST body | Task body is `{slug,name}` only; `join_mode` changes are MARATHON-6 PATCH |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":68,"content":"  \"slug\": \"acme\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":78,"content":"| `slug` | string | required | Unique cluster-wide; kebab per regex below; immutable in this task (no rename API) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":144,"content":"| `validation_error` | 400 | Bad slug/name |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":147,"content":"| `conflict` | 409 | Duplicate workspace slug |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":148,"content":"| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown slug **or** caller not a workspace member |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":154,"content":"| **Client (SPA / grader)** | `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; JSON `{ \"slug\", \"name\" }`. While slow: disable create submit / show pending (`workspace-create-form` lives in MARATHON-16). On 201: store returned workspace as current; navigate shell to its channels. On 400/409: show `error.message`. On 401: re-auth. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":160,"content":"{ \"slug\": \"acme\", \"name\": \"Acme Corp\" }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":163,"content":"- Required: `slug`, `name` (strings).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":182,"content":"  \"workspace\": { \"id\": \"...\", \"slug\": \"acme\", \"name\": \"Acme Corp\", \"owner_id\": \"<creator>\", \"join_mode\": \"open\" },","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":187,"content":"**Errors:** 401; 400 validation; 409 `conflict` message e.g. `\"slug already taken\"`; SQLite integrity race → same 409.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":202,"content":"- Order: `name ASC` (case-insensitive), tie-break `slug ASC`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":205,"content":"### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":210,"content":"| **Server** | Resolve by slug; require membership; build filtered `channels` + `read_state`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":235,"content":"  \"workspace\": { \"id\": \"...\", \"slug\": \"acme\", \"name\": \"Acme Corp\", \"owner_id\": \"...\", \"join_mode\": \"open\" },","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":255,"content":"**Errors:** 401; 404 `not_found` if slug missing **or** caller not a member (same message, e.g. `\"workspace not found\"` — do not leak invite-only existence).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":272,"content":"| `slug` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UNIQUE |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":343,"content":"On any failure: rollback; map UNIQUE(slug) → 409; unexpected → 500 (log).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":352,"content":"| `server/workspaces/store.py` | Slug/name validation; insert workspace; list for user; get by slug; membership check; row→`WorkspaceObj`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":353,"content":"| `server/workspaces/routes.py` | `POST \"\"`, `GET \"\"`, `GET \"/{slug}\"` under prefix `/api/workspaces`; Depend `get_current_user`; parse `include_archived` (`1` \\| case-insensitive `true`). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":356,"content":"| `tests/test_workspaces.py` | Contract tests for create/list/detail, authz, slug conflict, archive query (`1` and `true`), full `read_state` keys, envelope errors. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":426,"content":"| `GET/PATCH` members, transfer ownership | future `/api/workspaces/{slug}/members` | MARATHON-6 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":460,"content":"| Duplicate slug | **409** `conflict` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":461,"content":"| Concurrent duplicate slug inserts | IntegrityError → **409** (no 500) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":466,"content":"| Second create by same user different slug | Allowed (multi-workspace) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":468,"content":"| Detail unknown slug | **404** |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":469,"content":"| Detail existing slug, non-member | **404** (same body as unknown) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":486,"content":"1. `POST /api/workspaces` with valid Bearer + `{slug,name}` → **201** with `workspace` (`WorkspaceObj` keys exactly) and `general_channel` (`ChannelObj` keys exactly); `workspace.join_mode==\"open\"`; `workspace.owner_id` equals caller; `general_channel.name==\"general\"`; `is_private/is_dm/is_archived` are JSON `false`; `topic==\"\"`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":487,"content":"2. Duplicate `slug` → **409** envelope `code=conflict`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":488,"content":"3. Invalid slug (fails `^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`) or empty/whitespace name → **400** `validation_error`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":491,"content":"6. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as member → **200** with `workspace`, `channels` containing `#general`, and `read_state` (array; may be empty). When non-empty, **every** entry has exactly the keys `channel_id`, `last_read_seq`, `unread_count`, `mention_count` (integers ≥ 0 for the three numeric fields).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":492,"content":"7. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as different user with no membership → **404** (must **not** return 200).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":507,"content":"- Duplicate slug → 409.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":508,"content":"- Bad slug / blank name → 400 envelope.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":530,"content":"2. Second account cannot open the slug (404).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":36,"totalMatchedLines":36,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-5e37ec1f-d2f3-4de0-8f11-53f80bd94776-27\nfc_17012780-636c-9b9b-899c-7d2bbc5fb7c2_3","startedAtMs":"1787440362712","completedAtMs":"1787440363050"},"model_call_id