{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-43426fb4-6570-47c5-b68d-a708c33c8e3d-34\nfc_9033ac0d-5234-90d7-99d5-66d21f77e394_2","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"GET /|static|SPA|HTML","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-43426fb4-6570-47c5-b68d-a708c33c8e3d-34\nfc_9033ac0d-5234-90d7-99d5-66d21f77e394_2","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"GET /|static|SPA|HTML","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"../../../../../tmp/MARATHON-2-design.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":5,"content":"This task boots the Huddle cluster so the verifier (and every later feature task) has a live, self-contained process tree: `/app/start.sh` stays in the foreground, supervises a local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, and respawns any of those children after `SIGKILL`. Each node exposes a stub `GET /` and the contracted `GET /api/health`. The design also locks language/framework and the shared durable storage layout that Auth, messages, fan-out, IRC, and the SPA will all assume.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":52,"content":"#### `GET /api/health`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":71,"content":"#### `GET /`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":75,"content":"| **Server** | `200` with an HTML document (text/html). Minimal stub page titled or branded “Huddle” so a browser fetch succeeds on every node. No SPA, no auth UI yet (MARATHON-16 owns that). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":76,"content":"| **Client** | Expects HTML 200; must not depend on specific `data-testid`s until the SPA task. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":110,"content":"    app.py                 # FastAPI factory: GET /, GET /api/health","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":156,"content":"| `server/app.py` | FastAPI app: `GET /api/health` → JSON contract; `GET /` → minimal HTML stub. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":160,"content":"| `data/redis/redis.conf` | **Either** commit a static conf **or** generate from `start.sh`; must bind 127.0.0.1:6379 and set `dir`/`pidfile` under `/app/data`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":174,"content":"| IRC / SPA / Auth modules | Later tasks |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":195,"content":"| Stub `GET /` | Replaced by MARATHON-16 SPA (same route) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":217,"content":"| SPA + `data-testid`s (MARATHON-16+) | Replaces stub `GET /` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":251,"content":"4. `curl -sf http://127.0.0.1:8000/` (and 8001/8002) → `200` with `Content-Type` HTML (or text/html).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":281,"content":"2. Browser or curl `GET /` on each port — stub HTML loads.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":288,"content":"Auth flows, WS fan-out during Redis outage, IRC, SPA selectors — covered by later tasks/QA once those land.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":14,"totalMatchedLines":14,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-43426fb4-6570-47c5-b68d-a708c33c8e3d-34\nfc_9033ac0d-5234-90d7-99d5-66d21f77e394_2","startedAtMs":"1787440395807","completedAtMs":"1787440398619"},"model_call_id":"a74d7e62-a08d-4d88-aaf5-b4d85b65652b-8-usgf","session_id":"ce65663b-c70a-428f-a8bb-f87b51fd396c","timestamp_ms":1787440398638}
