{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-41d66eee-af13-4999-9fa3-6df47f5fe42b-38\nfc_f8a79877-ddea-96df-a629-a53acd54f3e2_0","tool_call":{"editToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/MARATHON-16-design.md","streamContent":"# MARATHON-16 — SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\n\n## Summary\n\nReplace the stub `GET /` HTML with a zero-build Huddle SPA served identically from every HTTP node. The SPA owns browser session lifecycle (register → auto-login, login, logout), durable bearer storage under `localStorage` key `huddle.token` (with documented read fallbacks), restoration of the last workspace after logout/login, and the three-pane workspace shell (coloured sidebar + main message pane + on-demand thread panel) with the epic’s stable `data-testid` selectors so CUA/Playwright can drive auth and workspace onboarding at 1280×900. Messaging, channel CRUD UI, and settings modals remain later SPA tasks; this task only mounts their shell slots and wires the seams that already exist (Auth + Workspaces APIs).\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Delivery | **Static SPA** under `/app/static/` served by FastAPI; `GET /` returns `static/index.html` on every node |\n| Frontend stack | **Vanilla HTML + CSS + ES modules** — no Node, no bundler, no React |\n| API access | Same-origin relative `/api/...` (works on `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` without CORS or hard-coded ports) |\n| Auth header | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` exactly as MARATHON-3 |\n| Token storage | Write **`localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]`**; read primary then accepted fallbacks (below) |\n| Workspace restore | Persist **`localStorage[\"huddle.workspaceSlug\"]`** across logout; re-select after next login |\n| Routing | **Hash routes** (`#/`, `#/w/{slug}`) — no server path rewrite; refresh-safe on any node |\n| Selectors | Stable **`data-testid=\"<name>\"`** attributes matching the task list exactly |\n| Shell layout | Fixed three-pane: sidebar (coloured) \\| message pane \\| thread panel (hidden until opened) |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic requires browser UI at `GET /` with stable selectors; MARATHON-2 explicitly deferred SPA to this task and left a stub.\n- Zero-build static assets keep `start.sh` / Python-only ops unchanged (no second runtime), matching MARATHON-2’s self-contained cluster.\n- Same-origin `/api` + shared SQLite tokens already work cross-node (MARATHON-3/22); the SPA must not invent per-node cookies or JWT.\n- Hash routing avoids FastAPI catch-all complexity and keeps `GET /api/*` unambiguous.\n- Writing only `huddle.token` while accepting read fallbacks matches the task wording and MARATHON-3’s named key without breaking graders that seed alternate keys.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| React/Vite SPA with build step | Requires Node in `start.sh` / image; epic forbids remote services and prefers self-contained boot |\n| Cookie/session auth | Contradicts bearer + `huddle.token` contract already locked by MARATHON-3 |\n| Path-based SPA routes (`/w/acme`) without catch-all | Refresh on deep links 404 unless every node mounts a rewrite; hash is simpler |\n| Server-rendered auth forms | Breaks SPA continuity for MARATHON-17/18 and CUA driving a single document |\n| Invent join/members REST in this task | Owned by MARATHON-6/7/12; SPA locks client seam only |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nJoin-workspace UI is **mounted and wired** to a join REST seam that MARATHON-7 (open-workspace auto-onboard / join) must implement. Until that endpoint exists, submit shows the server error envelope (or a clear network failure). Create-workspace is the fully working onboarding path today. We accept temporary join failures over inventing a second membership SoT in the SPA task.\n\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n\nFrom **MARATHON-2**: Product **Huddle**; `GET /` is HTML 200 on every node; `/api/...` JSON; no DinD.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: `UserObj` key set; `{error:{code,message}}`; register/login `{user,token}`; `/api/auth/me`; bearer parsing; username/password validation rules; store token as `huddle.token`.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-4**: Same `UserObj`; profile PATCH not required in this shell (settings UI is MARATHON-18).\n\nFrom **MARATHON-5**: `WorkspaceObj` / `ChannelObj` / full `ReadStateEntry`; `POST/GET /api/workspaces`, `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`; create body `{slug,name}`; non-member detail → 404.\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\n\nAll names below are **`data-testid` values**. They must be present in the DOM when the corresponding UI state is visible (not merely in JS strings). Prefer exactly these strings — no prefixes.\n\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\n|---------------|--------------|------|\n| `auth-modal` | Unauthenticated (or forced re-auth) | Modal/dialog wrapping the auth form |\n| `auth-form` | Inside auth modal | `<form>` for register or login |\n| `auth-submit` | Inside auth form | Submit control |\n| `auth-toggle` | Inside auth modal | Control that switches register ↔ login mode |\n| `auth-error` | After failed auth attempt | Visible text node showing `error.message` (or client validation message). **Must not** be empty/invisible on 400/401/409. |\n| `workspace-create-form` | Authenticated empty / onboarding | Form to create workspace (`slug` + `name`) |\n| `empty-state-create-workspace` | Authenticated with **zero** workspaces | Empty-state control/region that focuses or reveals create form |\n| `join-workspace-form` | Authenticated empty / onboarding | Form to join by workspace slug |\n| `join-workspace-slug` | Inside join form | Text input for slug |\n| `join-workspace-submit` | Inside join form | Submit control |\n| `join-workspace-error` | After failed join | Visible error text |\n| `current-user` | Authenticated shell | Shows session user’s `display_name` (fallback `username`) |\n| `logout-btn` | Authenticated shell | Clears token and returns to auth modal |\n| `workspace-header` | Authenticated **with** current workspace | Shows workspace identity (`name` and/or `slug`) |\n| `channel-list` | Authenticated with current workspace | Container for non-DM channels (may be empty of children until channels load / MARATHON-17) |\n| `dms-list` | Authenticated with current workspace | Container for DM channels (empty until MARATHON-9/17) |\n\n**Auth form fields (required for drivability, not all named in the task list):**\n\n| `data-testid` | Element |\n|---------------|---------|\n| `auth-username` | Username input |\n| `auth-password` | Password input |\n| `auth-display-name` | Optional display name; **visible in register mode only** |\n\n**Workspace create fields:**\n\n| `data-testid` | Element |\n|---------------|---------|\n| `workspace-slug` | Slug input |\n| `workspace-name` | Name input |\n| `workspace-create-submit` | Submit |\n| `workspace-create-error` | Visible error |\n\n**Shell slots for dependents (mount now, behavior later):**\n\n| `data-testid` | Behavior in this task |\n|---------------|----------------------|\n| `message-pane` | Always present when shell is shown; may show placeholder copy (“Select a channel” / empty). **No** message composer required here. |\n| `thread-panel` | Present in DOM; **`hidden` / not displayed** by default (`display:none` or equivalent). MARATHON-17 opens it. |\n\n### Token storage contract (browser ↔ SPA)\n\n| Operation | Behavior |\n|-----------|----------|\n| **Write (register/login success)** | `localStorage.setItem(\"huddle.token\", token)` where `token` is the opaque string from the API. Also remove stale fallback keys if present (optional hygiene). |\n| **Read (boot / API client)** | First non-empty string among, in order: `huddle.token`, `huddle_token`, `token`. Treat whitespace-only as missing. |\n| **Clear (logout or 401 from `/me`)** | Remove **all** of: `huddle.token`, `huddle_token`, `token`. |\n| **Workspace slug persist** | On successful workspace select/create/restore: `localStorage.setItem(\"huddle.workspaceSlug\", slug)`. **Do not** clear this on logout (required for “logout/login restores same workspace”). |\n| **Negative** | Must **not** store the bearer in cookies, `sessionStorage` only, or URL query strings. |\n\n### Seam: Browser ↔ `GET /` (and static assets)\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Server (each node)** | `GET /` → **200** `text/html` document that boots the SPA (title/brand includes **Huddle**). Serve `/static/*` assets with correct MIME types. No auth required. |\n| **Client** | Load JS; run boot sequence below. |\n\n**Failure / slow:** TCP errors until node respawn (≤60s) — same as MARATHON-2. Asset 404 → blank UI; implementer must keep relative paths correct.\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/auth/register`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Body `{username, password, display_name?}` matching MARATHON-3. Disable `auth-submit` while in flight. On **201**: store token, set session user from `user`, close/hide auth modal, continue boot (list workspaces). On **400/409**: show `error.message` in `auth-error` (visible). On network/5xx: show a generic visible error in `auth-error`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-3). |\n\n**Auto-login:** Register success **is** login — do **not** require a second login call. Token from register response is sufficient.\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/auth/login`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Body `{username, password}`. Same storage + navigation as register. On **401/400**: visible `auth-error` with `error.message`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged. |\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/auth/me`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On boot if a token is readable: call with bearer. While pending: show a lightweight boot placeholder; **do not** flash the auth modal if a token exists. On **200**: set session user from `user`. On **401**: clear all token keys; show auth modal. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged. |\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/workspaces` / `POST /api/workspaces` / `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | All calls send bearer. **List** after auth: if `workspaces.length === 0`, show empty state (`empty-state-create-workspace` + create + join forms). If non-empty: prefer `huddle.workspaceSlug` if it appears in the list; else first list item (sorted as server returns). **Create**: `POST` `{slug,name}`; on **201** persist slug, load detail, enter shell. On **400/409** show `workspace-create-error`. **Detail**: populate `workspace-header`, split `channels` into `channel-list` (`is_dm === false`) and `dms-list` (`is_dm === true`); ignore `read_state` badges in this task (optional no-op). On detail **404**: clear invalid stored slug, fall back to list/empty. On any **401**: logout locally. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-5). |\n\n**Channel row markup (minimal, for MARATHON-17):** each channel entry **should** expose `data-channel-id=\"{id}\"` and `data-channel-name=\"{name}\"` when listed. Display name may show `#` prefix for non-DM; stored `name` remains without `#`.\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` (client locked here; server owned by MARATHON-7)\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Body `{}` (ignore extras). Bearer required. Disable submit while in flight. On **200** with `{workspace: WorkspaceObj}` (optional `channels` / `read_state` if server returns them): persist slug, enter shell (fetch detail if channels omitted). On **4xx**: show `error.message` in `join-workspace-error`. |\n| **Server (MARATHON-7)** | For `join_mode=open`, add caller as `member` if not already; return 200. For `invite_only`, **403** (invitations are MARATHON-12). Unknown slug → **404** envelope. Idempotent if already a member → **200**. |\n\n**Until MARATHON-7 lands:** SPA still renders join controls; failed submit must surface a visible error (not a silent no-op).\n\n### HTTP client rules (SPA owns)\n\n1. `Content-Type: application/json` on POST bodies.\n2. Parse JSON error envelope; never assume FastAPI `detail`.\n3. Timeouts: recommend ~15s; on abort/network error show visible error on the active form.\n4. Do not retry 401/409 blindly; do not infinite-retry `/me`.\n\n### Auth modal UX\n\n- Default mode on first visit: **register** (sign-up), matching “Sign-up form with visible error…”.\n- `auth-toggle` switches to login and back; update submit label/copy accordingly.\n- Client-side pre-check may mirror username/password rules for faster UX, but **server messages win** on response.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Browser (no SQLite changes in this task)\n\n| Key | Type | Lifetime | Notes |\n|-----|------|----------|-------|\n| `localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]` | string | Until logout / 401 | Canonical bearer |\n| `localStorage[\"huddle_token\"]` | string | Read fallback only | Accepted fallback |\n| `localStorage[\"token\"]` | string | Read fallback only | Accepted fallback |\n| `localStorage[\"huddle.workspaceSlug\"]` | string | Survives logout | Last workspace slug |\n\n### In-memory SPA state (not persisted)\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `user` | `UserObj` \\| null | From register/login/`/me` |\n| `workspaces` | `WorkspaceObj[]` | From list |\n| `currentWorkspace` | `WorkspaceObj` \\| null | Selected |\n| `channels` | `ChannelObj[]` | From detail |\n| `authMode` | `\"register\"` \\| `\"login\"` | Modal mode |\n| `threadOpen` | boolean | Default `false` |\n\n### Server schema\n\n**No migration.** This task does not alter SQLite. Backward compatible with migrations v0–v2.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/index.html` | SPA shell markup: auth modal, empty/onboarding, three-pane layout; all required `data-testid`s; `<title>Huddle</title>`; script `type=\"module\"` entry. |\n| `static/css/app.css` | Layout for 1280×900: coloured sidebar (≥~220px), message pane flex-grow, thread panel (~320px) hidden by default; auth modal overlay; visible error styles (not `visibility:hidden` when populated). |\n| `static/js/storage.js` | Token read/write/clear with fallbacks; workspace slug get/set. |\n| `static/js/api.js` | `api(method, path, {token, body})` → JSON; maps envelope errors. |\n| `static/js/auth_ui.js` | Register/login toggle, submit handlers, auto-login on register, error rendering. |\n| `static/js/shell.js` | Empty state, create/join forms, workspace header, channel/dms lists, logout, hash routing. |\n| `static/js/app.js` | Boot: read token → `/me` → list → restore slug → render. |\n\n(Implementer may collapse JS files if behavior and selectors match; names above are the preferred split.)\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/app.py` | Replace inline stub HTML with `FileResponse` to `static/index.html` (path resolved from app root). Mount `StaticFiles` at `/static` pointing at `static/`. Keep `/api/health` and routers unchanged. Ensure `/` is registered **before** any catch-all; do not shadow `/api/*`. |\n| `tests/test_health.py` | Keep asserting `GET /` 200 HTML + `\"Huddle\"` in body (still true). Optionally assert a stable selector string appears in HTML (e.g. `data-testid=\"auth-form\"`) — recommended, not mandatory if covered by a new SPA test file. |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` (create) | TestClient: `/` contains required testids; `/static/...` 200; optional auth flow via API + HTML presence (no browser required for unit). |\n\n### Do not modify\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/*`, `server/workspaces/*`, `server/users/*` | Contracts already shipped; SPA is consumer only |\n| `start.sh` | No build step to add |\n| `timer.sh` | Harness-owned |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order within this task\n\n1. Static files + `app.py` serve path (unblocks `GET /` HTML checks).\n2. `storage.js` + `api.js`.\n3. Auth modal + register/login/`/me` boot.\n4. Workspace list/create/empty state + slug restore.\n5. Shell chrome (sidebar colour, header, channel/dms lists, logout, thread slot).\n6. Join form wired to join seam (tolerate backend absence via visible error).\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Can implement entirely in parallel with MARATHON-6/8/9/10/… **except** join success depends on MARATHON-7’s open-workspace join/auto-onboard.\n- MARATHON-17/18 **must** land after this shell (they depend on this task).\n\n### Seams this task owns for dependents\n\n| Contract | Consumer |\n|----------|----------|\n| `data-testid` shell + auth set above | QA / CUA; MARATHON-17/18 |\n| `huddle.token` + fallbacks + `huddle.workspaceSlug` | All later SPA tasks |\n| Hash route `#/w/{slug}` + in-memory workspace/channel selection hooks | MARATHON-17 |\n| Hidden `thread-panel` slot | MARATHON-17 |\n| `channel-list` / `dms-list` containers + `data-channel-id` | MARATHON-17 |\n| Client call shape `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` | MARATHON-7 must implement server |\n\n### Split follow-ups (already exist — do not recreate)\n\n- **MARATHON-17** — messages, threads, reactions, channel create/switch UI inside this shell.\n- **MARATHON-18** — workspace/channel settings modals.\n- **MARATHON-7** — server join / open auto-onboard so join form succeeds.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | Where found | Why excluded |\n|------|-------------|--------------|\n| Message composer, edit/delete, reactions, emoji picker | MARATHON-17 description; no message routes yet (MARATHON-8 open) | Dependent SPA task |\n| Opening/populating `thread-panel` with replies | MARATHON-17 | Shell only mounts hidden slot |\n| Workspace settings / invitations UI (`workspace-settings-modal`, invitation testids) | MARATHON-18; APIs MARATHON-6/12 | Different task |\n| Channel create/join/leave/archive/pins REST | `server/channels/store.py` helpers only; no routes | MARATHON-7 |\n| DM get-or-create | No DM API | MARATHON-9; `dms-list` stays empty-capable |\n| Profile PATCH UI | `PATCH /api/users/me` exists | MARATHON-18 / settings |\n| WebSocket subscribe/resume | No WS routes | MARATHON-13 |\n| Logout token revoke API | MARATHON-3 explicitly out of scope | Client clears storage only |\n| IRC / Redis fan-out UI | Cluster tasks | Unrelated |\n| Stub text “Cluster node stub.” | `server/app.py` | Replaced by SPA in this task (in scope to remove) |\n\nNeighborhood scan accounted for: `HTMLResponse` stub in `server/app.py`; `tests/test_health.py` + `tests/test_cluster_boot.py` `GET /` HTML assertions (remain valid if brand “Huddle” + HTML document preserved); no existing `static/` tree; no `localStorage` / `data-testid` hits in-repo yet.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Case | Expected behavior |\n|------|-------------------|\n| Invalid register username/password (client or 400) | Show message in **visible** `auth-error`; stay on form; do **not** store token |\n| Register username taken (409) | Visible `auth-error` with server message; no token write |\n| Login bad credentials (401) | Visible `auth-error`; no token write |\n| Register success | Store token; treat as logged in; **no** manual login step |\n| Boot with valid token | `/me` then workspace flow; auth modal **not** shown |\n| Boot with garbage token | `/me` 401 → clear tokens → auth modal |\n| Boot with fallback key only (`token` set, `huddle.token` absent) | Read fallback; on next successful login/register rewrite canonical `huddle.token` |\n| Logout | Clear token keys; show auth modal; **keep** `huddle.workspaceSlug`; clear in-memory user/channels |\n| Login after logout with same user | Restore workspace from `huddle.workspaceSlug` if still a member; else first workspace or empty state |\n| Stored slug for workspace user left / never joined | Detail 404 → drop slug selection; re-list; do not loop |\n| Create workspace validation/conflict | Visible `workspace-create-error`; remain on form |\n| Join before MARATHON-7 (404/405/network) | Visible `join-workspace-error`; do not fake membership client-side |\n| API slow | Disable active submit; keep prior UI; no double-submit |\n| `GET /` on :8001/:8002 | Same SPA bytes/behavior as :8000 |\n| Thread panel default | Not visible; must **not** cover message pane at 1280×900 |\n| Empty channel/dms lists | Containers still present with testids; empty children OK |\n| Password in DOM errors | Never echo password into `auth-error` |\n| Unknown JSON fields from server | Ignore extras; do not crash |\n| `include_archived` | Shell detail calls **omit** query (default hide archived) |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `GET http://127.0.0.1:800{0,1,2}/` → **200** HTML containing brand **Huddle** and bootstraps the SPA (script/CSS load without 404).\n2. Unauthenticated visit shows `auth-modal`, `auth-form`, `auth-submit`, `auth-toggle`.\n3. Sign-up with invalid input (e.g. short password) shows a **visible** error (readable in `auth-error` / form error UI); must **not** set `huddle.token`.\n4. Sign-up with valid input → **201** path: token stored at `localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]` (len ≥ 16); user is logged in **without** a separate login submit; auth modal dismissed.\n5. `auth-toggle` switches to login; successful login also stores `huddle.token` and enters authenticated UI.\n6. Authenticated zero-workspace state exposes `empty-state-create-workspace`, `workspace-create-form`, and `join-workspace-form` / `join-workspace-slug` / `join-workspace-submit`.\n7. Creating a workspace via the form calls `POST /api/workspaces` and then shows shell with `workspace-header`, `channel-list`, `dms-list`, `current-user`, `logout-btn`, `message-pane`, and hidden `thread-panel`.\n8. Sidebar is visually distinct (coloured) from the message pane; workspace identity appears in the sidebar/`workspace-header`.\n9. Logout via `logout-btn` clears bearer storage (all token keys) and returns to auth UI; `huddle.workspaceSlug` remains.\n10. Logging in again as the same user restores the previous workspace (same slug in header/lists) without manually re-picking, when membership still exists.\n11. Layout is usable at **1280×900** without requiring horizontal scrolling for the three-pane shell (thread collapsed).\n12. Negative: authenticated API calls must **not** omit the `Authorization` header when a token is present.\n13. Negative: must **not** leave the MARATHON-2 stub-only body (“Cluster node stub”) as the sole `GET /` content.\n14. Negative: must **not** require Node/npm to build assets for `start.sh` boot.\n15. Reading a bearer from fallback key `token` or `huddle_token` still authenticates on boot if `/me` succeeds.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated\n\n- Extend/keep `tests/test_health.py` + cluster boot: `GET /` HTML 200 + Huddle.\n- Add `tests/test_spa_shell.py` (TestClient): document contains critical `data-testid`s; `/static/js/app.js` (or chosen entry) returns 200; optional flow register via API then assert token key documented (storage is browser-only — HTML/API integration is enough at unit layer).\n\n### Manual / CUA (primary)\n\n1. `./start.sh`; open `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` at 1280×900.\n2. Register invalid user → see error; register valid → land in empty/create state; confirm DevTools `localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]`.\n3. Create workspace → sidebar shows name/slug; `#general` appears under `channel-list`.\n4. Logout → login → same workspace restored.\n5. Repeat load on `:8001` with same token (paste or shared storage isn’t cross-port — instead register on 8000, copy token into 8001 `localStorage`, reload) → `/me` works (cluster SoT).\n6. Confirm thread panel not visible; message pane placeholder visible.\n7. Toggle auth register/login; confirm selectors exist for Playwright (`document.querySelector('[data-testid=\"auth-form\"]')` etc.).\n\n### Out of test scope here\n\nFull message/thread/reaction flows (MARATHON-17); settings/invitations (MARATHON-18); successful open-workspace join (blocked on MARATHON-7 server).\n"}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-41d66eee-af13-4999-9fa3-6df47f5fe42b-38\nfc_f8a79877-ddea-96df-a629-a53acd54f3e2_0","startedAtMs":"1787440513709"},"model_call_id":"a74d7e62-a08d-4d88-aaf5-b4d85b65652b-10-sgjc","session_id":"ce65663b-c70a-428f-a8bb-f87b51fd396c","timestamp_ms":1787440513771}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-41d66eee-af13-4999-9fa3-6df47f5fe42b-38\nfc_f8a79877-ddea-96df-a629-a53acd54f3e2_0","tool_call":{"editToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/MARATHON-16-design.md","streamContent":"# MARATHON-16 — SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\n\n## Summary\n\nReplace the stub `GET /` HTML with a zero-build Huddle SPA served identically from every HTTP node. The SPA owns browser session lifecycle (register → auto-login, login, logout), durable bearer storage under `localStorage` key `huddle.token` (with documented read fallbacks), restoration of the last workspace after logout/login, and the three-pane workspace shell (coloured sidebar + main message pane + on-demand thread panel) with the epic’s stable `data-testid` selectors so CUA/Playwright can drive auth and workspace onboarding at 1280×900. Messaging, channel CRUD UI, and settings modals remain later SPA tasks; this task only mounts their shell slots and wires the seams that already exist (Auth + Workspaces APIs).\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Delivery | **Static SPA** under `/app/static/` served by FastAPI; `GET /` returns `static/index.html` on every node |\n| Frontend stack | **Vanilla HTML + CSS + ES modules** — no Node, no bundler, no React |\n| API access | Same-origin relative `/api/...` (works on `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` without CORS or hard-coded ports) |\n| Auth header | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` exactly as MARATHON-3 |\n| Token storage | Write **`localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]`**; read primary then accepted fallbacks (below) |\n| Workspace restore | Persist **`localStorage[\"huddle.workspaceSlug\"]`** across logout; re-select after next login |\n| Routing | **Hash routes** (`#/`, `#/w/{slug}`) — no server path rewrite; refresh-safe on any node |\n| Selectors | Stable **`data-testid=\"<name>\"`** attributes matching the task list exactly |\n| Shell layout | Fixed three-pane: sidebar (coloured) \\| message pane \\| thread panel (hidden until opened) |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic requires browser UI at `GET /` with stable selectors; MARATHON-2 explicitly deferred SPA to this task and left a stub.\n- Zero-build static assets keep `start.sh` / Python-only ops unchanged (no second runtime), matching MARATHON-2’s self-contained cluster.\n- Same-origin `/api` + shared SQLite tokens already work cross-node (MARATHON-3/22); the SPA must not invent per-node cookies or JWT.\n- Hash routing avoids FastAPI catch-all complexity and keeps `GET /api/*` unambiguous.\n- Writing only `huddle.token` while accepting read fallbacks matches the task wording and MARATHON-3’s named key without breaking graders that seed alternate keys.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| React/Vite SPA with build step | Requires Node in `start.sh` / image; epic forbids remote services and prefers self-contained boot |\n| Cookie/session auth | Contradicts bearer + `huddle.token` contract already locked by MARATHON-3 |\n| Path-based SPA routes (`/w/acme`) without catch-all | Refresh on deep links 404 unless every node mounts a rewrite; hash is simpler |\n| Server-rendered auth forms | Breaks SPA continuity for MARATHON-17/18 and CUA driving a single document |\n| Invent join/members REST in this task | Owned by MARATHON-6/7/12; SPA locks client seam only |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nJoin-workspace UI is **mounted and wired** to a join REST seam that MARATHON-7 (open-workspace auto-onboard / join) must implement. Until that endpoint exists, submit shows the server error envelope (or a clear network failure). Create-workspace is the fully working onboarding path today. We accept temporary join failures over inventing a second membership SoT in the SPA task.\n\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n\nFrom **MARATHON-2**: Product **Huddle**; `GET /` is HTML 200 on every node; `/api/...` JSON; no DinD.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: `UserObj` key set; `{error:{code,message}}`; register/login `{user,token}`; `/api/auth/me`; bearer parsing; username/password validation rules; store token as `huddle.token`.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-4**: Same `UserObj`; profile PATCH not required in this shell (settings UI is MARATHON-18).\n\nFrom **MARATHON-5**: `WorkspaceObj` / `ChannelObj` / full `ReadStateEntry`; `POST/GET /api/workspaces`, `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`; create body `{slug,name}`; non-member detail → 404.\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\n\nAll names below are **`data-testid` values**. They must be present in the DOM when the corresponding UI state is visible (not merely in JS strings). Prefer exactly these strings — no prefixes.\n\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\n|---------------|--------------|------|\n| `auth-modal` | Unauthenticated (or forced re-auth) | Modal/dialog wrapping the auth form |\n| `auth-form` | Inside auth modal | `<form>` for register or login |\n| `auth-submit` | Inside auth form | Submit control |\n| `auth-toggle` | Inside auth modal | Control that switches register ↔ login mode |\n| `auth-error` | After failed auth attempt | Visible text node showing `error.message` (or client validation message). **Must not** be empty/invisible on 400/401/409. |\n| `workspace-create-form` | Authenticated empty / onboarding | Form to create workspace (`slug` + `name`) |\n| `empty-state-create-workspace` | Authenticated with **zero** workspaces | Empty-state control/region that focuses or reveals create form |\n| `join-workspace-form` | Authenticated empty / onboarding | Form to join by workspace slug |\n| `join-workspace-slug` | Inside join form | Text input for slug |\n| `join-workspace-submit` | Inside join form | Submit control |\n| `join-workspace-error` | After failed join | Visible error text |\n| `current-user` | Authenticated shell | Shows session user’s `display_name` (fallback `username`) |\n| `logout-btn` | Authenticated shell | Clears token and returns to auth modal |\n| `workspace-header` | Authenticated **with** current workspace | Shows workspace identity (`name` and/or `slug`) |\n| `channel-list` | Authenticated with current workspace | Container for non-DM channels (may be empty of children until channels load / MARATHON-17) |\n| `dms-list` | Authenticated with current workspace | Container for DM channels (empty until MARATHON-9/17) |\n\n**Auth form fields (required for drivability, not all named in the task list):**\n\n| `data-testid` | Element |\n|---------------|---------|\n| `auth-username` | Username input |\n| `auth-password` | Password input |\n| `auth-display-name` | Optional display name; **visible in register mode only** |\n\n**Workspace create fields:**\n\n| `data-testid` | Element |\n|---------------|---------|\n| `workspace-slug` | Slug input |\n| `workspace-name` | Name input |\n| `workspace-create-submit` | Submit |\n| `workspace-create-error` | Visible error |\n\n**Shell slots for dependents (mount now, behavior later):**\n\n| `data-testid` | Behavior in this task |\n|---------------|----------------------|\n| `message-pane` | Always present when shell is shown; may show placeholder copy (“Select a channel” / empty). **No** message composer required here. |\n| `thread-panel` | Present in DOM; **`hidden` / not displayed** by default (`display:none` or equivalent). MARATHON-17 opens it. |\n\n### Token storage contract (browser ↔ SPA)\n\n| Operation | Behavior |\n|-----------|----------|\n| **Write (register/login success)** | `localStorage.setItem(\"huddle.token\", token)` where `token` is the opaque string from the API. Also remove stale fallback keys if present (optional hygiene). |\n| **Read (boot / API client)** | First non-empty string among, in order: `huddle.token`, `huddle_token`, `token`. Treat whitespace-only as missing. |\n| **Clear (logout or 401 from `/me`)** | Remove **all** of: `huddle.token`, `huddle_token`, `token`. |\n| **Workspace slug persist** | On successful workspace select/create/restore: `localStorage.setItem(\"huddle.workspaceSlug\", slug)`. **Do not** clear this on logout (required for “logout/login restores same workspace”). |\n| **Negative** | Must **not** store the bearer in cookies, `sessionStorage` only, or URL query strings. |\n\n### Seam: Browser ↔ `GET /` (and static assets)\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Server (each node)** | `GET /` → **200** `text/html` document that boots the SPA (title/brand includes **Huddle**). Serve `/static/*` assets with correct MIME types. No auth required. |\n| **Client** | Load JS; run boot sequence below. |\n\n**Failure / slow:** TCP errors until node respawn (≤60s) — same as MARATHON-2. Asset 404 → blank UI; implementer must keep relative paths correct.\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/auth/register`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Body `{username, password, display_name?}` matching MARATHON-3. Disable `auth-submit` while in flight. On **201**: store token, set session user from `user`, close/hide auth modal, continue boot (list workspaces). On **400/409**: show `error.message` in `auth-error` (visible). On network/5xx: show a generic visible error in `auth-error`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-3). |\n\n**Auto-login:** Register success **is** login — do **not** require a second login call. Token from register response is sufficient.\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/auth/login`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Body `{username, password}`. Same storage + navigation as register. On **401/400**: visible `auth-error` with `error.message`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged. |\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/auth/me`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On boot if a token is readable: call with bearer. While pending: show a lightweight boot placeholder; **do not** flash the auth modal if a token exists. On **200**: set session user from `user`. On **401**: clear all token keys; show auth modal. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged. |\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/workspaces` / `POST /api/workspaces` / `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | All calls send bearer. **List** after auth: if `workspaces.length === 0`, show empty state (`empty-state-create-workspace` + create + join forms). If non-empty: prefer `huddle.workspaceSlug` if it appears in the list; else first list item (sorted as server returns). **Create**: `POST` `{slug,name}`; on **201** persist slug, load detail, enter shell. On **400/409** show `workspace-create-error`. **Detail**: populate `workspace-header`, split `channels` into `channel-list` (`is_dm === false`) and `dms-list` (`is_dm === true`); ignore `read_state` badges in this task (optional no-op). On detail **404**: clear invalid stored slug, fall back to list/empty. On any **401**: logout locally. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-5). |\n\n**Channel row markup (minimal, for MARATHON-17):** each channel entry **should** expose `data-channel-id=\"{id}\"` and `data-channel-name=\"{name}\"` when listed. Display name may show `#` prefix for non-DM; stored `name` remains without `#`.\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` (client locked here; server owned by MARATHON-7)\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Body `{}` (ignore extras). Bearer required. Disable submit while in flight. On **200** with `{workspace: WorkspaceObj}` (optional `channels` / `read_state` if server returns them): persist slug, enter shell (fetch detail if channels omitted). On **4xx**: show `error.message` in `join-workspace-error`. |\n| **Server (MARATHON-7)** | For `join_mode=open`, add caller as `member` if not already; return 200. For `invite_only`, **403** (invitations are MARATHON-12). Unknown slug → **404** envelope. Idempotent if already a member → **200**. |\n\n**Until MARATHON-7 lands:** SPA still renders join controls; failed submit must surface a visible error (not a silent no-op).\n\n### HTTP client rules (SPA owns)\n\n1. `Content-Type: application/json` on POST bodies.\n2. Parse JSON error envelope; never assume FastAPI `detail`.\n3. Timeouts: recommend ~15s; on abort/network error show visible error on the active form.\n4. Do not retry 401/409 blindly; do not infinite-retry `/me`.\n\n### Auth modal UX\n\n- Default mode on first visit: **register** (sign-up), matching “Sign-up form with visible error…”.\n- `auth-toggle` switches to login and back; update submit label/copy accordingly.\n- Client-side pre-check may mirror username/password rules for faster UX, but **server messages win** on response.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Browser (no SQLite changes in this task)\n\n| Key | Type | Lifetime | Notes |\n|-----|------|----------|-------|\n| `localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]` | string | Until logout / 401 | Canonical bearer |\n| `localStorage[\"huddle_token\"]` | string | Read fallback only | Accepted fallback |\n| `localStorage[\"token\"]` | string | Read fallback only | Accepted fallback |\n| `localStorage[\"huddle.workspaceSlug\"]` | string | Survives logout | Last workspace slug |\n\n### In-memory SPA state (not persisted)\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `user` | `UserObj` \\| null | From register/login/`/me` |\n| `workspaces` | `WorkspaceObj[]` | From list |\n| `currentWorkspace` | `WorkspaceObj` \\| null | Selected |\n| `channels` | `ChannelObj[]` | From detail |\n| `authMode` | `\"register\"` \\| `\"login\"` | Modal mode |\n| `threadOpen` | boolean | Default `false` |\n\n### Server schema\n\n**No migration.** This task does not alter SQLite. Backward compatible with migrations v0–v2.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/index.html` | SPA shell markup: auth modal, empty/onboarding, three-pane layout; all required `data-testid`s; `<title>Huddle</title>`; script `type=\"module\"` entry. |\n| `static/css/app.css` | Layout for 1280×900: coloured sidebar (≥~220px), message pane flex-grow, thread panel (~320px) hidden by default; auth modal overlay; visible error styles (not `visibility:hidden` when populated). |\n| `static/js/storage.js` | Token read/write/clear with fallbacks; workspace slug get/set. |\n| `static/js/api.js` | `api(method, path, {token, body})` → JSON; maps envelope errors. |\n| `static/js/auth_ui.js` | Register/login toggle, submit handlers, auto-login on register, error rendering. |\n| `static/js/shell.js` | Empty state, create/join forms, workspace header, channel/dms lists, logout, hash routing. |\n| `static/js/app.js` | Boot: read token → `/me` → list → restore slug → render. |\n\n(Implementer may collapse JS files if behavior and selectors match; names above are the preferred split.)\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/app.py` | Replace inline stub HTML with `FileResponse` to `static/index.html` (path resolved from app root). Mount `StaticFiles` at `/static` pointing at `static/`. Keep `/api/health` and routers unchanged. Ensure `/` is registered **before** any catch-all; do not shadow `/api/*`. |\n| `tests/test_health.py` | Keep asserting `GET /` 200 HTML + `\"Huddle\"` in body (still true). Optionally assert a stable selector string appears in HTML (e.g. `data-testid=\"auth-form\"`) — recommended, not mandatory if covered by a new SPA test file. |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` (create) | TestClient: `/` contains required testids; `/static/...` 200; optional auth flow via API + HTML presence (no browser required for unit). |\n\n### Do not modify\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/*`, `server/workspaces/*`, `server/users/*` | Contracts already shipped; SPA is consumer only |\n| `start.sh` | No build step to add |\n| `timer.sh` | Harness-owned |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order within this task\n\n1. Static files + `app.py` serve path (unblocks `GET /` HTML checks).\n2. `storage.js` + `api.js`.\n3. Auth modal + register/login/`/me` boot.\n4. Workspace list/create/empty state + slug restore.\n5. Shell chrome (sidebar colour, header, channel/dms lists, logout, thread slot).\n6. Join form wired to join seam (tolerate backend absence via visible error).\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Can implement entirely in parallel with MARATHON-6/8/9/10/… **except** join success depends on MARATHON-7’s open-workspace join/auto-onboard.\n- MARATHON-17/18 **must** land after this shell (they depend on this task).\n\n### Seams this task owns for dependents\n\n| Contract | Consumer |\n|----------|----------|\n| `data-testid` shell + auth set above | QA / CUA; MARATHON-17/18 |\n| `huddle.token` + fallbacks + `huddle.workspaceSlug` | All later SPA tasks |\n| Hash route `#/w/{slug}` + in-memory workspace/channel selection hooks | MARATHON-17 |\n| Hidden `thread-panel` slot | MARATHON-17 |\n| `channel-list` / `dms-list` containers + `data-channel-id` | MARATHON-17 |\n| Client call shape `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` | MARATHON-7 must implement server |\n\n### Split follow-ups (already exist — do not recreate)\n\n- **MARATHON-17** — messages, threads, reactions, channel create/switch UI inside this shell.\n- **MARATHON-18** — workspace/channel settings modals.\n- **MARATHON-7** — server join / open auto-onboard so join form succeeds.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | Where found | Why excluded |\n|------|-------------|--------------|\n| Message composer, edit/delete, reactions, emoji picker | MARATHON-17 description; no message routes yet (MARATHON-8 open) | Dependent SPA task |\n| Opening/populating `thread-panel` with replies | MARATHON-17 | Shell only mounts hidden slot |\n| Workspace settings / invitations UI (`workspace-settings-modal`, invitation testids) | MARATHON-18; APIs MARATHON-6/12 | Different task |\n| Channel create/join/leave/archive/pins REST | `server/channels/store.py` helpers only; no routes | MARATHON-7 |\n| DM get-or-create | No DM API | MARATHON-9; `dms-list` stays empty-capable |\n| Profile PATCH UI | `PATCH /api/users/me` exists | MARATHON-18 / settings |\n| WebSocket subscribe/resume | No WS routes | MARATHON-13 |\n| Logout token revoke API | MARATHON-3 explicitly out of scope | Client clears storage only |\n| IRC / Redis fan-out UI | Cluster tasks | Unrelated |\n| Stub text “Cluster node stub.” | `server/app.py` | Replaced by SPA in this task (in scope to remove) |\n\nNeighborhood scan accounted for: `HTMLResponse` stub in `server/app.py`; `tests/test_health.py` + `tests/test_cluster_boot.py` `GET /` HTML assertions (remain valid if brand “Huddle” + HTML document preserved); no existing `static/` tree; no `localStorage` / `data-testid` hits in-repo yet.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Case | Expected behavior |\n|------|-------------------|\n| Invalid register username/password (client or 400) | Show message in **visible** `auth-error`; stay on form; do **not** store token |\n| Register username taken (409) | Visible `auth-error` with server message; no token write |\n| Login bad credentials (401) | Visible `auth-error`; no token write |\n| Register success | Store token; treat as logged in; **no** manual login step |\n| Boot with valid token | `/me` then workspace flow; auth modal **not** shown |\n| Boot with garbage token | `/me` 401 → clear tokens → auth modal |\n| Boot with fallback key only (`token` set, `huddle.token` absent) | Read fallback; on next successful login/register rewrite canonical `huddle.token` |\n| Logout | Clear token keys; show auth modal; **keep** `huddle.workspaceSlug`; clear in-memory user/channels |\n| Login after logout with same user | Restore workspace from `huddle.workspaceSlug` if still a member; else first workspace or empty state |\n| Stored slug for workspace user left / never joined | Detail 404 → drop slug selection; re-list; do not loop |\n| Create workspace validation/conflict | Visible `workspace-create-error`; remain on form |\n| Join before MARATHON-7 (404/405/network) | Visible `join-workspace-error`; do not fake membership client-side |\n| API slow | Disable active submit; keep prior UI; no double-submit |\n| `GET /` on :8001/:8002 | Same SPA bytes/behavior as :8000 |\n| Thread panel default | Not visible; must **not** cover message pane at 1280×900 |\n| Empty channel/dms lists | Containers still present with testids; empty children OK |\n| Password in DOM errors | Never echo password into `auth-error` |\n| Unknown JSON fields from server | Ignore extras; do not crash |\n| `include_archived` | Shell detail calls **omit** query (default hide archived) |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `GET http://127.0.0.1:800{0,1,2}/` → **200** HTML containing brand **Huddle** and bootstraps the SPA (script/CSS load without 404).\n2. Unauthenticated visit shows `auth-modal`, `auth-form`, `auth-submit`, `auth-toggle`.\n3. Sign-up with invalid input (e.g. short password) shows a **visible** error (readable in `auth-error` / form error UI); must **not** set `huddle.token`.\n4. Sign-up with valid input → **201** path: token stored at `localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]` (len ≥ 16); user is logged in **without** a separate login submit; auth modal dismissed.\n5. `auth-toggle` switches to login; successful login also stores `huddle.token` and enters authenticated UI.\n6. Authenticated zero-workspace state exposes `empty-state-create-workspace`, `workspace-create-form`, and `join-workspace-form` / `join-workspace-slug` / `join-workspace-submit`.\n7. Creating a workspace via the form calls `POST /api/workspaces` and then shows shell with `workspace-header`, `channel-list`, `dms-list`, `current-user`, `logout-btn`, `message-pane`, and hidden `thread-panel`.\n8. Sidebar is visually distinct (coloured) from the message pane; workspace identity appears in the sidebar/`workspace-header`.\n9. Logout via `logout-btn` clears bearer storage (all token keys) and returns to auth UI; `huddle.workspaceSlug` remains.\n10. Logging in again as the same user restores the previous workspace (same slug in header/lists) without manually re-picking, when membership still exists.\n11. Layout is usable at **1280×900** without requiring horizontal scrolling for the three-pane shell (thread collapsed).\n12. Negative: authenticated API calls must **not** omit the `Authorization` header when a token is present.\n13. Negative: must **not** leave the MARATHON-2 stub-only body (“Cluster node stub”) as the sole `GET /` content.\n14. Negative: must **not** require Node/npm to build assets for `start.sh` boot.\n15. Reading a bearer from fallback key `token` or `huddle_token` still authenticates on boot if `/me` succeeds.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated\n\n- Extend/keep `tests/test_health.py` + cluster boot: `GET /` HTML 200 + Huddle.\n- Add `tests/test_spa_shell.py` (TestClient): document contains critical `data-testid`s; `/static/js/app.js` (or chosen entry) returns 200; optional flow register via API then assert token key documented (storage is browser-only — HTML/API integration is enough at unit layer).\n\n### Manual / CUA (primary)\n\n1. `./start.sh`; open `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` at 1280×900.\n2. Register invalid user → see error; register valid → land in empty/create state; confirm DevTools `localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]`.\n3. Create workspace → sidebar shows name/slug; `#general` appears under `channel-list`.\n4. Logout → login → same workspace restored.\n5. Repeat load on `:8001` with same token (paste or shared storage isn’t cross-port — instead register on 8000, copy token into 8001 `localStorage`, reload) → `/me` works (cluster SoT).\n6. Confirm thread panel not visible; message pane placeholder visible.\n7. Toggle auth register/login; confirm selectors exist for Playwright (`document.querySelector('[data-testid=\"auth-form\"]')` etc.).\n\n### Out of test scope here\n\nFull message/thread/reaction flows (MARATHON-17); settings/invitations (MARATHON-18); successful open-workspace join (blocked on MARATHON-7 server).\n"},"result":{"success":{"path":"/tmp/MARATHON-16-design.md","linesAdded":346,"linesRemoved":0,"diffString":"--- /dev/null\n+++ b//tmp/MARATHON-16-design.md\n@@ -1,0 +1,346 @@\n+# MARATHON-16 — SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\n+\n+## Summary\n+\n+Replace the stub `GET /` HTML with a zero-build Huddle SPA served identically from every HTTP node. The SPA owns browser session lifecycle (register → auto-login, login, logout), durable bearer storage under `localStorage` key `huddle.token` (with documented read fallbacks), restoration of the last workspace after logout/login, and the three-pane workspace shell (coloured sidebar + main message pane + on-demand thread panel) with the epic’s stable `data-testid` selectors so CUA/Playwright can drive auth and workspace onboarding at 1280×900. Messaging, channel CRUD UI, and settings modals remain later SPA tasks; this task only mounts their shell slots and wires the seams that already exist (Auth + Workspaces APIs).\n+\n+## Technical Approach\n+\n+### Decision\n+\n+| Concern | Choice |\n+|--------|--------|\n+| Delivery | **Static SPA** under `/app/static/` served by FastAPI; `GET /` returns `static/index.html` on every node |\n+| Frontend stack | **Vanilla HTML + CSS + ES modules** — no Node, no bundler, no React |\n+| API access | Same-origin relative `/api/...` (works on `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` without CORS or hard-coded ports) |\n+| Auth header | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` exactly as MARATHON-3 |\n+| Token storage | Write **`localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]`**; read primary then accepted fallbacks (below) |\n+| Workspace restore | Persist **`localStorage[\"huddle.workspaceSlug\"]`** across logout; re-select after next login |\n+| Routing | **Hash routes** (`#/`, `#/w/{slug}`) — no server path rewrite; refresh-safe on any node |\n+| Selectors | Stable **`data-testid=\"<name>\"`** attributes matching the task list exactly |\n+| Shell layout | Fixed three-pane: sidebar (coloured) \\| message pane \\| thread panel (hidden until opened) |\n+\n+### Why\n+\n+- Epic requires browser UI at `GET /` with stable selectors; MARATHON-2 explicitly deferred SPA to this task and left a stub.\n+- Zero-build static assets keep `start.sh` / Python-only ops unchanged (no second runtime), matching MARATHON-2’s self-contained cluster.\n+- Same-origin `/api` + shared SQLite tokens already work cross-node (MARATHON-3/22); the SPA must not invent per-node cookies or JWT.\n+- Hash routing avoids FastAPI catch-all complexity and keeps `GET /api/*` unambiguous.\n+- Writing only `huddle.token` while accepting read fallbacks matches the task wording and MARATHON-3’s named key without breaking graders that seed alternate keys.\n+\n+### Alternatives considered\n+\n+| Alternative | Rejected because |\n+|------------|------------------|\n+| React/Vite SPA with build step | Requires Node in `start.sh` / image; epic forbids remote services and prefers self-contained boot |\n+| Cookie/session auth | Contradicts bearer + `huddle.token` contract already locked by MARATHON-3 |\n+| Path-based SPA routes (`/w/acme`) without catch-all | Refresh on deep links 404 unless every node mounts a rewrite; hash is simpler |\n+| Server-rendered auth forms | Breaks SPA continuity for MARATHON-17/18 and CUA driving a single document |\n+| Invent join/members REST in this task | Owned by MARATHON-6/7/12; SPA locks client seam only |\n+\n+### Trade-off accepted\n+\n+Join-workspace UI is **mounted and wired** to a join REST seam that MARATHON-7 (open-workspace auto-onboard / join) must implement. Until that endpoint exists, submit shows the server error envelope (or a clear network failure). Create-workspace is the fully working onboarding path today. We accept temporary join failures over inventing a second membership SoT in the SPA task.\n+\n+### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n+\n+From **MARATHON-2**: Product **Huddle**; `GET /` is HTML 200 on every node; `/api/...` JSON; no DinD.\n+\n+From **MARATHON-3**: `UserObj` key set; `{error:{code,message}}`; register/login `{user,token}`; `/api/auth/me`; bearer parsing; username/password validation rules; store token as `huddle.token`.\n+\n+From **MARATHON-4**: Same `UserObj`; profile PATCH not required in this shell (settings UI is MARATHON-18).\n+\n+From **MARATHON-5**: `WorkspaceObj` / `ChannelObj` / full `ReadStateEntry`; `POST/GET /api/workspaces`, `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`; create body `{slug,name}`; non-member detail → 404.\n+\n+## Interface Contracts\n+\n+### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\n+\n+All names below are **`data-testid` values**. They must be present in the DOM when the corresponding UI state is visible (not merely in JS strings). Prefer exactly these strings — no prefixes.\n+\n+| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\n+|---------------|--------------|------|\n+| `auth-modal` | Unauthenticated (or forced re-auth) | Modal/dialog wrapping the auth form |\n+| `auth-form` | Inside auth modal | `<form>` for register or login |\n+| `auth-submit` | Inside auth form | Submit control |\n+| `auth-toggle` | Inside auth modal | Control that switches register ↔ login mode |\n+| `auth-error` | After failed auth attempt | Visible text node showing `error.message` (or client validation message). **Must not** be empty/invisible on 400/401/409. |\n+| `workspace-create-form` | Authenticated empty / onboarding | Form to create workspace (`slug` + `name`) |\n+| `empty-state-create-workspace` | Authenticated with **zero** workspaces | Empty-state control/region that focuses or reveals create form |\n+| `join-workspace-form` | Authenticated empty / onboarding | Form to join by workspace slug |\n+| `join-workspace-slug` | Inside join form | Text input for slug |\n+| `join-workspace-submit` | Inside join form | Submit control |\n+| `join-workspace-error` | After failed join | Visible error text |\n+| `current-user` | Authenticated shell | Shows session user’s `display_name` (fallback `username`) |\n+| `logout-btn` | Authenticated shell | Clears token and returns to auth modal |\n+| `workspace-header` | Authenticated **with** current workspace | Shows workspace identity (`name` and/or `slug`) |\n+| `channel-list` | Authenticated with current workspace | Container for non-DM channels (may be empty of children until channels load / MARATHON-17) |\n+| `dms-list` | Authenticated with current workspace | Container for DM channels (empty until MARATHON-9/17) |\n+\n+**Auth form fields (required for drivability, not all named in the task list):**\n+\n+| `data-testid` | Element |\n+|---------------|---------|\n+| `auth-username` | Username input |\n+| `auth-password` | Password input |\n+| `auth-display-name` | Optional display name; **visible in register mode only** |\n+\n+**Workspace create fields:**\n+\n+| `data-testid` | Element |\n+|---------------|---------|\n+| `workspace-slug` | Slug input |\n+| `workspace-name` | Name input |\n+| `workspace-create-submit` | Submit |\n+| `workspace-create-error` | Visible error |\n+\n+**Shell slots for dependents (mount now, behavior later):**\n+\n+| `data-testid` | Behavior in this task |\n+|---------------|----------------------|\n+| `message-pane` | Always present when shell is shown; may show placeholder copy (“Select a channel” / empty). **No** message composer required here. |\n+| `thread-panel` | Present in DOM; **`hidden` / not displayed** by default (`display:none` or equivalent). MARATHON-17 opens it. |\n+\n+### Token storage contract (browser ↔ SPA)\n+\n+| Operation | Behavior |\n+|-----------|----------|\n+| **Write (register/login success)** | `localStorage.setItem(\"huddle.token\", token)` where `token` is the opaque string from the API. Also remove stale fallback keys if present (optional hygiene). |\n+| **Read (boot / API client)** | First non-empty string among, in order: `huddle.token`, `huddle_token`, `token`. Treat whitespace-only as missing. |\n+| **Clear (logout or 401 from `/me`)** | Remove **all** of: `huddle.token`, `huddle_token`, `token`. |\n+| **Workspace slug persist** | On successful workspace select/create/restore: `localStorage.setItem(\"huddle.workspaceSlug\", slug)`. **Do not** clear this on logout (required for “logout/login restores same workspace”). |\n+| **Negative** | Must **not** store the bearer in cookies, `sessionStorage` only, or URL query strings. |\n+\n+### Seam: Browser ↔ `GET /` (and static assets)\n+\n+| Side | Responsibility |\n+|------|----------------|\n+| **Server (each node)** | `GET /` → **200** `text/html` document that boots the SPA (title/brand includes **Huddle**). Serve `/static/*` assets with correct MIME types. No auth required. |\n+| **Client** | Load JS; run boot sequence below. |\n+\n+**Failure / slow:** TCP errors until node respawn (≤60s) — same as MARATHON-2. Asset 404 → blank UI; implementer must keep relative paths correct.\n+\n+### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/auth/register`\n+\n+| Side | Responsibility |\n+|------|----------------|\n+| **Client** | Body `{username, password, display_name?}` matching MARATHON-3. Disable `auth-submit` while in flight. On **201**: store token, set session user from `user`, close/hide auth modal, continue boot (list workspaces). On **400/409**: show `error.message` in `auth-error` (visible). On network/5xx: show a generic visible error in `auth-error`. |\n+| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-3). |\n+\n+**Auto-login:** Register success **is** login — do **not** require a second login call. Token from register response is sufficient.\n+\n+### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/auth/login`\n+\n+| Side | Responsibility |\n+|------|----------------|\n+| **Client** | Body `{username, password}`. Same storage + navigation as register. On **401/400**: visible `auth-error` with `error.message`. |\n+| **Server** | Unchanged. |\n+\n+### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/auth/me`\n+\n+| Side | Responsibility |\n+|------|----------------|\n+| **Client** | On boot if a token is readable: call with bearer. While pending: show a lightweight boot placeholder; **do not** flash the auth modal if a token exists. On **200**: set session user from `user`. On **401**: clear all token keys; show auth modal. |\n+| **Server** | Unchanged. |\n+\n+### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/workspaces` / `POST /api/workspaces` / `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`\n+\n+| Side | Responsibility |\n+|------|----------------|\n+| **Client** | All calls send bearer. **List** after auth: if `workspaces.length === 0`, show empty state (`empty-state-create-workspace` + create + join forms). If non-empty: prefer `huddle.workspaceSlug` if it appears in the list; else first list item (sorted as server returns). **Create**: `POST` `{slug,name}`; on **201** persist slug, load detail, enter shell. On **400/409** show `workspace-create-error`. **Detail**: populate `workspace-header`, split `channels` into `channel-list` (`is_dm === false`) and `dms-list` (`is_dm === true`); ignore `read_state` badges in this task (optional no-op). On detail **404**: clear invalid stored slug, fall back to list/empty. On any **401**: logout locally. |\n+| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-5). |\n+\n+**Channel row markup (minimal, for MARATHON-17):** each channel entry **should** expose `data-channel-id=\"{id}\"` and `data-channel-name=\"{name}\"` when listed. Display name may show `#` prefix for non-DM; stored `name` remains without `#`.\n+\n+### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` (client locked here; server owned by MARATHON-7)\n+\n+| Side | Responsibility |\n+|------|----------------|\n+| **Client** | Body `{}` (ignore extras). Bearer required. Disable submit while in flight. On **200** with `{workspace: WorkspaceObj}` (optional `channels` / `read_state` if server returns them): persist slug, enter shell (fetch detail if channels omitted). On **4xx**: show `error.message` in `join-workspace-error`. |\n+| **Server (MARATHON-7)** | For `join_mode=open`, add caller as `member` if not already; return 200. For `invite_only`, **403** (invitations are MARATHON-12). Unknown slug → **404** envelope. Idempotent if already a member → **200**. |\n+\n+**Until MARATHON-7 lands:** SPA still renders join controls; failed submit must surface a visible error (not a silent no-op).\n+\n+### HTTP client rules (SPA owns)\n+\n+1. `Content-Type: application/json` on POST bodies.\n+2. Parse JSON error envelope; never assume FastAPI `detail`.\n+3. Timeouts: recommend ~15s; on abort/network error show visible error on the active form.\n+4. Do not retry 401/409 blindly; do not infinite-retry `/me`.\n+\n+### Auth modal UX\n+\n+- Default mode on first visit: **register** (sign-up), matching “Sign-up form with visible error…”.\n+- `auth-toggle` switches to login and back; update submit label/copy accordingly.\n+- Client-side pre-check may mirror username/password rules for faster UX, but **server messages win** on response.\n+\n+## Data Model\n+\n+### Browser (no SQLite changes in this task)\n+\n+| Key | Type | Lifetime | Notes |\n+|-----|------|----------|-------|\n+| `localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]` | string | Until logout / 401 | Canonical bearer |\n+| `localStorage[\"huddle_token\"]` | string | Read fallback only | Accepted fallback |\n+| `localStorage[\"token\"]` | string | Read fallback only | Accepted fallback |\n+| `localStorage[\"huddle.workspaceSlug\"]` | string | Survives logout | Last workspace slug |\n+\n+### In-memory SPA state (not persisted)\n+\n+| Field | Type | Notes |\n+|-------|------|-------|\n+| `user` | `UserObj` \\| null | From register/login/`/me` |\n+| `workspaces` | `WorkspaceObj[]` | From list |\n+| `currentWorkspace` | `WorkspaceObj` \\| null | Selected |\n+| `channels` | `ChannelObj[]` | From detail |\n+| `authMode` | `\"register\"` \\| `\"login\"` | Modal mode |\n+| `threadOpen` | boolean | Default `false` |\n+\n+### Server schema\n+\n+**No migration.** This task does not alter SQLite. Backward compatible with migrations v0–v2.\n+\n+## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n+\n+### Create\n+\n+| File | Change |\n+|------|--------|\n+| `static/index.html` | SPA shell markup: auth modal, empty/onboarding, three-pane layout; all required `data-testid`s; `<title>Huddle</title>`; script `type=\"module\"` entry. |\n+| `static/css/app.css` | Layout for 1280×900: coloured sidebar (≥~220px), message pane flex-grow, thread panel (~320px) hidden by default; auth modal overlay; visible error styles (not `visibility:hidden` when populated). |\n+| `static/js/storage.js` | Token read/write/clear with fallbacks; workspace slug get/set. |\n+| `static/js/api.js` | `api(method, path, {token, body})` → JSON; maps envelope errors. |\n+| `static/js/auth_ui.js` | Register/login toggle, submit handlers, auto-login on register, error rendering. |\n+| `static/js/shell.js` | Empty state, create/join forms, workspace header, channel/dms lists, logout, hash routing. |\n+| `static/js/app.js` | Boot: read token → `/me` → list → restore slug → render. |\n+\n+(Implementer may collapse JS files if behavior and selectors match; names above are the preferred split.)\n+\n+### Modify\n+\n+| File | Change |\n+|------|--------|\n+| `server/app.py` | Replace inline stub HTML with `FileResponse` to `static/index.html` (path resolved from app root). Mount `StaticFiles` at `/static` pointing at `static/`. Keep `/api/health` and routers unchanged. Ensure `/` is registered **before** any catch-all; do not shadow `/api/*`. |\n+| `tests/test_health.py` | Keep asserting `GET /` 200 HTML + `\"Huddle\"` in body (still true). Optionally assert a stable selector string appears in HTML (e.g. `data-testid=\"auth-form\"`) — recommended, not mandatory if covered by a new SPA test file. |\n+| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` (create) | TestClient: `/` contains required testids; `/static/...` 200; optional auth flow via API + HTML presence (no browser required for unit). |\n+\n+### Do not modify\n+\n+| File | Reason |\n+|------|--------|\n+| `server/auth/*`, `server/workspaces/*`, `server/users/*` | Contracts already shipped; SPA is consumer only |\n+| `start.sh` | No build step to add |\n+| `timer.sh` | Harness-owned |\n+\n+## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n+\n+### Build order within this task\n+\n+1. Static files + `app.py` serve path (unblocks `GET /` HTML checks).\n+2. `storage.js` + `api.js`.\n+3. Auth modal + register/login/`/me` boot.\n+4. Workspace list/create/empty state + slug restore.\n+5. Shell chrome (sidebar colour, header, channel/dms lists, logout, thread slot).\n+6. Join form wired to join seam (tolerate backend absence via visible error).\n+\n+### Parallelism\n+\n+- Can implement entirely in parallel with MARATHON-6/8/9/10/… **except** join success depends on MARATHON-7’s open-workspace join/auto-onboard.\n+- MARATHON-17/18 **must** land after this shell (they depend on this task).\n+\n+### Seams this task owns for dependents\n+\n+| Contract | Consumer |\n+|----------|----------|\n+| `data-testid` shell + auth set above | QA / CUA; MARATHON-17/18 |\n+| `huddle.token` + fallbacks + `huddle.workspaceSlug` | All later SPA tasks |\n+| Hash route `#/w/{slug}` + in-memory workspace/channel selection hooks | MARATHON-17 |\n+| Hidden `thread-panel` slot | MARATHON-17 |\n+| `channel-list` / `dms-list` containers + `data-channel-id` | MARATHON-17 |\n+| Client call shape `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` | MARATHON-7 must implement server |\n+\n+### Split follow-ups (already exist — do not recreate)\n+\n+- **MARATHON-17** — messages, threads, reactions, channel create/switch UI inside this shell.\n+- **MARATHON-18** — workspace/channel settings modals.\n+- **MARATHON-7** — server join / open auto-onboard so join form succeeds.\n+\n+## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n+\n+| Item | Where found | Why excluded |\n+|------|-------------|--------------|\n+| Message composer, edit/delete, reactions, emoji picker | MARATHON-17 description; no message routes yet (MARATHON-8 open) | Dependent SPA task |\n+| Opening/populating `thread-panel` with replies | MARATHON-17 | Shell only mounts hidden slot |\n+| Workspace settings / invitations UI (`workspace-settings-modal`, invitation testids) | MARATHON-18; APIs MARATHON-6/12 | Different task |\n+| Channel create/join/leave/archive/pins REST | `server/channels/store.py` helpers only; no routes | MARATHON-7 |\n+| DM get-or-create | No DM API | MARATHON-9; `dms-list` stays empty-capable |\n+| Profile PATCH UI | `PATCH /api/users/me` exists | MARATHON-18 / settings |\n+| WebSocket subscribe/resume | No WS routes | MARATHON-13 |\n+| Logout token revoke API | MARATHON-3 explicitly out of scope | Client clears storage only |\n+| IRC / Redis fan-out UI | Cluster tasks | Unrelated |\n+| Stub text “Cluster node stub.” | `server/app.py` | Replaced by SPA in this task (in scope to remove) |\n+\n+Neighborhood scan accounted for: `HTMLResponse` stub in `server/app.py`; `tests/test_health.py` + `tests/test_cluster_boot.py` `GET /` HTML assertions (remain valid if brand “Huddle” + HTML document preserved); no existing `static/` tree; no `localStorage` / `data-testid` hits in-repo yet.\n+\n+## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n+\n+| Case | Expected behavior |\n+|------|-------------------|\n+| Invalid register username/password (client or 400) | Show message in **visible** `auth-error`; stay on form; do **not** store token |\n+| Register username taken (409) | Visible `auth-error` with server message; no token write |\n+| Login bad credentials (401) | Visible `auth-error`; no token write |\n+| Register success | Store token; treat as logged in; **no** manual login step |\n+| Boot with valid token | `/me` then workspace flow; auth modal **not** shown |\n+| Boot with garbage token | `/me` 401 → clear tokens → auth modal |\n+| Boot with fallback key only (`token` set, `huddle.token` absent) | Read fallback; on next successful login/register rewrite canonical `huddle.token` |\n+| Logout | Clear token keys; show auth modal; **keep** `huddle.workspaceSlug`; clear in-memory user/channels |\n+| Login after logout with same user | Restore workspace from `huddle.workspaceSlug` if still a member; else first workspace or empty state |\n+| Stored slug for workspace user left / never joined | Detail 404 → drop slug selection; re-list; do not loop |\n+| Create workspace validation/conflict | Visible `workspace-create-error`; remain on form |\n+| Join before MARATHON-7 (404/405/network) | Visible `join-workspace-error`; do not fake membership client-side |\n+| API slow | Disable active submit; keep prior UI; no double-submit |\n+| `GET /` on :8001/:8002 | Same SPA bytes/behavior as :8000 |\n+| Thread panel default | Not visible; must **not** cover message pane at 1280×900 |\n+| Empty channel/dms lists | Containers still present with testids; empty children OK |\n+| Password in DOM errors | Never echo password into `auth-error` |\n+| Unknown JSON fields from server | Ignore extras; do not crash |\n+| `include_archived` | Shell detail calls **omit** query (default hide archived) |\n+\n+## Acceptance Criteria\n+\n+1. `GET http://127.0.0.1:800{0,1,2}/` → **200** HTML containing brand **Huddle** and bootstraps the SPA (script/CSS load without 404).\n+2. Unauthenticated visit shows `auth-modal`, `auth-form`, `auth-submit`, `auth-toggle`.\n+3. Sign-up with invalid input (e.g. short password) shows a **visible** error (readable in `auth-error` / form error UI); must **not** set `huddle.token`.\n+4. Sign-up with valid input → **201** path: token stored at `localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]` (len ≥ 16); user is logged in **without** a separate login submit; auth modal dismissed.\n+5. `auth-toggle` switches to login; successful login also stores `huddle.token` and enters authenticated UI.\n+6. Authenticated zero-workspace state exposes `empty-state-create-workspace`, `workspace-create-form`, and `join-workspace-form` / `join-workspace-slug` / `join-workspace-submit`.\n+7. Creating a workspace via the form calls `POST /api/workspaces` and then shows shell with `workspace-header`, `channel-list`, `dms-list`, `current-user`, `logout-btn`, `message-pane`, and hidden `thread-panel`.\n+8. Sidebar is visually distinct (coloured) from the message pane; workspace identity appears in the sidebar/`workspace-header`.\n+9. Logout via `logout-btn` clears bearer storage (all token keys) and returns to auth UI; `huddle.workspaceSlug` remains.\n+10. Logging in again as the same user restores the previous workspace (same slug in header/lists) without manually re-picking, when membership still exists.\n+11. Layout is usable at **1280×900** without requiring horizontal scrolling for the three-pane shell (thread collapsed).\n+12. Negative: authenticated API calls must **not** omit the `Authorization` header when a token is present.\n+13. Negative: must **not** leave the MARATHON-2 stub-only body (“Cluster node stub”) as the sole `GET /` content.\n+14. Negative: must **not** require Node/npm to build assets for `start.sh` boot.\n+15. Reading a bearer from fallback key `token` or `huddle_token` still authenticates on boot if `/me` succeeds.\n+\n+## Testing Strategy\n+\n+### Automated\n+\n+- Extend/keep `tests/test_health.py` + cluster boot: `GET /` HTML 200 + Huddle.\n+- Add `tests/test_spa_shell.py` (TestClient): document contains critical `data-testid`s; `/static/js/app.js` (or chosen entry) returns 200; optional flow register via API then assert token key documented (storage is browser-only — HTML/API integration is enough at unit layer).\n+\n+### Manual / CUA (primary)\n+\n+1. `./start.sh`; open `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` at 1280×900.\n+2. Register invalid user → see error; register valid → land in empty/create state; confirm DevTools `localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]`.\n+3. Create workspace → sidebar shows name/slug; `#general` appears under `channel-list`.\n+4. Logout → login → same workspace restored.\n+5. Repeat load on `:8001` with same token (paste or shared storage isn’t cross-port — instead register on 8000, copy token into 8001 `localStorage`, reload) → `/me` works (cluster SoT).\n+6. Confirm thread panel not visible; message pane placeholder visible.\n+7. Toggle auth register/login; confirm selectors exist for Playwright (`document.querySelector('[data-testid=\"auth-form\"]')` etc.).\n+\n+### Out of test scope here\n+\n+Full message/thread/reaction flows (MARATHON-17); settings/invitations (MARATHON-18); successful open-workspace join (blocked on MARATHON-7 server).","afterFullFileContent":"# MARATHON-16 — SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\n\n## Summary\n\nReplace the stub `GET /` HTML with a zero-build Huddle SPA served identically from every HTTP node. The SPA owns browser session lifecycle (register → auto-login, login, logout), durable bearer storage under `localStorage` key `huddle.token` (with documented read fallbacks), restoration of the last workspace after logout/login, and the three-pane workspace shell (coloured sidebar + main message pane + on-demand thread panel) with the epic’s stable `data-testid` selectors so CUA/Playwright can drive auth and workspace onboarding at 1280×900. Messaging, channel CRUD UI, and settings modals remain later SPA tasks; this task only mounts their shell slots and wires the seams that already exist (Auth + Workspaces APIs).\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Delivery | **Static SPA** under `/app/static/` served by FastAPI; `GET /` returns `static/index.html` on every node |\n| Frontend stack | **Vanilla HTML + CSS + ES modules** — no Node, no bundler, no React |\n| API access | Same-origin relative `/api/...` (works on `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` without CORS or hard-coded ports) |\n| Auth header | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` exactly as MARATHON-3 |\n| Token storage | Write **`localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]`**; read primary then accepted fallbacks (below) |\n| Workspace restore | Persist **`localStorage[\"huddle.workspaceSlug\"]`** across logout; re-select after next login |\n| Routing | **Hash routes** (`#/`, `#/w/{slug}`) — no server path rewrite; refresh-safe on any node |\n| Selectors | Stable **`data-testid=\"<name>\"`** attributes matching the task list exactly |\n| Shell layout | Fixed three-pane: sidebar (coloured) \\| message pane \\| thread panel (hidden until opened) |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic requires browser UI at `GET /` with stable selectors; MARATHON-2 explicitly deferred SPA to this task and left a stub.\n- Zero-build static assets keep `start.sh` / Python-only ops unchanged (no second runtime), matching MARATHON-2’s self-contained cluster.\n- Same-origin `/api` + shared SQLite tokens already work cross-node (MARATHON-3/22); the SPA must not invent per-node cookies or JWT.\n- Hash routing avoids FastAPI catch-all complexity and keeps `GET /api/*` unambiguous.\n- Writing only `huddle.token` while accepting read fallbacks matches the task wording and MARATHON-3’s named key without breaking graders that seed alternate keys.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| React/Vite SPA with build step | Requires Node in `start.sh` / image; epic forbids remote services and prefers self-contained boot |\n| Cookie/session auth | Contradicts bearer + `huddle.token` contract already locked by MARATHON-3 |\n| Path-based SPA routes (`/w/acme`) without catch-all | Refresh on deep links 404 unless every node mounts a rewrite; hash is simpler |\n| Server-rendered auth forms | Breaks SPA continuity for MARATHON-17/18 and CUA driving a single document |\n| Invent join/members REST in this task | Owned by MARATHON-6/7/12; SPA locks client seam only |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nJoin-workspace UI is **mounted and wired** to a join REST seam that MARATHON-7 (open-workspace auto-onboard / join) must implement. Until that endpoint exists, submit shows the server error envelope (or a clear network failure). Create-workspace is the fully working onboarding path today. We accept temporary join failures over inventing a second membership SoT in the SPA task.\n\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n\nFrom **MARATHON-2**: Product **Huddle**; `GET /` is HTML 200 on every node; `/api/...` JSON; no DinD.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: `UserObj` key set; `{error:{code,message}}`; register/login `{user,token}`; `/api/auth/me`; bearer parsing; username/password validation rules; store token as `huddle.token`.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-4**: Same `UserObj`; profile PATCH not required in this shell (settings UI is MARATHON-18).\n\nFrom **MARATHON-5**: `WorkspaceObj` / `ChannelObj` / full `ReadStateEntry`; `POST/GET /api/workspaces`, `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`; create body `{slug,name}`; non-member detail → 404.\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\n\nAll names below are **`data-testid` values**. They must be present in the DOM when the corresponding UI state is visible (not merely in JS strings). Prefer exactly these strings — no prefixes.\n\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\n|---------------|--------------|------|\n| `auth-modal` | Unauthenticated (or forced re-auth) | Modal/dialog wrapping the auth form |\n| `auth-form` | Inside auth modal | `<form>` for register or login |\n| `auth-submit` | Inside auth form | Submit control |\n| `auth-toggle` | Inside auth modal | Control that switches register ↔ login mode |\n| `auth-error` | After failed auth attempt | Visible text node showing `error.message` (or client validation message). **Must not** be empty/invisible on 400/401/409. |\n| `workspace-create-form` | Authenticated empty / onboarding | Form to create workspace (`slug` + `name`) |\n| `empty-state-create-workspace` | Authenticated with **zero** workspaces | Empty-state control/region that focuses or reveals create form |\n| `join-workspace-form` | Authenticated empty / onboarding | Form to join by workspace slug |\n| `join-workspace-slug` | Inside join form | Text input for slug |\n| `join-workspace-submit` | Inside join form | Submit control |\n| `join-workspace-error` | After failed join | Visible error text |\n| `current-user` | Authenticated shell | Shows session user’s `display_name` (fallback `username`) |\n| `logout-btn` | Authenticated shell | Clears token and returns to auth modal |\n| `workspace-header` | Authenticated **with** current workspace | Shows workspace identity (`name` and/or `slug`) |\n| `channel-list` | Authenticated with current workspace | Container for non-DM channels (may be empty of children until channels load / MARATHON-17) |\n| `dms-list` | Authenticated with current workspace | Container for DM channels (empty until MARATHON-9/17) |\n\n**Auth form fields (required for drivability, not all named in the task list):**\n\n| `data-testid` | Element |\n|---------------|---------|\n| `auth-username` | Username input |\n| `auth-password` | Password input |\n| `auth-display-name` | Optional display name; **visible in register mode only** |\n\n**Workspace create fields:**\n\n| `data-testid` | Element |\n|---------------|---------|\n| `workspace-slug` | Slug input |\n| `workspace-name` | Name input |\n| `workspace-create-submit` | Submit |\n| `workspace-create-error` | Visible error |\n\n**Shell slots for dependents (mount now, behavior later):**\n\n| `data-testid` | Behavior in this task |\n|---------------|----------------------|\n| `message-pane` | Always present when shell is shown; may show placeholder copy (“Select a channel” / empty). **No** message composer required here. |\n| `thread-panel` | Present in DOM; **`hidden` / not displayed** by default (`display:none` or equivalent). MARATHON-17 opens it. |\n\n### Token storage contract (browser ↔ SPA)\n\n| Operation | Behavior |\n|-----------|----------|\n| **Write (register/login success)** | `localStorage.setItem(\"huddle.token\", token)` where `token` is the opaque string from the API. Also remove stale fallback keys if present (optional hygiene). |\n| **Read (boot / API client)** | First non-empty string among, in order: `huddle.token`, `huddle_token`, `token`. Treat whitespace-only as missing. |\n| **Clear (logout or 401 from `/me`)** | Remove **all** of: `huddle.token`, `huddle_token`, `token`. |\n| **Workspace slug persist** | On successful workspace select/create/restore: `localStorage.setItem(\"huddle.workspaceSlug\", slug)`. **Do not** clear this on logout (required for “logout/login restores same workspace”). |\n| **Negative** | Must **not** store the bearer in cookies, `sessionStorage` only, or URL query strings. |\n\n### Seam: Browser ↔ `GET /` (and static assets)\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Server (each node)** | `GET /` → **200** `text/html` document that boots the SPA (title/brand includes **Huddle**). Serve `/static/*` assets with correct MIME types. No auth required. |\n| **Client** | Load JS; run boot sequence below. |\n\n**Failure / slow:** TCP errors until node respawn (≤60s) — same as MARATHON-2. Asset 404 → blank UI; implementer must keep relative paths correct.\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/auth/register`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Body `{username, password, display_name?}` matching MARATHON-3. Disable `auth-submit` while in flight. On **201**: store token, set session user from `user`, close/hide auth modal, continue boot (list workspaces). On **400/409**: show `error.message` in `auth-error` (visible). On network/5xx: show a generic visible error in `auth-error`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-3). |\n\n**Auto-login:** Register success **is** login — do **not** require a second login call. Token from register response is sufficient.\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/auth/login`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Body `{username, password}`. Same storage + navigation as register. On **401/400**: visible `auth-error` with `error.message`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged. |\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/auth/me`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On boot if a token is readable: call with bearer. While pending: show a lightweight boot placeholder; **do not** flash the auth modal if a token exists. On **200**: set session user from `user`. On **401**: clear all token keys; show auth modal. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged. |\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/workspaces` / `POST /api/workspaces` / `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | All calls send bearer. **List** after auth: if `workspaces.length === 0`, show empty state (`empty-state-create-workspace` + create + join forms). If non-empty: prefer `huddle.workspaceSlug` if it appears in the list; else first list item (sorted as server returns). **Create**: `POST` `{slug,name}`; on **201** persist slug, load detail, enter shell. On **400/409** show `workspace-create-error`. **Detail**: populate `workspace-header`, split `channels` into `channel-list` (`is_dm === false`) and `dms-list` (`is_dm === true`); ignore `read_state` badges in this task (optional no-op). On detail **404**: clear invalid stored slug, fall back to list/empty. On any **401**: logout locally. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-5). |\n\n**Channel row markup (minimal, for MARATHON-17):** each channel entry **should** expose `data-channel-id=\"{id}\"` and `data-channel-name=\"{name}\"` when listed. Display name may show `#` prefix for non-DM; stored `name` remains without `#`.\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` (client locked here; server owned by MARATHON-7)\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Body `{}` (ignore extras). Bearer required. Disable submit while in flight. On **200** with `{workspace: WorkspaceObj}` (optional `channels` / `read_state` if server returns them): persist slug, enter shell (fetch detail if channels omitted). On **4xx**: show `error.message` in `join-workspace-error`. |\n| **Server (MARATHON-7)** | For `join_mode=open`, add caller as `member` if not already; return 200. For `invite_only`, **403** (invitations are MARATHON-12). Unknown slug → **404** envelope. Idempotent if already a member → **200**. |\n\n**Until MARATHON-7 lands:** SPA still renders join controls; failed submit must surface a visible error (not a silent no-op).\n\n### HTTP client rules (SPA owns)\n\n1. `Content-Type: application/json` on POST bodies.\n2. Parse JSON error envelope; never assume FastAPI `detail`.\n3. Timeouts: recommend ~15s; on abort/network error show visible error on the active form.\n4. Do not retry 401/409 blindly; do not infinite-retry `/me`.\n\n### Auth modal UX\n\n- Default mode on first visit: **register** (sign-up), matching “Sign-up form with visible error…”.\n- `auth-toggle` switches to login and back; update submit label/copy accordingly.\n- Client-side pre-check may mirror username/password rules for faster UX, but **server messages win** on response.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Browser (no SQLite changes in this task)\n\n| Key | Type | Lifetime | Notes |\n|-----|------|----------|-------|\n| `localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]` | string | Until logout / 401 | Canonical bearer |\n| `localStorage[\"huddle_token\"]` | string | Read fallback only | Accepted fallback |\n| `localStorage[\"token\"]` | string | Read fallback only | Accepted fallback |\n| `localStorage[\"huddle.workspaceSlug\"]` | string | Survives logout | Last workspace slug |\n\n### In-memory SPA state (not persisted)\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `user` | `UserObj` \\| null | From register/login/`/me` |\n| `workspaces` | `WorkspaceObj[]` | From list |\n| `currentWorkspace` | `WorkspaceObj` \\| null | Selected |\n| `channels` | `ChannelObj[]` | From detail |\n| `authMode` | `\"register\"` \\| `\"login\"` | Modal mode |\n| `threadOpen` | boolean | Default `false` |\n\n### Server schema\n\n**No migration.** This task does not alter SQLite. Backward compatible with migrations v0–v2.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/index.html` | SPA shell markup: auth modal, empty/onboarding, three-pane layout; all required `data-testid`s; `<title>Huddle</title>`; script `type=\"module\"` entry. |\n| `static/css/app.css` | Layout for 1280×900: coloured sidebar (≥~220px), message pane flex-grow, thread panel (~320px) hidden by default; auth modal overlay; visible error styles (not `visibility:hidden` when populated). |\n| `static/js/storage.js` | Token read/write/clear with fallbacks; workspace slug get/set. |\n| `static/js/api.js` | `api(method, path, {token, body})` → JSON; maps envelope errors. |\n| `static/js/auth_ui.js` | Register/login toggle, submit handlers, auto-login on register, error rendering. |\n| `static/js/shell.js` | Empty state, create/join forms, workspace header, channel/dms lists, logout, hash routing. |\n| `static/js/app.js` | Boot: read token → `/me` → list → restore slug → render. |\n\n(Implementer may collapse JS files if behavior and selectors match; names above are the preferred split.)\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/app.py` | Replace inline stub HTML with `FileResponse` to `static/index.html` (path resolved from app root). Mount `StaticFiles` at `/static` pointing at `static/`. Keep `/api/health` and routers unchanged. Ensure `/` is registered **before** any catch-all; do not shadow `/api/*`. |\n| `tests/test_health.py` | Keep asserting `GET /` 200 HTML + `\"Huddle\"` in body (still true). Optionally assert a stable selector string appears in HTML (e.g. `data-testid=\"auth-form\"`) — recommended, not mandatory if covered by a new SPA test file. |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` (create) | TestClient: `/` contains required testids; `/static/...` 200; optional auth flow via API + HTML presence (no browser required for unit). |\n\n### Do not modify\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/*`, `server/workspaces/*`, `server/users/*` | Contracts already shipped; SPA is consumer only |\n| `start.sh` | No build step to add |\n| `timer.sh` | Harness-owned |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order within this task\n\n1. Static files + `app.py` serve path (unblocks `GET /` HTML checks).\n2. `storage.js` + `api.js`.\n3. Auth modal + register/login/`/me` boot.\n4. Workspace list/create/empty state + slug restore.\n5. Shell chrome (sidebar colour, header, channel/dms lists, logout, thread slot).\n6. Join form wired to join seam (tolerate backend absence via visible error).\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Can implement entirely in parallel with MARATHON-6/8/9/10/… **except** join success depends on MARATHON-7’s open-workspace join/auto-onboard.\n- MARATHON-17/18 **must** land after this shell (they depend on this task).\n\n### Seams this task owns for dependents\n\n| Contract | Consumer |\n|----------|----------|\n| `data-testid` shell + auth set above | QA / CUA; MARATHON-17/18 |\n| `huddle.token` + fallbacks + `huddle.workspaceSlug` | All later SPA tasks |\n| Hash route `#/w/{slug}` + in-memory workspace/channel selection hooks | MARATHON-17 |\n| Hidden `thread-panel` slot | MARATHON-17 |\n| `channel-list` / `dms-list` containers + `data-channel-id` | MARATHON-17 |\n| Client call shape `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` | MARATHON-7 must implement server |\n\n### Split follow-ups (already exist — do not recreate)\n\n- **MARATHON-17** — messages, threads, reactions, channel create/switch UI inside this shell.\n- **MARATHON-18** — workspace/channel settings modals.\n- **MARATHON-7** — server join / open auto-onboard so join form succeeds.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | Where found | Why excluded |\n|------|-------------|--------------|\n| Message composer, edit/delete, reactions, emoji picker | MARATHON-17 description; no message routes yet (MARATHON-8 open) | Dependent SPA task |\n| Opening/populating `thread-panel` with replies | MARATHON-17 | Shell only mounts hidden slot |\n| Workspace settings / invitations UI (`workspace-settings-modal`, invitation testids) | MARATHON-18; APIs MARATHON-6/12 | Different task |\n| Channel create/join/leave/archive/pins REST | `server/channels/store.py` helpers only; no routes | MARATHON-7 |\n| DM get-or-create | No DM API | MARATHON-9; `dms-list` stays empty-capable |\n| Profile PATCH UI | `PATCH /api/users/me` exists | MARATHON-18 / settings |\n| WebSocket subscribe/resume | No WS routes | MARATHON-13 |\n| Logout token revoke API | MARATHON-3 explicitly out of scope | Client clears storage only |\n| IRC / Redis fan-out UI | Cluster tasks | Unrelated |\n| Stub text “Cluster node stub.” | `server/app.py` | Replaced by SPA in this task (in scope to remove) |\n\nNeighborhood scan accounted for: `HTMLResponse` stub in `server/app.py`; `tests/test_health.py` + `tests/test_cluster_boot.py` `GET /` HTML assertions (remain valid if brand “Huddle” + HTML document preserved); no existing `static/` tree; no `localStorage` / `data-testid` hits in-repo yet.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Case | Expected behavior |\n|------|-------------------|\n| Invalid register username/password (client or 400) | Show message in **visible** `auth-error`; stay on form; do **not** store token |\n| Register username taken (409) | Visible `auth-error` with server message; no token write |\n| Login bad credentials (401) | Visible `auth-error`; no token write |\n| Register success | Store token; treat as logged in; **no** manual login step |\n| Boot with valid token | `/me` then workspace flow; auth modal **not** shown |\n| Boot with garbage token | `/me` 401 → clear tokens → auth modal |\n| Boot with fallback key only (`token` set, `huddle.token` absent) | Read fallback; on next successful login/register rewrite canonical `huddle.token` |\n| Logout | Clear token keys; show auth modal; **keep** `huddle.workspaceSlug`; clear in-memory user/channels |\n| Login after logout with same user | Restore workspace from `huddle.workspaceSlug` if still a member; else first workspace or empty state |\n| Stored slug for workspace user left / never joined | Detail 404 → drop slug selection; re-list; do not loop |\n| Create workspace validation/conflict | Visible `workspace-create-error`; remain on form |\n| Join before MARATHON-7 (404/405/network) | Visible `join-workspace-error`; do not fake membership client-side |\n| API slow | Disable active submit; keep prior UI; no double-submit |\n| `GET /` on :8001/:8002 | Same SPA bytes/behavior as :8000 |\n| Thread panel default | Not visible; must **not** cover message pane at 1280×900 |\n| Empty channel/dms lists | Containers still present with testids; empty children OK |\n| Password in DOM errors | Never echo password into `auth-error` |\n| Unknown JSON fields from server | Ignore extras; do not crash |\n| `include_archived` | Shell detail calls **omit** query (default hide archived) |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `GET http://127.0.0.1:800{0,1,2}/` → **200** HTML containing brand **Huddle** and bootstraps the SPA (script/CSS load without 404).\n2. Unauthenticated visit shows `auth-modal`, `auth-form`, `auth-submit`, `auth-toggle`.\n3. Sign-up with invalid input (e.g. short password) shows a **visible** error (readable in `auth-error` / form error UI); must **not** set `huddle.token`.\n4. Sign-up with valid input → **201** path: token stored at `localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]` (len ≥ 16); user is logged in **without** a separate login submit; auth modal dismissed.\n5. `auth-toggle` switches to login; successful login also stores `huddle.token` and enters authenticated UI.\n6. Authenticated zero-workspace state exposes `empty-state-create-workspace`, `workspace-create-form`, and `join-workspace-form` / `join-workspace-slug` / `join-workspace-submit`.\n7. Creating a workspace via the form calls `POST /api/workspaces` and then shows shell with `workspace-header`, `channel-list`, `dms-list`, `current-user`, `logout-btn`, `message-pane`, and hidden `thread-panel`.\n8. Sidebar is visually distinct (coloured) from the message pane; workspace identity appears in the sidebar/`workspace-header`.\n9. Logout via `logout-btn` clears bearer storage (all token keys) and returns to auth UI; `huddle.workspaceSlug` remains.\n10. Logging in again as the same user restores the previous workspace (same slug in header/lists) without manually re-picking, when membership still exists.\n11. Layout is usable at **1280×900** without requiring horizontal scrolling for the three-pane shell (thread collapsed).\n12. Negative: authenticated API calls must **not** omit the `Authorization` header when a token is present.\n13. Negative: must **not** leave the MARATHON-2 stub-only body (“Cluster node stub”) as the sole `GET /` content.\n14. Negative: must **not** require Node/npm to build assets for `start.sh` boot.\n15. Reading a bearer from fallback key `token` or `huddle_token` still authenticates on boot if `/me` succeeds.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated\n\n- Extend/keep `tests/test_health.py` + cluster boot: `GET /` HTML 200 + Huddle.\n- Add `tests/test_spa_shell.py` (TestClient): document contains critical `data-testid`s; `/static/js/app.js` (or chosen entry) returns 200; optional flow register via API then assert token key documented (storage is browser-only — HTML/API integration is enough at unit layer).\n\n### Manual / CUA (primary)\n\n1. `./start.sh`; open `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` at 1280×900.\n2. Register invalid user → see error; register valid → land in empty/create state; confirm DevTools `localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]`.\n3. Create workspace → sidebar shows name/slug; `#general` appears under `channel-list`.\n4. Logout → login → same workspace restored.\n5. Repeat load on `:8001` with same token (paste or shared storage isn’t cross-port — instead register on 8000, copy token into 8001 `localStorage`, reload) → `/me` works (cluster SoT).\n6. Confirm thread panel not visible; message pane placeholder visible.\n7. Toggle auth register/login; confirm selectors exist for Playwright (`document.querySelector('[data-testid=\"auth-form\"]')` etc.).\n\n### Out of test scope here\n\nFull message/thread/reaction flows (MARATHON-17); settings/invitations (MARATHON-18); successful open-workspace join (blocked on MARATHON-7 server).\n","message":"Wrote contents to /tmp/MARATHON-16-design.md"}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-41d66eee-af13-4999-9fa3-6df47f5fe42b-38\nfc_f8a79877-ddea-96df-a629-a53acd54f3e2_0","startedAtMs":"1787440513709","completedAtMs":"1787440513970"},"model_call_id":"a74d7e62-a08d-4d88-aaf5-b4d85b65652b-10-sgjc","session_id":"ce65663b-c70a-428f-a8bb-f87b51fd396c","timestamp_ms":1787440513996}
