m\",\"data\",\"list\",\"--output\",\"json\"],text=True)\n# might be huge - just get MARATHON-11 and 18 descriptions\nfor tid in [\"MARATHON-11\",\"MARATHON-18\",\"MARATHON-8\",\"MARATHON-16\"]:\n    r=subprocess.check_output([\"loom\",\"data\",\"show\",tid,\"--output\",\"json\"],text=True)\n    lines=r.strip().splitlines()\n    d=json.loads(\"\\n\".join(lines[next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(\"{\")):]))\n    print(\"=\"*60, tid)\n    print(\"title:\", d[\"title\"])\n    print(\"desc:\", d.get(\"description\"))\n    print(\"labels:\", d.get(\"labels\"))\n    notes=d.get(\"notes\") or \"\"\n    if notes: print(\"notes:\", notes[:1500])\nPY","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"============================================================ MARATHON-11\ntitle: Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\ndesc: GET /api/search?q=&workspace_id=. Slash commands as message body: /me, /shrug, /topic, /invite @user, /archive, /unarchive; unknown and /me without text → 400; //literal posts literally; side-effect cmds return 201 message:null + channel/invited_user. Mentions: @username, @group-handle, @channel, @here rules per spec; no self mention_count. GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read for read_state; never move cursor backwards; workspace detail embeds same shape.\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\n============================================================ MARATHON-18\ntitle: SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\ndesc: Workspace settings modal: tabs general/members/invitations; name/join_mode; member rows with role-badge/role-select; create invitation form and list with invitation-code. Channel settings: members list/add, topic, archive/unarchive. DOM ids: channel-settings-modal, workspace-settings-modal, create-invitation-form. All settings-* and invitation-* testids from frontend hooks.\nlabels: ['architect', 'frontend']\n============================================================ MARATHON-8\ntitle: Messages, threads, reactions REST API\ndesc: Note: depends on channels task. POST channels/{id}/messages {body,parent_id?,file_ids?,blocks?}; empty body 400; MessageObj with author, reply_count, edited_at, files, reactions, mentions. GET messages newest-first with limit/before. PATCH author-only sets edited_at; edit deleted → 409. DELETE author or workspace owner, idempotent 200 {deleted:true}. GET messages/{parent_id}/replies oldest-first. Reactions POST/DELETE idempotent per (user,emoji) return {reactions}.\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\n============================================================ MARATHON-16\ntitle: SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\ndesc: Serve SPA from GET / on any node. Sign-up form with visible error on invalid input; auto-login on success. Logout/login restores same workspace. Store bearer in localStorage huddle.token (or accepted fallbacks). Three-pane layout shell: coloured sidebar + message pane + on-demand thread panel. Workspace identity in sidebar. Stable selectors: auth-form, auth-submit, auth-toggle, auth-modal, workspace-create-form, empty-state-create-workspace, join-workspace-*, current-user, logout-btn, workspace-header, channel-list, dms-list. Drivable at 1280x900.\nlabels: ['frontend']\nnotes: IMPL: Zero-build SPA at GET / (static/). Token write huddle.token; read fallbacks huddle_token/token. Workspace restore via huddle.workspaceSlug across logout. Join form POSTs /api/workspaces/{slug}/join (server still MARATHON-7). Verified via pytest + Playwright at 1280x900 (register/login/create/logout/restore; thread panel hidden).\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-22T23:49:37.002Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-22T23:49:37.021Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-22T23:49:37.031Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-22T23:49:37.041Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing em