{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-9944f4bc-8adb-46d7-97f2-f04e248656c0-29\nfc_32ed18f3-bd12-9113-bb58-2ac9817456c9_2","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"# Extract M3 conventions for status codes and envelopes; M5 for patterns\npython3 <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess,re\ndef show(id):\n    out=subprocess.check_output([\"loom\",\"data\",\"show\",id,\"--output\",\"json\"],stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,text=True)\n    return json.loads(out[out.find(\"{\"):])\nfor id in [\"MARATHON-3\",\"MARATHON-5\"]:\n    d=show(id)\n    design=d[\"design\"]\n    # print summary + technical approach first part\n    m=re.search(r\"## Summary.*?(?=## Interface)\", design, re.S)\n    print(\"=\"*40, id)\n    if m: print(m.group(0)[:2500])\n    # error codes table\n    m=re.search(r\"Error code.*?\\n\\n\", design, re.S|re.I)\nPY\n# list server directory structure for neighborhood scan\nls -la /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/\nls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/messages/\nls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/channels/\nls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/tests/\n","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-9944f4bc-8adb-46d7-97f2-f04e248656c0-29\nfc_32ed18f3-bd12-9113-bb58-2ac9817456c9_2","simpleCommands":["python3","ls","ls","ls","ls"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"python3","args":[],"fullText":"python3"},{"name":"ls","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-la"},{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/"}],"fullText":"ls -la /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/"},{"name":"ls","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/messages/"}],"fullText":"ls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/messages/"},{"name":"ls","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/channels/"}],"fullText":"ls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/channels/"},{"name":"ls","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/tests/"}],"fullText":"ls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/tests/"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"python3"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"M3/M5 summaries and directory scan","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"1a640bb2-8d05-4a48-8d50-08000443ede7","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"# Extract M3 conventions for status codes and envelopes; M5 for patterns\npython3 <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess,re\ndef show(id):\n    out=subprocess.check_output([\"loom\",\"data\",\"show\",id,\"--output\",\"json\"],stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,text=True)\n    return json.loads(out[out.find(\"{\"):])\nfor id in [\"MARATHON-3\",\"MARATHON-5\"]:\n    d=show(id)\n    design=d[\"design\"]\n    # print summary + technical approach first part\n    m=re.search(r\"## Summary.*?(?=## Interface)\", design, re.S)\n    print(\"=\"*40, id)\n    if m: print(m.group(0)[:2500])\n    # error codes table\n    m=re.search(r\"Error code.*?\\n\\n\", design, re.S|re.I)\nPY\n# list server directory structure for neighborhood scan\nls -la /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/\nls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/messages/\nls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/channels/\nls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/tests/\n","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"======================================== MARATHON-3\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the first product API surface for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, backed by durable users and bearer tokens in the shared SQLite database so any of the three HTTP nodes accepts the same credential. It locks the canonical `UserObj` JSON shape (consumed by Profiles, Workspaces, and the SPA), the error envelope convention for all later REST routes, and a reusable FastAPI auth dependency that every authenticated endpoint will import.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Durable auth store | **SQLite** at `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` (shared by all nodes) — tables `users` + `auth_tokens` |\n| Token transport | Opaque bearer string in `Authorization: Bearer <token>` |\n| Token persistence | Store **SHA-256 hex** of the token; return plaintext only in register/login responses |\n| Password storage | **stdlib `hashlib.scrypt`** (salt per user); never store plaintext |\n| User / token ids | Stable strings: **UUID4** hex/`str` for `users.id`; tokens identified by hash (no separate public token id) |\n| Route layout | FastAPI `APIRouter` in `server/auth/routes.py` mounted from `server/app.py` under `/api/auth` |\n| Auth dependency | `server/auth/deps.py::get_current_user` for `/me` and for MARATHON-4+ |\n| Schema evolution | Extend MARATHON-2 `schema_migrations`: apply version **1** (users + auth_tokens) idempotently on node lifespan |\n\n### Why\n\n- MARATHON-2 fixed SQLite as SoT and Redis as ephemeral fan-out only. Storing tokens in Redis would break “any node accepts the same token” after Redis `SIGKILL` and contradicts MARATHON-14. Shared SQLite is the only persistence already wired on every node.\n- Opaque bearer tokens match the epic (“REST + bearer auth”) and the SPA task (`localStorage` `huddle.token`) without JWT clock skew or shared signing secrets across processes.\n- Hashing stored tokens limits damage from a DB file read while still allowing constant-time lookup by hashing the presented bearer.\n- `scrypt` via stdlib avoids new native deps (bcrypt/argon2 wheels) on cold `pip install` in `start.sh`.\n- Establishing `UserObj` and the `{ \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\" } }` envelope here prevents Profiles/SPA from inventing competing shapes (MARATHON-2 deferred error envelopes to Auth).\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| JWT / signed tokens | Needs shared secret rotation; harder to revoke; no\n======================================== MARATHON-5\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the workspace tenancy root for Huddle: authenticated callers can create a workspace (unique kebab `slug`, display `name`, creator as `owner`, default `join_mode=open`), which atomically provisions the public `#general` channel and membership rows; list workspaces they own or belong to; and load a workspace by slug with the visible channel list plus embedded `read_state`. It locks `WorkspaceObj`, the initial `ChannelObj` shape used by later channel APIs, the SQLite schema for workspaces/members/channels, and the REST contracts the SPA shell (MARATHON-16) and members/channels tasks (MARATHON-6/7) consume.\n\n**Revision (needs-revision feedback):** `read_state` entries use the **full** `ReadStateEntry` shape shared with `GET /api/channels/{id}/read` (MARATHON-11): `{channel_id, last_read_seq, unread_count, mention_count}`. Empty `[]` until messages/read APIs write rows is fine; when entries are returned, all four fields are present (counts default to `0`). Query `include_archived` treats both literal `1` and `true` (case-insensitive) as “include archived.”\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite (MARATHON-2/3 SoT); **migration version 2** additive tables |\n| Route layout | FastAPI `APIRouter` prefix `/api/workspaces` in `server/workspaces/routes.py`, mounted from `server/app.py` |\n| Auth | Reuse `server.auth.deps.get_current_user`; all three endpoints require Bearer |\n| Identity | UUID4 strings for `workspaces.id`, `channels.id`, membership PKs |\n| `#general` | On create, insert a non-private, non-DM, non-archived channel with `name=\"general\"` (UI `#` is display-only); add creator as channel member |\n| Membership | Insert `workspace_members` row with `role=\"owner\"` in the same transaction as workspace create (MARATHON-6 owns member list/PATCH/transfer APIs but **needs these rows now** for list/detail authz) |\n| Private-channel filter | Detail omits channels where `is_private=1` and the caller has no `channel_members` row; public channels always listed (subject to archive filter) |\n| `read_state` | Embed `ReadStateEntry[]` for the caller with keys **`channel_id`, `last_read_seq`, `unread_count`, `mention_count`** — identical to MARATHON-11 `GET /api/channels/{id}/read` entry shape; return `[]` until rows exist; when mapping a row, missing/null counts → JSON `0` |\n| `include_archived` | **On** when query value is exactly `1` **or** case-insensitive `true`; otherwise of\ntotal 40\ndrwx------. 8 root root 4096 Aug 23 00:16 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 7 root root 4096 Aug 23 00:15 ..\n-rw-------. 1 root root   32 Aug 22 22:31 __init__.py\ndrwx------. 2 root root  126 Aug 22 23:55 __pycache__\n-rw-------. 1 root root 2569 Aug 23 00:16 app.py\ndrwx------. 3 root root  129 Aug 22 23:55 auth\ndrwx------. 3 root root   77 Aug 23 00:16 channels\n-rw-------. 1 root root 9221 Aug 23 00:16 db.py\n-rw-------. 1 root root 2059 Aug 22 23:11 errors.py\n-rw-------. 1 root root  581 Aug 22 23:11 events.py\ndrwx------. 2 root root   58 Aug 23 00:16 messages\n-rw-------. 1 root root 2342 Aug 22 22:31 settings.py\ndrwx------. 2 root root   42 Aug 22 23:11 users\ndrwx------. 3 root root   77 Aug 23 00:16 workspaces\n__init__.py\nroutes.py\nstore.py\n__init__.py\n__pycache__\nroutes.py\nstore.py\n__init__.py\ntest_auth.py\ntest_auth_cluster_token.py\ntest_auth_live.py\ntest_channels.py\ntest_cluster_boot.py\ntest_cluster_respawn.py\ntest_health.py\ntest_pins.py\ntest_profiles.py\ntest_spa_shell.py\ntest_workspace_members.py\ntest_workspaces.py\n","stderr":"","executionTime":175,"interleavedOutput"