l **member** required (public or private); then `assert_channel_writable`. Workspace owner without membership → **403** (same as pin).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":139,"content":"| **Client (SPA M17)** | Bearer; body `{body, parent_id?, file_ids?, blocks?}`; disable composer while in flight; on 201 append message / bump thread `reply_count`; on 400 show empty-message validation; on 423 show archived lock |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":156,"content":"- `parent_id` optional; if set: must exist, same `channel_id`, `deleted_at IS NULL`, and parent’s `parent_id IS NULL`; else **400**.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":157,"content":"- `file_ids` optional list of strings; default omit/`[]`. **Each** id must refer to a file owned by caller and not already attached (MARATHON-10). If files table/rows unavailable or any id fails → **400** `validation_error`. Empty list OK → `files: []`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":163,"content":"**Effects:** Insert row (`edited_at=null`, `deleted_at=null`); compute `mentions`; if `parent_id` set, child’s presence increases parent `reply_count` on subsequent reads; call `publish_message_created` after commit (no-op OK).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":179,"content":"Each element fully enriched (`author`, `reply_count`, `reactions`, `mentions`, `files`).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":185,"content":"| **Client** | Body `{body}`; show edited indicator from `edited_at`; on 409 treat as deleted |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":186,"content":"| **Server** | Author-only; not deleted; writable channel; set `body`, `edited_at=now`, re-resolve `mentions` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":192,"content":"- `deleted_at` set → **409** `conflict`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":210,"content":"- If already `deleted_at` set → still **200** `{\"deleted\": true}` (no-op).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":211,"content":"- Else set `deleted_at=now`; clear reaction rows for that message (so they “no longer count”); leave pin row if any (pin list uses tombstone mapping — see edge cases).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":218,"content":"| **Client (thread panel)** | Bearer; render oldest-first; bump parent reply badge from parent `reply_count` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":263,"content":"`messages(id, channel_id, author_id, body, parent_id, created_at, edited_at, deleted_at)` — already created in MARATHON-7 v3 + `idx_messages_channel_id`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":313,"content":"1. Soft-deleted messages have `deleted_at` non-null; excluded from history/reply lists.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":314,"content":"2. `reply_count` never includes deleted children.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":317,"content":"5. Pin routes continue to work; `get_message` / `row_to_message_obj` enrich reactions/mentions/files/reply_count for pin embeds too.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":333,"content":"| `server/messages/store.py` | Create/list/get with enrichment; soft delete; reply list; reaction insert/delete/aggregate; mention resolve helper; `row_to_message_obj` fills real `reply_count`/`reactions`/`mentions`/`files` (files empty until M10); keep `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` unchanged |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":338,"content":"| `tests/test_pins.py` | Only if enrichment changes assertions (prefer keep using `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`; update empty `reactions` expectations only if pins now return aggregates — still `[]` without reaction rows) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":383,"content":"- MARATHON-7 closed: v3 messages, pins, `assert_channel_writable`, channel membership matrix.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":414,"content":"| `server/channels/store.py` — `assert_channel_writable`, membership | **In scope** — reuse; no ChannelObj key changes |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":459,"content":"| Pin list after message soft-delete | Return pin entry with tombstone `MessageObj`: `body=\"\"`, `files=[]`, `reactions=[]`, `mentions=[]`, `reply_count` as computed; **or** skip pin — **prefer tombstone** so pin list length stable |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":465,"content":"1. `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages` `{body:\"hi\"}` as channel member → **201** `{message}` with exact `MessageObj` keys; `edited_at=null`; `parent_id=null`; `reply_count=0`; `reactions=[]`; `files=[]`; `mentions` reflects `@username` rules.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":466,"content":"2. Empty / whitespace body → **400** `validation_error`; message **not** inserted.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":468,"content":"4. Reply via `parent_id` → **201**; parent’s subsequent `reply_count` is 1; `GET /api/messages/{parent}/replies` → **200** `{replies:[…]}` oldest-first.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":469,"content":"5. `PATCH /api/messages/{id}` as author → **200**; `edited_at` set; non-author → **403**; after DELETE → PATCH **409**.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":483,"content":"- Thread create + replies ordering + `reply_count`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":484,"content":"- Edit sets `edited_at`; edit deleted → 409; delete idempotent; owner delete.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":42,"totalMatchedLines":42,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-c