nPY\n# also get notes via loom notes if available\nloom data show MARATHON-1 --output json > /tmp/epic.json\npython3 <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('/tmp/epic.json'))\nfor k,v in d.items():\n    if k!='dependents':\n        print(f'{k}: {repr(v)[:300]}')\nPY\nloom --help 2>&1 | head -80\nls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/\nls /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"MARATHON-2 status=closed has_design=True labels=[backend] Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis\nMARATHON-3 status=closed has_design=True labels=[backend] Auth API: register, login, me, bearer tokens\nMARATHON-5 status=closed has_design=True labels=[backend] Workspaces: create, list, detail, auto #general\nMARATHON-7 status=closed has_design=True labels=[backend] Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, pins\nMARATHON-8 status=review has_design=True labels=[architect,backend] Messages, threads, reactions REST API\nMARATHON-13 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,backend] WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\nMARATHON-14 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,backend] Cross-node fan-out and Redis-outage resilience\nMARATHON-4 status=closed has_design=True labels=[backend] Profiles API: UserObj get and patch me\nMARATHON-6 status=closed has_design=True labels=[backend] Workspace members, roles, ownership transfer\nMARATHON-11 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,backend] Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\nMARATHON-12 status=review has_design=True labels=[backend] User groups and workspace invitations\nMARATHON-15 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,backend] IRC gateway on :6667 with bidirectional bridge\nMARATHON-16 status=closed has_design=True labels=[frontend] SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\nMARATHON-17 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,frontend] SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\nMARATHON-19 status=closed has_design=False labels=[qa] Verify: cluster boot health Redis and stub GET /\nMARATHON-20 status=closed has_design=False labels=[qa] Verify: HTTP node and Redis SIGKILL respawn\nMARATHON-21 status=closed has_design=False labels=[qa] Verify: auth register login me envelopes\nMARATHON-22 status=closed has_design=False labels=[qa] Verify: auth token accepted on all HTTP nodes\nMARATHON-9 status=in_progress has_design=False labels=[architect,backend] DMs: get-or-create DM channel\nMARATHON-10 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,backend] Files: upload, metadata, download, attach\nMARATHON-18 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,frontend] SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\n---WITH DESIGNS---\nMARATHON-2 Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis\nMARATHON-3 Auth API: register, login, me, bearer tokens\nMARATHON-5 Workspaces: create, list, detail, auto #general\nMARATHON-7 Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, pins\nMARATHON-8 Messages, threads, reactions REST API\nMARATHON-4 Profiles API: UserObj get and patch me\nMARATHON-6 Workspace members, roles, ownership transfer\nMARATHON-12 User groups and workspace invitations\nMARATHON-16 SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\nid: 'MARATHON-1'\ntitle: 'Huddle: Slack-like team chat cluster'\nstatus: 'open'\npriority: 2\nissue_type: 'epic'\nowner: 'marathon-harness'\nhas_design: False\ncreated_at: '2026-08-22T22:16:35.53148094Z'\nupdated_at: '2026-08-22T22:16:35.53148094Z'\ncreated_by: 'marathon-harness'\ndescription: 'Build a self-contained Slack-like team chat at /app. Verifier runs /app/start.sh (foreground) which must keep serving while alive.\\n\\nExpose HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002, IRC on :6667, browser UI at GET /. Local Redis pub/sub on :6379. No remote services, no DinD, no Slack SDK.\\n\\nProduct\nloom - Agent Management CLI\n\nManage Claude Code agents working in parallel across workspace repos.\n\nGETTING STARTED\n  1. Select a FleetDB-backed workspace with registered repos.\n\n  2. Create tasks for agents to work on:\n     loom task create --title=\"Add login feature\" --type=feature --priority=2\n\n  3. Run agents:\n     loom plan falcon    # Creates design, sets status=review\n     loom lead           # Review and approve plans\n     loom task falcon    # Implements approved design\n\nKEY CONCEPTS\n  Workspaces   FleetDB-backed repo groups where agents work independently.\n\n  Agents       Claude processes that work on tasks:\n               - 'plan' agent: researches and creates designs\n               - 'task' agent: implements approved designs\n\n  FleetDB      Issue tracker. Tasks flow through states:\n               open → in_progress → review → open → closed\n\n  Auto Mode    --auto flag runs agents continuously, processing multiple\n               tasks until stopped (Ctrl+C) or idle timeout.\n\nCOMMANDS\n  plan         Run a planning agent (creates designs, marks for review)\n  task         Run an implementation agent (implements approved tasks)\n  lead         Interactive mode for reviewing plans and managing backlog\n  monitor      Dashboard showing agent status and task progress\n  recover      Recover agent from error state (clear stale locks, reset tasks)\n  push         Push worktree branches to target with AI conflict resolution\n  pull         Pull integration branch into worktrees with AI conflict resolution\n  sync         Full sync: push all completed work, then pull into all worktrees\n  reset        Hard reset worktrees to a specific branch\n  list         List all agents and their status\n\nGLOBAL FLAGS\n      --backend          AI backend CLI (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n\nENVIRONMENT VARIABLES\n  LOOM_DEFAULT_BRANCH    Default integration branch (default: main)\n  LOOM_BACKEND           AI backend CLI to use (default: codex)\n\nEXAMPLES\n  loom plan falcon              # Run planning agent in falcon worktree\n  loom task falcon --auto       # Continuous implementation mode\n  loom lead                     # Interactive backlog management\n  loom monitor                  # Watch agent progress\n  loom push --all               # Push all worktrees to main\n  loom pull --all               # Pull main into all worktrees\n  loom sync                     # Full sync: push all + pull all\n\nUsage:\n  loom [flags]\n  loom [command]\n\nAgent Commands:\n  agent           Run a custom agent with a user-defined prompt\n  daemon          Manage the agent supervisor daemon\n  lead            Run the interactive terminal-agent runtime\n  list            List all agents (worktrees)\n  plan            Run a planning agent\n  recover         Recover from agent error state\n  task            Run an implementation agent\n  usage           Display token usage and cost summaries\n  worker          Run a remote agent worker that connects to a control plane\n\nGit Operations:\n  pr              Create GitHub PR from worktree branch\n  pull            Pull branch into worktree\n  push            Push worktree branch to target branch\n  reset           Hard reset worktree to a specific branch\n  sync            Push completed work then pull latest into all worktrees\n\nConfiguration:\n  backend         Manage AI backends\ndata\nloom-prompts\nrequirements.txt\nserver\nstart.sh\nstatic\ntests\ntimer.sh\n__init__.py\n__pycache__\napp.py\nauth\nchannels\ndb.py\nerrors.py\nevents.py\nmessages\nsettings.py\nusers\nworkspaces\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T00:24:28.073Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T00:24:28.103Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":128,"interleavedOutput":"time=2026-08-23T00:24:28.073Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\nMARATHON-2 status=closed has_design=True labels=[backend] Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis\nMARATHON-3 status=closed has_design=True labels=[backend] Auth API: register, login, me, bearer tokens\nMARATHON-5 status=closed has_design=True labels=[backend] Workspaces: create, list, detail, auto #general\nMARATHON-7 status=closed has_design=True labels=[backend] Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, pins\nMARATHON-8 status=review has_design=True labels=[architect,backend] Messages, threads, reactions REST API\nMARATHON-13 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,backend] WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\nMARATHON-14 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,backend] Cross-node fan-out and Redis-outage resilience\nMARATHON-4 status=closed has_design=True labels=[backend] Profiles API: UserObj get and patch me\nMARATHON-6 status=closed has_design=True labels=[backend] Workspace members, roles, ownership transfer\nMARATHON-11 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,backend] Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\nMARATHON-12 status=review has_design=True labels=[backend] User groups and workspace invitations\nMARATHON-15 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,backend] IRC gateway on :6667 with bidirectional bridge\nMARATHON-16 status=closed has_design=True labels=[frontend] SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\nMARATHON-17 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,frontend] SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\nMARATHON-19 status=closed has_design=False labels=[qa] Verify: cluster boot health Redis and stub GET /\nMARATHON-20 status=closed has_design=False labels=[qa] Verify: HTTP node and Redis SIGKILL respawn\nMARATHON-21 status=closed has_design=False labels=[qa] Verify: auth register login me envelopes\nMARATHON-22 status=closed has_design=False labels=[qa] Verify: auth token accepted on all HTTP nodes\nMARATHON-9 status=in_progress has_design=False labels=[architect,backend] DMs: get-or-create DM channel\nMARATHON-10 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,backend] Files: upload, metadata, download, attach\nMARATHON-18 status=open has_design=False labels=[architect,frontend] SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\n---WITH DESIGNS---\nMARATHON-2 Scaffold cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis\nMARATHON-3 Auth API: register, login, me, bearer tokens\nMARATHON-5 Workspaces: create, list, detail, auto #general\nMARATHON-7 Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, pins\nMARATHON-8 Messages, threads, reactions REST API\nMARATHON-4 Profiles API: UserObj get and patch me\nMARATHON-6 Workspace members, roles, ownership transfer\nMARATHON-12 User groups and workspace invitations\nMARATHON-16 SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\ntime=2026-08-23T00:24:28.103Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\nid: 'MARATHON-1'\ntitle: 'Huddle: Slack-like team chat cluster'\nstatus: 'open'\npriority: 2\nissue_type: 'epic'\nowner: 'marathon-harness'\nhas_design: False\ncreated_at: '2026-08-22T22:16:35.53148094Z'\nupdated_at: '2026-08-22T22:16:35.53148094Z'\ncreated_by: 'marathon-harness'\ndescription: 'Build a self-contained Slack-like team chat at /app. Verifier runs /app/start.sh (foreground) which must keep serving while alive.\\n\\nExpose HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002, IRC on :6667, browser UI at GET /. Local Redis pub/sub on :6379. No remote services, no DinD, no Slack SDK.\\n\\nProduct\nloom - Agent Management CLI\n\nManage Claude Code agents working in parallel across workspace repos.\n\nGETTING STARTED\n  1. Select a FleetDB-backed workspace with registered repos.\n\n  2. Create tasks for agents to work on:\n     loom task create --title=\"Add login feature\" --type=feature --priority=2\n\n  3. Run agents:\n     loom plan falcon    # Creates design, sets status=review\n     loom lead           # Review and approve plans\n     loom task falcon    # Implements approved design\n\nKEY CONCEPTS\n  Workspaces   FleetDB-backed repo groups where agents work independently.\n\n  Agents       Claude processes that work on tasks:\n               - 'plan' agent: researches and creates designs\n               - 'task' agent: implements approved designs\n\n  FleetDB      Issue tracker. Tasks flow through states:\n               open → in_progress → review → open → closed\n\n  Auto Mode    --auto flag runs agents continuously, processing multiple\n               tasks until stopped (Ctrl+C) or idle timeout.\n\nCOMMANDS\n  plan         Run a planning agent (creates designs, marks for review)\n  task         Run an implementation agent (implements approved tasks)\n  lead         Interactive mode for reviewing plans and managing backlog\n  monitor      Dashboard showing agent status and task progress\n  recover      Recover agent from error state (clear stale locks, reset tasks)\n  push         Push worktree branches to target with AI conflict resolution\n  pull         Pull integration branch into worktrees with AI conflict resolution\n  sync         Full sync: push all completed work, then pull into all worktrees\n  reset        Hard reset worktrees to a specific branch\n  list         List all agents and their status\n\nGLOBAL FLAGS\n      --backend          AI backend CLI (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n\nENVIRONMENT VARIABLES\n  LOOM_DEFAULT_BRANCH    Default integration branch (default: main)\n  LOOM_BACKEND           AI backend CLI to use (default: codex)\n\nEXAMPLES\n  loom plan falcon              # Run planning agent in falcon worktree\n  loom task falcon --auto       # Continuous implementation mode\n  loom lead                     # Interactive backlog management\n  loom monitor                  # Watch agent progress\n  loom push --all               # Push all worktrees to main\n  loom pull --all               # Pull main into all worktrees\n  loom sync                     # Full sync: push all + pull all\n\nUsage:\n  loom [flags]\n  loom [command]\n\nAgent Commands:\n  agent           Run a custom agent with a user-defined prompt\n  daemon          Manage the agent supervisor daemon\n  lead            Run the interactive terminal-agent runtime\n  list            List all agents (worktrees)\n  plan            Run a planning agent\n  recover         Recover from agent error state\n  task            Run an implementation agent\n  usage           Display token usage and cost summaries\n  worker          Run a remote agent worker that connects to a control plane\n\nGit Operations:\n  pr              Create GitHub PR from worktree branch\n  pull            Pull branch into worktree\n  push            Push worktree branch to target branch\n  reset           Hard reset worktree to a specific branch\n  sync            Push completed work then pull latest into all worktrees\n\nConfiguration:\n  backend         Manage AI backends\ndata\nloom-prompts\nrequirements.txt\nserver\nstart.sh\nstatic\ntests\ntimer.sh\n__init__.py\n__pycache__\napp.py\nauth\nchannels\ndb.py\nerrors.py\nevents.py\nmessages\nsettings.py\nusers\nworkspaces\n","localExecutionTimeMs":86},"isBackground":false},"description":"List siblings and epic details"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-04c5c484-3a64-478a-a61e-86048a66388a-8\nfc_2e822c0b-dd1f-9ca6-9d92-f766c1518733_0","startedAtMs":"1787444668034","completedAtMs":"1787444668163"},"model_call_id":"b6dbef0b-e6fb-4ca9-8c38-d48246858510-3-tchm","session_id":"3f743427-f194-44bc-92dc-836b7b6940f7","timestamp_ms":1787444668184}
