embers.role='member'` (never owner/admin/guest). 4. At most one pin row per `message_id`. 5. `is_dm` channels are not creatable via `POST .../channels` (`is\n  eactions | MARATHON-8 | | Invitations / private invite redeem | MARATHON-12 | | DM get-or-create | MARATHON-9 | | Slash `/archive` `/topic` | MARATHON-11 (will call same store helpers) |  ## Sequencin\n  lient join path.  ### Declared dependents  - MARATHON-8 (messages), MARATHON-9 (DMs) block on this task.  ### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)  - Message CRUD / reactions / reply_count maintenan\n   → MARATHON-8. - `POST /api/dms` → MARATHON-9. - Private channel add-member / invitations → MARATHON-12 (+ optional channel invite API if still missin\n  eactions endpoints | `/api/messages/{id}/reactions` | MARATHON-8 | | `POST /api/dms` | — | MARATHON-9 | | Invitation redeem unlocking invite_only join | — | MARATHON-12; this task only 403s non-member\n  es public channel | **403** | | Member creates `is_private:true` | **403** | | Admin/owner creates private | **201**; creator is only initial channel member | | Topic length 250 OK; 251 → **400** | | \n  0** `{channel}` | | Leave `#general` | Allowed; channel remains | | Archive by admin | **403** | | Archive by owner | **200**; `is_archived=true` | | PATCH topic on archived | **423** `archived` | | P\n  **403** | | Workspace join open idempotent | **200**; single membership row | | DM channel create via this POST | Impossible (`is_dm` forced false) | | SQLite busy | busy_timeout; still fail closed af\n   member → **201** `{channel}` with `ChannelObj` keys; `topic` default `\"\"`; `is_dm=false`; creator in `channel_members`. 2. Duplicate channel name in workspace → **409** `conflict`. 3. Invalid kebab n\n  validation_error`. 4. Guest create → **403**; member create private → **403**; admin/owner create private → **201**. 5. `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` on open as non-member → **200** and subsequen\n  ate workspace; exercise create public/private + role matrix (seed guest/member/admin via SQL or members PATCH). - Workspace join open vs invite_only (PATCH join_mode as owner first). - Channel join au\n\n### SECTION: ## Summary\n## Summary\n\nThis task completes channel lifecycle for Huddle on top of the workspace tenancy shipped in MARATHON-5/6: authenticated callers can create public/private channels under a workspace slug, join and leave channels (with open-workspace auto-onboard and invite_only/guest/private gates), list channel members as `UserObj`, patch topic, archive/unarchive (owner-only), and pin/unpin messages. It also implements the SPA-locked workspace join seam (`POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join`) that MARATHON-16 already calls. It locks the `/api/channels/*` and pin REST contracts, introduces migration **v3** (`messages` minimal + `channel_pins`), and exports a shared **archived-write guard** (`423`) that MARATHON-8/11 must reuse.\n\n...(len 729 )\n\n### SECTION: ## Technical Approach\n## Technical Approach\n\n...(len 22 )\n\n### SECTION: ## Interface Contracts\n## Interface Contracts\n\n...(len 23 )\n\n### SECTION: ### Role / join capability matrix (normative)\n### Role / join capability matrix (normative)\n\n| Action | owner | admin | member | guest | non-member (open ws) | non-member (invite_only) |\n|--------|-------|-------|--------|-------|----------------------|---------------------------|\n| `POST .../workspaces/{slug}/join` | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | **200** add as `member` | **403** |\n| `POST .../workspaces/{slug}/channels` public | yes | yes | yes | **403** | **404** | **404** |\n| `POST .../channels` private (`is_private:true`) | yes | yes | **403** | **403** | **404** | **404** |\n| `POST /channels/{id}/join` public | yes | yes | yes | **403** | **200** + auto workspace `member` | **403** |\n| `POST /channels/{id}/join` private, not channel member | **403** | **403** | **403** | **403** | **403** (open) / **403** (invite_only) | **403** |\n| `POST /channels/{id}/join` private, already channel member | 200 | 200 | 200 | 200* | n/a | n/a |\n| `POST .../leave` | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | 200 idem | see edge cases | |\n| `PATCH` topic | channel member **or** workspace owner | same | same | same if channel member | — | — |\n| `POST archive/unarchive` | **yes** (workspace owner only) | **403** | **403** | **403** | **404** | **404** |\n\n\\* Guest who somehow has channel membership (seeded) may leave; guest **cannot** newly join public.\n\n...(len 1319 )\n\n### SECTION: ### Client slow/fail summary\n### Client slow/fail summary\n\n| Condition | Client behavior |\n|-----------|-----------------|\n| In flight | Disable create/join/topic/archive/pin controls; keep prior lists |\n| 401 | Re-auth (M16) |\n| 403 | Show `error.message`; do not optimistic-join |\n| 409 | Duplicate channel name inline validation |\n| 423 | Show archived/locked state; disable composers (M17/18) |\n| 404 | Treat channel/workspace inaccessible |\n| Network/5xx | Retry; do not assume membership/pin applied |\n\n...(len 479 )\n\n### SECTION: ## Data Model\n## Data Model\n\n...(len 14 )\n\n### SECTION: ### Schema change summary\n### Schema change summary\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| v3 new tables | **Yes** — additive |\n| No alters to v2 columns | **Yes** |\n\n...(len 154 )\n\n### SECTION: ## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n...(len 37 )\n\n### SECTION: ## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n...(len 35 )\n\n### SECTION: ## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages` and message list/edit/delete | future `server/messages/routes.py` CRUD | MARATHON-8 |\n| Reactions endpoints | `/api/messages/{id}/reactions` | MARATHON-8 |\n| `POST /api/dms` | — | MARATHON-9 |\n| Invitation redeem unlocking invite_only join | — | MARATHON-12; this task only 403s non-members |\n| Explicit `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` add-member | SPA `channel-add-member-*` | Not in product Channels section; file follow-up if M18 needs it before invites — **neighborhood hit**: frontend hooks list add-member controls; **excluded** here; recommend small follow-up or fold into M12/M18 backend notes |\n| `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` | — | MARATHON-11 |\n| Slash `/topic` `/archive` | message body commands | MARATHON-11 |\n| Redis/WS fan-out on join/archive | `server/events.py` | MARATHON-13/14 |\n| SPA create-channel-modal / settings | `static/**` | MARATHON-17/18 |\n| Changing workspace detail visibility rules | `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` | Already correct in M5 |\n| IRC JOIN mapping | — | MARATHON-15 |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `server/channels/store.py` — ChannelObj, general, list, read_state | **In scope** — extend |\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` — create/list/detail/members | **In scope** — add join + create channel only |\n| `server/workspaces/store.py` — membership helpers | **In scope** — add member insert for open join |\n| `server/db.py` — v1/v2 | **In scope** — add v3 |\n| `server/app.py` — routers | **In scope** — mount new routers |\n| `static/js/shell.js` — `POST .../join` | **Out of scope** — already client-complete; server must satisfy |\n| `tests/test_workspaces.py` archive fixtures | **Out of scope** — keep green; new tests in `test_channels.py` |\n| Grep: no `/api/channels` routes yet | Greenfield routes |\n| `channel-add-member-*` testids in product frontend hooks | **Out of scope** — no REST in Channels contract; separate task |\n| `server/events.py` | **Out of scope** — no-op OK |\n\n...(len 2141 )\n\n### SECTION: ## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Unauthenticated any new route | **401** |\n| Create channel name `General` / `eng_ops` / `e` / empty | **400** |\n| Create name `general` when `#general` exists | **409** |\n| Concurrent duplicate name | IntegrityError → **409** (no 500) |\n| Guest creates public channel | **403** |\n| Member creates `is_private:true` | **403** |\n| Admin/owner creates private | **201**; creator is only initial channel member |\n| Topic length 250 OK; 251 → **400** |\n| Topic PATCH by workspace owner who left channel | **200** allowed (owner clause) |\n| Topic PATCH by random workspace member not in channel | **403** |\n| Join public on open as non-member | Workspace row `member` + channel member; **200** |\n| Join public on invite_only as non-member | **403** (even if they know channel id) |\n| Join public as guest workspace member | **403** |\n| Join private without channel_members | **403** |\n| Join unknown id | **404** |\n| Leave twice | Both **200** `{channel}` |\n| Leave `#general` | Allowed; channel remains |\n| Archive by admin | **403** |\n| Archive by owner | **200**; `is_archived=true` |\n| PATCH topic on archived | **423** `archived` |\n| POST pin on archived | **423** |\n| GET pins on archived | **200** (read OK) |\n| Unarchive then pin | **200** |\n| POST pin twice | Same `pinned_at`/`pinned_by` as first |\n| DELETE pin when absent | **200** `{unpinned:true}` |\n| Pin message in other channel’s pin list | Listed only under its `channel_id` |\n| Workspace join invite_only | **403** |\n| Workspace join open idempotent | **200**; single membership row |\n| DM channel create via this POST | Impossible (`is_dm` forced false) |\n| SQLite busy | busy_timeout; still fail closed after timeout |\n| Extra JSON fields | Ignore |\n\n...(len 1817 )\n\n### SECTION: ## Acceptance Criteria\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` with valid `{name}` as member → **201** `{channel}` with `ChannelObj` keys; `topic` default `\"\"`; `is_dm=false`; creator in `channel_members`.\n2. Duplicate channel name in workspace → **409** `conflict`.\n3. Invalid kebab name or topic > 250 → **400** `validation_error`.\n4. Guest create → **403**; member create private → **403**; admin/owner create private → **201**.\n5. `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` on open as non-member → **200** and subsequent workspace detail succeeds; invite_only → **403**; unknown slug → **404**; already member → **200** idempotent.\n6. `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` public on open workspace auto-onboards non-member as workspace `member` + channel member → **200**; invite_only non-member → **403**; guest → **403**; private without membership → **403**; unknown → **404**; already member → **200**.\n7. `POST /api/channels/{id}/leave` twice → both **200** `{channel}`; membership removed after first.\n8. `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` → **200** `{members:[UserObj,…]}` with exact UserObj keys; private non-member → **403** (unless workspace owner per contract above).\n9. `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}` as channel member or workspace owner → **200** `{channel}`; archived → **423** `archived`.\n10. `POST .../archive` and `.../unarchive` owner-only → **200**; non-owner member → **403**.\n11. `GET /api/channels/{id}/pins` newest-first; private non-member → **403**.\n12. `POST /api/messages/{id}/pin` idempotent → **200** `{pin:{message_id,pinned_by,pinned_at}}`; `DELETE` → **200** `{unpinned:true}` idempotent; archived channel → **423** on POST/DELETE pin.\n13. **Cluster:** create channel / join on `:8000`, read members/pins on `:8001` with same token (shared DB).\n14. **Negative:** must **not** accept `description` as topic; must **not** allow guest public join; must **not** implement message CRUD routes; must **not** store channel SoT in Redis; must **not** change `ChannelObj` key set; must **not** use 404 for archived writes.\n\n...(len 2042 )\n\n### SECTION: ## Testing Strategy\n## Testing Strategy\n\n...(len 20 )\n============================================================ MARATHON-5 Workspaces: create, list, detail, aut