ry** entry has exactly the keys `channel_id`, `last_read_seq`, `unread_count`, `mention_count` (integers ≥ 0 for the three numeric fields).\n7. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as different user with no membership → **404** (must **not** return 200).\n8. With only `#general` present, `channels` length is 1 and name is `general`.\n9. When an archived channel exists visible to the user: default detail omits it; `?include_archived=1` **and** `?include_archived=true` both include it.\n10. When a private channel exists without `channel_members` for the caller: detail omits it even with `include_archived=1` or `true`.\n11. **Cluster:** workspace created via `:8000` is listed/detailed via `:8001`/`:8002` with the same token.\n12. **Negative:** must **not** create workspace without `#general`; must **not** store workspace SoT in Redis; must **not** add member-list or channel-CRUD routes; must **not** change `/api/health` shape/auth; must **not** include `email` or password fields anywhere; must **not** emit truncated `read_state` entries missing `unread_count` or `mention_count`.\n13. Migration v2 applied idempotently; fresh and v1-upgraded DBs both serve the routes; `channel_read_state` includes `unread_count` and `mention_count` columns.\n\n...(len 2105 )\n\n### SECTION: ## Testing Strategy\n## Testing Strategy\n\n...(len 20 )\n============================================================ MARATHON-16 SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\n--- DESIGN DM hits ---\n  ) | | `channel-list` | Authenticated with current workspace | Container for non-DM channels (may be empty of children until channels load / MARATHON-17) | | `dms-list` | Authenticated with current wor\n  pace | Container for DM channels (empty until MARATHON-9/17) |  **Auth form fields (required for drivability, not all named in the task list):*\n  etail**: populate `workspace-header`, split `channels` into `channel-list` (`is_dm === false`) and `dms-list` (`is_dm === true`); ignore `read_state` badges in this ta