hon3 <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess,re\nfor tid in ['MARATHON-17','MARATHON-7','MARATHON-5']:\n    raw=subprocess.check_output(['loom','data','show',tid,'--output','json'],text=True)\n    lines=raw.splitlines()\n    json_start=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('{'))\n    d=json.loads('\\n'.join(lines[json_start:]))\n    print('='*40, tid)\n    print('DESC:', d.get('description','')[:1500])\n    print('NOTES:', (d.get('notes') or '')[:2000])\n    if tid=='MARATHON-7':\n        design=d.get('design') or ''\n        # extract list_channels visibility and ChannelObj\n        for pat in ['list_channels','is_private','Visibility','ChannelObj','name.*dm','canonical']:\n            pass\n        # print data model channels section\n        m=re.search(r'## Data Model.*?(?=## Files to Create)', design, re.S)\n        if m:\n            print(m.group(0)[:5000])\nPY\n# Also dump full MARATHON-7 interface for create channel name rules\nloom data show MARATHON-7 --output json | python3 -c '\nimport json,sys,re\nraw=sys.stdin.read()\nd=json.loads(raw[raw.index(\"{\"):])\ndesign=d[\"design\"]\n# find name validation and any mention of dm name\nfor m in re.finditer(r\"(?i).{0,40}(dm.?name|name for dm|canonical|pair|sorted user).{0,200}\", design):\n    print(\"HIT:\", m.group(0).replace(\"\\n\",\" \")[:300])\nprint(\"---CHANNEL NAME RE---\")\nidx=design.find(\"CHANNEL_NAME\")\nprint(design[max(0,idx-200):idx+400] if idx>=0 else \"n/a\")\nidx=design.find(\"ChannelObj\")\nprint(design[idx:idx+1200])\n'","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"======================================== MARATHON-17\nDESC: Channel list/create/switch; duplicate-name validation; data-channel-id/name on entries; hashtag-prefixed names; channel header name+topic; empty-channel non-blank copy. Messages: post/edit/delete via hover-toolbar; edited indicator; survive hard reload; empty-message validation. Message rows: avatar+author+human-readable timestamp+body. Threads: right-side panel; bump N replies. Reactions via emoji-picker grid (not prompt()); reaction badge with count. Pinned testids: channel-*, message-*, thread-*, reaction-*, emoji-*, create-channel-modal, etc. per frontend hooks.\nNOTES: \n======================================== MARATHON-7\nDESC: ChannelObj {id,workspace_id,name,is_private,is_dm,topic,is_archived}; topic default \\\"\\\", max 250. POST workspaces/{slug}/channels; name kebab <=32; duplicate 409. Role rules: guest cannot join public or create channels (403); member cannot create private (403); private create admin/owner. Join: open workspace auto-onboards non-members; invite_only non-members 403; private without invite 403. leave idempotent; members list; PATCH topic (member or workspace owner); archive/unarchive owner-only; archived writes → 423. Pins: GET channels/{id}/pins; POST/DELETE messages/{id}/pin per contract.\nNOTES: Shipped channels create/join/leave/topic/archive + workspace join + pins. Migration v3 messages+channel_pins; assert_channel_writable → 423 archived for M8. Tests: test_channels.py + test_pins.py; full suite 175 passed. Cluster two-app shared data_dir covered.\n## Data Model\n\n### Migration v3 (additive, backward compatible)\n\n#### `messages` (minimal — MARATHON-8 extends)\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | UUID4 |\n| `channel_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → channels ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `author_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → users |\n| `body` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| `parent_id` | TEXT | NULL | FK → messages (threads later) |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| `edited_at` | TEXT | NULL | |\n| `deleted_at` | TEXT | NULL | reserved for M8 soft-delete |\n\nIndexes: `idx_messages_channel_id` on `channel_id`.\n\n**This task does not expose message CRUD.** Rows exist for pin tests / future M8.\n\n#### `channel_pins`\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `message_id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | FK → messages ON DELETE CASCADE; one pin per message |\n| `channel_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → channels (denormalized for list-by-channel) |\n| `pinned_by` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → users |\n| `pinned_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UTC Z |\n\nIndex: `idx_channel_pins_channel_pinned_at` on `(channel_id, pinned_at DESC)`.\n\n### Existing tables used (no change to DDL)\n\n- `channels`, `channel_members`, `workspaces`, `workspace_members`, `users`, `channel_read_state`\n\n### Schema change summary\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| v3 new tables | **Yes** — additive |\n| No alters to v2 columns | **Yes** |\n\n### Invariants\n\n1. `UNIQUE(workspace_id, name)` on channels enforced; API maps violations to 409.\n2. Channel create always inserts creator into `channel_members`.\n3. Open workspace join/channel-join auto-onboard inserts `workspace_members.role='member'` (never owner/admin/guest).\n4. At most one pin row per `message_id`.\n5. `is_dm` channels are not creatable via `POST .../channels` (`is_dm=0` always).\n\n\n======================================== MARATHON-5\nDESC: WorkspaceObj {id, slug, name, owner_id, join_mode} with join_mode open|invite_only default open. POST /api/workspaces {slug,name} → 201 {workspace, general_channel}; slug kebab ^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$; duplicate slug 409; creator is owner; auto-create #general. GET /api/workspaces → member/owned list. GET /api/workspaces/{slug} → {workspace, channels, read_state}; omit private channels caller is not in; ?include_archived=1 supported.\nNOTES: Shipped workspaces create/list/detail per design. Migration v2 + routes. read_state uses full ReadStateEntry {channel_id,last_read_seq,unread_count,mention_count}; include_archived accepts 1 and case-insensitive true. errors.py already broadened by MARATHON-4. Tests: tests/test_workspaces.py; full unit suite green; cluster verified create:8000 list:8001 detail:8002.\n---CHANNEL NAME RE---\nn/a\nChannelObj` | **Unchanged** key set from MARATHON-5 (`CHANNEL_OBJ_KEYS`); this task owns create/mutate behavior |\n| Workspace join vs channel join | **Both**: SPA uses workspace join (M16); product grader uses channel join with open auto-onboard. Same membership insert helper |\n| Private “invite” | No private-invite table yet (MARATHON-12). “Without invite” ≡ caller lacks `channel_members` row → **403** on join. Creator is auto-member on create; tests may SQL-seed members until add-member API exists |\n| Pins without full Message API | Minimal `messages` table + thin `MessageObj` mapper (empty `files`/`reactions`/`mentions`, `reply_count=0`) so pin list/embed works; MARATHON-8 owns message CRUD and enriches the same object |\n| Archived writes | Shared helper `assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived`; used by topic PATCH + pin mutate now; documented for M8 message/reaction writes |\n| Events / Redis | No pub/sub (MARATHON-13/14); optional no-op hooks OK but not required |\n| Timestamps | Reuse `utc_now_z()` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`) consistent with M3–M6 |\n\n### Why\n\n- Product contract is explicit on paths, envelopes, role matrix, 423, and pin shapes; inventing alternate routes woul\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T00:25:10.468Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T00:25:10.481Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T00:25:10.497Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T00:25:10.511Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":154,"interleavedOutput":"time=2026-08-23T00:25:10.468Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T00:25:10.481Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T00:25:10.497Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db clie