{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-94e36e22-aaa6-4943-80dc-4232031203ce-29\nfc_82e07faa-6f1d-91eb-a29c-85c8895b5827_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cat > /tmp/marathon-9-design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds authenticated **get-or-create** for 1:1 direct-message channels: `POST /api/dms` resolves a workspace-scoped DM between the caller and a peer `user_id`, returning the same `channel_id` for both directions and on every repeat call. The channel is persisted as a normal `channels` row with `is_dm=true` (and `is_private=true` for visibility), both users in `channel_members`, so existing channel/message authz (MARATHON-7/8) and the SPA `dms-list` split (MARATHON-16) work without a separate message transport. It does not build group DMs, DM UI, or message posting.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Route | Top-level `POST /api/dms` (task-mandated), not nested under `/api/workspaces/{slug}` |\n| Request body | `{ \"user_id\", \"workspace_id\" }` — both required UUID strings. Task text abbreviated `{user_id}`; **workspace is mandatory** because every channel row has non-null `workspace_id` (MARATHON-5) and the shell lists DMs per current workspace |\n| Response | Always **200** `{ \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\" }` (not `201`, not a full `ChannelObj` wrapper) |\n| Pair identity | Canonical unordered pair: `user_lo, user_hi = sorted([caller_id, peer_id])` within a workspace |\n| Dedup without competing for migration v4 | **No new table.** Deterministic synthetic `channels.name` under existing `UNIQUE(workspace_id, name)`: `dm-` + first 29 hex chars of `SHA-256(workspace_id \\|\\| \":\" \\|\\| user_lo \\|\\| \":\" \\|\\| user_hi)` (ASCII, lower hex). Satisfies `CHANNEL_NAME_RE` (`^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`). Lookup = `SELECT` by `(workspace_id, name, is_dm=1)` |\n| Flags | Insert with `is_dm=1`, `is_private=1`, `topic=\"\"`, `is_archived=0` |\n| Membership | On create: insert **both** users into `channel_members`. On get (existing row): **ensure** both memberships exist (re-add if a party previously `leave`d) |\n| Package | New `server/dms/` router + thin store orchestration; channel row helpers live in `server/channels/store.py` next to `create_channel` |\n| DM privacy vs workspace owner | **Tighten** read/mutate gates for `is_dm`: channel **membership required**; workspace `owner_id` alone must **not** bypass (diverges from private-channel owner bypass in MARATHON-7 — justified so DMs are not readable by the workspace owner) |\n| List visibility | Keep/adjust `list_channels_for_workspace_user` so DMs never appear to non-members (defense in depth even if `is_private` were wrong) |\n| Migration | **None** for the happy path (avoids collision with MARATHON-8 and MARATHON-12, both designed as **v4**). Optional later `dm_pairs` table is out of scope |\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; error envelope `{error:{code,message}}` unchanged |\n| Ids / time | UUID4 channel ids; `utc_now_z()` timestamps |\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|-------------|------------------|\n| Body only `{user_id}` with implicit workspace | Multi-workspace users make the pair ambiguous; channels are workspace-scoped |\n| `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/dms` | Contradicts task path `POST /api/dms` already reserved by MARATHON-7 out-of-scope |\n| New `dm_pairs` table (migration) | Cleaner join, but **v4 is double-booked** by M8/M12; name-hash uniqueness reuses existing UNIQUE and ships without schema races |\n| Username-based channel `name` for display | Usernames allow `_` and up to 32 chars; fail `CHANNEL_NAME_RE` / length; display is asymmetric per viewer anyway |\n| Return full `{channel: ChannelObj}` | Task mandates `{channel_id}`; client refreshes workspace detail for list rows |\n| Global (non-workspace) DMs | No place in current schema; SPA DMs are per-workspace sidebar |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nOpaque synthetic `ChannelObj.name` for DMs (not a human display label). **MARATHON-17** must render DM sidebar labels from the peer `UserObj` (e.g. via `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` or members already known client-side), not from `name`. Until then, `dms-list` may show the synthetic name — acceptable for this backend-only task.\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Shared conventions (inherited)\n\n- Bearer `Authorization` required → missing/invalid → **401** `unauthorized` (MARATHON-3).\n- Errors: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"<code>\", \"message\": \"<human>\" } }` (MARATHON-3/4).\n- Pydantic bodies: `extra=\"ignore\"`; unknown keys ignored.\n- `ChannelObj` keys unchanged: `id`, `workspace_id`, `name`, `is_private`, `is_dm`, `topic`, `is_archived` (MARATHON-5/7).\n- Timestamps UTC `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/dms`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** (MARATHON-17 / future) | While user picks a peer in the current workspace, `POST /api/dms` with bearer + JSON body. On **200**, store/use `channel_id` (navigate message pane, refresh workspace detail so `dms-list` updates). Disable submit while in flight; do not invent a local channel id. |\n| **Server** | Validate body; authorize workspace membership for caller + peer; get-or-create DM; return `{channel_id}` only. |\n\n**Request**\n\n```http\nPOST /api/dms\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>\nContent-Type: application/json\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"user_id\": \"<peer-user-uuid>\",\n  \"workspace_id\": \"<workspace-uuid>\"\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Rules |\n|-------|------|----------|-------|\n| `user_id` | string | yes | Peer user id; must exist; must not equal caller; must be a `workspace_members` row for `workspace_id` |\n| `workspace_id` | string | yes | Existing workspace id; caller must be a member |\n\n**Response 200**\n\n```json\n{ \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\" }\n```\n\nExact key: `channel_id` only (no `channel` object, no extra fields required).\n\n**Status / error matrix**\n\n| Condition | Status | `code` | Notes |\n|-----------|--------|--------|-------|\n| Success (create or existing) | **200** | — | Same id both directions / repeats |\n| Missing/invalid bearer | **401** | `unauthorized` | |\n| Missing field / wrong type / empty string | **400** | `validation_error` | FastAPI envelope or explicit `ApiError` |\n| `user_id` == caller | **400** | `validation_error` | Message e.g. `cannot dm yourself` |\n| Unknown `workspace_id` or caller not a workspace member | **404** | `not_found` | Message `workspace not found` (no existence leak) |\n| Unknown `user_id` **or** peer not a member of that workspace | **404** | `not_found` | Message `user not found` (do not distinguish “exists globally but not in workspace”) |\n| SQLite busy after timeout | fail closed | — | Same as other routes; no partial membership |\n\n**Not used:** **403** for “peer not in workspace” (prefer 404 to match workspace non-member leak policy). Guests **may** DM other workspace members (no role gate beyond membership).\n\n### Seam: DM channel appearance on `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Server** | After create, both members see a `ChannelObj` with `is_dm=true` in `channels` (subject to archive filter). Non-members must **not** see it. |\n| **Client** (MARATHON-16 already) | Split `is_dm === true` → `dms-list`, else → `channel-list`. |\n\n### Seam: Authz tweaks for `is_dm` (server-owned)\n\nFor any existing channel route that today allows **workspace owner without channel membership** on private channels, when `channel.is_dm` is true:\n\n- **Require** `channel_members` row for the caller.\n- If workspace member but not channel member → **403** `forbidden` (same message family as private denial is fine).\n- If not a workspace member → **404** `not_found`.\n\nApplies at least to: channel members list, PATCH topic, GET pins, pin/unpin message, and (when MARATHON-8 lands) message read/write helpers — document for M8 implementer: **DM ⇒ member-only, no owner bypass**.\n\n`POST /api/channels/{id}/join` on a DM remains **403** for non-members (MARATHON-7); get-or-create is the only supported add path.\n\n### Client slow / fail summary\n\n| Condition | Client behavior |\n|-----------|-----------------|\n| In flight | Disable “open DM” control; keep prior `dms-list` |\n| 401 | Re-auth (MARATHON-16) |\n| 400 | Show `error.message`; stay on picker |\n| 404 | Show not-found / peer unavailable; do not add sidebar row |\n| Network / 5xx / timeout | Retry; do not assume channel exists until **200** |\n| 200 | Use `channel_id`; optionally re-fetch workspace detail |\n\n## Data Model\n\n### No new migration (preferred)\n\nUses existing v2 tables:\n\n- `channels` — new rows with `is_dm=1`, `is_private=1`, synthetic `name`, empty `topic`\n- `channel_members` — exactly the two participants (after ensure-membership)\n- `workspaces` / `workspace_members` / `users` — authz only\n\n### Synthetic name algorithm (normative)\n\n```\nuser_lo, user_hi = sorted([caller_id, peer_id])  # lexicographic UUID string order\ndigest = SHA-256( f\"{workspace_id}:{user_lo}:{user_hi}\".encode(\"utf-8\") ).hexdigest()\nname = \"dm-\" + digest[:29]   # length 32; charset [a-z0-9-]\n```\n\nInvariant: name depends only on `(workspace_id, unordered user pair)` — **not** on who called.\n\n### Channel row fields on create\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|--------|\n| `id` | new UUID4 |\n| `workspace_id` | from body |\n| `name` | synthetic as above |\n| `is_private` | `1` |\n| `is_dm` | `1` |\n| `topic` | `\"\"` |\n| `is_archived` | `0` |\n| `created_at` / `updated_at` | `utc_now_z()` |\n\n### List-query defense (in scope)\n\nUpdate `list_channels_for_workspace_user` visibility predicate from “public OR member” to:\n\n- visible if **member**, OR\n- visible if **`is_dm=0` AND `is_private=0`** (true public)\n\nEquivalently: `(c.is_dm = 0 AND c.is_private = 0) OR cm.user_id IS NOT NULL`.\n\n### Schema change summary\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| No DDL | **Yes** |\n| List SQL predicate tighten | **Yes** — only hides rows that should not have been visible |\n| DM owner-bypass removal | Behavior change for owners on `is_dm` only |\n\n### Invariants\n\n1. At most one `is_dm` channel per `(workspace_id, unordered user pair)` (enforced by deterministic name + UNIQUE).\n2. `POST .../channels` still forces `is_dm=false` (MARATHON-7).\n3. Get-or-create never creates a second row for the same pair.\n4. After a successful `POST /api/dms`, both users have `channel_members` rows.\n5. `ChannelObj.is_dm === true` for these rows; SPA list split continues to work.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/dms/__init__.py` | Package marker / docstring: DM get-or-create owned here |\n| `server/dms/routes.py` | `APIRouter(prefix=\"/api/dms\")`; `POST \"\"` handler; pydantic body; transaction; map errors |\n| `server/dms/store.py` | `canonical_dm_name(...)`; `get_or_create_dm_channel(conn, *, workspace_id, caller_id, peer_id) -> channel_id`; peer/workspace checks raising `ApiError` |\n| `tests/test_dms.py` | Contract tests (see Testing Strategy) |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` for dms router |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | Add `create_dm_channel(...)` (bypass public name validation path used by user-created channels **or** validate synthetic name after generation); fix `list_channels_for_workspace_user` predicate for DM/private; optional `find_dm_by_name` |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | In `_require_channel_read_access`, pin list, PATCH, leave as needed: **`is_dm` ⇒ membership required** (no owner-only bypass) |\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | Same DM membership rule in `_require_pin_access` (and document for M8 shared helper) |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/**` | MARATHON-17 owns DM picker UI; M16 list split already correct |\n| `server/db.py` | No migration in this design |\n| `server/auth/**`, `server/users/**` | Consume `get_user_by_id` / deps only |\n| Message CRUD routes | MARATHON-8 |\n| IRC / WS / Redis | MARATHON-13/14/15 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order (this task)\n\n1. `channels/store.py` — `create_dm_channel` + list predicate.\n2. `dms/store.py` + `dms/routes.py` + mount in `app.py`.\n3. Authz tighten for `is_dm` in channel/message routes.\n4. `tests/test_dms.py` (+ any small assertion updates if list tests assume old predicate).\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Independent of MARATHON-8 message CRUD **except** shared DM authz rule (coordinate via this design’s Interface Contracts).\n- Independent of MARATHON-12 groups/invitations.\n- MARATHON-17 can stub against this contract once merged.\n\n### Cross-task seams\n\n| Contract | Owner | Consumer |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| `POST /api/dms` → `{channel_id}` | **MARATHON-9** | MARATHON-17 (DM open), graders |\n| `ChannelObj.is_dm` + list visibility | MARATHON-5/7 + **this list fix** | MARATHON-16 shell, MARATHON-17 |\n| DM member-only authz (no owner bypass) | **MARATHON-9** | MARATHON-8 message helpers must match |\n| Message post in DM channel | MARATHON-8 | Needs channel membership (created here) |\n| DM display labels / picker UI | MARATHON-17 | Uses `channel_id` + members/profiles |\n\n### Declared dependents\n\n- MARATHON-17 (SPA channels/DMs UX)\n- MARATHON-8 (messages in DM channels; authz note)\n\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n\n- Group DMs / multi-user conversations.\n- `dm_pairs` table if hash-in-name is ever insufficient.\n- Forbidding archive/leave on DMs.\n- Client-side peer label rendering.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| SPA DM picker / open-DM button / peer label | `static/js/*`, MARATHON-17 | Frontend task; shell already has empty-capable `dms-list` |\n| Message send/list inside DM | MARATHON-8 | Separate REST surface |\n| Search / read_state / slash | MARATHON-11 | |\n| WS fan-out `channel` events | MARATHON-13/14 | |\n| IRC DM mapping | MARATHON-15 | |\n| Group DMs | — | Not in task |\n| Changing private-channel **owner** bypass for non-DM privates | `channels/routes.py` | Keep MARATHON-7 behavior for `is_private && !is_dm` |\n| `POST /api/channels` creating `is_dm` | already forbidden | Remains forbidden |\n| Migration v4/v5 DDL | `server/db.py` | Avoid M8/M12 version collision; name uniqueness sufficient |\n| `channel-add-member-*` for DMs | SPA hooks | DMs are pair-only via this endpoint |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `server/channels/store.py` `is_dm` always false on create; list predicate | **In scope** — DM create helper + list fix |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` private/DM treated alike; owner bypass | **In scope** — DM membership tighten |\n| `server/messages/routes.py` private/DM pin authz | **In scope** — same DM rule |\n| `server/db.py` `is_dm` column | **Unchanged** |\n| `static/js/shell.js` `dms-list` / `is_dm` split | **Out of scope** — already correct |\n| `tests/test_channels.py` `is_dm is False` on normal create | **Out of scope** — keep; add `test_dms.py` |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` / `test_workspaces.py` `is_dm` assertions | **Out of scope** unless list predicate breaks a fixture |\n| Grep: no `/api/dms` router yet | Greenfield `server/dms` |\n| MARATHON-7/8/16 designs reserving `POST /api/dms` | **This task** |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| A→B then B→A | Same `channel_id` |\n| Repeat A→B | Same `channel_id`; **200**; no second row |\n| Concurrent A→B and B→A | One INSERT wins; loser hits UNIQUE/`IntegrityError` on `(workspace_id,name)` → re-SELECT by name → return existing id (no **500**) |\n| Caller left DM earlier | Ensure re-INSERT `channel_members` for caller (and peer if missing); return same id |\n| Peer left DM earlier | Same ensure-both-memberships |\n| Self `user_id` | **400** `validation_error` |\n| Peer not in workspace | **404** `user not found` |\n| Caller not in workspace | **404** `workspace not found` |\n| Archived DM exists | Still return its `channel_id` (do not create replacement). Messaging may **423** via existing guard (MARATHON-7/8) |\n| Workspace owner not in DM opens channel routes | **403** (member of ws) / **404** (stranger) — **not** owner bypass |\n| Guest DMs a member | **200** if both are workspace members |\n| Extra body keys | Ignored |\n| `workspace_id` is a slug string | **404** (id lookup fails) — clients must send UUID `workspace.id` |\n| User creates public channel whose name collides with a DM hash | Astronomically unlikely; if IntegrityError on DM insert and re-read finds non-`is_dm` row → **409** `conflict` with clear message (abort; do not hijack) |\n| Unauthenticated | **401** |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Authenticated `POST /api/dms` with `{user_id, workspace_id}` for two distinct workspace members → **200** `{ \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\" }`.\n2. Calling again with the same pair (same caller) → **200** with **identical** `channel_id`.\n3. Peer calling with the caller’s id (swapped direction) → **200** with the **same** `channel_id`.\n4. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as either participant includes a channel with that id where `is_dm === true` (and typically `is_private === true`).\n5. A third workspace member’s workspace detail must **NOT** include that DM channel.\n6. Persisted row has `is_dm=1` (verify via API list/detail or DB in tests).\n7. Self-DM → **400** `validation_error`; must **NOT** create a channel.\n8. Unknown peer id → **404**; must **NOT** create a channel.\n9. Peer registered globally but not in workspace → **404**; must **NOT** create a channel.\n10. Caller not in workspace → **404**.\n11. Unauthenticated → **401**.\n12. After participant `POST /api/channels/{id}/leave`, a subsequent `POST /api/dms` for the same pair returns the **same** `channel_id` and restores membership (subsequent channel member list / message write authz succeeds for that user).\n13. Workspace owner who is **not** a DM member must **NOT** read DM pins/members via owner bypass (**403** or **404** per rules above).\n14. Negative: `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` still cannot create `is_dm=true` channels.\n15. Negative: response must **NOT** require a `channel` object key for success (only `channel_id`).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated (`tests/test_dms.py`)\n\n- Happy path create + idempotent repeat + reverse direction same id.\n- Both users see DM on workspace detail; third member does not.\n- Self / missing peer / non-member peer / non-member caller / unauthenticated.\n- Leave then get-or-create restores membership.\n- Owner-without-membership denied on `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` (or pins) for the DM.\n- Optional: concurrent create smoke (two threads) still yields one row.\n- Regression: existing `tests/test_channels.py` / `test_workspaces.py` stay green.\n\n### Manual / cluster\n\n1. Register users A,B,C; create workspace; add B and C as members.\n2. On `:8000`, A `POST /api/dms` with B → note `channel_id`.\n3. On `:8001`, B `POST /api/dms` with A → same id (shared SQLite).\n4. A and B `GET` workspace detail → DM present; C’s detail → absent.\n5. Confirm `is_dm` true in listed channel object.\n\n### Human verify\n\n- No SPA change required; `curl`/httpie against any node with bearer token is enough for this task.\nDESIGN_EOF\nwc -l /tmp/marathon-9-design.md\nloom data update MARATHON-9 --design=\"$(cat /tmp/marathon-9-design.md)\" --design-format=markdown\nloom data update MARATHON-9 --notes=\"Design complete for POST /api/dms get-or-create. Key decisions: body requires user_id+workspace_id (workspace-scoped channels); always 200 {channel_id}; dedupe via deterministic dm- name hash (no migration — avoids M8/M12 v4 clash); is_dm+is_private; ensure both memberships; tighten DM authz to members-only (no workspace-owner bypass). Handed to review; implementer label remains backend.\" --status review --assignee=\"\"\nloom data show MARATHON-9 --output json | python3 -c '\nimport json,sys\nraw=sys.stdin.read()\nd=json.loads(raw[raw.index(\"{\"):])\nprint(\"status:\", d[\"status\"])\nprint(\"assignee:\", repr(d.get(\"assignee\")))\nprint(\"labels:\", d.get(\"labels\"))\nprint(\"has_design:\", d.get(\"has_design\"))\nprint(\"design_len:\", len(d.get(\"design\") or \"\"))\nprint(\"notes:\", (d.get(\"notes\") or \"\")[:300])\n'\nloom complete\n","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-94e36e22-aaa6-4943-80dc-4232031203ce-29\nfc_82e07faa-6f1d-91eb-a29c-85c8895b5827_0","simpleCommands":["cat","wc","loom","cat","loom","loom","python3","loom"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cat","args":[],"fullText":"cat"},{"name":"wc","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-l"},{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/marathon-9-design.md"}],"fullText":"wc -l /tmp/marathon-9-design.md"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"update"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-9"},{"type":"concatenation","value":"--design=\"$(cat /tmp/marathon-9-design.md)\""},{"type":"word","value":"--design-format=markdown"}],"fullText":"loom data update MARATHON-9 --design=\"$(cat /tmp/marathon-9-design.md)\" --design-format=markdown"},{"name":"cat","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/marathon-9-design.md"}],"fullText":"cat /tmp/marathon-9-design.md"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"update"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-9"},{"type":"concatenation","value":"--notes=\"Design complete for POST /api/dms get-or-create. Key decisions: body requires user_id+workspace_id (workspace-scoped channels); always 200 {channel_id}; dedupe via deterministic dm- name hash (no migration — avoids M8/M12 v4 clash); is_dm+is_private; ensure both memberships; tighten DM authz to members-only (no workspace-owner bypass). Handed to review; implementer label remains backend.\""},{"type":"word","value":"--status"},{"type":"word","value":"review"},{"type":"concatenation","value":"--assignee=\"\""}],"fullText":"loom data update MARATHON-9 --notes=\"Design complete for POST /api/dms get-or-create. Key decisions: body requires user_id+workspace_id (workspace-scoped channels); always 200 {channel_id}; dedupe via deterministic dm- name hash (no migration — avoids M8/M12 v4 clash); is_dm+is_private; ensure both memberships; tighten DM authz to members-only (no workspace-owner bypass). Handed to review; implementer label remains backend.\" --status review --assignee=\"\""},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-9"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-9 --output json"},{"name":"python3","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"raw_string","value":"'\nimport json,sys\nraw=sys.stdin.read()\nd=json.loads(raw[raw.index(\"{\"):])\nprint(\"status:\", d[\"status\"])\nprint(\"assignee:\", repr(d.get(\"assignee\")))\nprint(\"labels:\", d.get(\"labels\"))\nprint(\"has_design:\", d.get(\"has_design\"))\nprint(\"design_len:\", len(d.get(\"design\") or \"\"))\nprint(\"notes:\", (d.get(\"notes\") or \"\")[:300])\n'"}],"fullText":"python3 -c '\nimport json,sys\nraw=sys.stdin.read()\nd=json.loads(raw[raw.index(\"{\"):])\nprint(\"status:\", d[\"status\"])\nprint(\"assignee:\", repr(d.get(\"assignee\")))\nprint(\"labels:\", d.get(\"labels\"))\nprint(\"has_design:\", d.get(\"has_design\"))\nprint(\"design_len:\", len(d.get(\"design\") or \"\"))\nprint(\"notes:\", (d.get(\"notes\") or \"\")[:300])\n'"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"complete"}],"fullText":"loom complete"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":true,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":false,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/marathon-9-design.md"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"cat"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Save design, hand off, loom complete","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"3f743427-f194-44bc-92dc-836b7b6940f7","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"description":"Save design, hand off, loom complete"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-94e36e22-aaa6-4943-80dc-4232031203ce-29\nfc_82e07faa-6f1d-91eb-a29c-85c8895b5827_0","startedAtMs":"1787444889359"},"model_call_id":"b6dbef0b-e6fb-4ca9-8c38-d48246858510-10-bia0","session_id":"3f743427-f194-44bc-92dc-836b7b6940f7","timestamp_ms":1787444889397}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-94e36e22-aaa6-4943-80dc-4232031203ce-29\nfc_82e07faa-6f1d-91eb-a29c-85c8895b5827_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cat > /tmp/marathon-9-design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds authenticated **get-or-create** for 1:1 direct-message channels: `POST /api/dms` resolves a workspace-scoped DM between the caller and a peer `user_id`, returning the same `channel_id` for both directions and on every repeat call. The channel is persisted as a normal `channels` row with `is_dm=true` (and `is_private=true` for visibility), both users in `channel_members`, so existing channel/message authz (MARATHON-7/8) and the SPA `dms-list` split (MARATHON-16) work without a separate message transport. It does not build group DMs, DM UI, or message posting.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Route | Top-level `POST /api/dms` (task-mandated), not nested under `/api/workspaces/{slug}` |\n| Request body | `{ \"user_id\", \"workspace_id\" }` — both required UUID strings. Task text abbreviated `{user_id}`; **workspace is mandatory** because every channel row has non-null `workspace_id` (MARATHON-5) and the shell lists DMs per current workspace |\n| Response | Always **200** `{ \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\" }` (not `201`, not a full `ChannelObj` wrapper) |\n| Pair identity | Canonical unordered pair: `user_lo, user_hi = sorted([caller_id, peer_id])` within a workspace |\n| Dedup without competing for migration v4 | **No new table.** Deterministic synthetic `channels.name` under existing `UNIQUE(workspace_id, name)`: `dm-` + first 29 hex chars of `SHA-256(workspace_id \\|\\| \":\" \\|\\| user_lo \\|\\| \":\" \\|\\| user_hi)` (ASCII, lower hex). Satisfies `CHANNEL_NAME_RE` (`^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`). Lookup = `SELECT` by `(workspace_id, name, is_dm=1)` |\n| Flags | Insert with `is_dm=1`, `is_private=1`, `topic=\"\"`, `is_archived=0` |\n| Membership | On create: insert **both** users into `channel_members`. On get (existing row): **ensure** both memberships exist (re-add if a party previously `leave`d) |\n| Package | New `server/dms/` router + thin store orchestration; channel row helpers live in `server/channels/store.py` next to `create_channel` |\n| DM privacy vs workspace owner | **Tighten** read/mutate gates for `is_dm`: channel **membership required**; workspace `owner_id` alone must **not** bypass (diverges from private-channel owner bypass in MARATHON-7 — justified so DMs are not readable by the workspace owner) |\n| List visibility | Keep/adjust `list_channels_for_workspace_user` so DMs never appear to non-members (defense in depth even if `is_private` were wrong) |\n| Migration | **None** for the happy path (avoids collision with MARATHON-8 and MARATHON-12, both designed as **v4**). Optional later `dm_pairs` table is out of scope |\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; error envelope `{error:{code,message}}` unchanged |\n| Ids / time | UUID4 channel ids; `utc_now_z()` timestamps |\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|-------------|------------------|\n| Body only `{user_id}` with implicit workspace | Multi-workspace users make the pair ambiguous; channels are workspace-scoped |\n| `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/dms` | Contradicts task path `POST /api/dms` already reserved by MARATHON-7 out-of-scope |\n| New `dm_pairs` table (migration) | Cleaner join, but **v4 is double-booked** by M8/M12; name-hash uniqueness reuses existing UNIQUE and ships without schema races |\n| Username-based channel `name` for display | Usernames allow `_` and up to 32 chars; fail `CHANNEL_NAME_RE` / length; display is asymmetric per viewer anyway |\n| Return full `{channel: ChannelObj}` | Task mandates `{channel_id}`; client refreshes workspace detail for list rows |\n| Global (non-workspace) DMs | No place in current schema; SPA DMs are per-workspace sidebar |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nOpaque synthetic `ChannelObj.name` for DMs (not a human display label). **MARATHON-17** must render DM sidebar labels from the peer `UserObj` (e.g. via `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` or members already known client-side), not from `name`. Until then, `dms-list` may show the synthetic name — acceptable for this backend-only task.\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Shared conventions (inherited)\n\n- Bearer `Authorization` required → missing/invalid → **401** `unauthorized` (MARATHON-3).\n- Errors: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"<code>\", \"message\": \"<human>\" } }` (MARATHON-3/4).\n- Pydantic bodies: `extra=\"ignore\"`; unknown keys ignored.\n- `ChannelObj` keys unchanged: `id`, `workspace_id`, `name`, `is_private`, `is_dm`, `topic`, `is_archived` (MARATHON-5/7).\n- Timestamps UTC `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/dms`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** (MARATHON-17 / future) | While user picks a peer in the current workspace, `POST /api/dms` with bearer + JSON body. On **200**, store/use `channel_id` (navigate message pane, refresh workspace detail so `dms-list` updates). Disable submit while in flight; do not invent a local channel id. |\n| **Server** | Validate body; authorize workspace membership for caller + peer; get-or-create DM; return `{channel_id}` only. |\n\n**Request**\n\n```http\nPOST /api/dms\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>\nContent-Type: application/json\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"user_id\": \"<peer-user-uuid>\",\n  \"workspace_id\": \"<workspace-uuid>\"\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Rules |\n|-------|------|----------|-------|\n| `user_id` | string | yes | Peer user id; must exist; must not equal caller; must be a `workspace_members` row for `workspace_id` |\n| `workspace_id` | string | yes | Existing workspace id; caller must be a member |\n\n**Response 200**\n\n```json\n{ \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\" }\n```\n\nExact key: `channel_id` only (no `channel` object, no extra fields required).\n\n**Status / error matrix**\n\n| Condition | Status | `code` | Notes |\n|-----------|--------|--------|-------|\n| Success (create or existing) | **200** | — | Same id both directions / repeats |\n| Missing/invalid bearer | **401** | `unauthorized` | |\n| Missing field / wrong type / empty string | **400** | `validation_error` | FastAPI envelope or explicit `ApiError` |\n| `user_id` == caller | **400** | `validation_error` | Message e.g. `cannot dm yourself` |\n| Unknown `workspace_id` or caller not a workspace member | **404** | `not_found` | Message `workspace not found` (no existence leak) |\n| Unknown `user_id` **or** peer not a member of that workspace | **404** | `not_found` | Message `user not found` (do not distinguish “exists globally but not in workspace”) |\n| SQLite busy after timeout | fail closed | — | Same as other routes; no partial membership |\n\n**Not used:** **403** for “peer not in workspace” (prefer 404 to match workspace non-member leak policy). Guests **may** DM other workspace members (no role gate beyond membership).\n\n### Seam: DM channel appearance on `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Server** | After create, both members see a `ChannelObj` with `is_dm=true` in `channels` (subject to archive filter). Non-members must **not** see it. |\n| **Client** (MARATHON-16 already) | Split `is_dm === true` → `dms-list`, else → `channel-list`. |\n\n### Seam: Authz tweaks for `is_dm` (server-owned)\n\nFor any existing channel route that today allows **workspace owner without channel membership** on private channels, when `channel.is_dm` is true:\n\n- **Require** `channel_members` row for the caller.\n- If workspace member but not channel member → **403** `forbidden` (same message family as private denial is fine).\n- If not a workspace member → **404** `not_found`.\n\nApplies at least to: channel members list, PATCH topic, GET pins, pin/unpin message, and (when MARATHON-8 lands) message read/write helpers — document for M8 implementer: **DM ⇒ member-only, no owner bypass**.\n\n`POST /api/channels/{id}/join` on a DM remains **403** for non-members (MARATHON-7); get-or-create is the only supported add path.\n\n### Client slow / fail summary\n\n| Condition | Client behavior |\n|-----------|-----------------|\n| In flight | Disable “open DM” control; keep prior `dms-list` |\n| 401 | Re-auth (MARATHON-16) |\n| 400 | Show `error.message`; stay on picker |\n| 404 | Show not-found / peer unavailable; do not add sidebar row |\n| Network / 5xx / timeout | Retry; do not assume channel exists until **200** |\n| 200 | Use `channel_id`; optionally re-fetch workspace detail |\n\n## Data Model\n\n### No new migration (preferred)\n\nUses existing v2 tables:\n\n- `channels` — new rows with `is_dm=1`, `is_private=1`, synthetic `name`, empty `topic`\n- `channel_members` — exactly the two participants (after ensure-membership)\n- `workspaces` / `workspace_members` / `users` — authz only\n\n### Synthetic name algorithm (normative)\n\n```\nuser_lo, user_hi = sorted([caller_id, peer_id])  # lexicographic UUID string order\ndigest = SHA-256( f\"{workspace_id}:{user_lo}:{user_hi}\".encode(\"utf-8\") ).hexdigest()\nname = \"dm-\" + digest[:29]   # length 32; charset [a-z0-9-]\n```\n\nInvariant: name depends only on `(workspace_id, unordered user pair)` — **not** on who called.\n\n### Channel row fields on create\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|--------|\n| `id` | new UUID4 |\n| `workspace_id` | from body |\n| `name` | synthetic as above |\n| `is_private` | `1` |\n| `is_dm` | `1` |\n| `topic` | `\"\"` |\n| `is_archived` | `0` |\n| `created_at` / `updated_at` | `utc_now_z()` |\n\n### List-query defense (in scope)\n\nUpdate `list_channels_for_workspace_user` visibility predicate from “public OR member” to:\n\n- visible if **member**, OR\n- visible if **`is_dm=0` AND `is_private=0`** (true public)\n\nEquivalently: `(c.is_dm = 0 AND c.is_private = 0) OR cm.user_id IS NOT NULL`.\n\n### Schema change summary\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| No DDL | **Yes** |\n| List SQL predicate tighten | **Yes** — only hides rows that should not have been visible |\n| DM owner-bypass removal | Behavior change for owners on `is_dm` only |\n\n### Invariants\n\n1. At most one `is_dm` channel per `(workspace_id, unordered user pair)` (enforced by deterministic name + UNIQUE).\n2. `POST .../channels` still forces `is_dm=false` (MARATHON-7).\n3. Get-or-create never creates a second row for the same pair.\n4. After a successful `POST /api/dms`, both users have `channel_members` rows.\n5. `ChannelObj.is_dm === true` for these rows; SPA list split continues to work.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/dms/__init__.py` | Package marker / docstring: DM get-or-create owned here |\n| `server/dms/routes.py` | `APIRouter(prefix=\"/api/dms\")`; `POST \"\"` handler; pydantic body; transaction; map errors |\n| `server/dms/store.py` | `canonical_dm_name(...)`; `get_or_create_dm_channel(conn, *, workspace_id, caller_id, peer_id) -> channel_id`; peer/workspace checks raising `ApiError` |\n| `tests/test_dms.py` | Contract tests (see Testing Strategy) |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` for dms router |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | Add `create_dm_channel(...)` (bypass public name validation path used by user-created channels **or** validate synthetic name after generation); fix `list_channels_for_workspace_user` predicate for DM/private; optional `find_dm_by_name` |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | In `_require_channel_read_access`, pin list, PATCH, leave as needed: **`is_dm` ⇒ membership required** (no owner-only bypass) |\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | Same DM membership rule in `_require_pin_access` (and document for M8 shared helper) |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/**` | MARATHON-17 owns DM picker UI; M16 list split already correct |\n| `server/db.py` | No migration in this design |\n| `server/auth/**`, `server/users/**` | Consume `get_user_by_id` / deps only |\n| Message CRUD routes | MARATHON-8 |\n| IRC / WS / Redis | MARATHON-13/14/15 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order (this task)\n\n1. `channels/store.py` — `create_dm_channel` + list predicate.\n2. `dms/store.py` + `dms/routes.py` + mount in `app.py`.\n3. Authz tighten for `is_dm` in channel/message routes.\n4. `tests/test_dms.py` (+ any small assertion updates if list tests assume old predicate).\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Independent of MARATHON-8 message CRUD **except** shared DM authz rule (coordinate via this design’s Interface Contracts).\n- Independent of MARATHON-12 groups/invitations.\n- MARATHON-17 can stub against this contract once merged.\n\n### Cross-task seams\n\n| Contract | Owner | Consumer |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| `POST /api/dms` → `{channel_id}` | **MARATHON-9** | MARATHON-17 (DM open), graders |\n| `ChannelObj.is_dm` + list visibility | MARATHON-5/7 + **this list fix** | MARATHON-16 shell, MARATHON-17 |\n| DM member-only authz (no owner bypass) | **MARATHON-9** | MARATHON-8 message helpers must match |\n| Message post in DM channel | MARATHON-8 | Needs channel membership (created here) |\n| DM display labels / picker UI | MARATHON-17 | Uses `channel_id` + members/profiles |\n\n### Declared dependents\n\n- MARATHON-17 (SPA channels/DMs UX)\n- MARATHON-8 (messages in DM channels; authz note)\n\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n\n- Group DMs / multi-user conversations.\n- `dm_pairs` table if hash-in-name is ever insufficient.\n- Forbidding archive/leave on DMs.\n- Client-side peer label rendering.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| SPA DM picker / open-DM button / peer label | `static/js/*`, MARATHON-17 | Frontend task; shell already has empty-capable `dms-list` |\n| Message send/list inside DM | MARATHON-8 | Separate REST surface |\n| Search / read_state / slash | MARATHON-11 | |\n| WS fan-out `channel` events | MARATHON-13/14 | |\n| IRC DM mapping | MARATHON-15 | |\n| Group DMs | — | Not in task |\n| Changing private-channel **owner** bypass for non-DM privates | `channels/routes.py` | Keep MARATHON-7 behavior for `is_private && !is_dm` |\n| `POST /api/channels` creating `is_dm` | already forbidden | Remains forbidden |\n| Migration v4/v5 DDL | `server/db.py` | Avoid M8/M12 version collision; name uniqueness sufficient |\n| `channel-add-member-*` for DMs | SPA hooks | DMs are pair-only via this endpoint |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `server/channels/store.py` `is_dm` always false on create; list predicate | **In scope** — DM create helper + list fix |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` private/DM treated alike; owner bypass | **In scope** — DM membership tighten |\n| `server/messages/routes.py` private/DM pin authz | **In scope** — same DM rule |\n| `server/db.py` `is_dm` column | **Unchanged** |\n| `static/js/shell.js` `dms-list` / `is_dm` split | **Out of scope** — already correct |\n| `tests/test_channels.py` `is_dm is False` on normal create | **Out of scope** — keep; add `test_dms.py` |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` / `test_workspaces.py` `is_dm` assertions | **Out of scope** unless list predicate breaks a fixture |\n| Grep: no `/api/dms` router yet | Greenfield `server/dms` |\n| MARATHON-7/8/16 designs reserving `POST /api/dms` | **This task** |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| A→B then B→A | Same `channel_id` |\n| Repeat A→B | Same `channel_id`; **200**; no second row |\n| Concurrent A→B and B→A | One INSERT wins; loser hits UNIQUE/`IntegrityError` on `(workspace_id,name)` → re-SELECT by name → return existing id (no **500**) |\n| Caller left DM earlier | Ensure re-INSERT `channel_members` for caller (and peer if missing); return same id |\n| Peer left DM earlier | Same ensure-both-memberships |\n| Self `user_id` | **400** `validation_error` |\n| Peer not in workspace | **404** `user not found` |\n| Caller not in workspace | **404** `workspace not found` |\n| Archived DM exists | Still return its `channel_id` (do not create replacement). Messaging may **423** via existing guard (MARATHON-7/8) |\n| Workspace owner not in DM opens channel routes | **403** (member of ws) / **404** (stranger) — **not** owner bypass |\n| Guest DMs a member | **200** if both are workspace members |\n| Extra body keys | Ignored |\n| `workspace_id` is a slug string | **404** (id lookup fails) — clients must send UUID `workspace.id` |\n| User creates public channel whose name collides with a DM hash | Astronomically unlikely; if IntegrityError on DM insert and re-read finds non-`is_dm` row → **409** `conflict` with clear message (abort; do not hijack) |\n| Unauthenticated | **401** |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Authenticated `POST /api/dms` with `{user_id, workspace_id}` for two distinct workspace members → **200** `{ \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\" }`.\n2. Calling again with the same pair (same caller) → **200** with **identical** `channel_id`.\n3. Peer calling with the caller’s id (swapped direction) → **200** with the **same** `channel_id`.\n4. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as either participant includes a channel with that id where `is_dm === true` (and typically `is_private === true`).\n5. A third workspace member’s workspace detail must **NOT** include that DM channel.\n6. Persisted row has `is_dm=1` (verify via API list/detail or DB in tests).\n7. Self-DM → **400** `validation_error`; must **NOT** create a channel.\n8. Unknown peer id → **404**; must **NOT** create a channel.\n9. Peer registered globally but not in workspace → **404**; must **NOT** create a channel.\n10. Caller not in workspace → **404**.\n11. Unauthenticated → **401**.\n12. After participant `POST /api/channels/{id}/leave`, a subsequent `POST /api/dms` for the same pair returns the **same** `channel_id` and restores membership (subsequent channel member list / message write authz succeeds for that user).\n13. Workspace owner who is **not** a DM member must **NOT** read DM pins/members via owner bypass (**403** or **404** per rules above).\n14. Negative: `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` still cannot create `is_dm=true` channels.\n15. Negative: response must **NOT** require a `channel` object key for success (only `channel_id`).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated (`tests/test_dms.py`)\n\n- Happy path create + idempotent repeat + reverse direction same id.\n- Both users see DM on workspace detail; third member does not.\n- Self / missing peer / non-member peer / non-member caller / unauthenticated.\n- Leave then get-or-create restores membership.\n- Owner-without-membership denied on `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` (or pins) for the DM.\n- Optional: concurrent create smoke (two threads) still yields one row.\n- Regression: existing `tests/test_channels.py` / `test_workspaces.py` stay green.\n\n### Manual / cluster\n\n1. Register users A,B,C; create workspace; add B and C as members.\n2. On `:8000`, A `POST /api/dms` with B → note `channel_id`.\n3. On `:8001`, B `POST /api/dms` with A → same id (shared SQLite).\n4. A and B `GET` workspace detail → DM present; C’s detail → absent.\n5. Confirm `is_dm` true in listed channel object.\n\n### Human verify\n\n- No SPA change required; `curl`/httpie against any node with bearer token is enough for this task.\nDESIGN_EOF\nwc -l /tmp/marathon-9-design.md\nloom data update MARATHON-9 --design=\"$(cat /tmp/marathon-9-design.md)\" --design-format=markdown\nloom data update MARATHON-9 --notes=\"Design complete for POST /api/dms get-or-create. Key decisions: body requires user_id+workspace_id (workspace-scoped channels); always 200 {channel_id}; dedupe via deterministic dm- name hash (no migration — avoids M8/M12 v4 clash); is_dm+is_private; ensure both memberships; tighten DM authz to members-only (no workspace-owner bypass). Handed to review; implementer label remains backend.\" --status review --assignee=\"\"\nloom data show MARATHON-9 --output json | python3 -c '\nimport json,sys\nraw=sys.stdin.read()\nd=json.loads(raw[raw.index(\"{\"):])\nprint(\"status:\", d[\"status\"])\nprint(\"assignee:\", repr(d.get(\"assignee\")))\nprint(\"labels:\", d.get(\"labels\"))\nprint(\"has_design:\", d.get(\"has_design\"))\nprint(\"design_len:\", len(d.get(\"design\") or \"\"))\nprint(\"notes:\", (d.get(\"notes\") or \"\")[:300])\n'\nloom complete\n","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-94e36e22-aaa6-4943-80dc-4232031203ce-29\nfc_82e07faa-6f1d-91eb-a29c-85c8895b5827_0","simpleCommands":["cat","wc","loom","cat","loom","loom","python3","loom"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cat","args":[],"fullText":"cat"},{"name":"wc","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-l"},{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/marathon-9-design.md"}],"fullText":"wc -l /tmp/marathon-9-design.md"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"update"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-9"},{"type":"concatenation","value":"--design=\"$(cat /tmp/marathon-9-design.md)\""},{"type":"word","value":"--design-format=markdown"}],"fullText":"loom data update MARATHON-9 --design=\"$(cat /tmp/marathon-9-design.md)\" --design-format=markdown"},{"name":"cat","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/marathon-9-design.md"}],"fullText":"cat /tmp/marathon-9-design.md"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"update"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-9"},{"type":"concatenation","value":"--notes=\"Design complete for POST /api/dms get-or-create. Key decisions: body requires user_id+workspace_id (workspace-scoped channels); always 200 {channel_id}; dedupe via deterministic dm- name hash (no migration — avoids M8/M12 v4 clash); is_dm+is_private; ensure both memberships; tighten DM authz to members-only (no workspace-owner bypass). Handed to review; implementer label remains backend.\""},{"type":"word","value":"--status"},{"type":"word","value":"review"},{"type":"concatenation","value":"--assignee=\"\""}],"fullText":"loom data update MARATHON-9 --notes=\"Design complete for POST /api/dms get-or-create. Key decisions: body requires user_id+workspace_id (workspace-scoped channels); always 200 {channel_id}; dedupe via deterministic dm- name hash (no migration — avoids M8/M12 v4 clash); is_dm+is_private; ensure both memberships; tighten DM authz to members-only (no workspace-owner bypass). Handed to review; implementer label remains backend.\" --status review --assignee=\"\""},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-9"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-9 --output json"},{"name":"python3","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"raw_string","value":"'\nimport json,sys\nraw=sys.stdin.read()\nd=json.loads(raw[raw.index(\"{\"):])\nprint(\"status:\", d[\"status\"])\nprint(\"assignee:\", repr(d.get(\"assignee\")))\nprint(\"labels:\", d.get(\"labels\"))\nprint(\"has_design:\", d.get(\"has_design\"))\nprint(\"design_len:\", len(d.get(\"design\") or \"\"))\nprint(\"notes:\", (d.get(\"notes\") or \"\")[:300])\n'"}],"fullText":"python3 -c '\nimport json,sys\nraw=sys.stdin.read()\nd=json.loads(raw[raw.index(\"{\"):])\nprint(\"status:\", d[\"status\"])\nprint(\"assignee:\", repr(d.get(\"assignee\")))\nprint(\"labels:\", d.get(\"labels\"))\nprint(\"has_design:\", d.get(\"has_design\"))\nprint(\"design_len:\", len(d.get(\"design\") or \"\"))\nprint(\"notes:\", (d.get(\"notes\") or \"\")[:300])\n'"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"complete"}],"fullText":"loom complete"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":true,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":false,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/marathon-9-design.md"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"cat"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Save design, hand off, loom complete","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"3f743427-f194-44bc-92dc-836b7b6940f7","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"cat > /tmp/marathon-9-design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds authenticated **get-or-create** for 1:1 direct-message channels: `POST /api/dms` resolves a workspace-scoped DM between the caller and a peer `user_id`, returning the same `channel_id` for both directions and on every repeat call. The channel is persisted as a normal `channels` row with `is_dm=true` (and `is_private=true` for visibility), both users in `channel_members`, so existing channel/message authz (MARATHON-7/8) and the SPA `dms-list` split (MARATHON-16) work without a separate message transport. It does not build group DMs, DM UI, or message posting.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Route | Top-level `POST /api/dms` (task-mandated), not nested under `/api/workspaces/{slug}` |\n| Request body | `{ \"user_id\", \"workspace_id\" }` — both required UUID strings. Task text abbreviated `{user_id}`; **workspace is mandatory** because every channel row has non-null `workspace_id` (MARATHON-5) and the shell lists DMs per current workspace |\n| Response | Always **200** `{ \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\" }` (not `201`, not a full `ChannelObj` wrapper) |\n| Pair identity | Canonical unordered pair: `user_lo, user_hi = sorted([caller_id, peer_id])` within a workspace |\n| Dedup without competing for migration v4 | **No new table.** Deterministic synthetic `channels.name` under existing `UNIQUE(workspace_id, name)`: `dm-` + first 29 hex chars of `SHA-256(workspace_id \\|\\| \":\" \\|\\| user_lo \\|\\| \":\" \\|\\| user_hi)` (ASCII, lower hex). Satisfies `CHANNEL_NAME_RE` (`^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`). Lookup = `SELECT` by `(workspace_id, name, is_dm=1)` |\n| Flags | Insert with `is_dm=1`, `is_private=1`, `topic=\"\"`, `is_archived=0` |\n| Membership | On create: insert **both** users into `channel_members`. On get (existing row): **ensure** both memberships exist (re-add if a party previously `leave`d) |\n| Package | New `server/dms/` router + thin store orchestration; channel row helpers live in `server/channels/store.py` next to `create_channel` |\n| DM privacy vs workspace owner | **Tighten** read/mutate gates for `is_dm`: channel **membership required**; workspace `owner_id` alone must **not** bypass (diverges from private-channel owner bypass in MARATHON-7 — justified so DMs are not readable by the workspace owner) |\n| List visibility | Keep/adjust `list_channels_for_workspace_user` so DMs never appear to non-members (defense in depth even if `is_private` were wrong) |\n| Migration | **None** for the happy path (avoids collision with MARATHON-8 and MARATHON-12, both designed as **v4**). Optional later `dm_pairs` table is out of scope |\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; error envelope `{error:{code,message}}` unchanged |\n| Ids / time | UUID4 channel ids; `utc_now_z()` timestamps |\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|-------------|------------------|\n| Body only `{user_id}` with implicit workspace | Multi-workspace users make the pair ambiguous; channels are workspace-scoped |\n| `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/dms` | Contradicts task path `POST /api/dms` already reserved by MARATHON-7 out-of-scope |\n| New `dm_pairs` table (migration) | Cleaner join, but **v4 is double-booked** by M8/M12; name-hash uniqueness reuses existing UNIQUE and ships without schema races |\n| Username-based channel `name` for display | Usernames allow `_` and up to 32 chars; fail `CHANNEL_NAME_RE` / length; display is asymmetric per viewer anyway |\n| Return full `{channel: ChannelObj}` | Task mandates `{channel_id}`; client refreshes workspace detail for list rows |\n| Global (non-workspace) DMs | No place in current schema; SPA DMs are per-workspace sidebar |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nOpaque synthetic `ChannelObj.name` for DMs (not a human display label). **MARATHON-17** must render DM sidebar labels from the peer `UserObj` (e.g. via `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` or members already known client-side), not from `name`. Until then, `dms-list` may show the synthetic name — acceptable for this backend-only task.\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Shared conventions (inherited)\n\n- Bearer `Authorization` required → missing/invalid → **401** `unauthorized` (MARATHON-3).\n- Errors: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"<code>\", \"message\": \"<human>\" } }` (MARATHON-3/4).\n- Pydantic bodies: `extra=\"ignore\"`; unknown keys ignored.\n- `ChannelObj` keys unchanged: `id`, `workspace_id`, `name`, `is_private`, `is_dm`, `topic`, `is_archived` (MARATHON-5/7).\n- Timestamps UTC `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/dms`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** (MARATHON-17 / future) | While user picks a peer in the current workspace, `POST /api/dms` with bearer + JSON body. On **200**, store/use `channel_id` (navigate message pane, refresh workspace detail so `dms-list` updates). Disable submit while in flight; do not invent a local channel id. |\n| **Server** | Validate body; authorize workspace membership for caller + peer; get-or-create DM; return `{channel_id}` only. |\n\n**Request**\n\n```http\nPOST /api/dms\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>\nContent-Type: application/json\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"user_id\": \"<peer-user-uuid>\",\n  \"workspace_id\": \"<workspace-uuid>\"\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Rules |\n|-------|------|----------|-------|\n| `user_id` | string | yes | Peer user id; must exist; must not equal caller; must be a `workspace_members` row for `workspace_id` |\n| `workspace_id` | string | yes | Existing workspace id; caller must be a member |\n\n**Response 200**\n\n```json\n{ \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\" }\n```\n\nExact key: `channel_id` only (no `channel` object, no extra fields required).\n\n**Status / error matrix**\n\n| Condition | Status | `code` | Notes |\n|-----------|--------|--------|-------|\n| Success (create or existing) | **200** | — | Same id both directions / repeats |\n| Missing/invalid bearer | **401** | `unauthorized` | |\n| Missing field / wrong type / empty string | **400** | `validation_error` | FastAPI envelope or explicit `ApiError` |\n| `user_id` == caller | **400** | `validation_error` | Message e.g. `cannot dm yourself` |\n| Unknown `workspace_id` or caller not a workspace member | **404** | `not_found` | Message `workspace not found` (no existence leak) |\n| Unknown `user_id` **or** peer not a member of that workspace | **404** | `not_found` | Message `user not found` (do not distinguish “exists globally but not in workspace”) |\n| SQLite busy after timeout | fail closed | — | Same as other routes; no partial membership |\n\n**Not used:** **403** for “peer not in workspace” (prefer 404 to match workspace non-member leak policy). Guests **may** DM other workspace members (no role gate beyond membership).\n\n### Seam: DM channel appearance on `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Server** | After create, both members see a `ChannelObj` with `is_dm=true` in `channels` (subject to archive filter). Non-members must **not** see it. |\n| **Client** (MARATHON-16 already) | Split `is_dm === true` → `dms-list`, else → `channel-list`. |\n\n### Seam: Authz tweaks for `is_dm` (server-owned)\n\nFor any existing channel route that today allows **workspace owner without channel membership** on private channels, when `channel.is_dm` is true:\n\n- **Require** `channel_members` row for the caller.\n- If workspace member but not channel member → **403** `forbidden` (same message family as private denial is fine).\n- If not a workspace member → **404** `not_found`.\n\nApplies at least to: channel members list, PATCH topic, GET pins, pin/unpin message, and (when MARATHON-8 lands) message read/write helpers — document for M8 implementer: **DM ⇒ member-only, no owner bypass**.\n\n`POST /api/channels/{id}/join` on a DM remains **403** for non-members (MARATHON-7); get-or-create is the only supported add path.\n\n### Client slow / fail summary\n\n| Condition | Client behavior |\n|-----------|-----------------|\n| In flight | Disable “open DM” control; keep prior `dms-list` |\n| 401 | Re-auth (MARATHON-16) |\n| 400 | Show `error.message`; stay on picker |\n| 404 | Show not-found / peer unavailable; do not add sidebar row |\n| Network / 5xx / timeout | Retry; do not assume channel exists until **200** |\n| 200 | Use `channel_id`; optionally re-fetch workspace detail |\n\n## Data Model\n\n### No new migration (preferred)\n\nUses existing v2 tables:\n\n- `channels` — new rows with `is_dm=1`, `is_private=1`, synthetic `name`, empty `topic`\n- `channel_members` — exactly the two participants (after ensure-membership)\n- `workspaces` / `workspace_members` / `users` — authz only\n\n### Synthetic name algorithm (normative)\n\n```\nuser_lo, user_hi = sorted([caller_id, peer_id])  # lexicographic UUID string order\ndigest = SHA-256( f\"{workspace_id}:{user_lo}:{user_hi}\".encode(\"utf-8\") ).hexdigest()\nname = \"dm-\" + digest[:29]   # length 32; charset [a-z0-9-]\n```\n\nInvariant: name depends only on `(workspace_id, unordered user pair)` — **not** on who called.\n\n### Channel row fields on create\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|--------|\n| `id` | new UUID4 |\n| `workspace_id` | from body |\n| `name` | synthetic as above |\n| `is_private` | `1` |\n| `is_dm` | `1` |\n| `topic` | `\"\"` |\n| `is_archived` | `0` |\n| `created_at` / `updated_at` | `utc_now_z()` |\n\n### List-query defense (in scope)\n\nUpdate `list_channels_for_workspace_user` visibility predicate from “public OR member” to:\n\n- visible if **member**, OR\n- visible if **`is_dm=0` AND `is_private=0`** (true public)\n\nEquivalently: `(c.is_dm = 0 AND c.is_private = 0) OR cm.user_id IS NOT NULL`.\n\n### Schema change summary\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| No DDL | **Yes** |\n| List SQL predicate tighten | **Yes** — only hides rows that should not have been visible |\n| DM owner-bypass removal | Behavior change for owners on `is_dm` only |\n\n### Invariants\n\n1. At most one `is_dm` channel per `(workspace_id, unordered user pair)` (enforced by deterministic name + UNIQUE).\n2. `POST .../channels` still forces `is_dm=false` (MARATHON-7).\n3. Get-or-create never creates a second row for the same pair.\n4. After a successful `POST /api/dms`, both users have `channel_members` rows.\n5. `ChannelObj.is_dm === true` for these rows; SPA list split continues to work.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/dms/__init__.py` | Package marker / docstring: DM get-or-create owned here |\n| `server/dms/routes.py` | `APIRouter(prefix=\"/api/dms\")`; `POST \"\"` handler; pydantic body; transaction; map errors |\n| `server/dms/store.py` | `canonical_dm_name(...)`; `get_or_create_dm_channel(conn, *, workspace_id, caller_id, peer_id) -> channel_id`; peer/workspace checks raising `ApiError` |\n| `tests/test_dms.py` | Contract tests (see Testing Strategy) |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/app.py` | `include_router` for dms router |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | Add `create_dm_channel(...)` (bypass public name validation path used by user-created channels **or** validate synthetic name after generation); fix `list_channels_for_workspace_user` predicate for DM/private; optional `find_dm_by_name` |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | In `_require_channel_read_access`, pin list, PATCH, leave as needed: **`is_dm` ⇒ membership required** (no owner-only bypass) |\n| `server/messages/routes.py` | Same DM membership rule in `_require_pin_access` (and document for M8 shared helper) |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/**` | MARATHON-17 owns DM picker UI; M16 list split already correct |\n| `server/db.py` | No migration in this design |\n| `server/auth/**`, `server/users/**` | Consume `get_user_by_id` / deps only |\n| Message CRUD routes | MARATHON-8 |\n| IRC / WS / Redis | MARATHON-13/14/15 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order (this task)\n\n1. `channels/store.py` — `create_dm_channel` + list predicate.\n2. `dms/store.py` + `dms/routes.py` + mount in `app.py`.\n3. Authz tighten for `is_dm` in channel/message routes.\n4. `tests/test_dms.py` (+ any small assertion updates if list tests assume old predicate).\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Independent of MARATHON-8 message CRUD **except** shared DM authz rule (coordinate via this design’s Interface Contracts).\n- Independent of MARATHON-12 groups/invitations.\n- MARATHON-17 can stub against this contract once merged.\n\n### Cross-task seams\n\n| Contract | Owner | Consumer |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| `POST /api/dms` → `{channel_id}` | **MARATHON-9** | MARATHON-17 (DM open), graders |\n| `ChannelObj.is_dm` + list visibility | MARATHON-5/7 + **this list fix** | MARATHON-16 shell, MARATHON-17 |\n| DM member-only authz (no owner bypass) | **MARATHON-9** | MARATHON-8 message helpers must match |\n| Message post in DM channel | MARATHON-8 | Needs channel membership (created here) |\n| DM display labels / picker UI | MARATHON-17 | Uses `channel_id` + members/profiles |\n\n### Declared dependents\n\n- MARATHON-17 (SPA channels/DMs UX)\n- MARATHON-8 (messages in DM channels; authz note)\n\n### Follow-up cuts (do not implement here)\n\n- Group DMs / multi-user conversations.\n- `dm_pairs` table if hash-in-name is ever insufficient.\n- Forbidding archive/leave on DMs.\n- Client-side peer label rendering.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| SPA DM picker / open-DM button / peer label | `static/js/*`, MARATHON-17 | Frontend task; shell already has empty-capable `dms-list` |\n| Message send/list inside DM | MARATHON-8 | Separate REST surface |\n| Search / read_state / slash | MARATHON-11 | |\n| WS fan-out `channel` events | MARATHON-13/14 | |\n| IRC DM mapping | MARATHON-15 | |\n| Group DMs | — | Not in task |\n| Changing private-channel **owner** bypass for non-DM privates | `channels/routes.py` | Keep MARATHON-7 behavior for `is_private && !is_dm` |\n| `POST /api/channels` creating `is_dm` | already forbidden | Remains forbidden |\n| Migration v4/v5 DDL | `server/db.py` | Avoid M8/M12 version collision; name uniqueness sufficient |\n| `channel-add-member-*` for DMs | SPA hooks | DMs are pair-only via this endpoint |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `server/channels/store.py` `is_dm` always false on create; list predicate | **In scope** — DM create helper + list fix |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` private/DM treated alike; owner bypass | **In scope** — DM membership tighten |\n| `server/messages/routes.py` private/DM pin authz | **In scope** — same DM rule |\n| `server/db.py` `is_dm` column | **Unchanged** |\n| `static/js/shell.js` `dms-list` / `is_dm` split | **Out of scope** — already correct |\n| `tests/test_channels.py` `is_dm is False` on normal create | **Out of scope** — keep; add `test_dms.py` |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` / `test_workspaces.py` `is_dm` assertions | **Out of scope** unless list predicate breaks a fixture |\n| Grep: no `/api/dms` router yet | Greenfield `server/dms` |\n| MARATHON-7/8/16 designs reserving `POST /api/dms` | **This task** |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| A→B then B→A | Same `channel_id` |\n| Repeat A→B | Same `channel_id`; **200**; no second row |\n| Concurrent A→B and B→A | One INSERT wins; loser hits UNIQUE/`IntegrityError` on `(workspace_id,name)` → re-SELECT by name → return existing id (no **500**) |\n| Caller left DM earlier | Ensure re-INSERT `channel_members` for caller (and peer if missing); return same id |\n| Peer left DM earlier | Same ensure-both-memberships |\n| Self `user_id` | **400** `validation_error` |\n| Peer not in workspace | **404** `user not found` |\n| Caller not in workspace | **404** `workspace not found` |\n| Archived DM exists | Still return its `channel_id` (do not create replacement). Messaging may **423** via existing guard (MARATHON-7/8) |\n| Workspace owner not in DM opens channel routes | **403** (member of ws) / **404** (stranger) — **not** owner bypass |\n| Guest DMs a member | **200** if both are workspace members |\n| Extra body keys | Ignored |\n| `workspace_id` is a slug string | **404** (id lookup fails) — clients must send UUID `workspace.id` |\n| User creates public channel whose name collides with a DM hash | Astronomically unlikely; if IntegrityError on DM insert and re-read finds non-`is_dm` row → **409** `conflict` with clear message (abort; do not hijack) |\n| Unauthenticated | **401** |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Authenticated `POST /api/dms` with `{user_id, workspace_id}` for two distinct workspace members → **200** `{ \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\" }`.\n2. Calling again with the same pair (same caller) → **200** with **identical** `channel_id`.\n3. Peer calling with the caller’s id (swapped direction) → **200** with the **same** `channel_id`.\n4. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` as either participant includes a channel with that id where `is_dm === true` (and typically `is_private === true`).\n5. A third workspace member’s workspace detail must **NOT** include that DM channel.\n6. Persisted row has `is_dm=1` (verify via API list/detail or DB in tests).\n7. Self-DM → **400** `validation_error`; must **NOT** create a channel.\n8. Unknown peer id → **404**; must **NOT** create a channel.\n9. Peer registered globally but not in workspace → **404**; must **NOT** create a channel.\n10. Caller not in workspace → **404**.\n11. Unauthenticated → **401**.\n12. After participant `POST /api/channels/{id}/leave`, a subsequent `POST /api/dms` for the same pair returns the **same** `channel_id` and restores membership (subsequent channel member list / message write authz succeeds for that user).\n13. Workspace owner who is **not** a DM member must **NOT** read DM pins/members via owner bypass (**403** or **404** per rules above).\n14. Negative: `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` still cannot create `is_dm=true` channels.\n15. Negative: response must **NOT** require a `channel` object key for success (only `channel_id`).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated (`tests/test_dms.py`)\n\n- Happy path create + idempotent repeat + reverse direction same id.\n- Both users see DM on workspace detail; third member does not.\n- Self / missing peer / non-member peer / non-member caller / unauthenticated.\n- Leave then get-or-create restores membership.\n- Owner-without-membership denied on `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` (or pins) for the DM.\n- Optional: concurrent create smoke (two threads) still yields one row.\n- Regression: existing `tests/test_channels.py` / `test_workspaces.py` stay green.\n\n### Manual / cluster\n\n1. Register users A,B,C; create workspace; add B and C as members.\n2. On `:8000`, A `POST /api/dms` with B → note `channel_id`.\n3. On `:8001`, B `POST /api/dms` with A → same id (shared SQLite).\n4. A and B `GET` workspace detail → DM present; C’s detail → absent.\n5. Confirm `is_dm` true in listed channel object.\n\n### Human verify\n\n- No SPA change required; `curl`/httpie against any node with bearer token is enough for this task.\nDESIGN_EOF\nwc -l /tmp/marathon-9-design.md\nloom data update MARATHON-9 --design=\"$(cat /tmp/marathon-9-design.md)\" --design-format=markdown\nloom data update MARATHON-9 --notes=\"Design complete for POST /api/dms get-or-create. Key decisions: body requires user_id+workspace_id (workspace-scoped channels); always 200 {channel_id}; dedupe via deterministic dm- name hash (no migration — avoids M8/M12 v4 clash); is_dm+is_private; ensure both memberships; tighten DM authz to members-only (no workspace-owner bypass). Handed to review; implementer label remains backend.\" --status review --assignee=\"\"\nloom data show MARATHON-9 --output json | python3 -c '\nimport json,sys\nraw=sys.stdin.read()\nd=json.loads(raw[raw.index(\"{\"):])\nprint(\"status:\", d[\"status\"])\nprint(\"assignee:\", repr(d.get(\"assignee\")))\nprint(\"labels:\", d.get(\"labels\"))\nprint(\"has_design:\", d.get(\"has_design\"))\nprint(\"design_len:\", len(d.get(\"design\") or \"\"))\nprint(\"notes:\", (d.get(\"notes\") or \"\")[:300])\n'\nloom complete\n","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"343 /tmp/marathon-9-design.md\nupdated MARATHON-9\nupdated MARATHON-9\nstatus: review\nassignee: None\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\nhas_design: True\ndesign_len: 18939\nnotes: Design complete for POST /api/dms get-or-create. Key decisions: body requires user_id+workspace_id (workspace-scoped channels); always 200 {channel_id}; dedupe via deterministic dm- name hash (no migration — avoids M8/M12 v4 clash); is_dm+is_private; ensure both memberships; tighten DM authz to memb\nTask completion signaled\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T00:28:09.520Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":198,"interleavedOutput":"343 /tmp/marathon-9-design.md\nupdated MARATHON-9\nupdated MARATHON-9\ntime=2026-08-23T00:28:09.520Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\nstatus: review\nassignee: None\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\nhas_design: True\ndesign_len: 18939\nnotes: Design complete for POST /api/dms get-or-create. Key decisions: body requires user_id+workspace_id (workspace-scoped channels); always 200 {channel_id}; dedupe via deterministic dm- name hash (no migration — avoids M8/M12 v4 clash); is_dm+is_private; ensure both memberships; tighten DM authz to memb\nTask completion signaled\n","localExecutionTimeMs":90},"isBackground":false},"description":"Save design, hand off, loom complete"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-94e36e22-aaa6-4943-80dc-4232031203ce-29\nfc_82e07faa-6f1d-91eb-a29c-85c8895b5827_0","startedAtMs":"1787444889359","completedAtMs":"1787444889557"},"model_call_id":"b6dbef0b-e6fb-4ca9-8c38-d48246858510-10-bia0","session_id":"3f743427-f194-44bc-92dc-836b7b6940f7","timestamp_ms":1787444889584}
