{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-7bb3e7d2-436f-4bd5-ad8f-c072f1d79931-52\nfc_09c64263-1886-982a-8d37-44886c1841f2_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cat > /tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n# MARATHON-18 — SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the Huddle SPA settings surface on top of the MARATHON-16 shell: a **workspace settings modal** (tabs General / Members / Invitations) and a **channel settings modal** (members list/add, topic, archive/unarchive). It wires those UIs to the already-shipped REST seams from MARATHON-6/7/12 (`PATCH` workspace, members/roles/transfer, invitations create/list/revoke/accept, channel members/topic/archive) and locks the epic’s stable DOM ids plus `settings-*` / `invitation-*` / role / channel-member `data-testid`s so CUA/Playwright can drive admin flows at 1280×900. It also specifies the missing **channel add-member** REST seam that MARATHON-7 deferred, because the channel-settings “add” control cannot work against join alone for private channels.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Delivery | Extend the **zero-build vanilla SPA** (`static/` ES modules) — same stack as MARATHON-16; no bundler |\n| Module split | New `static/js/settings_ui.js` owns both modals; `shell.js` exposes open triggers + active workspace/channel; reuse `api.js` / `storage.js` |\n| Modal pattern | Match `auth-modal`: overlay + panel, `hidden` attribute, `role=\"dialog\"`, Escape/close dismiss; **one settings modal open at a time** |\n| Workspace entry | `data-testid=\"workspace-settings-btn\"` in `workspace-header` (visible whenever shell shows a workspace) |\n| Channel entry | Selecting a non-DM channel in `channel-list` sets active channel; `data-testid=\"channel-settings-btn\"` in message-pane header chrome (or beside channel list) opens channel settings for that id — **does not** require MARATHON-17 message composer |\n| Tabs | Workspace modal: exactly three tabs — `general`, `members`, `invitations`; only one panel visible |\n| Authz UX | Client **hides/disables** privileged controls from cached caller role; server remains SoT (403/404 still shown as `error.message`) |\n| Invitation redeem | Onboarding gains an **accept-by-code** form (M12 assigned redeem UX to this task); settings tab is create/list/revoke only |\n| Channel add-member | New backend seam `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (this design owns the contract); frontend labeled implementer may land the thin route or a tiny backend follow-up must land first — see Sequencing |\n| Selectors | Exact strings below; prefer `data-testid`; required **DOM ids**: `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic requires settings + invitations in the SPA with stable selectors; M16 explicitly deferred settings modals here.\n- Backend contracts for name/join_mode, roles, invitations, topic, archive, channel member list are closed (M6/7/12); inventing alternate envelopes would break graders and sibling designs.\n- M7’s neighborhood note already flagged `channel-add-member-*` without REST — shipping UI without an add seam leaves private-channel “add” untestable.\n- Keeping vanilla modules preserves `start.sh` / no-Node ops.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Fold settings into MARATHON-17 message chrome only | Blocks settings QA until messages land; task is independent with `frontend` label |\n| “Add member” = tell user to `POST .../join` | Fails for private channels (403 without membership); hooks expect add controls |\n| Profile PATCH inside General tab | Task tabs are name/join_mode/members/invitations only; profile is a different surface |\n| Groups CRUD UI | MARATHON-12 groups API exists but is not in this task description |\n| React settings app | Diverges from M16 zero-build convention |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nChannel add-member needs a **small backend POST** that did not ship in M7. This design locks that seam so SPA and server can be implemented in parallel; if the implementer is frontend-only, the lead should keep `frontend` and optionally add a short backend subtask — **do not** fake add via SQL in the browser.\n\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n\nFrom **MARATHON-16**: vanilla SPA; `api()` + bearer; `{error:{code,message}}`; visible form errors; `hidden` for unused chrome; hash `#/w/{slug}`; token keys unchanged.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-5/6**: `WorkspaceObj` keys `{id,slug,name,owner_id,join_mode}`; `join_mode` ∈ {`open`,`invite_only`}; `MemberObj` `{user_id,role,username,display_name}`; roles `owner|admin|member|guest`; non-member → 404; privilege → 403; PATCH workspace name/join_mode; PATCH member role matrix; `POST .../transfer_ownership`.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj` keys; `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` → `{members: UserObj[]}`; `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}`; `POST .../archive` / `.../unarchive` owner-only; archived topic writes → **423** `archived`; leave/join exist but settings “add” is not join.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-12**: `InvitationObj`; create/list/revoke/accept envelopes; invite_only join still 403 without accept.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-3/4**: `UserObj` keys on channel members list; bearer auth.\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\n\nAll names are **`data-testid` values** unless noted as **DOM `id`**. Elements must exist in the DOM when the corresponding UI is shown (not only as JS string constants). Product “frontend hooks” are not checked into this repo; the table below is **normative** for this task and matches the task wording (`settings-*`, `invitation-*`, role/channel-member names from sibling designs).\n\n#### Required DOM ids\n\n| `id` | Element |\n|------|---------|\n| `workspace-settings-modal` | Workspace settings overlay/dialog root |\n| `channel-settings-modal` | Channel settings overlay/dialog root |\n| `create-invitation-form` | Form that creates a workspace invitation |\n\nAlso set matching `data-testid` equal to the id string for the three roots/forms above (so either selector style works).\n\n#### Open / chrome\n\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\n|---------------|--------------|------|\n| `workspace-settings-btn` | Shell with current workspace | Opens workspace settings modal |\n| `channel-settings-btn` | Shell with an active non-DM channel | Opens channel settings for that channel |\n| `workspace-settings-close` | Workspace modal open | Closes workspace modal |\n| `channel-settings-close` | Channel modal open | Closes channel modal |\n\n#### Workspace settings — tabs & general\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `settings-tab-general` | Selects General tab |\n| `settings-tab-members` | Selects Members tab |\n| `settings-tab-invitations` | Selects Invitations tab |\n| `settings-panel-general` | General panel region |\n| `settings-panel-members` | Members panel region |\n| `settings-panel-invitations` | Invitations panel region |\n| `settings-name` | Workspace display name `<input>` |\n| `settings-join-mode` | `<select>` or radio group; values `open` \\| `invite_only` |\n| `settings-general-save` | Submit/save general settings |\n| `settings-general-error` | Visible error text for general save failures |\n| `settings-general-success` | Optional brief success indicator (may be aria-live); not required if save is silently successful and fields reflect server |\n\n**Negative:** Member/guest must **not** successfully persist general changes; controls may be disabled **or** save shows `settings-general-error` with server `error.message` (403).\n\n#### Workspace settings — members\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `settings-members-list` | Container for member rows |\n| `settings-member-row` | One row per `MemberObj` (may appear multiple times) |\n| `role-badge` | Read-only role label on a row (always present) |\n| `role-select` | `<select>` to change role when actor may edit that row; **absent or `disabled`** when actor cannot |\n| `settings-members-error` | Visible error for list/PATCH failures |\n| `settings-members-loading` | Optional loading marker while `GET .../members` in flight |\n| `settings-transfer-owner` | Owner-only control to transfer ownership (confirm + target admin) |\n| `settings-transfer-owner-select` | Admin target picker |\n| `settings-transfer-owner-submit` | Confirm transfer |\n| `settings-transfer-error` | Transfer error text |\n\nEach `settings-member-row` **must** expose `data-user-id=\"{user_id}\"`.\n\n`role-select` options: `admin`, `member`, `guest` only (never `owner` — ownership uses transfer).\n\n#### Workspace settings — invitations\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `create-invitation-form` | Same as DOM id; create form |\n| `invitation-max-uses` | Optional number input (default server 1 if empty) |\n| `invitation-expires-seconds` | Optional expiry seconds input |\n| `invitation-username` | Optional targeted username |\n| `invitation-create-submit` | Create submit control |\n| `invitation-create-error` | Visible create error |\n| `invitation-list` | Active invitations list container |\n| `invitation-row` | One row per active invitation |\n| `invitation-code` | Displays `InvitationObj.code` (copyable text) |\n| `invitation-revoke` | Revoke control on a row |\n| `invitation-list-error` | List/revoke error |\n\nEach `invitation-row` **must** expose `data-invitation-code=\"{code}\"` (and/or `data-invitation-id`).\n\nNon-admin: invitations tab may show a short “Admins only” empty state; create form and list fetch must **not** be required to succeed for members (hide form **or** show 403 in `invitation-list-error` without crashing).\n\n#### Onboarding — accept invitation (redeem)\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `invitation-accept-form` | Onboarding form (sibling to join-by-slug) |\n| `invitation-accept-code` | Code input |\n| `invitation-accept-submit` | Submit |\n| `invitation-accept-error` | Visible error |\n\n#### Channel settings\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `channel-settings-modal` | Modal root (also DOM id) |\n| `settings-topic` | Topic `<input>` / textarea |\n| `settings-topic-save` | Save topic |\n| `settings-topic-error` | Topic error (incl. 423 archived) |\n| `settings-archive` | Archive button (owner) |\n| `settings-unarchive` | Unarchive button (owner) |\n| `settings-archive-error` | Archive/unarchive error |\n| `channel-members-list` | Channel members container |\n| `channel-member-row` | One row per `UserObj` |\n| `channel-add-member-input` | Username or user id input for add |\n| `channel-add-member-submit` | Add submit |\n| `channel-add-member-error` | Add error |\n| `channel-members-error` | List error |\n\nEach `channel-member-row` **must** expose `data-user-id=\"{id}\"` (UserObj `id`).\n\nArchive vs unarchive: show the action that matches current `is_archived` (one primary control is enough; the other may stay in DOM but `hidden`).\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET/PATCH /api/workspaces/{slug}` (General tab)\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On open: seed `settings-name` / `settings-join-mode` from in-memory `WorkspaceObj`. Save → `PATCH` body subset `{name?, join_mode?}`. Disable `settings-general-save` while in flight. On **200**: replace cached workspace; refresh `workspace-header`. On **400/403**: show `error.message` in `settings-general-error`. On **401**: logout (M16). On **404**: close modal, leave workspace. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-6). |\n\n**Slow:** keep prior field values; do not clear the form.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}/members` + `PATCH .../members/{user_id}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On Members tab select / modal open: `GET` members. While slow: show `settings-members-loading` or keep prior rows. On **200**: render rows ordered as server returns; every row has `role-badge`; editable rows get `role-select` preselected to current role. On change of `role-select`: `PATCH` `{role}` immediately (or on explicit apply — **prefer immediate**). On **403/400**: revert select to last known role; show `settings-members-error`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-6 matrix). |\n\n**Who sees `role-select`:**\n\n| Actor role | Target | UI |\n|------------|--------|-----|\n| owner | admin/member/guest | `role-select` enabled |\n| owner | owner (self) | badge only |\n| admin | member/guest | `role-select` enabled |\n| admin | admin/owner | badge only |\n| member/guest | anyone | badge only |\n\nCaller role: derive from members list (`user_id === session user`) or from detail if already known.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/transfer_ownership`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Visible only if caller is workspace owner. Body `{new_owner_id}` from admin-only select. Confirm (browser `confirm` OK). On **200**: refresh workspace + members. On **400/403**: `settings-transfer-error`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-6). |\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ invitations (create / list / revoke / accept)\n\n#### Create — `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations` → **201** `{invitation}`\n\nClient body (omit empty optionals):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"expires_in_seconds\": 86400,\n  \"max_uses\": 5,\n  \"invited_username\": \"ada\"\n}\n```\n\nDisable submit while in flight; on success prepend/refresh list and show `invitation-code` on the new row; on 400/403 show `invitation-create-error`.\n\n#### List — `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations` → **200** `{invitations:[InvitationObj]}`\n\nLoad when Invitations tab opens (admin). On 403 show admin-only message.\n\n#### Revoke — `DELETE /api/invitations/{code}` → **200** `{revoked:true}`\n\nRemove row on success; on 404 refresh list.\n\n#### Accept — `POST /api/invitations/{code}/accept` → **200** `{workspace, channels?, read_state?}`\n\nFrom onboarding form: on success call existing `enterWorkspace` path (persist slug, show shell) using returned payload (fetch detail if channels omitted). On 403/404 show `invitation-accept-error`.\n\n**Server:** Unchanged (MARATHON-12).\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ channel topic / archive / members list\n\n| API | Client behavior |\n|-----|-----------------|\n| `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` | Fill `channel-members-list`; slow → keep prior / empty with loading |\n| `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}` | Save from `settings-topic`; **423** → message in `settings-topic-error` and disable further topic edits until unarchived |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/archive` | Owner; on 200 set local `is_archived=true`, swap buttons, refresh shell channel list if archived channels are hidden by default |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/unarchive` | Owner; opposite |\n\nNon-owner: hide `settings-archive` / `settings-unarchive` (or disable). Topic save allowed for channel member or workspace owner per M7; others show 403 in error region.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (**new**; owned by this design)\n\nMissing today (M7 out-of-scope). Required for channel settings add.\n\n**Request**\n\n```http\nPOST /api/channels/{channel_id}/members\nAuthorization: Bearer …\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{ \"username\": \"ada\" }\n```\n\nAlternate accepted field: `{ \"user_id\": \"<uuid>\" }`. If both sent, must resolve to the same user else **400**. Unknown keys ignored. Exactly one of `username` / `user_id` required.\n\n**Authz / rules**\n\n1. Unknown channel → **404**.\n2. Caller must be **workspace member**; else **404** (no leak).\n3. Caller must be workspace **owner or admin**, **or** an existing **channel member** with workspace role ∈ {owner, admin, member} — **guest cannot add** → **403**.\n4. Target user must be a **workspace member** → else **400** `validation_error` (cannot add outsiders via this route; use workspace invitations first).\n5. Private or public: INSERT into `channel_members` if missing; idempotent if already member → **200**.\n6. DM channels (`is_dm=true`): **403** (DM membership is MARATHON-9).\n7. Archived channel: add membership **allowed** (membership mgmt, not a 423 “write” like topic/pin) — consistent with leave-on-archived in M7.\n\n**Response 200**\n\n```json\n{ \"members\": [ /* UserObj[], same shape/order as GET members */ ] }\n```\n\n(Prefer full refreshed list so SPA can re-render without a second GET.)\n\n**Client:** submit `channel-add-member-input` as username (trim); disable submit in flight; on 200 replace list; on 4xx show `channel-add-member-error`.\n\n---\n\n### HTTP client rules\n\nReuse MARATHON-16 `api()`: JSON, bearer, 15s timeout, envelope parse, 401 → logout. Never invent cookies.\n\n### Modal UX rules\n\n1. Opening workspace settings closes channel settings (and vice versa).\n2. Backdrop click and Escape close the active modal without saving pending edits (except already-fired role PATCH / invitation create).\n3. Switching workspace (hash/list) closes both modals.\n4. Viewport: usable at **1280×900**; modal panel scrollable if members list is long.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Browser / in-memory (no SQLite migration required for SPA-only path)\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `currentWorkspace` | `WorkspaceObj` | Already in shell; General tab mutates via PATCH |\n| `callerRole` | string \\| null | From members list or inferred |\n| `workspaceMembers` | `MemberObj[]` | Settings cache |\n| `invitations` | `InvitationObj[]` | Admin cache |\n| `activeChannel` | `ChannelObj` \\| null | For channel settings |\n| `channelMembers` | `UserObj[]` | Channel settings cache |\n\n### Server schema\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| SPA-only selectors/HTML/JS | N/A — no schema |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` | **No DDL** — uses existing `channel_members` (v2). Backward compatible additive route |\n\n### Entities (unchanged shapes)\n\n- `WorkspaceObj`, `MemberObj`, `InvitationObj`, `ChannelObj`, `UserObj` — exact keys per M5/6/7/12. **Do not** nest extra fields in settings payloads.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/js/settings_ui.js` | Workspace + channel modal controllers; tab switching; all settings API calls; role-select / invitation / topic / archive / add-member handlers; exports `initSettingsUi(ctx)` |\n| `tests/test_spa_settings.py` | TestClient: HTML contains required ids/testids; static JS references key API paths; optional smoke that create_app still serves `/` |\n| `tests/test_channel_add_member.py` | **If** backend route lands with this task: authz matrix, idempotent add, guest 403, non-workspace target 400, DM 403 |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/index.html` | Add both modals (hidden), invitation accept form in onboarding, workspace/channel settings buttons hooks; all required testids/ids in markup (rows may be JS-generated but modal chrome + forms must be present for SPA shell tests) |\n| `static/css/app.css` | Modal/tab/list styles consistent with auth-modal; do not break 1280×900 shell |\n| `static/js/shell.js` | Wire `workspace-settings-btn`; track `activeChannel` on channel-list click; expose getters (`getWorkspace`, `getActiveChannel`, `refreshWorkspaceDetail`, `enterWorkspace`) to settings module; mount invitation-accept form submit |\n| `static/js/app.js` | `initSettingsUi` after shell init |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | Extend `REQUIRED_TESTIDS` (or sibling list) with stable settings chrome ids that must appear in initial HTML (`workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form`, tab testids, invitation-accept-*) |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Add `POST /{channel_id}/members` per contract above |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | Helper `add_channel_member` / reuse insert; list members after add |\n\n### Do not modify\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/workspaces/**`, `server/invitations/**` | Contracts already ship; SPA consumes |\n| `server/db.py` migrations | No schema change |\n| `start.sh` / `timer.sh` | No build step |\n| Message composer / thread panel behavior | MARATHON-17 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order within this task\n\n1. HTML modal shells + CSS + required testids (unblocks selector tests).\n2. `settings_ui.js` General tab → PATCH workspace.\n3. Members tab → GET/PATCH members + transfer.\n4. Invitations tab → create/list/revoke; onboarding accept form.\n5. Channel settings → topic/archive/members list.\n6. Channel add-member route + UI last (or parallel once contract fixed).\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- SPA work can proceed against existing M6/7/12 APIs immediately.\n- Add-member UI blocked on `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` implementation (same PR or tiny backend follow-up).\n- Independent of MARATHON-17 messages **except** shared `channel-list` click / active channel — this task may set active channel for settings without opening thread panel.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumer |\n|----------|----------|\n| Settings / invitation / role / channel-member `data-testid` set | QA / CUA |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` | SPA channel settings; future slash invites |\n| `initSettingsUi` / open-modal hooks | MARATHON-17 may call `openChannelSettings(channelId)` from message header |\n\n### Dependencies\n\n- **Requires closed:** MARATHON-16 (shell), MARATHON-6 (members), MARATHON-7 (channel topic/archive/members GET), MARATHON-12 (invitations).\n- **Does not require:** MARATHON-8/13/14/17.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not recreate existing tasks)\n\n- User groups settings UI → new task if needed (not this description).\n- Profile / `PATCH /api/users/me` UI → separate settings surface.\n- Channel leave button in settings → optional later; leave API exists (M7) but not required by this task text.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| Message composer, reactions, thread panel open | `static/js/*`, MARATHON-17 | Different SPA task |\n| User groups CRUD UI | `settings-*` could grow; `server/groups` | Not in MARATHON-18 description |\n| Profile PATCH UI | `PATCH /api/users/me` | M16 deferred “profile” vaguely to settings; **this** task’s General tab is workspace name/join_mode only |\n| Pins UI | `/api/channels/{id}/pins` | Channel settings text is members/topic/archive only |\n| WebSocket live member updates | MARATHON-13 | Poll/refetch on tab open is enough |\n| IRC | MARATHON-15 | Unrelated |\n| Changing invitation accept semantics / join_mode gates | `server/invitations/**`, `server/workspaces/routes.py` join | Already shipped; SPA consumes |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` as substitute for add-member | existing join route | Wrong authz for private add; out of scope as the add mechanism |\n| React/Vite migration | — | Conflicts with M16 |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `static/index.html`, `static/js/shell.js`, `static/js/app.js`, `static/css/app.css` | **In scope** — extend |\n| `static/js/api.js`, `storage.js`, `auth_ui.js` | **Reuse** — no contract change |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | **In scope** — extend required selectors |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` GET members / PATCH / archive | **Consume**; add POST members |\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` PATCH/members/transfer | **Consume only** |\n| `server/invitations/routes.py` | **Consume only** |\n| `tests/test_workspace_members.py`, `test_invitations.py`, `test_channels.py` | **Out of scope** to rewrite; keep green; add new tests |\n| Grep `settings-` / `invitation-` in `static/` | No hits yet — greenfield UI |\n| M7 note `channel-add-member-*` | **In scope** via new POST + testids |\n| Groups package | **Out of scope** UI |\n| `server/events.py` | **Out of scope** |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Open workspace settings without admin role | Modal opens; General fields disabled or save → 403 visible; Members badge-only; Invitations admin-only empty/error |\n| PATCH general with blank name | Client may pre-check; server **400** → `settings-general-error` |\n| Invalid join_mode option | Must not be choosable in UI; if forced, server 400 |\n| Role select to `owner` | **Must not** be an option |\n| Admin tries to demote another admin | No select **or** PATCH 403 → revert + error |\n| Transfer to non-admin | Client only lists admins; server 400 if forced |\n| Create invitation as member | 403 → `invitation-create-error`; modal stays open |\n| Revoke already-used/expired code | 404 → refresh list (row disappears) |\n| Accept invalid/expired code | 404 → `invitation-accept-error`; stay on onboarding |\n| Accept targeted invite as wrong user | 403 → visible error |\n| Accept success while already member | 200 → enter workspace (idempotent) |\n| Topic save on archived channel | 423 → `settings-topic-error`; suggest unarchive |\n| Archive by non-owner | Control hidden/disabled; if called, 403 error |\n| Archive `#general` | Allowed if owner (server permits); UI does not special-case unless server errors |\n| Add member unknown username | 400 → `channel-add-member-error` |\n| Add member who is not workspace member | 400 → same |\n| Add to DM channel | Button hidden for `is_dm`; if called, 403 |\n| Add when already member | 200; list unchanged except refresh |\n| Network timeout | Visible error on active form; re-enable controls |\n| 401 on any settings call | Clear tokens; show auth modal; close settings |\n| Double-click save | Disable control until response; single in-flight request |\n| Modal open during workspace switch | Close modals; drop stale channel id |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `GET /` HTML includes DOM ids `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` and the normative `data-testid`s listed above for modal chrome, tabs, general fields, invitation accept form, and channel settings fields (list rows may be empty until data loads).\n2. Authenticated owner/admin can open workspace settings, change **name** and **join_mode**, save, and see updates in `workspace-header` / subsequent `GET` workspace detail.\n3. Member/guest **cannot** persist general settings (disabled UI and/or visible 403); must **not** silently succeed.\n4. Members tab lists all workspace members with `role-badge`; owner/admin can change permitted roles via `role-select`; forbidden changes show error and do **not** leave a lying UI role.\n5. Owner can transfer ownership to an admin via transfer controls; previous owner becomes admin in the refreshed list.\n6. Admin/owner can create an invitation; `invitation-code` is visible; list shows active invites; revoke removes the row.\n7. Onboarding `invitation-accept-*` redeems a valid code and enters the workspace shell; invite_only workspaces become accessible without using broken join-by-slug alone.\n8. With an active public/private channel, channel settings shows members (`channel-member-row`), allows topic save for authorized callers, and owner can archive/unarchive with UI reflecting `is_archived`.\n9. Topic save on archived channel surfaces **423** message and must **not** clear the topic field to empty on failure.\n10. Channel add-member with a workspace member username adds them to `channel_members` (UI list updates); guest cannot add; outsider username fails visibly.\n11. Opening one settings modal closes the other; logout closes modals and clears privileged data from the DOM on next login.\n12. Existing MARATHON-16 selectors and auth/workspace flows remain green (`tests/test_spa_shell.py` + prior SPA behavior).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated\n\n- Extend/add TestClient tests asserting required ids/testids in `GET /` and that `settings_ui.js` is served as a static asset.\n- Backend tests for `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` matrix (owner/admin/member/guest, private/public, idempotent, DM rejection, non-member target).\n- Do **not** require a browser in unit CI; optional Playwright (as M16 notes) at 1280×900 for human/agent verification.\n\n### Manual / CUA script (1280×900)\n\n1. Register → create workspace → open workspace settings → rename + set `invite_only` → save → reload → values stick.\n2. Add second user via invitation create → copy `invitation-code` → logout → register other user → accept code → lands in workspace.\n3. As owner, change member role member→admin; confirm badge/select; attempt illegal admin-on-admin as admin user → error.\n4. Select `#general` → channel settings → set topic → archive → confirm topic save fails with archived error → unarchive → topic save works.\n5. Create private channel (API or future M17 UI) → add workspace member via `channel-add-member-*` → member appears in list.\n6. As guest/member, confirm invitations tab and archive controls are not usable.\n\n### Verification mindset\n\nOutside-in: selectors + REST envelopes + visible errors. No reliance on reading JS internals beyond confirming assets load.\nDESIGN_EOF\nwc -c /tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md\n","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-7bb3e7d2-436f-4bd5-ad8f-c072f1d79931-52\nfc_09c64263-1886-982a-8d37-44886c1841f2_0","simpleCommands":["cat","wc"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cat","args":[],"fullText":"cat"},{"name":"wc","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md"}],"fullText":"wc -c /tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":false,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"cat"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Write complete MARATHON-18 design file","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"83d80305-f80e-4005-a214-b95749113409","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"description":"Write complete MARATHON-18 design file"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-7bb3e7d2-436f-4bd5-ad8f-c072f1d79931-52\nfc_09c64263-1886-982a-8d37-44886c1841f2_0","startedAtMs":"1787445220686"},"model_call_id":"9f6c9f7b-0f6e-481b-af84-0b50164c6a84-17-464x","session_id":"83d80305-f80e-4005-a214-b95749113409","timestamp_ms":1787445220725}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-7bb3e7d2-436f-4bd5-ad8f-c072f1d79931-52\nfc_09c64263-1886-982a-8d37-44886c1841f2_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cat > /tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n# MARATHON-18 — SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the Huddle SPA settings surface on top of the MARATHON-16 shell: a **workspace settings modal** (tabs General / Members / Invitations) and a **channel settings modal** (members list/add, topic, archive/unarchive). It wires those UIs to the already-shipped REST seams from MARATHON-6/7/12 (`PATCH` workspace, members/roles/transfer, invitations create/list/revoke/accept, channel members/topic/archive) and locks the epic’s stable DOM ids plus `settings-*` / `invitation-*` / role / channel-member `data-testid`s so CUA/Playwright can drive admin flows at 1280×900. It also specifies the missing **channel add-member** REST seam that MARATHON-7 deferred, because the channel-settings “add” control cannot work against join alone for private channels.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Delivery | Extend the **zero-build vanilla SPA** (`static/` ES modules) — same stack as MARATHON-16; no bundler |\n| Module split | New `static/js/settings_ui.js` owns both modals; `shell.js` exposes open triggers + active workspace/channel; reuse `api.js` / `storage.js` |\n| Modal pattern | Match `auth-modal`: overlay + panel, `hidden` attribute, `role=\"dialog\"`, Escape/close dismiss; **one settings modal open at a time** |\n| Workspace entry | `data-testid=\"workspace-settings-btn\"` in `workspace-header` (visible whenever shell shows a workspace) |\n| Channel entry | Selecting a non-DM channel in `channel-list` sets active channel; `data-testid=\"channel-settings-btn\"` in message-pane header chrome (or beside channel list) opens channel settings for that id — **does not** require MARATHON-17 message composer |\n| Tabs | Workspace modal: exactly three tabs — `general`, `members`, `invitations`; only one panel visible |\n| Authz UX | Client **hides/disables** privileged controls from cached caller role; server remains SoT (403/404 still shown as `error.message`) |\n| Invitation redeem | Onboarding gains an **accept-by-code** form (M12 assigned redeem UX to this task); settings tab is create/list/revoke only |\n| Channel add-member | New backend seam `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (this design owns the contract); frontend labeled implementer may land the thin route or a tiny backend follow-up must land first — see Sequencing |\n| Selectors | Exact strings below; prefer `data-testid`; required **DOM ids**: `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic requires settings + invitations in the SPA with stable selectors; M16 explicitly deferred settings modals here.\n- Backend contracts for name/join_mode, roles, invitations, topic, archive, channel member list are closed (M6/7/12); inventing alternate envelopes would break graders and sibling designs.\n- M7’s neighborhood note already flagged `channel-add-member-*` without REST — shipping UI without an add seam leaves private-channel “add” untestable.\n- Keeping vanilla modules preserves `start.sh` / no-Node ops.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Fold settings into MARATHON-17 message chrome only | Blocks settings QA until messages land; task is independent with `frontend` label |\n| “Add member” = tell user to `POST .../join` | Fails for private channels (403 without membership); hooks expect add controls |\n| Profile PATCH inside General tab | Task tabs are name/join_mode/members/invitations only; profile is a different surface |\n| Groups CRUD UI | MARATHON-12 groups API exists but is not in this task description |\n| React settings app | Diverges from M16 zero-build convention |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nChannel add-member needs a **small backend POST** that did not ship in M7. This design locks that seam so SPA and server can be implemented in parallel; if the implementer is frontend-only, the lead should keep `frontend` and optionally add a short backend subtask — **do not** fake add via SQL in the browser.\n\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n\nFrom **MARATHON-16**: vanilla SPA; `api()` + bearer; `{error:{code,message}}`; visible form errors; `hidden` for unused chrome; hash `#/w/{slug}`; token keys unchanged.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-5/6**: `WorkspaceObj` keys `{id,slug,name,owner_id,join_mode}`; `join_mode` ∈ {`open`,`invite_only`}; `MemberObj` `{user_id,role,username,display_name}`; roles `owner|admin|member|guest`; non-member → 404; privilege → 403; PATCH workspace name/join_mode; PATCH member role matrix; `POST .../transfer_ownership`.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj` keys; `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` → `{members: UserObj[]}`; `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}`; `POST .../archive` / `.../unarchive` owner-only; archived topic writes → **423** `archived`; leave/join exist but settings “add” is not join.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-12**: `InvitationObj`; create/list/revoke/accept envelopes; invite_only join still 403 without accept.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-3/4**: `UserObj` keys on channel members list; bearer auth.\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\n\nAll names are **`data-testid` values** unless noted as **DOM `id`**. Elements must exist in the DOM when the corresponding UI is shown (not only as JS string constants). Product “frontend hooks” are not checked into this repo; the table below is **normative** for this task and matches the task wording (`settings-*`, `invitation-*`, role/channel-member names from sibling designs).\n\n#### Required DOM ids\n\n| `id` | Element |\n|------|---------|\n| `workspace-settings-modal` | Workspace settings overlay/dialog root |\n| `channel-settings-modal` | Channel settings overlay/dialog root |\n| `create-invitation-form` | Form that creates a workspace invitation |\n\nAlso set matching `data-testid` equal to the id string for the three roots/forms above (so either selector style works).\n\n#### Open / chrome\n\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\n|---------------|--------------|------|\n| `workspace-settings-btn` | Shell with current workspace | Opens workspace settings modal |\n| `channel-settings-btn` | Shell with an active non-DM channel | Opens channel settings for that channel |\n| `workspace-settings-close` | Workspace modal open | Closes workspace modal |\n| `channel-settings-close` | Channel modal open | Closes channel modal |\n\n#### Workspace settings — tabs & general\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `settings-tab-general` | Selects General tab |\n| `settings-tab-members` | Selects Members tab |\n| `settings-tab-invitations` | Selects Invitations tab |\n| `settings-panel-general` | General panel region |\n| `settings-panel-members` | Members panel region |\n| `settings-panel-invitations` | Invitations panel region |\n| `settings-name` | Workspace display name `<input>` |\n| `settings-join-mode` | `<select>` or radio group; values `open` \\| `invite_only` |\n| `settings-general-save` | Submit/save general settings |\n| `settings-general-error` | Visible error text for general save failures |\n| `settings-general-success` | Optional brief success indicator (may be aria-live); not required if save is silently successful and fields reflect server |\n\n**Negative:** Member/guest must **not** successfully persist general changes; controls may be disabled **or** save shows `settings-general-error` with server `error.message` (403).\n\n#### Workspace settings — members\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `settings-members-list` | Container for member rows |\n| `settings-member-row` | One row per `MemberObj` (may appear multiple times) |\n| `role-badge` | Read-only role label on a row (always present) |\n| `role-select` | `<select>` to change role when actor may edit that row; **absent or `disabled`** when actor cannot |\n| `settings-members-error` | Visible error for list/PATCH failures |\n| `settings-members-loading` | Optional loading marker while `GET .../members` in flight |\n| `settings-transfer-owner` | Owner-only control to transfer ownership (confirm + target admin) |\n| `settings-transfer-owner-select` | Admin target picker |\n| `settings-transfer-owner-submit` | Confirm transfer |\n| `settings-transfer-error` | Transfer error text |\n\nEach `settings-member-row` **must** expose `data-user-id=\"{user_id}\"`.\n\n`role-select` options: `admin`, `member`, `guest` only (never `owner` — ownership uses transfer).\n\n#### Workspace settings — invitations\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `create-invitation-form` | Same as DOM id; create form |\n| `invitation-max-uses` | Optional number input (default server 1 if empty) |\n| `invitation-expires-seconds` | Optional expiry seconds input |\n| `invitation-username` | Optional targeted username |\n| `invitation-create-submit` | Create submit control |\n| `invitation-create-error` | Visible create error |\n| `invitation-list` | Active invitations list container |\n| `invitation-row` | One row per active invitation |\n| `invitation-code` | Displays `InvitationObj.code` (copyable text) |\n| `invitation-revoke` | Revoke control on a row |\n| `invitation-list-error` | List/revoke error |\n\nEach `invitation-row` **must** expose `data-invitation-code=\"{code}\"` (and/or `data-invitation-id`).\n\nNon-admin: invitations tab may show a short “Admins only” empty state; create form and list fetch must **not** be required to succeed for members (hide form **or** show 403 in `invitation-list-error` without crashing).\n\n#### Onboarding — accept invitation (redeem)\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `invitation-accept-form` | Onboarding form (sibling to join-by-slug) |\n| `invitation-accept-code` | Code input |\n| `invitation-accept-submit` | Submit |\n| `invitation-accept-error` | Visible error |\n\n#### Channel settings\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `channel-settings-modal` | Modal root (also DOM id) |\n| `settings-topic` | Topic `<input>` / textarea |\n| `settings-topic-save` | Save topic |\n| `settings-topic-error` | Topic error (incl. 423 archived) |\n| `settings-archive` | Archive button (owner) |\n| `settings-unarchive` | Unarchive button (owner) |\n| `settings-archive-error` | Archive/unarchive error |\n| `channel-members-list` | Channel members container |\n| `channel-member-row` | One row per `UserObj` |\n| `channel-add-member-input` | Username or user id input for add |\n| `channel-add-member-submit` | Add submit |\n| `channel-add-member-error` | Add error |\n| `channel-members-error` | List error |\n\nEach `channel-member-row` **must** expose `data-user-id=\"{id}\"` (UserObj `id`).\n\nArchive vs unarchive: show the action that matches current `is_archived` (one primary control is enough; the other may stay in DOM but `hidden`).\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET/PATCH /api/workspaces/{slug}` (General tab)\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On open: seed `settings-name` / `settings-join-mode` from in-memory `WorkspaceObj`. Save → `PATCH` body subset `{name?, join_mode?}`. Disable `settings-general-save` while in flight. On **200**: replace cached workspace; refresh `workspace-header`. On **400/403**: show `error.message` in `settings-general-error`. On **401**: logout (M16). On **404**: close modal, leave workspace. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-6). |\n\n**Slow:** keep prior field values; do not clear the form.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}/members` + `PATCH .../members/{user_id}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On Members tab select / modal open: `GET` members. While slow: show `settings-members-loading` or keep prior rows. On **200**: render rows ordered as server returns; every row has `role-badge`; editable rows get `role-select` preselected to current role. On change of `role-select`: `PATCH` `{role}` immediately (or on explicit apply — **prefer immediate**). On **403/400**: revert select to last known role; show `settings-members-error`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-6 matrix). |\n\n**Who sees `role-select`:**\n\n| Actor role | Target | UI |\n|------------|--------|-----|\n| owner | admin/member/guest | `role-select` enabled |\n| owner | owner (self) | badge only |\n| admin | member/guest | `role-select` enabled |\n| admin | admin/owner | badge only |\n| member/guest | anyone | badge only |\n\nCaller role: derive from members list (`user_id === session user`) or from detail if already known.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/transfer_ownership`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Visible only if caller is workspace owner. Body `{new_owner_id}` from admin-only select. Confirm (browser `confirm` OK). On **200**: refresh workspace + members. On **400/403**: `settings-transfer-error`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-6). |\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ invitations (create / list / revoke / accept)\n\n#### Create — `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations` → **201** `{invitation}`\n\nClient body (omit empty optionals):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"expires_in_seconds\": 86400,\n  \"max_uses\": 5,\n  \"invited_username\": \"ada\"\n}\n```\n\nDisable submit while in flight; on success prepend/refresh list and show `invitation-code` on the new row; on 400/403 show `invitation-create-error`.\n\n#### List — `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations` → **200** `{invitations:[InvitationObj]}`\n\nLoad when Invitations tab opens (admin). On 403 show admin-only message.\n\n#### Revoke — `DELETE /api/invitations/{code}` → **200** `{revoked:true}`\n\nRemove row on success; on 404 refresh list.\n\n#### Accept — `POST /api/invitations/{code}/accept` → **200** `{workspace, channels?, read_state?}`\n\nFrom onboarding form: on success call existing `enterWorkspace` path (persist slug, show shell) using returned payload (fetch detail if channels omitted). On 403/404 show `invitation-accept-error`.\n\n**Server:** Unchanged (MARATHON-12).\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ channel topic / archive / members list\n\n| API | Client behavior |\n|-----|-----------------|\n| `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` | Fill `channel-members-list`; slow → keep prior / empty with loading |\n| `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}` | Save from `settings-topic`; **423** → message in `settings-topic-error` and disable further topic edits until unarchived |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/archive` | Owner; on 200 set local `is_archived=true`, swap buttons, refresh shell channel list if archived channels are hidden by default |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/unarchive` | Owner; opposite |\n\nNon-owner: hide `settings-archive` / `settings-unarchive` (or disable). Topic save allowed for channel member or workspace owner per M7; others show 403 in error region.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (**new**; owned by this design)\n\nMissing today (M7 out-of-scope). Required for channel settings add.\n\n**Request**\n\n```http\nPOST /api/channels/{channel_id}/members\nAuthorization: Bearer …\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{ \"username\": \"ada\" }\n```\n\nAlternate accepted field: `{ \"user_id\": \"<uuid>\" }`. If both sent, must resolve to the same user else **400**. Unknown keys ignored. Exactly one of `username` / `user_id` required.\n\n**Authz / rules**\n\n1. Unknown channel → **404**.\n2. Caller must be **workspace member**; else **404** (no leak).\n3. Caller must be workspace **owner or admin**, **or** an existing **channel member** with workspace role ∈ {owner, admin, member} — **guest cannot add** → **403**.\n4. Target user must be a **workspace member** → else **400** `validation_error` (cannot add outsiders via this route; use workspace invitations first).\n5. Private or public: INSERT into `channel_members` if missing; idempotent if already member → **200**.\n6. DM channels (`is_dm=true`): **403** (DM membership is MARATHON-9).\n7. Archived channel: add membership **allowed** (membership mgmt, not a 423 “write” like topic/pin) — consistent with leave-on-archived in M7.\n\n**Response 200**\n\n```json\n{ \"members\": [ /* UserObj[], same shape/order as GET members */ ] }\n```\n\n(Prefer full refreshed list so SPA can re-render without a second GET.)\n\n**Client:** submit `channel-add-member-input` as username (trim); disable submit in flight; on 200 replace list; on 4xx show `channel-add-member-error`.\n\n---\n\n### HTTP client rules\n\nReuse MARATHON-16 `api()`: JSON, bearer, 15s timeout, envelope parse, 401 → logout. Never invent cookies.\n\n### Modal UX rules\n\n1. Opening workspace settings closes channel settings (and vice versa).\n2. Backdrop click and Escape close the active modal without saving pending edits (except already-fired role PATCH / invitation create).\n3. Switching workspace (hash/list) closes both modals.\n4. Viewport: usable at **1280×900**; modal panel scrollable if members list is long.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Browser / in-memory (no SQLite migration required for SPA-only path)\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `currentWorkspace` | `WorkspaceObj` | Already in shell; General tab mutates via PATCH |\n| `callerRole` | string \\| null | From members list or inferred |\n| `workspaceMembers` | `MemberObj[]` | Settings cache |\n| `invitations` | `InvitationObj[]` | Admin cache |\n| `activeChannel` | `ChannelObj` \\| null | For channel settings |\n| `channelMembers` | `UserObj[]` | Channel settings cache |\n\n### Server schema\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| SPA-only selectors/HTML/JS | N/A — no schema |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` | **No DDL** — uses existing `channel_members` (v2). Backward compatible additive route |\n\n### Entities (unchanged shapes)\n\n- `WorkspaceObj`, `MemberObj`, `InvitationObj`, `ChannelObj`, `UserObj` — exact keys per M5/6/7/12. **Do not** nest extra fields in settings payloads.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/js/settings_ui.js` | Workspace + channel modal controllers; tab switching; all settings API calls; role-select / invitation / topic / archive / add-member handlers; exports `initSettingsUi(ctx)` |\n| `tests/test_spa_settings.py` | TestClient: HTML contains required ids/testids; static JS references key API paths; optional smoke that create_app still serves `/` |\n| `tests/test_channel_add_member.py` | **If** backend route lands with this task: authz matrix, idempotent add, guest 403, non-workspace target 400, DM 403 |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/index.html` | Add both modals (hidden), invitation accept form in onboarding, workspace/channel settings buttons hooks; all required testids/ids in markup (rows may be JS-generated but modal chrome + forms must be present for SPA shell tests) |\n| `static/css/app.css` | Modal/tab/list styles consistent with auth-modal; do not break 1280×900 shell |\n| `static/js/shell.js` | Wire `workspace-settings-btn`; track `activeChannel` on channel-list click; expose getters (`getWorkspace`, `getActiveChannel`, `refreshWorkspaceDetail`, `enterWorkspace`) to settings module; mount invitation-accept form submit |\n| `static/js/app.js` | `initSettingsUi` after shell init |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | Extend `REQUIRED_TESTIDS` (or sibling list) with stable settings chrome ids that must appear in initial HTML (`workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form`, tab testids, invitation-accept-*) |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Add `POST /{channel_id}/members` per contract above |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | Helper `add_channel_member` / reuse insert; list members after add |\n\n### Do not modify\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/workspaces/**`, `server/invitations/**` | Contracts already ship; SPA consumes |\n| `server/db.py` migrations | No schema change |\n| `start.sh` / `timer.sh` | No build step |\n| Message composer / thread panel behavior | MARATHON-17 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order within this task\n\n1. HTML modal shells + CSS + required testids (unblocks selector tests).\n2. `settings_ui.js` General tab → PATCH workspace.\n3. Members tab → GET/PATCH members + transfer.\n4. Invitations tab → create/list/revoke; onboarding accept form.\n5. Channel settings → topic/archive/members list.\n6. Channel add-member route + UI last (or parallel once contract fixed).\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- SPA work can proceed against existing M6/7/12 APIs immediately.\n- Add-member UI blocked on `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` implementation (same PR or tiny backend follow-up).\n- Independent of MARATHON-17 messages **except** shared `channel-list` click / active channel — this task may set active channel for settings without opening thread panel.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumer |\n|----------|----------|\n| Settings / invitation / role / channel-member `data-testid` set | QA / CUA |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` | SPA channel settings; future slash invites |\n| `initSettingsUi` / open-modal hooks | MARATHON-17 may call `openChannelSettings(channelId)` from message header |\n\n### Dependencies\n\n- **Requires closed:** MARATHON-16 (shell), MARATHON-6 (members), MARATHON-7 (channel topic/archive/members GET), MARATHON-12 (invitations).\n- **Does not require:** MARATHON-8/13/14/17.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not recreate existing tasks)\n\n- User groups settings UI → new task if needed (not this description).\n- Profile / `PATCH /api/users/me` UI → separate settings surface.\n- Channel leave button in settings → optional later; leave API exists (M7) but not required by this task text.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| Message composer, reactions, thread panel open | `static/js/*`, MARATHON-17 | Different SPA task |\n| User groups CRUD UI | `settings-*` could grow; `server/groups` | Not in MARATHON-18 description |\n| Profile PATCH UI | `PATCH /api/users/me` | M16 deferred “profile” vaguely to settings; **this** task’s General tab is workspace name/join_mode only |\n| Pins UI | `/api/channels/{id}/pins` | Channel settings text is members/topic/archive only |\n| WebSocket live member updates | MARATHON-13 | Poll/refetch on tab open is enough |\n| IRC | MARATHON-15 | Unrelated |\n| Changing invitation accept semantics / join_mode gates | `server/invitations/**`, `server/workspaces/routes.py` join | Already shipped; SPA consumes |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` as substitute for add-member | existing join route | Wrong authz for private add; out of scope as the add mechanism |\n| React/Vite migration | — | Conflicts with M16 |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `static/index.html`, `static/js/shell.js`, `static/js/app.js`, `static/css/app.css` | **In scope** — extend |\n| `static/js/api.js`, `storage.js`, `auth_ui.js` | **Reuse** — no contract change |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | **In scope** — extend required selectors |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` GET members / PATCH / archive | **Consume**; add POST members |\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` PATCH/members/transfer | **Consume only** |\n| `server/invitations/routes.py` | **Consume only** |\n| `tests/test_workspace_members.py`, `test_invitations.py`, `test_channels.py` | **Out of scope** to rewrite; keep green; add new tests |\n| Grep `settings-` / `invitation-` in `static/` | No hits yet — greenfield UI |\n| M7 note `channel-add-member-*` | **In scope** via new POST + testids |\n| Groups package | **Out of scope** UI |\n| `server/events.py` | **Out of scope** |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Open workspace settings without admin role | Modal opens; General fields disabled or save → 403 visible; Members badge-only; Invitations admin-only empty/error |\n| PATCH general with blank name | Client may pre-check; server **400** → `settings-general-error` |\n| Invalid join_mode option | Must not be choosable in UI; if forced, server 400 |\n| Role select to `owner` | **Must not** be an option |\n| Admin tries to demote another admin | No select **or** PATCH 403 → revert + error |\n| Transfer to non-admin | Client only lists admins; server 400 if forced |\n| Create invitation as member | 403 → `invitation-create-error`; modal stays open |\n| Revoke already-used/expired code | 404 → refresh list (row disappears) |\n| Accept invalid/expired code | 404 → `invitation-accept-error`; stay on onboarding |\n| Accept targeted invite as wrong user | 403 → visible error |\n| Accept success while already member | 200 → enter workspace (idempotent) |\n| Topic save on archived channel | 423 → `settings-topic-error`; suggest unarchive |\n| Archive by non-owner | Control hidden/disabled; if called, 403 error |\n| Archive `#general` | Allowed if owner (server permits); UI does not special-case unless server errors |\n| Add member unknown username | 400 → `channel-add-member-error` |\n| Add member who is not workspace member | 400 → same |\n| Add to DM channel | Button hidden for `is_dm`; if called, 403 |\n| Add when already member | 200; list unchanged except refresh |\n| Network timeout | Visible error on active form; re-enable controls |\n| 401 on any settings call | Clear tokens; show auth modal; close settings |\n| Double-click save | Disable control until response; single in-flight request |\n| Modal open during workspace switch | Close modals; drop stale channel id |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `GET /` HTML includes DOM ids `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` and the normative `data-testid`s listed above for modal chrome, tabs, general fields, invitation accept form, and channel settings fields (list rows may be empty until data loads).\n2. Authenticated owner/admin can open workspace settings, change **name** and **join_mode**, save, and see updates in `workspace-header` / subsequent `GET` workspace detail.\n3. Member/guest **cannot** persist general settings (disabled UI and/or visible 403); must **not** silently succeed.\n4. Members tab lists all workspace members with `role-badge`; owner/admin can change permitted roles via `role-select`; forbidden changes show error and do **not** leave a lying UI role.\n5. Owner can transfer ownership to an admin via transfer controls; previous owner becomes admin in the refreshed list.\n6. Admin/owner can create an invitation; `invitation-code` is visible; list shows active invites; revoke removes the row.\n7. Onboarding `invitation-accept-*` redeems a valid code and enters the workspace shell; invite_only workspaces become accessible without using broken join-by-slug alone.\n8. With an active public/private channel, channel settings shows members (`channel-member-row`), allows topic save for authorized callers, and owner can archive/unarchive with UI reflecting `is_archived`.\n9. Topic save on archived channel surfaces **423** message and must **not** clear the topic field to empty on failure.\n10. Channel add-member with a workspace member username adds them to `channel_members` (UI list updates); guest cannot add; outsider username fails visibly.\n11. Opening one settings modal closes the other; logout closes modals and clears privileged data from the DOM on next login.\n12. Existing MARATHON-16 selectors and auth/workspace flows remain green (`tests/test_spa_shell.py` + prior SPA behavior).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated\n\n- Extend/add TestClient tests asserting required ids/testids in `GET /` and that `settings_ui.js` is served as a static asset.\n- Backend tests for `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` matrix (owner/admin/member/guest, private/public, idempotent, DM rejection, non-member target).\n- Do **not** require a browser in unit CI; optional Playwright (as M16 notes) at 1280×900 for human/agent verification.\n\n### Manual / CUA script (1280×900)\n\n1. Register → create workspace → open workspace settings → rename + set `invite_only` → save → reload → values stick.\n2. Add second user via invitation create → copy `invitation-code` → logout → register other user → accept code → lands in workspace.\n3. As owner, change member role member→admin; confirm badge/select; attempt illegal admin-on-admin as admin user → error.\n4. Select `#general` → channel settings → set topic → archive → confirm topic save fails with archived error → unarchive → topic save works.\n5. Create private channel (API or future M17 UI) → add workspace member via `channel-add-member-*` → member appears in list.\n6. As guest/member, confirm invitations tab and archive controls are not usable.\n\n### Verification mindset\n\nOutside-in: selectors + REST envelopes + visible errors. No reliance on reading JS internals beyond confirming assets load.\nDESIGN_EOF\nwc -c /tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md\n","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-7bb3e7d2-436f-4bd5-ad8f-c072f1d79931-52\nfc_09c64263-1886-982a-8d37-44886c1841f2_0","simpleCommands":["cat","wc"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cat","args":[],"fullText":"cat"},{"name":"wc","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md"}],"fullText":"wc -c /tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":false,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"cat"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Write complete MARATHON-18 design file","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"83d80305-f80e-4005-a214-b95749113409","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"cat > /tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n# MARATHON-18 — SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the Huddle SPA settings surface on top of the MARATHON-16 shell: a **workspace settings modal** (tabs General / Members / Invitations) and a **channel settings modal** (members list/add, topic, archive/unarchive). It wires those UIs to the already-shipped REST seams from MARATHON-6/7/12 (`PATCH` workspace, members/roles/transfer, invitations create/list/revoke/accept, channel members/topic/archive) and locks the epic’s stable DOM ids plus `settings-*` / `invitation-*` / role / channel-member `data-testid`s so CUA/Playwright can drive admin flows at 1280×900. It also specifies the missing **channel add-member** REST seam that MARATHON-7 deferred, because the channel-settings “add” control cannot work against join alone for private channels.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Delivery | Extend the **zero-build vanilla SPA** (`static/` ES modules) — same stack as MARATHON-16; no bundler |\n| Module split | New `static/js/settings_ui.js` owns both modals; `shell.js` exposes open triggers + active workspace/channel; reuse `api.js` / `storage.js` |\n| Modal pattern | Match `auth-modal`: overlay + panel, `hidden` attribute, `role=\"dialog\"`, Escape/close dismiss; **one settings modal open at a time** |\n| Workspace entry | `data-testid=\"workspace-settings-btn\"` in `workspace-header` (visible whenever shell shows a workspace) |\n| Channel entry | Selecting a non-DM channel in `channel-list` sets active channel; `data-testid=\"channel-settings-btn\"` in message-pane header chrome (or beside channel list) opens channel settings for that id — **does not** require MARATHON-17 message composer |\n| Tabs | Workspace modal: exactly three tabs — `general`, `members`, `invitations`; only one panel visible |\n| Authz UX | Client **hides/disables** privileged controls from cached caller role; server remains SoT (403/404 still shown as `error.message`) |\n| Invitation redeem | Onboarding gains an **accept-by-code** form (M12 assigned redeem UX to this task); settings tab is create/list/revoke only |\n| Channel add-member | New backend seam `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (this design owns the contract); frontend labeled implementer may land the thin route or a tiny backend follow-up must land first — see Sequencing |\n| Selectors | Exact strings below; prefer `data-testid`; required **DOM ids**: `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic requires settings + invitations in the SPA with stable selectors; M16 explicitly deferred settings modals here.\n- Backend contracts for name/join_mode, roles, invitations, topic, archive, channel member list are closed (M6/7/12); inventing alternate envelopes would break graders and sibling designs.\n- M7’s neighborhood note already flagged `channel-add-member-*` without REST — shipping UI without an add seam leaves private-channel “add” untestable.\n- Keeping vanilla modules preserves `start.sh` / no-Node ops.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Fold settings into MARATHON-17 message chrome only | Blocks settings QA until messages land; task is independent with `frontend` label |\n| “Add member” = tell user to `POST .../join` | Fails for private channels (403 without membership); hooks expect add controls |\n| Profile PATCH inside General tab | Task tabs are name/join_mode/members/invitations only; profile is a different surface |\n| Groups CRUD UI | MARATHON-12 groups API exists but is not in this task description |\n| React settings app | Diverges from M16 zero-build convention |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nChannel add-member needs a **small backend POST** that did not ship in M7. This design locks that seam so SPA and server can be implemented in parallel; if the implementer is frontend-only, the lead should keep `frontend` and optionally add a short backend subtask — **do not** fake add via SQL in the browser.\n\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n\nFrom **MARATHON-16**: vanilla SPA; `api()` + bearer; `{error:{code,message}}`; visible form errors; `hidden` for unused chrome; hash `#/w/{slug}`; token keys unchanged.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-5/6**: `WorkspaceObj` keys `{id,slug,name,owner_id,join_mode}`; `join_mode` ∈ {`open`,`invite_only`}; `MemberObj` `{user_id,role,username,display_name}`; roles `owner|admin|member|guest`; non-member → 404; privilege → 403; PATCH workspace name/join_mode; PATCH member role matrix; `POST .../transfer_ownership`.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj` keys; `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` → `{members: UserObj[]}`; `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}`; `POST .../archive` / `.../unarchive` owner-only; archived topic writes → **423** `archived`; leave/join exist but settings “add” is not join.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-12**: `InvitationObj`; create/list/revoke/accept envelopes; invite_only join still 403 without accept.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-3/4**: `UserObj` keys on channel members list; bearer auth.\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\n\nAll names are **`data-testid` values** unless noted as **DOM `id`**. Elements must exist in the DOM when the corresponding UI is shown (not only as JS string constants). Product “frontend hooks” are not checked into this repo; the table below is **normative** for this task and matches the task wording (`settings-*`, `invitation-*`, role/channel-member names from sibling designs).\n\n#### Required DOM ids\n\n| `id` | Element |\n|------|---------|\n| `workspace-settings-modal` | Workspace settings overlay/dialog root |\n| `channel-settings-modal` | Channel settings overlay/dialog root |\n| `create-invitation-form` | Form that creates a workspace invitation |\n\nAlso set matching `data-testid` equal to the id string for the three roots/forms above (so either selector style works).\n\n#### Open / chrome\n\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\n|---------------|--------------|------|\n| `workspace-settings-btn` | Shell with current workspace | Opens workspace settings modal |\n| `channel-settings-btn` | Shell with an active non-DM channel | Opens channel settings for that channel |\n| `workspace-settings-close` | Workspace modal open | Closes workspace modal |\n| `channel-settings-close` | Channel modal open | Closes channel modal |\n\n#### Workspace settings — tabs & general\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `settings-tab-general` | Selects General tab |\n| `settings-tab-members` | Selects Members tab |\n| `settings-tab-invitations` | Selects Invitations tab |\n| `settings-panel-general` | General panel region |\n| `settings-panel-members` | Members panel region |\n| `settings-panel-invitations` | Invitations panel region |\n| `settings-name` | Workspace display name `<input>` |\n| `settings-join-mode` | `<select>` or radio group; values `open` \\| `invite_only` |\n| `settings-general-save` | Submit/save general settings |\n| `settings-general-error` | Visible error text for general save failures |\n| `settings-general-success` | Optional brief success indicator (may be aria-live); not required if save is silently successful and fields reflect server |\n\n**Negative:** Member/guest must **not** successfully persist general changes; controls may be disabled **or** save shows `settings-general-error` with server `error.message` (403).\n\n#### Workspace settings — members\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `settings-members-list` | Container for member rows |\n| `settings-member-row` | One row per `MemberObj` (may appear multiple times) |\n| `role-badge` | Read-only role label on a row (always present) |\n| `role-select` | `<select>` to change role when actor may edit that row; **absent or `disabled`** when actor cannot |\n| `settings-members-error` | Visible error for list/PATCH failures |\n| `settings-members-loading` | Optional loading marker while `GET .../members` in flight |\n| `settings-transfer-owner` | Owner-only control to transfer ownership (confirm + target admin) |\n| `settings-transfer-owner-select` | Admin target picker |\n| `settings-transfer-owner-submit` | Confirm transfer |\n| `settings-transfer-error` | Transfer error text |\n\nEach `settings-member-row` **must** expose `data-user-id=\"{user_id}\"`.\n\n`role-select` options: `admin`, `member`, `guest` only (never `owner` — ownership uses transfer).\n\n#### Workspace settings — invitations\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `create-invitation-form` | Same as DOM id; create form |\n| `invitation-max-uses` | Optional number input (default server 1 if empty) |\n| `invitation-expires-seconds` | Optional expiry seconds input |\n| `invitation-username` | Optional targeted username |\n| `invitation-create-submit` | Create submit control |\n| `invitation-create-error` | Visible create error |\n| `invitation-list` | Active invitations list container |\n| `invitation-row` | One row per active invitation |\n| `invitation-code` | Displays `InvitationObj.code` (copyable text) |\n| `invitation-revoke` | Revoke control on a row |\n| `invitation-list-error` | List/revoke error |\n\nEach `invitation-row` **must** expose `data-invitation-code=\"{code}\"` (and/or `data-invitation-id`).\n\nNon-admin: invitations tab may show a short “Admins only” empty state; create form and list fetch must **not** be required to succeed for members (hide form **or** show 403 in `invitation-list-error` without crashing).\n\n#### Onboarding — accept invitation (redeem)\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `invitation-accept-form` | Onboarding form (sibling to join-by-slug) |\n| `invitation-accept-code` | Code input |\n| `invitation-accept-submit` | Submit |\n| `invitation-accept-error` | Visible error |\n\n#### Channel settings\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `channel-settings-modal` | Modal root (also DOM id) |\n| `settings-topic` | Topic `<input>` / textarea |\n| `settings-topic-save` | Save topic |\n| `settings-topic-error` | Topic error (incl. 423 archived) |\n| `settings-archive` | Archive button (owner) |\n| `settings-unarchive` | Unarchive button (owner) |\n| `settings-archive-error` | Archive/unarchive error |\n| `channel-members-list` | Channel members container |\n| `channel-member-row` | One row per `UserObj` |\n| `channel-add-member-input` | Username or user id input for add |\n| `channel-add-member-submit` | Add submit |\n| `channel-add-member-error` | Add error |\n| `channel-members-error` | List error |\n\nEach `channel-member-row` **must** expose `data-user-id=\"{id}\"` (UserObj `id`).\n\nArchive vs unarchive: show the action that matches current `is_archived` (one primary control is enough; the other may stay in DOM but `hidden`).\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET/PATCH /api/workspaces/{slug}` (General tab)\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On open: seed `settings-name` / `settings-join-mode` from in-memory `WorkspaceObj`. Save → `PATCH` body subset `{name?, join_mode?}`. Disable `settings-general-save` while in flight. On **200**: replace cached workspace; refresh `workspace-header`. On **400/403**: show `error.message` in `settings-general-error`. On **401**: logout (M16). On **404**: close modal, leave workspace. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-6). |\n\n**Slow:** keep prior field values; do not clear the form.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}/members` + `PATCH .../members/{user_id}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On Members tab select / modal open: `GET` members. While slow: show `settings-members-loading` or keep prior rows. On **200**: render rows ordered as server returns; every row has `role-badge`; editable rows get `role-select` preselected to current role. On change of `role-select`: `PATCH` `{role}` immediately (or on explicit apply — **prefer immediate**). On **403/400**: revert select to last known role; show `settings-members-error`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-6 matrix). |\n\n**Who sees `role-select`:**\n\n| Actor role | Target | UI |\n|------------|--------|-----|\n| owner | admin/member/guest | `role-select` enabled |\n| owner | owner (self) | badge only |\n| admin | member/guest | `role-select` enabled |\n| admin | admin/owner | badge only |\n| member/guest | anyone | badge only |\n\nCaller role: derive from members list (`user_id === session user`) or from detail if already known.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/transfer_ownership`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Visible only if caller is workspace owner. Body `{new_owner_id}` from admin-only select. Confirm (browser `confirm` OK). On **200**: refresh workspace + members. On **400/403**: `settings-transfer-error`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-6). |\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ invitations (create / list / revoke / accept)\n\n#### Create — `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations` → **201** `{invitation}`\n\nClient body (omit empty optionals):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"expires_in_seconds\": 86400,\n  \"max_uses\": 5,\n  \"invited_username\": \"ada\"\n}\n```\n\nDisable submit while in flight; on success prepend/refresh list and show `invitation-code` on the new row; on 400/403 show `invitation-create-error`.\n\n#### List — `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations` → **200** `{invitations:[InvitationObj]}`\n\nLoad when Invitations tab opens (admin). On 403 show admin-only message.\n\n#### Revoke — `DELETE /api/invitations/{code}` → **200** `{revoked:true}`\n\nRemove row on success; on 404 refresh list.\n\n#### Accept — `POST /api/invitations/{code}/accept` → **200** `{workspace, channels?, read_state?}`\n\nFrom onboarding form: on success call existing `enterWorkspace` path (persist slug, show shell) using returned payload (fetch detail if channels omitted). On 403/404 show `invitation-accept-error`.\n\n**Server:** Unchanged (MARATHON-12).\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ channel topic / archive / members list\n\n| API | Client behavior |\n|-----|-----------------|\n| `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` | Fill `channel-members-list`; slow → keep prior / empty with loading |\n| `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}` | Save from `settings-topic`; **423** → message in `settings-topic-error` and disable further topic edits until unarchived |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/archive` | Owner; on 200 set local `is_archived=true`, swap buttons, refresh shell channel list if archived channels are hidden by default |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/unarchive` | Owner; opposite |\n\nNon-owner: hide `settings-archive` / `settings-unarchive` (or disable). Topic save allowed for channel member or workspace owner per M7; others show 403 in error region.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (**new**; owned by this design)\n\nMissing today (M7 out-of-scope). Required for channel settings add.\n\n**Request**\n\n```http\nPOST /api/channels/{channel_id}/members\nAuthorization: Bearer …\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{ \"username\": \"ada\" }\n```\n\nAlternate accepted field: `{ \"user_id\": \"<uuid>\" }`. If both sent, must resolve to the same user else **400**. Unknown keys ignored. Exactly one of `username` / `user_id` required.\n\n**Authz / rules**\n\n1. Unknown channel → **404**.\n2. Caller must be **workspace member**; else **404** (no leak).\n3. Caller must be workspace **owner or admin**, **or** an existing **channel member** with workspace role ∈ {owner, admin, member} — **guest cannot add** → **403**.\n4. Target user must be a **workspace member** → else **400** `validation_error` (cannot add outsiders via this route; use workspace invitations first).\n5. Private or public: INSERT into `channel_members` if missing; idempotent if already member → **200**.\n6. DM channels (`is_dm=true`): **403** (DM membership is MARATHON-9).\n7. Archived channel: add membership **allowed** (membership mgmt, not a 423 “write” like topic/pin) — consistent with leave-on-archived in M7.\n\n**Response 200**\n\n```json\n{ \"members\": [ /* UserObj[], same shape/order as GET members */ ] }\n```\n\n(Prefer full refreshed list so SPA can re-render without a second GET.)\n\n**Client:** submit `channel-add-member-input` as username (trim); disable submit in flight; on 200 replace list; on 4xx show `channel-add-member-error`.\n\n---\n\n### HTTP client rules\n\nReuse MARATHON-16 `api()`: JSON, bearer, 15s timeout, envelope parse, 401 → logout. Never invent cookies.\n\n### Modal UX rules\n\n1. Opening workspace settings closes channel settings (and vice versa).\n2. Backdrop click and Escape close the active modal without saving pending edits (except already-fired role PATCH / invitation create).\n3. Switching workspace (hash/list) closes both modals.\n4. Viewport: usable at **1280×900**; modal panel scrollable if members list is long.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Browser / in-memory (no SQLite migration required for SPA-only path)\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `currentWorkspace` | `WorkspaceObj` | Already in shell; General tab mutates via PATCH |\n| `callerRole` | string \\| null | From members list or inferred |\n| `workspaceMembers` | `MemberObj[]` | Settings cache |\n| `invitations` | `InvitationObj[]` | Admin cache |\n| `activeChannel` | `ChannelObj` \\| null | For channel settings |\n| `channelMembers` | `UserObj[]` | Channel settings cache |\n\n### Server schema\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| SPA-only selectors/HTML/JS | N/A — no schema |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` | **No DDL** — uses existing `channel_members` (v2). Backward compatible additive route |\n\n### Entities (unchanged shapes)\n\n- `WorkspaceObj`, `MemberObj`, `InvitationObj`, `ChannelObj`, `UserObj` — exact keys per M5/6/7/12. **Do not** nest extra fields in settings payloads.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/js/settings_ui.js` | Workspace + channel modal controllers; tab switching; all settings API calls; role-select / invitation / topic / archive / add-member handlers; exports `initSettingsUi(ctx)` |\n| `tests/test_spa_settings.py` | TestClient: HTML contains required ids/testids; static JS references key API paths; optional smoke that create_app still serves `/` |\n| `tests/test_channel_add_member.py` | **If** backend route lands with this task: authz matrix, idempotent add, guest 403, non-workspace target 400, DM 403 |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/index.html` | Add both modals (hidden), invitation accept form in onboarding, workspace/channel settings buttons hooks; all required testids/ids in markup (rows may be JS-generated but modal chrome + forms must be present for SPA shell tests) |\n| `static/css/app.css` | Modal/tab/list styles consistent with auth-modal; do not break 1280×900 shell |\n| `static/js/shell.js` | Wire `workspace-settings-btn`; track `activeChannel` on channel-list click; expose getters (`getWorkspace`, `getActiveChannel`, `refreshWorkspaceDetail`, `enterWorkspace`) to settings module; mount invitation-accept form submit |\n| `static/js/app.js` | `initSettingsUi` after shell init |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | Extend `REQUIRED_TESTIDS` (or sibling list) with stable settings chrome ids that must appear in initial HTML (`workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form`, tab testids, invitation-accept-*) |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` | Add `POST /{channel_id}/members` per contract above |\n| `server/channels/store.py` | Helper `add_channel_member` / reuse insert; list members after add |\n\n### Do not modify\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/workspaces/**`, `server/invitations/**` | Contracts already ship; SPA consumes |\n| `server/db.py` migrations | No schema change |\n| `start.sh` / `timer.sh` | No build step |\n| Message composer / thread panel behavior | MARATHON-17 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order within this task\n\n1. HTML modal shells + CSS + required testids (unblocks selector tests).\n2. `settings_ui.js` General tab → PATCH workspace.\n3. Members tab → GET/PATCH members + transfer.\n4. Invitations tab → create/list/revoke; onboarding accept form.\n5. Channel settings → topic/archive/members list.\n6. Channel add-member route + UI last (or parallel once contract fixed).\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- SPA work can proceed against existing M6/7/12 APIs immediately.\n- Add-member UI blocked on `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` implementation (same PR or tiny backend follow-up).\n- Independent of MARATHON-17 messages **except** shared `channel-list` click / active channel — this task may set active channel for settings without opening thread panel.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumer |\n|----------|----------|\n| Settings / invitation / role / channel-member `data-testid` set | QA / CUA |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` | SPA channel settings; future slash invites |\n| `initSettingsUi` / open-modal hooks | MARATHON-17 may call `openChannelSettings(channelId)` from message header |\n\n### Dependencies\n\n- **Requires closed:** MARATHON-16 (shell), MARATHON-6 (members), MARATHON-7 (channel topic/archive/members GET), MARATHON-12 (invitations).\n- **Does not require:** MARATHON-8/13/14/17.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not recreate existing tasks)\n\n- User groups settings UI → new task if needed (not this description).\n- Profile / `PATCH /api/users/me` UI → separate settings surface.\n- Channel leave button in settings → optional later; leave API exists (M7) but not required by this task text.\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| Message composer, reactions, thread panel open | `static/js/*`, MARATHON-17 | Different SPA task |\n| User groups CRUD UI | `settings-*` could grow; `server/groups` | Not in MARATHON-18 description |\n| Profile PATCH UI | `PATCH /api/users/me` | M16 deferred “profile” vaguely to settings; **this** task’s General tab is workspace name/join_mode only |\n| Pins UI | `/api/channels/{id}/pins` | Channel settings text is members/topic/archive only |\n| WebSocket live member updates | MARATHON-13 | Poll/refetch on tab open is enough |\n| IRC | MARATHON-15 | Unrelated |\n| Changing invitation accept semantics / join_mode gates | `server/invitations/**`, `server/workspaces/routes.py` join | Already shipped; SPA consumes |\n| `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` as substitute for add-member | existing join route | Wrong authz for private add; out of scope as the add mechanism |\n| React/Vite migration | — | Conflicts with M16 |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `static/index.html`, `static/js/shell.js`, `static/js/app.js`, `static/css/app.css` | **In scope** — extend |\n| `static/js/api.js`, `storage.js`, `auth_ui.js` | **Reuse** — no contract change |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | **In scope** — extend required selectors |\n| `server/channels/routes.py` GET members / PATCH / archive | **Consume**; add POST members |\n| `server/workspaces/routes.py` PATCH/members/transfer | **Consume only** |\n| `server/invitations/routes.py` | **Consume only** |\n| `tests/test_workspace_members.py`, `test_invitations.py`, `test_channels.py` | **Out of scope** to rewrite; keep green; add new tests |\n| Grep `settings-` / `invitation-` in `static/` | No hits yet — greenfield UI |\n| M7 note `channel-add-member-*` | **In scope** via new POST + testids |\n| Groups package | **Out of scope** UI |\n| `server/events.py` | **Out of scope** |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Open workspace settings without admin role | Modal opens; General fields disabled or save → 403 visible; Members badge-only; Invitations admin-only empty/error |\n| PATCH general with blank name | Client may pre-check; server **400** → `settings-general-error` |\n| Invalid join_mode option | Must not be choosable in UI; if forced, server 400 |\n| Role select to `owner` | **Must not** be an option |\n| Admin tries to demote another admin | No select **or** PATCH 403 → revert + error |\n| Transfer to non-admin | Client only lists admins; server 400 if forced |\n| Create invitation as member | 403 → `invitation-create-error`; modal stays open |\n| Revoke already-used/expired code | 404 → refresh list (row disappears) |\n| Accept invalid/expired code | 404 → `invitation-accept-error`; stay on onboarding |\n| Accept targeted invite as wrong user | 403 → visible error |\n| Accept success while already member | 200 → enter workspace (idempotent) |\n| Topic save on archived channel | 423 → `settings-topic-error`; suggest unarchive |\n| Archive by non-owner | Control hidden/disabled; if called, 403 error |\n| Archive `#general` | Allowed if owner (server permits); UI does not special-case unless server errors |\n| Add member unknown username | 400 → `channel-add-member-error` |\n| Add member who is not workspace member | 400 → same |\n| Add to DM channel | Button hidden for `is_dm`; if called, 403 |\n| Add when already member | 200; list unchanged except refresh |\n| Network timeout | Visible error on active form; re-enable controls |\n| 401 on any settings call | Clear tokens; show auth modal; close settings |\n| Double-click save | Disable control until response; single in-flight request |\n| Modal open during workspace switch | Close modals; drop stale channel id |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `GET /` HTML includes DOM ids `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` and the normative `data-testid`s listed above for modal chrome, tabs, general fields, invitation accept form, and channel settings fields (list rows may be empty until data loads).\n2. Authenticated owner/admin can open workspace settings, change **name** and **join_mode**, save, and see updates in `workspace-header` / subsequent `GET` workspace detail.\n3. Member/guest **cannot** persist general settings (disabled UI and/or visible 403); must **not** silently succeed.\n4. Members tab lists all workspace members with `role-badge`; owner/admin can change permitted roles via `role-select`; forbidden changes show error and do **not** leave a lying UI role.\n5. Owner can transfer ownership to an admin via transfer controls; previous owner becomes admin in the refreshed list.\n6. Admin/owner can create an invitation; `invitation-code` is visible; list shows active invites; revoke removes the row.\n7. Onboarding `invitation-accept-*` redeems a valid code and enters the workspace shell; invite_only workspaces become accessible without using broken join-by-slug alone.\n8. With an active public/private channel, channel settings shows members (`channel-member-row`), allows topic save for authorized callers, and owner can archive/unarchive with UI reflecting `is_archived`.\n9. Topic save on archived channel surfaces **423** message and must **not** clear the topic field to empty on failure.\n10. Channel add-member with a workspace member username adds them to `channel_members` (UI list updates); guest cannot add; outsider username fails visibly.\n11. Opening one settings modal closes the other; logout closes modals and clears privileged data from the DOM on next login.\n12. Existing MARATHON-16 selectors and auth/workspace flows remain green (`tests/test_spa_shell.py` + prior SPA behavior).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated\n\n- Extend/add TestClient tests asserting required ids/testids in `GET /` and that `settings_ui.js` is served as a static asset.\n- Backend tests for `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` matrix (owner/admin/member/guest, private/public, idempotent, DM rejection, non-member target).\n- Do **not** require a browser in unit CI; optional Playwright (as M16 notes) at 1280×900 for human/agent verification.\n\n### Manual / CUA script (1280×900)\n\n1. Register → create workspace → open workspace settings → rename + set `invite_only` → save → reload → values stick.\n2. Add second user via invitation create → copy `invitation-code` → logout → register other user → accept code → lands in workspace.\n3. As owner, change member role member→admin; confirm badge/select; attempt illegal admin-on-admin as admin user → error.\n4. Select `#general` → channel settings → set topic → archive → confirm topic save fails with archived error → unarchive → topic save works.\n5. Create private channel (API or future M17 UI) → add workspace member via `channel-add-member-*` → member appears in list.\n6. As guest/member, confirm invitations tab and archive controls are not usable.\n\n### Verification mindset\n\nOutside-in: selectors + REST envelopes + visible errors. No reliance on reading JS internals beyond confirming assets load.\nDESIGN_EOF\nwc -c /tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md\n","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"28740 /tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md\n","stderr":"","executionTime":127,"interleavedOutput":"28740 /tmp/MARATHON-18.design.md\n","localExecutionTimeMs":26},"isBackground":false},"description":"Write complete MARATHON-18 design file"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-7bb3e7d2-436f-4bd5-ad8f-c072f1d79931-52\nfc_09c64263-1886-982a-8d37-44886c1841f2_0","startedAtMs":"17874452