{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-5fbd408c-21b6-49b7-b716-371c7aaac01e-11\nfc_a00c47e1-f142-988b-acc1-ebd17cc231b2_0","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"seq|WebSocket|websocket|subscribe|head_seq|channel_events|publish_|MARATHON-13|MARATHON-14","path":"/root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-app-architect-1/agent-tools/1d506913-28ef-4a96-8c52-4476bd30cf51.txt","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-5fbd408c-21b6-49b7-b716-371c7aaac01e-11\nfc_a00c47e1-f142-988b-acc1-ebd17cc231b2_0","offset":0}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-5fbd408c-21b6-49b7-b716-371c7aaac01e-11\nfc_a00c47e1-f142-988b-acc1-ebd17cc231b2_0","startedAtMs":"1787446920489"},"model_call_id":"172f6423-0041-4028-b2a0-99b2879096f8-4-kypw","session_id":"32a6295e-3abd-45c5-ac4d-eb7723abadf6","timestamp_ms":1787446924668}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-5fbd408c-21b6-49b7-b716-371c7aaac01e-11\nfc_a00c47e1-f142-988b-acc1-ebd17cc231b2_0","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"seq|WebSocket|websocket|subscribe|head_seq|channel_events|publish_|MARATHON-13|MARATHON-14","path":"/root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-app-architect-1/agent-tools/1d506913-28ef-4a96-8c52-4476bd30cf51.txt","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-5fbd408c-21b6-49b7-b716-371c7aaac01e-11\nfc_a00c47e1-f142-988b-acc1-ebd17cc231b2_0","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"seq|WebSocket|websocket|subscribe|head_seq|channel_events|publish_|MARATHON-13|MARATHON-14","path":"/root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-app-architect-1/agent-tools/1d506913-28ef-4a96-8c52-4476bd30cf51.txt","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"../../../../../root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-app-architect-1/agent-tools/1d506913-28ef-4a96-8c52-4476bd30cf51.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":29,"content":"- Epic/instruction leave language open; Python 3.12, `sqlite3`, and `redis-server` are already on the image. FastAPI covers REST + future WebSockets (Starlette) without a second runtime for the backend/IRC path.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":30,"content":"- Redis outage requirements (MARATHON-14: writes and dense `seq` continue while Redis is dead) **forbid** using Redis as the durable store. SQLite on a shared filesystem path is the simplest self-contained SoT that all three processes can open.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":172,"content":"- MARATHON-2 fixed SQLite as SoT and Redis as ephemeral fan-out only. Storing tokens in Redis would break “any node accepts the same token” after Redis `SIGKILL` and contradicts MARATHON-14. Shared SQLite is the only persistence already wired on every node.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":311,"content":"Profiles GET /api/users/{id} + PATCH /api/users/me shipped. No migration (v1 users columns). publish_user_updated is a documented no-op (no channel_id/seq) for MARATHON-13/14. Broadened RequestValidationError envelope to /api/* except /api/health. Tests: tests/test_profiles.py; full suite 73 passed. Cluster boundary: PATCH :8000 visible on GET :8001/:8002.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":317,"content":"This task adds the Profiles REST surface on top of the Auth-owned `users` table: authenticated `GET /api/users/{id}` returns a canonical `UserObj` (or 404), and authenticated `PATCH /api/users/me` applies any subset of mutable profile fields with IANA timezone and length validation (400 on failure). It does **not** change the `UserObj` shape locked by MARATHON-3; it only mutates profile columns already present in migration v1 and leaves a clear, channel-less `user.updated` event contract so MARATHON-13/14 can fan profile changes over WebSocket later.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":332,"content":"| WebSocket readiness | After a successful PATCH that changes ≥1 stored field, call `publish_user_updated(user)` with a documented payload that has **no** `channel_id` / `seq`. Implementation is a **local no-op hook** until MARATHON-13/14 wire Redis/WS fan-out |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":340,"content":"- A no-op publish hook + frozen event shape lets this task satisfy “ready to broadcast” without blocking on WebSocket work.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":349,"content":"| Emit Redis pub/sub from this task | Fan-out ownership is MARATHON-13/14; premature Redis SoT risk |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":434,"content":"| **Server** | Auth → validate provided fields → UPDATE row → bump `updated_at` → return full `UserObj` → invoke `publish_user_updated`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":463,"content":"Shipped workspaces create/list/detail per design. Migration v2 + routes. read_state uses full ReadStateEntry {channel_id,last_read_seq,unread_count,mention_count}; include_archived accepts 1 and case-insensitive true. errors.py already broadened by MARATHON-4. Tests: tests/test_workspaces.py; full unit suite green; cluster verified create:8000 list:8001 detail:8002.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":471,"content":"**Revision (needs-revision feedback):** `read_state` entries use the **full** `ReadStateEntry` shape shared with `GET /api/channels/{id}/read` (MARATHON-11): `{channel_id, last_read_seq, unread_count, mention_count}`. Empty `[]` until messages/read APIs write rows is fine; when entries are returned, all four fields are present (counts default to `0`). Query `include_archived` treats both literal `1` and `true` (case-insensitive) as “include archived.”","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":486,"content":"| `read_state` | Embed `ReadStateEntry[]` for the caller with keys **`channel_id`, `last_read_seq`, `unread_count`, `mention_count`** — identical to MARATHON-11 `GET /api/channels/{id}/read` entry shape; return `[]` until rows exist; when mapping a row, missing/null counts → JSON `0` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":496,"content":"- Embedding the **full** `read_state` entry shape now (not a truncated `{channel_id, last_read_seq}`) prevents SPA/MARATHON-11 divergence on badge fields.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":578,"content":"  \"last_read_seq\": 0,","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":587,"content":"| `last_read_seq` | integer | Non-negative; dense per-channel seq; **never** JSON `null` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":622,"content":"| Events / Redis | No pub/sub in this task (MARATHON-13/14); no Redis SoT |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":805,"content":"| Events / Redis | No pub/sub (MARATHON-13/14); optional no-op hooks OK but not required |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":943,"content":"This task completes the core chat write/read path for Huddle on top of MARATHON-7 channels and the minimal `messages` / pin embed already shipped: authenticated channel members can post top-level messages and one-level thread replies, list channel history (newest-first, cursor pagination) and thread replies (oldest-first), edit their own messages, soft-delete as author or workspace owner, and add/remove emoji reactions. It locks the REST `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` contracts the SPA (MARATHON-17) and downstream search/WS tasks consume, extends schema with reaction (and optional attachment join) tables while **preserving** the v3 `messages` table and pin routes, and leaves slash-command interception, full mention forms, file upload ownership, and dense `seq` fan-out to their owning tasks.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":954,"content":"| `MessageObj` | **Same key set as MARATHON-7** (`MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`); enrich `reply_count`, `files`, `reactions`, `mentions` for real data; **no `seq`** on REST objects (product: seq lives on WS frames — MARATHON-13) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":964,"content":"| Events | Add no-op hooks in `server/events.py` (`publish_message_created` / `updated` / `deleted` / `reaction_changed`) for MARATHON-13; call after successful commit; must not raise |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":973,"content":"- Deferring seq, slash, file upload, and advanced mentions prevents this task from blocking on MARATHON-10/11/13 while still accepting forward-compatible POST fields.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":983,"content":"| Include `seq` on `MessageObj` | Product: seq on WS frames only |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1006,"content":"#### `MessageObj` (normative keys — do not omit; do not add `seq` / `blocks` / `deleted_at` to JSON)","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1221,"content":"| Events / Redis | No pub/sub (MARATHON-13/14) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1343,"content":"======== MARATHON-14 ========","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":25,"totalMatchedLines":25,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-5fbd408c-21b6-49b7-b716-371c7aaac01e-11\nfc_a00c47e1-f142-988b-acc1-ebd17cc231b2_0","startedAtMs":"1787446920489","completedAtMs":"1787446924705"},"model_call_id":"172f6423-0041-4028-b2a0-99b2879096f8-4-kypw","session_id":"32a6295e-3abd-45c5-ac4d-eb7723abadf6","timestamp_ms":1787446924728}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-5fbd408c-21b6-49b7-b716-371c7aaac01e-12\nfc_a00c47e1-f142-988b-acc1-ebd17cc231b2_1","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"python3 <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nfor id in [\"MARATHON-8\",\"MARATHON-7\",\"MARATHON-4\",\"MARATHON-14\",\"MARATHON-15\",\"MARATHON-9\",\"MARATHON-3\"]:\n  out=subprocess.check_output([\"loom\",\"data\",\"show\",id,\"--output\",\"json\"],text=True)\n  # strip log lines\n  lines=out.strip().splitlines()\n  json_start=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('{'))\n  d=json.loads('\\n'.join(lines[json_start:]))\n  design=d.get('design') or ''\n  notes=d.get('notes') or ''\n  print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\\n{id}: {d.get('title')} status={d.get('status')} labels={d.get('labels')}\")\n  print(f\"design_len={len(design)} notes_len={len(notes)}\")\n  # print full design for key ones\n  if id in (\"MARATHON-8\",\"MARATHON-7\",\"MARATHON-4\",\"MARATHON-14\"):\n    print(\"---FULL DESIGN---\")\n    print(design if design else \"(none)\")\n    print(\"---NOTES---\")\n    print(notes if notes else \"(none)\")\nPY","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-5fbd408c-21b6-49b7-b716-371c7aaac01e-12\nfc_a00c47e1-f142-988b-acc1-ebd17cc231b2_1","simpleCommands":["python3"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"python3","args":[],"fullText":"python3"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"python3"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Extract key sibling full designs","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"32a6295e-3abd-45c5-ac4d-eb7723abadf6","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"description":"Extract key sibling full designs"},"hookAddition