{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-c19fd540-e4f8-4f7f-ad1f-7767e36c4c72-14\nfc_45e9b575-7995-921b-b5b0-88c11617fc8c_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-app-architect-1/agent-tools/7528b5ed-a329-440b-bd42-fb09752ad0ef.txt","offset":1,"limit":200}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-c19fd540-e4f8-4f7f-ad1f-7767e36c4c72-14\nfc_45e9b575-7995-921b-b5b0-88c11617fc8c_0","startedAtMs":"1787446929738"},"model_call_id":"172f6423-0041-4028-b2a0-99b2879096f8-5-dg86","session_id":"32a6295e-3abd-45c5-ac4d-eb7723abadf6","timestamp_ms":1787446939366}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-c19fd540-e4f8-4f7f-ad1f-7767e36c4c72-14\nfc_45e9b575-7995-921b-b5b0-88c11617fc8c_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-app-architect-1/agent-tools/7528b5ed-a329-440b-bd42-fb09752ad0ef.txt","offset":1,"limit":200},"result":{"success":{"content":"time=2026-08-23T01:02:05.584Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n\n============================================================\nMARATHON-8: Messages, threads, reactions REST API status=closed labels=['backend']\ndesign_len=28212 notes_len=478\n---FULL DESIGN---\n# MARATHON-8 — Messages, threads, reactions REST API\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task completes the core chat write/read path for Huddle on top of MARATHON-7 channels and the minimal `messages` / pin embed already shipped: authenticated channel members can post top-level messages and one-level thread replies, list channel history (newest-first, cursor pagination) and thread replies (oldest-first), edit their own messages, soft-delete as author or workspace owner, and add/remove emoji reactions. It locks the REST `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` contracts the SPA (MARATHON-17) and downstream search/WS tasks consume, extends schema with reaction (and optional attachment join) tables while **preserving** the v3 `messages` table and pin routes, and leaves slash-command interception, full mention forms, file upload ownership, and dense `seq` fan-out to their owning tasks.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite SoT; **migration version 4** additive: `message_reactions`, optional `message_files`, optional `messages.blocks_json`; **do not** drop/recreate v3 `messages` |\n| Route layout | Channel-scoped on `server/channels/routes.py`: `POST`/`GET /api/channels/{id}/messages`. Message-scoped on existing `server/messages/routes.py`: `PATCH`/`DELETE /{id}`, `GET /{parent_id}/replies`, `POST`/`DELETE .../reactions`, keep existing pin routes |\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all endpoints require Bearer |\n| `MessageObj` | **Same key set as MARATHON-7** (`MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`); enrich `reply_count`, `files`, `reactions`, `mentions` for real data; **no `seq`** on REST objects (product: seq lives on WS frames — MARATHON-13) |\n| Soft delete | Set `deleted_at`; **exclude** deleted rows from channel history and reply lists; DELETE idempotent; PATCH / react on deleted → **409** `conflict` |\n| Archived writes | Reuse `server.channels.store.assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived` for POST message, PATCH, DELETE (mutating), POST/DELETE reaction (same as pin) |\n| Membership for writes | Same as pin mutate: caller must be **channel member**; workspace owner without membership → **403** |\n| Membership for reads | Same as GET pins: public → workspace member else 404; private/DM → channel member else 403 (non-member workspace) / 404 (stranger) |\n| Threads | Single level only: `parent_id` must reference a **top-level** (`parent_id IS NULL`), same-channel, non-deleted message |\n| Reactions | Table unique on `(message_id, user_id, emoji)`; aggregate to `[{emoji, count, user_ids}]`; POST/DELETE idempotent |\n| `file_ids` / `blocks` | Accept on POST for product shape; `blocks` persisted as JSON text (not exposed on `MessageObj` keys); `file_ids` validated against files when present — **non-empty `file_ids` → 400** until MARATHON-10 provides attachable `files` rows (seam documented) |\n| Mentions (this task) | Resolve `@username` only (word-boundary, no mid-word, no self, dedupe, must be workspace member); `@channel`/`@here`/`@group-handle` → MARATHON-11 |\n| Slash commands | **Not** interpreted here; body stored literally (including `/me`, `/shrug`, …). MARATHON-11 intercepts |\n| Events | Add no-op hooks in `server/events.py` (`publish_message_created` / `updated` / `deleted` / `reaction_changed`) for MARATHON-13; call after successful commit; must not raise |\n| Timestamps | `utc_now_z()` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`) |\n| Ids | UUID4 strings |\n\n### Why\n\n- Product contract (epic planning) is explicit on paths, envelopes (`201 {message}`, `{replies}`, `{reactions}`, `{deleted:true}`), reaction shape, and delete/edit conflict semantics; inventing alternates breaks graders and MARATHON-17.\n- Extending v3 (not replacing) keeps pin FKs and MARATHON-7 tests stable; `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` remains the single key source (pin tests import it).\n- Aligning write authz with pin membership + `assert_channel_writable` avoids a second archived/private matrix.\n- Deferring seq, slash, file upload, and advanced mentions prevents this task from blocking on MARATHON-10/11/13 while still accepting forward-compatible POST fields.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Put all routes under `/api/messages` only | Product: `POST/GET /api/channels/{id}/messages` |\n| Hard-delete rows | Breaks pin FK / audit; product soft-delete + 409 on edit |\n| Tombstone deleted messages in channel history | Product allows either; **excluding** from listings is simpler for SPA empty states and matches “disappear”; pins still resolve via store for already-pinned ids |\n| Nested threads (reply-to-reply) | Product is parent/replies one level; reject deep `parent_id` with 400 |\n| Include `seq` on `MessageObj` | Product: seq on WS frames only |\n| Implement slash / @channel in this task | Owned by MARATHON-11 |\n| Create full `files` upload schema here | Owned by MARATHON-10; accept `file_ids` but 400 when unsatisfiable |\n| Allow any workspace member to post in public without join | Diverges from pin write rule (must be channel member) |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\n`file_ids` and rich mention forms are accepted or partially implemented: non-empty attachments fail closed with 400 until MARATHON-10; only `@username` mentions populate `mentions` until MARATHON-11. Implementers must not invent FileObj upload or slash side effects here.\n\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: UUID4 ids; `ApiError` + `{error:{code,message}}`; ignore unknown JSON fields; `400` `validation_error`; `401` `unauthorized`; `409` `conflict`.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-4**: nested `author` is full `UserObj` via `row_to_user_obj` / joined columns.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-5/6**: workspace slug/`owner_id`; roles; non-member → **404** (no leak); privilege lack → **403**.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj`; `assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived`; minimal `MessageObj` key set; pin routes stay; private vs public visibility matrix for pins/messages reads; channel-member required for pin/message **writes**.\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Shared types\n\n#### `MessageObj` (normative keys — do not omit; do not add `seq` / `blocks` / `deleted_at` to JSON)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"…\",\n  \"channel_id\": \"…\",\n  \"author_id\": \"…\",\n  \"author\": { \"id\": \"…\", \"username\": \"…\", \"display_name\": \"…\", \"timezone\": null, \"avatar_url\": null, \"status_text\": null, \"status_emoji\": null },\n  \"body\": \"hello\",\n  \"parent_id\": null,\n  \"reply_count\": 0,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-23T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"edited_at\": null,\n  \"files\": [],\n  \"reactions\": [],\n  \"mentions\": []\n}\n```\n\nExact keys = `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` already in `server/messages/store.py`.\n\n| Field | Rules |\n|-------|--------|\n| `reply_count` | Count of **non-deleted** children with `parent_id = this.id` |\n| `edited_at` | `null` until first successful PATCH; then UTC Z timestamp |\n| `files` | `FileObj[]` (see MARATHON-10). Until files exist / attach works → always `[]` |\n| `reactions` | `ReactionObj[]` aggregated (below) |\n| `mentions` | `string[]` of user ids (deduped), from `@username` resolution at create/edit |\n\n#### `ReactionObj`\n\n```json\n{ \"emoji\": \"👍\", \"count\": 2, \"user_ids\": [\"uuid-a\", \"uuid-b\"] }\n```\n\nProduct name for the emoji field is **`emoji`** (not `name`). Do not add a `me` boolean; clients derive that from `user_ids` containing the caller id.\n\n- Group by exact `emoji` string.\n- `count` = `len(user_ids)`.\n- `user_ids` ordered by reaction `created_at ASC`, then `user_id ASC`.\n- Reaction groups ordered by first-reaction `created_at ASC`, tie-break `emoji ASC`.\n\n#### `FileObj` (embed only; created by MARATHON-10)\n\n`{id, uploader_id, filename, content_type, size, created_at}` per product Files section — M8 returns `files: []` unless MARATHON-10 rows are resolvable.\n\n#### Error codes (this task)\n\n| `code` | HTTP | When |\n|--------|------|------|\n| `validation_error` | 400 | Empty/whitespace body; body too long; bad `limit`/`before`; bad `parent_id`; bad `emoji`; non-empty unsatisfiable `file_ids`; `blocks` not a list when present |\n| `unauthorized` | 401 | Missing/invalid bearer |\n| `forbidden` | 403 | Not channel member on write; not author on PATCH; not author/owner on DELETE; private read without membership |\n| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown channel/message; public channel + non-workspace-member; stranger on private |\n| `conflict` | 409 | PATCH or react on soft-deleted message |\n| `archived` | 423 | Mutating write on archived channel |\n\n### Authz helpers (implement once, reuse)\n\nMirror MARATHON-7 pin access:\n\n**`require_channel_message_read(channel, user)`** — same rules as `GET /api/channels/{id}/pins` (public: workspace member; private/DM: channel member).\n\n**`require_channel_message_write(channel, user)`** — channel **member** required (public or private); then `assert_channel_writable`. Workspace owner without membership → **403** (same as pin).\n\nFor message-id routes: load message → load channel → apply read or write helper; missing message → **404** (do not leak across workspaces).\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client (SPA M17)** | Bearer; body `{body, parent_id?, file_ids?, blocks?}`; disable composer while in flight; on 201 append message / bump thread `reply_count`; on 400 show empty-message validation; on 423 show archived lock |\n| **Server** | Authz write; validate; insert; resolve mentions; optional file attach; bump nothing external yet; return **201** |\n\n**Request:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"body\": \"hello @alice\",\n  \"parent_id\": null,\n  \"file_ids\": [],\n  \"blocks\": null\n}\n```\n\n**Validation:**\n\n- `body` required string; after Unicode trim of leading/trailing whitespace, length **1..4000** code points; empty/whitespace-only → **400**.\n- `parent_id` optional; if set: must exist, same `channel_id`, `deleted_at IS NULL`, and parent’s `parent_id IS NULL`; else **400**.\n- `file_ids` optional list of strings; default omit/`[]`. **Each** id must refer to a file owned by caller and not already attached (MARATHON-10). If files table/rows unavailable or any id fails → **400** `validation_error`. Empty list OK → `files: []`.\n- `blocks` optional; if present must be a **JSON array** (elements unchecked beyond JSON); persist as `blocks_json`; **not** included in `MessageObj` response keys.\n- Unknown fields ignored.\n\n**Response:** `201 { \"message\": MessageObj }`\n\n**Effects:** Insert row (`edited_at=null`, `deleted_at=null`); compute `mentions`; if `parent_id` set, child’s presence increases parent `reply_count` on subsequent reads; call `publish_message_created` after commit (no-op OK).\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages?limit=&before=`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Bearer; initial load + scroll-up with `before=<oldest_seen_id>`; keep prior list on error; render newest at bottom per UI |\n| **Server** | Authz read; return **only top-level** (`parent_id IS NULL`) **non-deleted** messages; **newest-first** |\n\n**Query:**\n\n- `limit` optional int, default **50**, min 1, max **100**; invalid → 400.\n- `before` optional message id cursor: return messages strictly older than the cursor message’s (`created_at`, `id`) pair within the same channel; cursor must be a message in this channel (deleted cursor still OK as position); unknown id → **400**.\n\n**Response:** `200 { \"messages\": [MessageObj, ...] }`\n\nEach element fully enriched (`author`, `reply_count`, `reactions`, `mentions`, `files`).\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ `PATCH /api/messages/{message_id}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Body `{body}`; show edited indicator from `edited_at`; on 409 treat as deleted |\n| **Server** | Author-only; not deleted; writable channel; set `body`, `edited_at=now`, re-resolve `mentions` |\n\n**Rules:**\n\n- Unknown → 404 (after read visibility check on channel).\n- `caller.id != author_id` → **403**.\n- `deleted_at` set → **409** `conflict`.\n- Archived channel → **423**.\n- Same body validation as create (empty → 400).","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":1505,"fileSize":83206,"path":"/root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-app-architect-1/agent-tools/7528b5ed-a329-440b-bd42-fb09752ad0ef.txt","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":200},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-c19fd540-e4f8-4f7f-ad1f-7767e36c4c72-14\nfc_45e9b575-7995-921b-b5b0-88c11617fc8c_0","startedAtMs":"1787446929738","completedAtMs":"1787446939391"},"model_call_id":"172f6423-0041-4028-b2a0-99b2879096f8-5-dg86","session_id":"32a6295e-3abd-45c5-ac4d-eb7723abadf6","timestamp_ms":1787446939414}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-c19fd540-e4f8-4f7f-ad1f-7767e36c4c72-15\nfc_45e9b575-7995-921b-b5b0-88c11617fc8c_1","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"python3 <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nfor id in [\"MARATHON-8\",\"MARATHON-7\",\"MARATHON-4\",\"MARATHON-14\",\"MARATHON-2\"]:\n  out=subprocess.check_output([\"loom\",\"data\",\"show\",id,\"--output\",\"json\"],text=True)\n  lines=out.strip().splitlines()\n  json_start=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('{'))\n  d=json.loads('\\n'.join(lines[json_start:]))\n  design=d.get('design') or ''\n  # extract sections mentioning seq, websocket, events, membership\n  print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\\n{id} design length {len(design)}\")\n  if not design:\n    notes=d.get('notes') or ''\n    print(\"NO DESIGN; notes:\", notes[:2000])\n    continue\n  # print Interface Contracts and Data Model and Out of Scope related\n  for marker in [\"### Summary\",\"### Technical Approach\",\"### Interface Contracts\",\"### Data Model\",\"### Files\",\"### Sequencing\",\"### Out of Scope\",\"### Edge Cases\",\"### Acceptance\",\"### Testing\"]:\n    idx=design.find(marker)\n    if idx>=0:\n      print(f\"\\nFOUND {marker} at {idx}\")\n  # print excerpts with keywords\n  for kw in [\"seq\", \"WebSocket\", \"websocket\", \"subscribe\", \"resume\", \"user.updated\", \"message.created\", \"channel.\", \"membership\", \"publish_\", \"events\", \"Redis\", \"head_seq\", \"since_seq\", \"gap\"]:\n    pass\n  # dump full for 14 and relevant parts\n  if id==\"MARATHON-14\":\n    print(design[:5000] if design else \"empty\")\n    print(\"NOTES:\", (d.get('notes') or '')[:3000])\nPY\n# Also get MARATHON-7 and 8 sections on events\npython3 <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess,re\nfor id in [\"MARATHON-8\",\"MARATHON-7\",\"MARATHON-4\"]:\n  out=subprocess.check_output([\"loom\",\"data\",\"show\",id,\"--output\",\"json\"],text=True)\n  lines=out.strip().splitlines()\n  json_start=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('{'))\n  d=json.loads('\\n'.join(lines[json_start:]))\n  design=d.get('design') or ''\n  print(f\"\\n######## {id} EVENT/SEQ EXCERPTS ########\")\n  for m in re.finditer(r'.{0,80}(seq|WebSocket|websocket|publish_|user\\.updated|message\\.|channel\\.|membership|events\\.py|resume|subscribe).{0,120}', design, re.I|re.S):\n    s=' '.join(m.group(0).split())\n    if len(s)>200: s=s[:200]\n    print('-', s)\nPY","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-c19fd540-e4f8-4f7f-ad1f-7767e36c4c72-15\nfc_45e9b575-7995-921b-b5b0-88c11617fc8c_1","simpleCommands":["python3","python3"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"python3","args":[],"fullText":"python3"},{"name":"python3","args":[],"fullText":"python3"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"python3"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"python3"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Extract event/seq excerpts from designs","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"32a6295e-3abd-45c5-ac4d-eb7723abadf6","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"description":"Extract event/seq excerpts from designs"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-c19fd540-e4f8-4f7f-ad1f-7767e36c4c72-15\nfc_45e9b575-7995-921b-b5b0-88c11617fc8c_1","startedAtMs":"1787446939711"},"model_call_id":"172f6423-0041-4028-b2a0-99b2879096f8-5-dg86","session_id":"32a6295e-3abd-45c5-ac4d-eb7723abadf6","timestamp_ms":1787446939734}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-c19fd540-e4f8-4f7f-ad1f-7767e36c4c72-16\nfc_45e9b575-7995-921b-b5b0-88c11617fc8c_2","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/messages/routes.py","limit":100}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-c19fd540-e4f8-4f7f-ad1f-7767e36c4c72-16\nfc_45e9b575-7995-921b-b5b0-88c11617fc8c_2","startedAtMs":"1787446939713"},"model_call_id":"172f6423-0041-4028-b2a0-99b2879096f8-5-dg86","session_id":"32a6295e-3abd-45c5-ac4d-eb7723abadf6","timestamp_ms":1787446940115}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-c19fd540-e4f8-4f7f-ad1f-7767e36c4c72-16\nfc_45e9b575-7995-921b-b5b0-88c11617fc8c_2","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/messages/routes.py","limit":100},"result":{"success":{"content":"\"\"\"Message CRUD, threads, reactions, and pin routes (MARATHON-8).\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom urllib.parse import unquote\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, Request\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict\n\nfrom server import db, events\nfrom server.auth.deps import get_current_user\nfrom server.channels import store as channels_store\nfrom server.errors import ApiError\nfrom server.messages import store as messages_store\nfrom server.settings import Settings\n\nrouter = APIRouter(prefix=\"/api/messages\", tags=[\"messages\"])\n\n\nclass PatchMessageBody(BaseModel):\n    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"ignore\")\n\n    body: str\n\n\nclass ReactionBody(BaseModel):\n    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"ignore\")\n\n    emoji: str\n\n\ndef _settings(request: Request) -> Settings:\n    return request.app.state.settings\n\n\ndef _workspace_owner_id(conn: Any, workspace_id: str) -> str | None:\n    row = conn.execute(\n        \"SELECT owner_id FROM workspaces WHERE id = ?\", (workspace_id,)\n    ).fetchone()\n    return str(row[\"owner_id\"]) if row is not None else None\n\n\ndef _load_message_and_channel(\n    conn: Any, message_id: str\n) -> tuple[Any, dict[str, Any]]:\n    msg_row = messages_store.get_message_row(conn, message_id)\n    if msg_row is None:\n        raise ApiError(404, \"not_found\", \"message not found\")\n    channel = channels_store.get_channel(conn, msg_row[\"channel_id\"])\n    if channel is None:\n        raise ApiError(404, \"not_found\", \"message not found\")\n    return msg_row, channel\n\n\ndef _require_message_channel_access(\n    conn: Any,\n    *,\n    message_id: str,\n    user_id: str,\n    mode: str,\n) -> tuple[Any, dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Load message + channel; enforce read or write access.\"\"\"\n    msg_row, channel = _load_message_and_channel(conn, message_id)\n    if mode == \"write\":\n        messages_store.require_channel_message_write(\n            conn,\n            channel=channel,\n            user_id=user_id,\n            not_found=\"message not found\",\n        )\n    else:\n        messages_store.require_channel_message_read(\n            conn,\n            channel=channel,\n            user_id=user_id,\n            not_found=\"message not found\",\n        )\n    return msg_row, channel\n\n\n@router.post(\"/{message_id}/pin\")\ndef pin_message(\n    message_id: str,\n    request: Request,\n    caller: dict[str, Any] = Depends(get_current_user),\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    settings = _settings(request)\n    conn = db.connect(settings.sqlite_path)\n    try:\n        conn.execute(\"BEGIN\")\n        _msg_row, channel = _require_message_channel_access(\n            conn, message_id=message_id, user_id=caller[\"id\"], mode=\"write\"\n        )\n        pin = channels_store.insert_pin(\n            conn,\n            message_id=message_id,\n            channel_id=channel[\"id\"],\n            pinned_by=caller[\"id\"],\n        )","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":313,"fileSize":9222,"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/messages/routes.py","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":100},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-c19fd540-e4f8-4f7f-ad1f-7767e36c4c72-16\nfc_45e9b575-7995-921b-b5b0-88c11617fc8c_2","startedAtMs":"1787446939713","completedAtMs":"1787446940136"},"model_call_id":"172f6423-0041-4028-b2a0-99b2879096f8-5-dg86","session_id":"32a6295e-3abd-45c5-ac4d-eb7723abadf6","timestamp_ms":1787446940158}
