{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-87d82fd0-5d73-4f7e-b6f6-99c7ffc89b67-26\nfc_e088664f-2ac0-9c69-8fda-96b6d54fca63_1","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"python3 <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\n# Get epic notes if any via full show text\nimport subprocess as sp\nr=sp.run([\"loom\",\"data\",\"show\",\"MARATHON-1\"],capture_output=True,text=True)\nprint(r.stdout)\n# Also check MARATHON-9,16,17,15 descriptions\nfor id in [\"MARATHON-9\",\"MARATHON-15\",\"MARATHON-16\",\"MARATHON-17\",\"MARATHON-11\",\"MARATHON-10\"]:\n  out=sp.check_output([\"loom\",\"data\",\"show\",id,\"--output\",\"json\"],text=True)\n  lines=out.strip().splitlines()\n  js=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('{'))\n  d=json.loads('\\n'.join(lines[js:]))\n  print(f\"\\n==== {id} ====\")\n  print(\"title:\", d.get(\"title\"))\n  print(\"status:\", d.get(\"status\"), \"labels:\", d.get(\"labels\"))\n  print(\"desc:\", (d.get(\"description\") or \"\")[:800])\n  print(\"has_design:\", bool(d.get(\"design\")), \"design_len:\", len(d.get(\"design\") or \"\"))\n  notes=(d.get(\"notes\") or \"\")\n  if notes: print(\"notes:\", notes[:600])\nPY","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-87d82fd0-5d73-4f7e-b6f6-99c7ffc89b67-26\nfc_e088664f-2ac0-9c69-8fda-96b6d54fca63_1","simpleCommands":["python3"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"python3","args":[],"fullText":"python3"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"python3"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Epic notes and dependent task descriptions","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"32a6295e-3abd-45c5-ac4d-eb7723abadf6","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"python3 <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\n# Get epic notes if any via full show text\nimport subprocess as sp\nr=sp.run([\"loom\",\"data\",\"show\",\"MARATHON-1\"],capture_output=True,text=True)\nprint(r.stdout)\n# Also check MARATHON-9,16,17,15 descriptions\nfor id in [\"MARATHON-9\",\"MARATHON-15\",\"MARATHON-16\",\"MARATHON-17\",\"MARATHON-11\",\"MARATHON-10\"]:\n  out=sp.check_output([\"loom\",\"data\",\"show\",id,\"--output\",\"json\"],text=True)\n  lines=out.strip().splitlines()\n  js=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('{'))\n  d=json.loads('\\n'.join(lines[js:]))\n  print(f\"\\n==== {id} ====\")\n  print(\"title:\", d.get(\"title\"))\n  print(\"status:\", d.get(\"status\"), \"labels:\", d.get(\"labels\"))\n  print(\"desc:\", (d.get(\"description\") or \"\")[:800])\n  print(\"has_design:\", bool(d.get(\"design\")), \"design_len:\", len(d.get(\"design\") or \"\"))\n  notes=(d.get(\"notes\") or \"\")\n  if notes: print(\"notes:\", notes[:600])\nPY","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"ID:       MARATHON-1\nTitle:    Huddle: Slack-like team chat cluster\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 2\nType:     epic\nOwner:    marathon-harness\n\nDescription:\nBuild a self-contained Slack-like team chat at /app. Verifier runs /app/start.sh (foreground) which must keep serving while alive.\n\nExpose HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002, IRC on :6667, browser UI at GET /. Local Redis pub/sub on :6379. No remote services, no DinD, no Slack SDK.\n\nProduct: auth, profiles, workspaces, invitations, roles, public/private channels, DMs, messages, threads, reactions, pins, files, search, user groups, slash commands, mentions, read state, settings, SPA.\n\nCluster: dense per-channel seq shared across HTTP+IRC; replay after reconnect to different node; fan-out across nodes; survive one HTTP node SIGKILL (respawn <60s); survive Redis SIGKILL with continued dense fan-out within 5s then Redis respawn.\n\nAPI: REST + bearer auth, JSON envelopes, stable ids, UTC timestamps. UI: stable data-testid/selectors for CUA/Playwright at 1280x900.\n\n\n==== MARATHON-9 ====\ntitle: DMs: get-or-create DM channel\nstatus: in_progress labels: ['backend']\ndesc: POST /api/dms {user_id} → 200 {channel_id}. Same channel id both directions and on repeated calls. Channel is_dm=true.\nhas_design: True design_len: 18939\nnotes: Design complete for POST /api/dms get-or-create. Key decisions: body requires user_id+workspace_id (workspace-scoped channels); always 200 {channel_id}; dedupe via deterministic dm- name hash (no migration — avoids M8/M12 v4 clash); is_dm+is_private; ensure both memberships; tighten DM authz to members-only (no workspace-owner bypass). Handed to review; implementer label remains backend.\n\n==== MARATHON-15 ====\ntitle: IRC gateway on :6667 with bidirectional bridge\nstatus: open labels: ['architect', 'backend']\ndesc: Listen 0.0.0.0:6667. PASS token before NICK/USER; bad → 464. Registration 001-005 then 422 NOMOTD. JOIN unknown → 403; nick collision → 433 keep connection; unknown cmd → 421. Map web channels to #{workspace-slug}-{channel-name}. JOIN → JOIN prefix, 353, 366; topic 332/331. PRIVMSG commits into same dense per-channel seq as HTTP messages; web messages fan out to IRC as PRIVMSG. Support PING/PONG/QUIT/NAMES/WHO/LIST/TOPIC/MODE; QUIT closes without error reply. Survives HTTP node kill via remaining cluster.\nhas_design: False design_len: 0\n\n==== MARATHON-16 ====\ntitle: SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\nstatus: closed labels: ['frontend']\ndesc: Serve SPA from GET / on any node. Sign-up form with visible error on invalid input; auto-login on success. Logout/login restores same workspace. Store bearer in localStorage huddle.token (or accepted fallbacks). Three-pane layout shell: coloured sidebar + message pane + on-demand thread panel. Workspace identity in sidebar. Stable selectors: auth-form, auth-submit, auth-toggle, auth-modal, workspace-create-form, empty-state-create-workspace, join-workspace-*, current-user, logout-btn, workspace-header, channel-list, dms-list. Drivable at 1280x900.\nhas_design: True design_len: 23433\nnotes: IMPL: Zero-build SPA at GET / (static/). Token write huddle.token; read fallbacks huddle_token/token. Workspace restore via huddle.workspaceSlug across logout. Join form POSTs /api/workspaces/{slug}/join (server still MARATHON-7). Verified via pytest + Playwright at 1280x900 (register/login/create/logout/restore; thread panel hidden).\n\n==== MARATHON-17 ====\ntitle: SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\nstatus: open labels: ['architect', 'frontend']\ndesc: Channel list/create/switch; duplicate-name validation; data-channel-id/name on entries; hashtag-prefixed names; channel header name+topic; empty-channel non-blank copy. Messages: post/edit/delete via hover-toolbar; edited indicator; survive hard reload; empty-message validation. Message rows: avatar+author+human-readable timestamp+body. Threads: right-side panel; bump N replies. Reactions via emoji-picker grid (not prompt()); reaction badge with count. Pinned testids: channel-*, message-*, thread-*, reaction-*, emoji-*, create-channel-modal, etc. per frontend hooks.\nhas_design: False design_len: 0\n\n==== MARATHON-11 ====\ntitle: Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\nstatus: open labels: ['architect', 'backend']\ndesc: GET /api/search?q=&workspace_id=. Slash commands as message body: /me, /shrug, /topic, /invite @user, /archive, /unarchive; unknown and /me without text → 400; //literal posts literally; side-effect cmds return 201 message:null + channel/invited_user. Mentions: @username, @group-handle, @channel, @here rules per spec; no self mention_count. GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read for read_state; never move cursor backwards; workspace detail embeds same shape.\nhas_design: False design_len: 0\n\n==== MARATHON-10 ====\ntitle: Files: upload, metadata, download, attach\nstatus: open labels: ['architect', 'backend']\ndesc: POST /api/files multipart file part → 201 {file:FileObj}; >10MiB → 413. GET /api/files/{id}; GET download with Content-Type and Content-Disposition. Attaching via file_ids on message create requires caller's own unattached file else 400. Integrate with messages endpoint once available (may land after or coordinate with messages task).\nhas_design: False design_len: 0\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T01:02:41.663Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:02:41.674Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:02:41.684Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:02:41.697Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:02:41.706Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:02:41.714Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":169,"interleavedOutput":"time=2026-08-23T01:02:41.663Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:02:41.674Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:02:41.684Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:02:41.697Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:02:41.706Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:02:41.714Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\nID:       MARATHON-1\nTitle:    Huddle: Slack-like team chat cluster\nStatus:   open\nPriority: 2\nType:     epic\nOwner:    marathon-harness\n\nDescription:\nBuild a self-contained Slack-like team chat at /app. Verifier runs /app/start.sh (foreground) which must keep serving while alive.\n\nExpose HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002, IRC on :6667, browser UI at GET /. Local Redis pub/sub on :6379. No remote services, no DinD, no Slack SDK.\n\nProduct: auth, profiles, workspaces, invitations, roles, public/private channels, DMs, messages, threads, reactions, pins, files, search, user groups, slash commands, mentions, read state, settings, SPA.\n\nCluster: dense per-channel seq shared across HTTP+IRC; replay after reconnect to different node; fan-out across nodes; survive one HTTP node SIGKILL (respawn <60s); survive Redis SIGKILL with continued dense fan-out within 5s then Redis respawn.\n\nAPI: REST + bearer auth, JSON envelopes, stable ids, UTC timestamps. UI: stable data-testid/selectors for CUA/Playwright at 1280x900.\n\n\n==== MARATHON-9 ====\ntitle: DMs: get-or-create DM channel\nstatus: in_progress labels: ['backend']\ndesc: POST /api/dms {user_id} → 200 {channel_id}. Same channel id both directions and on repeated calls. Channel is_dm=true.\nhas_design: True design_len: 18939\nnotes: Design complete for POST /api/dms get-or-create. Key decisions: body requires user_id+workspace_id (workspace-scoped channels); always 200 {channel_id}; dedupe via deterministic dm- name hash (no migration — avoids M8/M12 v4 clash); is_dm+is_private; ensure both memberships; tighten DM authz to members-only (no workspace-owner bypass). Handed to review; implementer label remains backend.\n\n==== MARATHON-15 ====\ntitle: IRC gateway on :6667 with bidirectional bridge\nstatus: open labels: ['architect', 'backend']\ndesc: Listen 0.0.0.0:6667. PASS token before NICK/USER; bad → 464. Registration 001-005 then 422 NOMOTD. JOIN unknown → 403; nick collision → 433 keep connection; unknown cmd → 421. Map web channels to #{workspace-slug}-{channel-name}. JOIN → JOIN prefix, 353, 366; topic 332/331. PRIVMSG commits into same dense per-channel seq as HTTP messages; web messages fan out to IRC as PRIVMSG. Support PING/PONG/QUIT/NAMES/WHO/LIST/TOPIC/MODE; QUIT closes without error reply. Survives HTTP node kill via remaining cluster.\nhas_design: False design_len: 0\n\n==== MARATHON-16 ====\ntitle: SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\nstatus: closed labels: ['frontend']\ndesc: Serve SPA from GET / on any node. Sign-up form with visible error on invalid input; auto-login on success. Logout/login restores same workspace. Store bearer in localStorage huddle.token (or accepted fallbacks). Three-pane layout shell: coloured sidebar + message pane + on-demand thread panel. Workspace identity in sidebar. Stable selectors: auth-form, auth-submit, auth-toggle, auth-modal, workspace-create-form, empty-state-create-workspace, join-workspace-*, current-user, logout-btn, workspace-header, channel-list, dms-list. Drivable at 1280x900.\nhas_design: True design_len: 23433\nnotes: IMPL: Zero-build SPA at GET / (static/). Token write huddle.token; read fallbacks huddle_token/token. Workspace restore via huddle.workspaceSlug across logout. Join form POSTs /api/workspaces/{slug}/join (server still MARATHON-7). Verified via pytest + Playwright at 1280x900 (register/login/create/logout/restore; thread panel hidden).\n\n==== MARATHON-17 ====\ntitle: SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\nstatus: open labels: ['architect', 'frontend']\ndesc: Channel list/create/switch; duplicate-name validation; data-channel-id/name on entries; hashtag-prefixed names; channel header name+topic; empty-channel non-blank copy. Messages: post/edit/delete via hover-toolbar; edited indicator; survive hard reload; empty-message validation. Message rows: avatar+author+human-readable timestamp+body. Threads: right-side panel; bump N replies. Reactions via emoji-picker grid (not prompt()); reaction badge with count. Pinned testids: channel-*, message-*, thread-*, reaction-*, emoji-*, create-channel-modal, etc. per frontend hooks.\nhas_design: False design_len: 0\n\n==== MARATHON-11 ====\ntitle: Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\nstatus: open labels: ['architect', 'backend']\ndesc: GET /api/search?q=&workspace_id=. Slash commands as message body: /me, /shrug, /topic, /invite @user, /archive, /unarchive; unknown and /me without text → 400; //literal posts literally; side-effect cmds return 201 message:null + channel/invited_user. Mentions: @username, @group-handle, @channel, @here rules per spec; no self mention_count. GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read for read_state; never move cursor backwards; workspace detail embeds same shape.\nhas_design: False design_len: 0\n\n==== MARATHON-10 ====\ntitle: Files: upload, metadata, download, attach\nstatus: open labels: ['architect', 'backend']\ndesc: POST /api/files multipart file part → 201 {file:FileObj}; >10MiB → 413. GET /api/files/{id}; GET download with Content-Type and Content-Disposition. Attaching via file_ids on message create requires caller's own unattached file else 400. Integrate with messages endpoint once available (may land after or coordinate with messages task).\nhas_design: False design_len: 0\n","localExecutionTimeMs":128},"isBackground":false},"description":"Epic notes and dependent task descriptions"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-87d82fd0-5d73-4f7e-b6f6-99c7ffc89b67-26\nfc_e088664f-2ac0-9c69-8fda-96b6d54fca63_1","startedAtMs":"1787446961573","completedAtMs":"1787446961743"},"model_call_id":"172f6423-0041-4028-b2a0-99b2879096f8-7-ypi7","session_id":"32a6295e-3abd-45c5-ac4d-eb7723abadf6","timestamp_ms":1787446961764}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-87d82fd0-5d73-4f7e-b6f6-99c7ffc89b67-27\nfc_e088664f-2ac0-9c69-8fda-96b6d54fca63_2","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/auth/tokens.py"}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-87d82fd0-5d73-4f7e-b6f6-99c7ffc89b67-27\nfc_e088664f-2ac0-9c69-8fda-96b6d54fca63_2","startedAtMs":"1787446961574"},"model_call_id":"172f6423-0041-4028-b2a0-99b2879096f8-7-ypi7","session_id":"32a6295e-3abd-45c5-ac4d-eb7723abadf6","timestamp_ms":1787446962010}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-87d82fd0-5d73-4f7e-b6f6-99c7ffc89b67-27\nfc_e088664f-2ac0-9c69-8fda-96b6d54fca63_2","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/auth/tokens.py"},"result":{"success":{"content":"\"\"\"Opaque bearer token minting and SQLite persistence.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport secrets\nimport sqlite3\n\nfrom server.db import utc_now_z\n\n\ndef hash_token(raw_token: str) -> str:\n    return hashlib.sha256(raw_token.encode(\"ascii\")).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef mint_raw_token() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return a new opaque bearer token (length always >= 16).\"\"\"\n    return secrets.token_urlsafe(32)\n\n\ndef insert_token(conn: sqlite3.Connection, user_id: str, raw_token: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Persist SHA-256 hex of raw_token for user_id.\"\"\"\n    conn.execute(\n        \"\"\"\n        INSERT INTO auth_tokens (token_hash, user_id, created_at)\n        VALUES (?, ?, ?)\n        \"\"\",\n        (hash_token(raw_token), user_id, utc_now_z()),\n    )\n\n\ndef resolve_user_id(conn: sqlite3.Connection, raw_token: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Look up user_id by hashing the presented bearer token.\"\"\"\n    if not raw_token or any(ch.isspace() for ch in raw_token):\n        return None\n    row = conn.execute(\n        \"SELECT user_id FROM auth_tokens WHERE token_hash = ?\",\n        (hash_token(raw_token),),\n    ).fetchone()\n    if row is None:\n        return None\n    return str(row[\"user_id\"])\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":43,"fileSize":1185,"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/auth/tokens.py","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":43},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-87d82fd0-5d73-4f7e-b6f6-99c7ffc89b67-27\nfc_e088664f-2ac0-9c69-8fda-96b6d54fca63_2","startedAtMs":"1787446961574","completedAtMs":"1787446962031"},"model_call_id":"172f64