{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-004124a5-025f-4436-a59e-25513285d1d9-37\nfc_0892c7b7-30c1-9711-b16d-8c3bdb2a0051_1","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"\"type\":","path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/events.py","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-004124a5-025f-4436-a59e-25513285d1d9-37\nfc_0892c7b7-30c1-9711-b16d-8c3bdb2a0051_1","offset":0}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-004124a5-025f-4436-a59e-25513285d1d9-37\nfc_0892c7b7-30c1-9711-b16d-8c3bdb2a0051_1","startedAtMs":"1787447267032"},"model_call_id":"172f6423-0041-4028-b2a0-99b2879096f8-11-chri","session_id":"32a6295e-3abd-45c5-ac4d-eb7723abadf6","timestamp_ms":1787447267081}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-004124a5-025f-4436-a59e-25513285d1d9-36\nfc_0892c7b7-30c1-9711-b16d-8c3bdb2a0051_0","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"user\\.|membership\\.|reaction\\.|message\\.|resume\\.|subscribed|since_seq|head_seq|channel_id|channel\\.id","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-13-design.md","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-004124a5-025f-4436-a59e-25513285d1d9-36\nfc_0892c7b7-30c1-9711-b16d-8c3bdb2a0051_0","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"user\\.|membership\\.|reaction\\.|message\\.|resume\\.|subscribed|since_seq|head_seq|channel_id|channel\\.id","path":"/tmp/MARATHON-13-design.md","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"../../../../../tmp/MARATHON-13-design.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":5,"content":"This task adds the real-time seam for Huddle: an authenticated WebSocket at `GET /api/ws?token=…`, client `subscribe` / `resume` control frames, and a **dense per-channel `seq`** assigned in shared SQLite so every durable channel mutation (messages including thread replies, reactions, membership, channel mutations, pins) gets a gap-free monotonic frame `{type, seq, channel_id, …}`. Profile changes keep the existing channel-less `user.updated` shape (no `seq`). Same `seq` / event rows are visible from every HTTP node via the shared DB; **live cross-node push** remains MARATHON-14 (this task delivers live frames to connections on the writing node and makes catch-up via `resume` work on any node).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":14,"content":"| Dense rule | Per `channel_id`, `seq` starts at **0** (empty) and first durable event is **1**, then `+1` per committed durable event. No gaps, no duplicates, no reuse. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":16,"content":"| Control protocol | Client JSON: `subscribe`, `resume` (with `since_seq`). Server JSON: `subscribed`, `resumed`, `resume.gap`, plus durable/live event frames and `user.updated`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":17,"content":"| History vs live | `subscribe` = watch from **now** (ack `head_seq`, no backlog). `resume` = authorize + **replay** `(since_seq+1)…head` then live, or `resume.gap` if `since_seq` is older than the retained tail. Channel history UI still uses REST (MARATHON-8). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":18,"content":"| Retention | Keep the last **`CHANNEL_EVENT_RETAIN = 10_000`** events per channel (constant in code). After append, prune `seq < head_seq - RETAIN + 1`. Tail = minimum retained `seq` (or `1` if none pruned yet / empty head). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":22,"content":"| Thread replies | Same frame type `message.created`; “reply” is `message.parent_id != null` inside the nested `MessageObj` (no separate `reply.*` type). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":44,"content":"Retention is finite (`10_000` events/channel). Clients that disconnect longer than the retained window get `resume.gap` and must reload via REST — acceptable for the marathon cluster and keeps SQLite bounded. Live multi-node push waits for M14; until then a client subscribed only on node B will not see live frames for writes on node A until it `resume`s (or reconnects).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":50,"content":"- **MARATHON-4:** `user.updated` = `{type,user}` with **no** `channel_id`/`seq`; `UserObj` keys unchanged.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":64,"content":"  \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\"","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":71,"content":"| `seq` | integer ≥ 1; dense per `channel_id` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":72,"content":"| `channel_id` | string; never null on durable frames |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":78,"content":"{ \"type\": \"user.updated\", \"user\": { /* UserObj */ } }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":81,"content":"No `channel_id`, no `seq`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":87,"content":"| `message.created` | `message`: `MessageObj` | Successful message create (top-level or reply) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":88,"content":"| `message.updated` | `message`: `MessageObj` | Successful edit |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":89,"content":"| `message.deleted` | `message_id`: string | Successful soft-delete |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":90,"content":"| `reaction.changed` | `message_id`, `reactions`: `ReactionObj[]` | Successful add/remove reaction (full aggregate, same as REST) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":91,"content":"| `membership.joined` | `user`: `UserObj` | Channel membership row **inserted** (join, create-channel creator, DM ensure-membership that inserts) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":92,"content":"| `membership.left` | `user_id`: string | Channel membership row **deleted** (leave) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":106,"content":"| **Client (SPA M17 / tools)** | Open `ws://127.0.0.1:800x/api/ws?token=<token>` (or `wss` if ever TLS). On open, `subscribe` each active channel; store last `seq` per channel; on reconnect `resume` with `since_seq`. While connecting/reconnecting: keep last REST snapshot; show reconnecting affordance (M17). Do not invent REST `seq`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":115,"content":"**Wire encoding:** one JSON object per WebSocket text message. Binary frames ignored (no error). Unknown client `type` → server sends:","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":126,"content":"{ \"type\": \"subscribe\", \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\" }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":132,"content":"| Success | Add `channel_id` to connection set (idempotent if already subscribed). Reply **`subscribed`**. **No** historical replay. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":133,"content":"| `head_seq` | Current dense head for that channel (`0` if no events yet). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":136,"content":"{ \"type\": \"subscribed\", \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\", \"head_seq\": 0 }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":142,"content":"{ \"type\": \"resume\", \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\", \"since_seq\": 10 }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":147,"content":"| `since_seq` | Required integer; must be ≥ 0. Non-int / missing / negative → `error` `validation_error`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":149,"content":"| Subscription | On success path (including gap), connection **is** subscribed to `channel_id` (resume implies subscribe). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":151,"content":"| `head == 0` | Reply `{type:\"resumed\", channel_id, head_seq:0}` with no event frames. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":152,"content":"| `since_seq > head` | `{type:\"error\", code:\"validation_error\", message:\"since_seq ahead of head\"}`; **do not** change subscription if not already subscribed; if already subscribed, leave it. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":153,"content":"| `since_seq < tail` (retained) | Send **`resume.gap`** then **do not** replay; client must REST-reload. Still subscribed. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":154,"content":"| `tail ≤ since_seq ≤ head` | Send each stored event with `seq` in `(since_seq, head]` in ascending `seq` order, then **`resumed`**. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":157,"content":"{ \"type\": \"resume.gap\", \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\", \"head_seq\": 50, \"tail_seq\": 20 }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":161,"content":"{ \"type\": \"resumed\", \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\", \"head_seq\": 50 }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":168,"content":"- After a connection is subscribed to `channel_id`, deliver every new durable frame for that channel (local hub).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":169,"content":"- Deliver `user.updated` to **every** authenticated connection on the node (no subscribe required).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":178,"content":"| `resume.gap` | Re-fetch channel history via REST; set local cursor to `head_seq`; continue live | Still subscribed |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":186,"content":"| **HTTP route / store (existing modules)** | Inside the write transaction, after the durable row change succeeds, call `events.append_channel_event(conn, …)` (or typed helpers that wrap it). On idempotent no-op, skip. After **successful commit**, call `events.deliver(frame)` (and for profiles `deliver` of `user.updated`). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":191,"content":"- `publish_message_created(conn, *, channel_id, message) -> dict`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":192,"content":"- `publish_message_updated(conn, *, channel_id, message) -> dict`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":193,"content":"- `publish_message_deleted(conn, *, channel_id, message_id) -> dict`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":194,"content":"- `publish_reaction_changed(conn, *, channel_id, message_id, reactions) -> dict`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":195,"content":"- `publish_user_updated(user) -> dict` — builds `{type:\"user.updated\", user}`; **no** conn/seq; caller delivers after commit.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":199,"content":"- `publish_membership_joined(conn, *, channel_id, user)`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":200,"content":"- `publish_membership_left(conn, *, channel_id, user_id)`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":202,"content":"- `publish_channel_pin_added/removed(conn, *, channel_id, …)`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":236,"content":"  channel_id TEXT NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":237,"content":"  head_seq INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":238,"content":"    CHECK (head_seq >= 0),","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":239,"content":"  FOREIGN KEY (channel_id) REFERENCES channels(id) ON DELETE CASCADE","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":243,"content":"- Row created lazily on first event for a channel (or optionally on channel create with `head_seq=0`).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":244,"content":"- Allocate: in a transaction, `INSERT … head_seq=1` on miss, else `UPDATE channel_seq SET head_seq = head_seq + 1 WHERE channel_id=?`, then read `head_seq`. Use a single-statement pattern that cannot race across nodes (SQLite write lock serializes).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":250,"content":"  channel_id TEXT NOT NULL,","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":255,"content":"  PRIMARY KEY (channel_id, seq),","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":256,"content":"  FOREIGN KEY (channel_id) REFERENCES channels(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":261,"content":"  ON channel_events(channel_id, seq);","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":264,"content":"- `payload_json`: JSON object of **extra** fields only (not duplicating `type`/`seq`/`channel_id`), e.g. `{\"message\":{…}}`. On read, merge into the wire frame.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":279,"content":"| `channel_seq.head_seq` | int | never |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":292,"content":"| `server/ws/hub.py` | Process-local connection registry: add/remove socket, subscribe set, `broadcast_channel(channel_id, frame)`, `broadcast_global(frame)`, slow-consumer policy |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":295,"content":"| `tests/test_ws.py` | Unit/integration tests for auth, subscribe, dense seq, resume, gap, user.updated, multi-channel |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":307,"content":"| `server/workspaces/routes.py` | On create-channel success path: `channel.created` + `membership.joined` for creator |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":308,"content":"| `server/dms/routes.py` / DM store (when present from M9) | On create: `channel.created` + `membership.joined` for each **new** membership insert |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":310,"content":"| `tests/test_messages.py` / `test_profiles.py` | Update spies/expectations if publish signatures gain `conn` / return frames; keep “no `seq` on MessageObj / user.updated” assertions |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":343,"content":"| `user.updated` shape | MARATHON-4 (shape) + **M13** (delivery) | M17 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":397,"content":"| Double subscribe | Second `subscribed` ack; still one subscription entry |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":398,"content":"| Resume with `since_seq == head` | `resumed` only; no event frames |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":399,"content":"| Resume with `since_seq == head - 1` | One event then `resumed` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":400,"content":"| Resume when pruned (`since_seq < tail`) | `resume.gap` with `tail_seq`/`head_seq`; no partial replay |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":401,"content":"| Empty channel (`head=0`) resume | `resumed` with `head_seq:0` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":407,"content":"| Channel deleted while subscribed | Stop delivering; optional `error` `not_found` on next resume; cascade deletes event rows |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":412,"content":"| Profile PATCH no-op | No `user.updated` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":418,"content":"2. After `subscribe` to a channel the caller can read, server replies `subscribed` with correct `head_seq`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":419,"content":"3. Posting a message (REST) on the **same node** as the WS connection delivers exactly one `message.created` frame with `seq == previous_head + 1`, matching nested `MessageObj` keys (no `seq` inside `message`).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":420,"content":"4. A thread reply also emits `message.created` (with `parent_id` set), consuming the next dense seq.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":421,"content":"5. Edit / delete / reaction emit `message.updated` / `message.deleted` / `reaction.changed` with dense seq and required fields.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":422,"content":"6. Join/leave that change membership emit `membership.joined` / `membership.left`; idempotent join/leave emit **nothing**.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":424,"content":"8. N durable events in one channel produce seqs `1…N` with **no gaps/duplicates** when read from `channel_events` or via resume.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":425,"content":"9. `resume` with `since_seq = k` (retained) replays `k+1…head` in order then `resumed`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":426,"content":"10. After pruning (or with `since_seq` below tail), server sends `resume.gap` and does **not** send a partial replay.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":427,"content":"11. `PATCH /api/users/me` that changes a field delivers `{type:\"user.updated\", user}` to the WS client **without** `channel_id`/`seq`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":428,"content":"12. Write message on `:8000`, open WS on `:8001`, `resume` with `since_seq=0` → receives the event(s) from SQLite (cross-node **catch-up** works without M14).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":441,"content":"- Gap: insert >`CHANNEL_EVENT_RETAIN` events (or temporarily lower retain in test) → resume from 0 → `resume.gap`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":443,"content":"- `user.updated` global delivery.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":446,"content":"- Keep profiles test: published user.updated has no seq/channel_id.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":452,"content":"3. `{\"type\":\"subscribe\",\"channel_id\":\"…\"}` → note `head_seq`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":453,"content":"4. POST a message via curl; observe `message.created` with `seq`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":455,"content":"6. PATCH profile; observe `user.updated` on an open socket.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":87,"totalMatchedLines":87,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-004124a5-025f-4436-a59e-25513285d1d9-36\nfc_0892c7b7-30c1-9711-b16d-8c3bdb2a0051_0","startedAtMs":"1787447266829","completedAtMs":"1787447267364"},"model_call_id"