{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-0362375e-d726-4b9e-ad8a-8b71e9ab2b12-12\nfc_af9a94a3-353e-9a3e-bc8f-1484bebced04_1","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"slash|search|/me|mention|read_state|@channel|@here|MARATHON-11","path":"/root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-app-architect-1/agent-tools/627646a9-728a-407a-85a6-0ba3806d158b.txt","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-0362375e-d726-4b9e-ad8a-8b71e9ab2b12-12\nfc_af9a94a3-353e-9a3e-bc8f-1484bebced04_1","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"slash|search|/me|mention|read_state|@channel|@here|MARATHON-11","path":"/root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-app-architect-1/agent-tools/627646a9-728a-407a-85a6-0ba3806d158b.txt","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"../../../../../root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-app-architect-1/agent-tools/627646a9-728a-407a-85a6-0ba3806d158b.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":4,"content":"notes: IMPL: Messages/threads/reactions REST shipped. Schema is migration v5 (design text said v4; v4 already used by MARATHON-12 groups/invitations). Additive only — preserved v3 messages. file_ids non-empty → 400 until MARATHON-10; @username mentions only; slash bodies stored literally. Unit tests green (151 excl. live/cluster port-bound); port 8000 held by another agent so live cluster pytest left unrun here — cluster read-after-write covered via dual TestClient sharing sqlite.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":10,"content":"This task completes the core chat write/read path for Huddle on top of MARATHON-7 channels and the minimal `messages` / pin embed already shipped: authenticated channel members can post top-level messages and one-level thread replies, list channel history (newest-first, cursor pagination) and thread replies (oldest-first), edit their own messages, soft-delete as author or workspace owner, and add/remove emoji reactions. It locks the REST `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` contracts the SPA (MARATHON-17) and downstream search/WS tasks consume, extends schema with reaction (and optional attachment join) tables while **preserving** the v3 `messages` table and pin routes, and leaves slash-command interception, full mention forms, file upload ownership, and dense `seq` fan-out to their owning tasks.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":19,"content":"| Route layout | Channel-scoped on `server/channels/routes.py`: `POST`/`GET /api/channels/{id}/messages`. Message-scoped on existing `server/messages/routes.py`: `PATCH`/`DELETE /{id}`, `GET /{parent_id}/replies`, `POST`/`DELETE .../reactions`, keep existing pin routes |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":21,"content":"| `MessageObj` | **Same key set as MARATHON-7** (`MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`); enrich `reply_count`, `files`, `reactions`, `mentions` for real data; **no `seq`** on REST objects (product: seq lives on WS frames — MARATHON-13) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":29,"content":"| Mentions (this task) | Resolve `@username` only (word-boundary, no mid-word, no self, dedupe, must be workspace member); `@channel`/`@here`/`@group-handle` → MARATHON-11 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":30,"content":"| Slash commands | **Not** interpreted here; body stored literally (including `/me`, `/shrug`, …). MARATHON-11 intercepts |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":40,"content":"- Deferring seq, slash, file upload, and advanced mentions prevents this task from blocking on MARATHON-10/11/13 while still accepting forward-compatible POST fields.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":46,"content":"| Put all routes under `/api/messages` only | Product: `POST/GET /api/channels/{id}/messages` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":51,"content":"| Implement slash / @channel in this task | Owned by MARATHON-11 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":57,"content":"`file_ids` and rich mention forms are accepted or partially implemented: non-empty attachments fail closed with 400 until MARATHON-10; only `@username` mentions populate `mentions` until MARATHON-11. Implementers must not invent FileObj upload or slash side effects here.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":67,"content":"From **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj`; `assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived`; minimal `MessageObj` key set; pin routes stay; private vs public visibility matrix for pins/messages reads; channel-member required for pin/message **writes**.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":88,"content":"  \"mentions\": []","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":92,"content":"Exact keys = `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` already in `server/messages/store.py`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":100,"content":"| `mentions` | `string[]` of user ids (deduped), from `@username` resolution at create/edit |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":126,"content":"| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown channel/message; public channel + non-workspace-member; stranger on private |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":140,"content":"### Seam: Client ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":145,"content":"| **Server** | Authz write; validate; insert; resolve mentions; optional file attach; bump nothing external yet; return **201** |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":168,"content":"**Effects:** Insert row (`edited_at=null`, `deleted_at=null`); compute `mentions`; if `parent_id` set, child’s presence increases parent `reply_count` on subsequent reads; call `publish_message_created` after commit (no-op OK).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":170,"content":"### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages?limit=&before=`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":184,"content":"Each element fully enriched (`author`, `reply_count`, `reactions`, `mentions`, `files`).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":186,"content":"### Seam: Client ↔ `PATCH /api/messages/{message_id}`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":191,"content":"| **Server** | Author-only; not deleted; writable channel; set `body`, `edited_at=now`, re-resolve `mentions` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":207,"content":"### Seam: Client ↔ `DELETE /api/messages/{message_id}`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":223,"content":"### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/messages/{parent_id}/replies`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":239,"content":"#### `POST /api/messages/{message_id}/reactions` body `{ \"emoji\": \"👍\" }` → `200 { \"reactions\": [ReactionObj, ...] }`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":248,"content":"#### `DELETE /api/messages/{message_id}/reactions/{emoji}` → `200 { \"reactions\": [...] }`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":265,"content":"| 404 | Channel/message inaccessible |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":326,"content":"5. Pin routes continue to work; `get_message` / `row_to_message_obj` enrich reactions/mentions/files/reply_count for pin embeds too.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":342,"content":"| `server/messages/store.py` | Create/list/get with enrichment; soft delete; reply list; reaction insert/delete/aggregate; mention resolve helper; `row_to_message_obj` fills real `reply_count`/`reactions`/`mentions`/`files` (files empty until M10); keep `MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS` unchanged |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":343,"content":"| `server/messages/routes.py` | Add PATCH, DELETE, GET replies, POST/DELETE reactions; keep pin routes; factor `_require_pin_access` into shared `_require_message_channel_access(read|write)` used by pins + CRUD + reactions |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":344,"content":"| `server/channels/routes.py` | Add `POST`/`GET /{channel_id}/messages` using messages store + same authz patterns as pins |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":346,"content":"| `server/messages/__init__.py` | Docstring: CRUD owned here |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":357,"content":"| Search / slash / read_state | MARATHON-11 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":366,"content":"2. `messages/store.py` enrichment + CRUD + reactions + mentions.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":381,"content":"| `MessageObj` + POST/GET channel messages + PATCH/DELETE | MARATHON-17 SPA; MARATHON-11 search/slash (reads body); MARATHON-13 event payloads |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":385,"content":"| `mentions: user_id[]` from `@username` | MARATHON-11 extends forms / mention_count |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":397,"content":"- Slash commands + `@channel`/`@here`/`@group` + read_state → MARATHON-11.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":406,"content":"| Slash `/me` `/shrug` `/topic` … interception | message POST body | MARATHON-11 (M8 stores literal body) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":407,"content":"| `@channel` / `@here` / `@group-handle` | mentions | MARATHON-11 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":408,"content":"| `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` | read_state | MARATHON-11 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":409,"content":"| `GET /api/search` | search | MARATHON-11 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":413,"content":"| Changing pin route semantics | `server/messages/routes.py` pin | Already shipped; only share helpers/enrichment |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":420,"content":"| `server/messages/store.py` — thin `MessageObj` / get | **In scope** — enrich + CRUD |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":421,"content":"| `server/messages/routes.py` — pin only | **In scope** — add CRUD/reactions; keep pins |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":472,"content":"| Route layout | (1) Extend `server/workspaces/routes.py`: `POST /{slug}/join`, `POST /{slug}/channels`. (2) New `server/channels/routes.py` prefix `/api/channels`: join, leave, PATCH, members, archive, unarchive, pins. (3) New `server/messages/routes.py` (or pin routes mounted under `/api/messages`) for `POST/DELETE /{id}/pin` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":477,"content":"| Pins without full Message API | Minimal `messages` table + thin `MessageObj` mapper (empty `files`/`reactions`/`mentions`, `reply_count=0`) so pin list/embed works; MARATHON-8 owns message CRUD and enriches the same object |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":487,"content":"- Centralizing the archived guard prevents M8 from inventing a second 423 code/message.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":515,"content":"From **MARATHON-16**: `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` body `{}`; **200** `{workspace}` (+ optional `channels`/`read_state`); open → member; invite_only → 403; unknown → 404; idempotent if already member.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":556,"content":"  \"mentions\": []","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":589,"content":"| `not_found` | 404 | Unknown workspace slug (create/join workspace); unknown channel/message id; non-member on workspace-scoped create (same as M5/6) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":614,"content":"| **Server** | Resolve slug; if missing → 404; if already workspace member → 200 `{workspace}` (+ optional channels/read_state); if `join_mode=open` → insert `workspace_members` role=`member`, then return 200; if `invite_only` → 403 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":622,"content":"  \"read_state\": [ /* ReadStateEntry[] */ ]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":626,"content":"`channels`/`read_state` **should** be included using the same visibility rules as `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` (default: exclude archived). Minimum required by M16 is `{workspace}`; including channels avoids a second round-trip.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":695,"content":"### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/channels/{id}/members`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":749,"content":"#### `POST /api/messages/{id}/pin` → `200 {pin:{message_id,pinned_by,pinned_at}}` idempotent","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":758,"content":"#### `DELETE /api/messages/{id}/pin` → `200 {\"unpinned\":true}` idempotent","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":761,"content":"- Same visibility/membership as POST pin.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":811,"content":"- `channels`, `channel_members`, `workspaces`, `workspace_members`, `users`, `channel_read_state`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":835,"content":"| `server/messages/__init__.py` | Package init |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":836,"content":"| `server/messages/store.py` | Minimal message fetch + `row_to_message_obj` (thin); pin helpers may live here or in channels store |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":837,"content":"| `server/messages/routes.py` | `POST/DELETE /api/messages/{id}/pin` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":864,"content":"| Slash `/archive` `/topic` | MARATHON-11 (will call same store helpers) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":873,"content":"4. Channels routes: join/leave/patch/members/archive.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":889,"content":"| leave / members / PATCH topic / archive | MARATHON-18 settings; MARATHON-11 slash cmds |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":890,"content":"| `assert_channel_writable` → 423 `archived` | MARATHON-8 messages/reactions; MARATHON-11 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":908,"content":"- Slash command side effects → MARATHON-11 (reuse archive/topic store).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":916,"content":"| `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages` and message list/edit/delete | future `server/messages/routes.py` CRUD | MARATHON-8 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":917,"content":"| Reactions endpoints | `/api/messages/{id}/reactions` | MARATHON-8 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":920,"content":"| Explicit `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` add-member | SPA `channel-add-member-*` | Not in product Channels section; file follow-up if M18 needs it before invites — **neighborhood hit**: frontend hooks list add-member controls; **excluded** here; recommend small follow-up or fold into M12/M18 backend notes |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":921,"content":"| `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` | — | MARATHON-11 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":922,"content":"| Slash `/topic` `/archive` | message body commands | MARATHON-11 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":932,"content":"| `server/channels/store.py` — ChannelObj, general, list, read_state | **In scope** — extend |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":933,"content":"| `server/workspaces/routes.py` — create/list/detail/members | **In scope** — add join + create channel only |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":938,"content":"notes: Shipped workspaces create/list/detail per design. Migration v2 + routes. read_state uses full ReadStateEntry {channel_id,last_read_seq,unread_count,mention_count}; include_archived accepts 1 and case-insensitive true. errors.py already broadened by MARATHON-4. Tests: tests/test_workspaces.py; full unit suite green; cluster verified create:8000 list:8001 detail:8002.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":944,"content":"This task adds the workspace tenancy root for Huddle: authenticated callers can create a workspace (unique kebab `slug`, display `name`, creator as `owner`, default `join_mode=open`), which atomically provisions the public `#general` channel and membership rows; list workspaces they own or belong to; and load a workspace by slug with the visible channel list plus embedded `read_state`. It locks `WorkspaceObj`, the initial `ChannelObj` shape used by later channel APIs, the SQLite schema for workspaces/members/channels, and the REST contracts the SPA shell (MARATHON-16) and members/channels tasks (MARATHON-6/7) consume.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":946,"content":"**Revision (needs-revision feedback):** `read_state` entries use the **full** `ReadStateEntry` shape shared with `GET /api/channels/{id}/read` (MARATHON-11): `{channel_id, last_read_seq, unread_count, mention_count}`. Empty `[]` until messages/read APIs write rows is fine; when entries are returned, all four fields are present (counts default to `0`). Query `include_archived` treats both literal `1` and `true` (case-insensitive) as “include archived.”","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":961,"content":"| `read_state` | Embed `ReadStateEntry[]` for the caller with keys **`channel_id`, `last_read_seq`, `unread_count`, `mention_count`** — identical to MARATHON-11 `GET /api/channels/{id}/read` entry shape; return `[]` until rows exist; when mapping a row, missing/null counts → JSON `0` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":971,"content":"- Embedding the **full** `read_state` entry shape now (not a truncated `{channel_id, last_read_seq}`) prevents SPA/MARATHON-11 divergence on badge fields.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":983,"content":"| Truncate embedded `read_state` to cursor-only fields | **Rejected by review** — must match channel read API shape |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":988,"content":"This task introduces **minimal** channel + membership schema ahead of MARATHON-6/7 so create/list/detail work end-to-end. Full join/leave/role/archive/pin behavior stays out of scope; implementers must not invent those routes here. We accept a slightly larger migration v2 (including `unread_count` / `mention_count` columns on `channel_read_state`) in exchange for a single coherent create transaction and stable JSON types shared with MARATHON-11.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1048,"content":"#### `ReadStateEntry` (embedded list; **same shape as** MARATHON-11 `GET /api/channels/{id}/read`)","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1055,"content":"  \"mention_count\": 0","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1064,"content":"| `mention_count` | integer | Non-negative; default **0**; **never** JSON `null`; MARATHON-11: no self-mention inflation |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1068,"content":"- Workspace detail returns `read_state: ReadStateEntry[]` for the **caller**, only for channels included in that response’s `channels` array (omit entries for filtered-out private/archived channels).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1070,"content":"- When a `channel_read_state` row **does** exist for a visible channel, map **all four** JSON keys. If DB columns for counts are somehow missing in a fixture, coerce to `0` — do **not** omit keys.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1071,"content":"- **Negative:** must **not** return truncated entries like `{channel_id, last_read_seq}` only; SPA and MARATHON-11 depend on `unread_count` / `mention_count` always being present on each entry.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1148,"content":"| **Client** | Bearer; optional query `include_archived=1` or `include_archived=true`. While slow: keep prior shell or show workspace loading. On 200: bind sidebar channel list + header from payload; treat each `read_state` entry’s `unread_count` / `mention_count` as badge inputs (zeros until MARATHON-11). On 404: treat as unknown/inaccessible workspace (do not distinguish). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1149,"content":"| **Server** | Resolve by slug; require membership; build filtered `channels` + `read_state`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1170,"content":"  \"read_state\": [ /* ReadStateEntry, ... */ ]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1174,"content":"Example with a populated cursor (after MARATHON-11 / test fixture):","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1182,"content":"  \"read_state\": [","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1183,"content":"    { \"channel_id\": \"c-general\", \"last_read_seq\": 12, \"unread_count\": 3, \"mention_count\": 1 }","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1188,"content":"Fresh workspace (no read rows yet): `\"read_state\": []`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1258,"content":"#### `channel_read_state`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1264,"content":"| `last_read_seq` | INTEGER | NOT NULL | DEFAULT 0; never decreases (enforced in MARATHON-11) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1266,"content":"| `mention_count` | INTEGER | NOT NULL | DEFAULT 0; JSON field of same name |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1270,"content":"**No Redis keys.** Booleans in JSON are real booleans; SQLite stores 0/1. This task **does not** insert `channel_read_state` rows on workspace create (detail returns `[]`).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1298,"content":"| `server/channels/store.py` | `ChannelObj` mapping; `create_general_channel`; `list_channels_for_workspace_user` (private + archive filters); `list_read_state_for_channels` → full `ReadStateEntry` dicts. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1299,"content":"| `tests/test_workspaces.py` | Contract tests for create/list/detail, authz, slug conflict, archive query (`1` and `true`), full `read_state` keys, envelope errors. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1319,"content":"| Read POST/GET routes, search, slash | MARATHON-11 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1345,"content":"| Embedded `read_state[]` **full** `ReadStateEntry` shape | MARATHON-11 (writes + `GET/POST .../read`); MARATHON-16 (badges) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1362,"content":"- Populating/updating `channel_read_state` and computing unread/mention → MARATHON-11.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1369,"content":"| `GET/PATCH` members, transfer ownership | future `/api/workspaces/{slug}/members` | MARATHON-6 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1375,"content":"| `POST/GET /api/channels/{id}/read` | — | MARATHON-11 (embeds **same** shape here; does not implement those routes) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1376,"content":"| Computing live unread/mention from messages | — | MARATHON-11; this task only maps stored columns / returns `[]` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1390,"content":"| `server/auth/**` — register/login/me, deps | **Out of scope** — consume dependency only |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1393,"content":"| Grep `workspace`/`channel`/`read_state`/`general` / `include_archived` | **No matches** in application code — greenfield modules |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1408,"content":"| Create success | Creator is `owner_id` and sole `workspace_members` row with `role=owner`; `#general` exists exactly once; no `channel_read_state` rows yet |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1413,"content":"| Detail as owner/member | **200**; `channels` includes `general`; `read_state` is `[]` until rows exist |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1414,"content":"| Private channel (future data) without membership | Omitted from `channels` and from `read_state` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1425,"content":"This task adds workspace **user groups** and **invitation codes** so invite-only workspaces become joinable and @group mentions (MARATHON-11) have a durable handle→members map. It locks `GroupObj` / `InvitationObj`, the REST seams under `/api/workspaces/{slug}/groups`, `/api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations`, and `/api/invitations/{code}`, and the accept path that inserts `workspace_members` (+ `#general` channel membership) so MARATHON-7’s invite_only join gates and the SPA settings UI (MARATHON-18) have a complete onboarding loop.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1437,"content":"| Group identity | UUID4 `id`; workspace-scoped unique `handle` (mention key); display `name`; members as `member_user_ids: string[]` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1451,"content":"- Groups with stable `handle` are required for MARATHON-11 `@group-handle` resolution; storing `member_user_ids` on the resource avoids N+1 for mention expansion.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1661,"content":"  \"read_state\": []","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1664,"content":"Shape mirrors workspace detail / join success so SPA can `enterWorkspace` without a second round-trip. `channels` at minimum includes public `#general` (and any other publics per M5 visibility). `read_state` may be `[]`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1793,"content":"| Existing workspace/member tests | Keep green; add new test modules |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1794,"content":"| Message/search/mention expansion | MARATHON-8/11 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1817,"content":"| `GroupObj` + groups CRUD | MARATHON-11 `@group-handle`; future SPA |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1835,"content":"- `@group-handle` mention expansion → MARATHON-11.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1836,"content":"- Explicit `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` add-member → separate task if M18 needs it beyond invites.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1845,"content":"| `@group-handle` / `@channel` mention parsing | MARATHON-11 | Consumes GroupObj; does not define CRUD |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1916,"content":"notes: Implemented POST /api/dms get-or-create: deterministic dm- name hash (no migration); is_dm+is_private; ensure both memberships; list predicate hides DMs from non-members; DM authz member-only (no owner bypass) on members/PATCH; pins/messages already member-only. Tests: tests/test_dms.py (12). Full suite 204 passed. Live boundary: A→B and B→A same channel_id on :8000.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1920,"content":"This task adds authenticated **get-or-create** for 1:1 direct-message channels: `POST /api/dms` resolves a workspace-scoped DM between the caller and a peer `user_id`, returning the same `channel_id` for both directions and on every repeat call. The channel is persisted as a normal `channels` row with `is_dm=true` (and `is_private=true` for visibility), both users in `channel_members`, so existing channel/message authz (MARATHON-7/8) and the SPA `dms-list` split (MARATHON-16) work without a separate message transport. It does not build group DMs, DM UI, or message posting.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":1955,"content":"Opaque synthetic `ChannelObj.name` for DMs (not a human display label). **MARATHON-17** must render DM sidebar labels from the peer `UserObj` (e.g. via `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` or members already known client-side), not from `name`. Until then, `dms-list` may show the synthetic name — acceptable for this backend-only task.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2122,"content":"| `server/messages/routes.py` | Same DM membership rule in `_require_pin_access` (and document for M8 shared helper) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2140,"content":"3. Authz tighten for `is_dm` in channel/message routes.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2181,"content":"| Search / read_state / slash | MARATHON-11 | |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2196,"content":"| `server/messages/routes.py` private/DM pin authz | **In scope** — same DM rule |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2238,"content":"13. Workspace owner who is **not** a DM member must **NOT** read DM pins/members via owner bypass (**403** or **404** per rules above).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2250,"content":"- Owner-without-membership denied on `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` (or pins) for the DM.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2288,"content":"| Role changes | `PATCH .../members/{user_id}` never creates owners; only `POST .../transfer_ownership` promotes to owner |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2379,"content":"| `GET .../members` | yes | yes | yes | yes | **404** |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2381,"content":"| `PATCH .../members/{id}` | yes* | yes† | **403** | **403** | **404** |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2388,"content":"### Seam: Client ↔ `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}/members`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2448,"content":"### Seam: Client ↔ `PATCH /api/workspaces/{slug}/members/{user_id}`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2486,"content":"**Errors:** 401; 404 workspace/member; 403; 400.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2509,"content":"- Target role ≠ `admin` → **400** same code/message family (member/guest/owner-as-target all 400; do not 403 here — task says 400 for non-admin target).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2597,"content":"| `server/workspaces/routes.py` | Add routes: `PATCH /{slug}`, `GET /{slug}/members`, `PATCH /{slug}/members/{user_id}`, `POST /{slug}/transfer_ownership`; Pydantic bodies with `extra=\"ignore\"`; transactional BEGIN/COMMIT like create. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2629,"content":"| `MemberObj` + `GET .../members` | MARATHON-18 settings; MARATHON-7/12 authz helpers may reuse store functions |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2631,"content":"| Role hierarchy + `forbidden` usage | MARATHON-7 guest/member channel rules; MARATHON-12 invitation admin/owner |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2671,"content":"| `server/workspaces/routes.py` — POST/GET workspaces | **In scope** — add PATCH/members/transfer; do not change create/list/detail behavior |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2714,"content":"1. `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}/members` as any member → **200** `{members:[MemberObj,…]}` with exact keys `user_id`,`role`,`username`,`display_name`; ordering per contract; includes the owner created by MARATHON-5.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2719,"content":"6. `PATCH .../members/{user_id}` with `role: \"owner\"` → **400**.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2726,"content":"13. After transfer, `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}` shows updated `owner_id`; `GET .../members` reflects both role changes.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2738,"content":"- PATCH role matrix: owner/admin/member/guest actors × targets; role=`owner` → 400; owner target → 403.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2753,"content":"curl -sS http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/workspaces/acme/members \\","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2995,"content":"### Seam: MARATHON-11 `last_read_seq`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":2997,"content":"`channel_read_state.last_read_seq` refers to this same dense per-channel seq. M11 must treat head/read cursors as these event seqs (not message ids). M13 does not implement read APIs.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3078,"content":"| `server/messages/routes.py` | Same for patch/delete/reactions/pins if pin routes live here |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3114,"content":"| Dense `seq` + `channel_events` + append API | **MARATHON-13** | M14 fan-out, M15 IRC, M11 read_state, M17 SPA |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3127,"content":"- Read-state advancement → MARATHON-11.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3138,"content":"| `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` | read_state routes | MARATHON-11 (consumes seq) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3139,"content":"| Search / slash / advanced mentions | messages routes | MARATHON-11 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3151,"content":"| `server/messages/routes.py` publish_* | **In scope** |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3154,"content":"| `server/channels/store.py` read_state embed | **Out of scope** — M11 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3185,"content":"notes: Auth API implemented: POST /api/auth/register|login, GET /api/auth/me; SQLite users+auth_tokens (migration v1); scrypt passwords; SHA-256 bearer tokens; error envelope; get_current_user dependency. Tests: tests/test_auth.py (33 suite total green). Cluster verified token across :8000/:8001/:8002. Logout/revoke out of scope per design.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3191,"content":"This task adds the first product API surface for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, backed by durable users and bearer tokens in the shared SQLite database so any of the three HTTP nodes accepts the same credential. It locks the canonical `UserObj` JSON shape (consumed by Profiles, Workspaces, and the SPA), the error envelope convention for all later REST routes, and a reusable FastAPI auth dependency that every authenticated endpoint will import.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3205,"content":"| Auth dependency | `server/auth/deps.py::get_current_user` for `/me` and for MARATHON-4+ |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3353,"content":"### `GET /api/auth/me`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3382,"content":"Register on `:8000`, then `GET /api/auth/me` on `:8001` / `:8002` with the same token **must** succeed. Implementer verifies this; design requires single shared SQLite SoT (already true via `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3489,"content":"| `UserObj` JSON shape | MARATHON-4 (Profiles), MARATHON-5+ (owner/member displays), MARATHON-16 (SPA session user) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3515,"content":"| Workspace/member authz | — | MARATHON-5/6 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3530,"content":"| `tests/test_health.py` — asserts health JSON; mentions Authorization absence | Keep green; auth tests are separate file |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3553,"content":"| Token valid on node 0, used on node 2 | **200** `/me` (shared DB) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3570,"content":"6. `GET /api/auth/me` with `Authorization: Bearer <token>` from register or login → **200** `{user}` matching the registered user.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3571,"content":"7. `/me` without header, with bad token, or with non-Bearer scheme → **401**.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3572,"content":"8. **Cluster:** token minted via `:8000` is accepted by `/api/auth/me` on `:8001` and `:8002` while `./start.sh` is running (shared SQLite).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3601,"content":"curl -sS http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/auth/me -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3602,"content":"curl -sS http://127.0.0.1:8002/api/auth/me -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3604,"content":"curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\\n' http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/me","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3616,"content":"notes: Profiles GET /api/users/{id} + PATCH /api/users/me shipped. No migration (v1 users columns). publish_user_updated is a documented no-op (no channel_id/seq) for MARATHON-13/14. Broadened RequestValidationError envelope to /api/* except /api/health. Tests: tests/test_profiles.py; full suite 73 passed. Cluster boundary: PATCH :8000 visible on GET :8001/:8002.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3622,"content":"This task adds the Profiles REST surface on top of the Auth-owned `users` table: authenticated `GET /api/users/{id}` returns a canonical `UserObj` (or 404), and authenticated `PATCH /api/users/me` applies any subset of mutable profile fields with IANA timezone and length validation (400 on failure). It does **not** change the `UserObj` shape locked by MARATHON-3; it only mutates profile columns already present in migration v1 and leaves a clear, channel-less `user.updated` event contract so MARATHON-13/14 can fan profile changes over WebSocket later.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3642,"content":"- MARATHON-3 already created nullable profile columns and the exact `UserObj` keys; inventing a parallel profile store would diverge sibling contracts and break SPA/`/api/auth/me` consistency.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3655,"content":"| Put PATCH under `/api/auth/me` | Task path is `/api/users/me`; Auth `/me` stays read-only session check |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3660,"content":"Any authenticated user may `GET` any other user’s public `UserObj` (no workspace membership gate). That unlocks mentions/DMs/member lists later at the cost of a cluster-global user directory. Acceptable for marathon scope; workspace-scoped visibility can be a later task if needed.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3725,"content":"- 401 — missing/invalid bearer (same messages/behavior as `/api/auth/me`).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3731,"content":"- Path value `me` is **not** special-cased: lookup id `\"me\"` → 404 (UUIDs never equal `\"me\"`). Session self-read remains `GET /api/auth/me`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3734,"content":"### Seam: Client ↔ `PATCH /api/users/me`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3777,"content":"**Errors:** 401; 400 validation. **No 404** on PATCH `/me` (auth user always exists; if token’s user row vanished → 401 via dependency, same as Auth).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3836,"content":"| `server/users/routes.py` | `GET /{id}` and `PATCH /me` under prefix `/api/users`; `Depends(get_current_user)`. |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3859,"content":"| `tests/test_auth.py` | Keep green; do not weaken Auth contracts (optional: one assert that PATCH’d fields appear on `/api/auth/me` can live in `test_profiles.py`) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3883,"content":"| `GET /api/users/{id}` → `{user}` | MARATHON-6/9/12/16/17 (member displays, DMs, mentions UI) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3884,"content":"| `PATCH /api/users/me` → `{user}` | MARATHON-16/18 settings/profile forms |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3913,"content":"| Workspace membership-gated user visibility | workspaces/members | Not required; directory is cluster-global here |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3914,"content":"| `GET /api/users` list/search | — | Search is MARATHON-11; no list endpoint in this task |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3915,"content":"| Changing `/api/auth/me` behavior | `server/auth/routes.py` | Remains session read; PATCH is `/api/users/me` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3925,"content":"| `server/auth/routes.py` — `/api/auth/*` | Out of scope (read-only `/me` stays) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3956,"content":"| PATCH then GET `/api/auth/me` | Returns updated fields (same DB row) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3969,"content":"4. `PATCH /api/users/me` with a valid subset (e.g. `{ \"display_name\": \"Ada\", \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\" }`) → **200** full `user` reflecting changes.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3973,"content":"8. After PATCH, `GET /api/auth/me` and `GET /api/users/{own_id}` return the same updated profile fields.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":3990,"content":"- PATCH display_name + timezone happy path; assert `/api/auth/me` matches.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":4003,"content":"2. `PATCH /api/users/me` with timezone + status; confirm 200.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":192,"totalMatchedLines":192,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-0362375e-d726-4b9e-ad8a-8b71e9ab2b12-12\nfc_af9a94a3-353e-9a3e-bc8f-1484bebced04_1","startedAtMs":"1787447385281","completedAtMs":"1787447386256"},"model_call_id":"55bd136e-e714-4a8d-bf22-33ab4486a9a4-4-8en9","session_id":"9a845f2e-de95-46d5-9fa0-61fc2c5131af","timestamp_ms":1787447386375}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-0362375e-d726-4b9e-ad8a-8b71e9ab2b12-13\nfc_af9a94a3-353e-9a3e-bc8f-1484bebced04_2","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/channels/store.py","offset":300,"limit":80},"result":{"success":{"content":"    user_id: str,\n    include_archived: bool,\n) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Visible: member, or true public (is_dm=0 AND is_private=0). Archive filter.\"\"\"\n    rows = conn.execute(\n        \"\"\"\n        SELECT c.*\n        FROM channels c\n        LEFT JOIN channel_members cm\n            ON cm.channel_id = c.id AND cm.user_id = ?\n        WHERE c.workspace_id = ?\n          AND (\n            (c.is_dm = 0 AND c.is_private = 0)\n            OR cm.user_id IS NOT NULL\n          )\n          AND (? = 1 OR c.is_archived = 0)\n        ORDER BY LOWER(c.name) ASC, c.name ASC\n        \"\"\",\n        (user_id, workspace_id, 1 if include_archived else 0),\n    ).fetchall()\n    return [row_to_channel_obj(row) for row in rows]\n\n\ndef list_read_state_for_channels(\n    conn: sqlite3.Connection,\n    *,\n    user_id: str,\n    channel_ids: list[str],\n) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Full ReadStateEntry list for caller, only for the given visible channel ids.\"\"\"\n    if not channel_ids:\n        return []\n    placeholders = \",\".join(\"?\" for _ in channel_ids)\n    rows = conn.execute(\n        f\"\"\"\n        SELECT channel_id, last_read_seq, unread_count, mention_count\n        FROM channel_read_state\n        WHERE user_id = ?\n          AND channel_id IN ({placeholders})\n        ORDER BY channel_id ASC\n        \"\"\",\n        (user_id, *channel_ids),\n    ).fetchall()\n    entries: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    for row in rows:\n        unread = row[\"unread_count\"]\n        mention = row[\"mention_count\"]\n        entries.append(\n            {\n                \"channel_id\": row[\"channel_id\"],\n                \"last_read_seq\": int(row[\"last_read_seq\"] or 0),\n                \"unread_count\": int(0 if unread is None else unread),\n                \"mention_count\": int(0 if mention is None else mention),\n            }\n        )\n    return entries\n\n\ndef list_members_as_users(\n    conn: sqlite3.Connection, *, channel_id: str\n) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Channel members as UserObj[], ordered by username ASC / id ASC.\"\"\"\n    rows = conn.execute(\n        \"\"\"\n        SELECT u.*\n        FROM channel_members cm\n        INNER JOIN users u ON u.id = cm.user_id\n        WHERE cm.channel_id = ?\n        ORDER BY LOWER(u.username) ASC, u.id ASC\n        \"\"\",\n        (channel_id,),\n    ).fetchall()\n    return [row_to_user_obj(row) for row in rows]\n\n\ndef update_topic(\n    conn: sqlite3.Connection, *, channel_id: str, topic: str\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    topic = validate_topic(topic)\n    now = utc_now_z()","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":502,"fileSize":13971,"path":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1/server/channels/store.py","readRange":{"startLine":300,"endLine":379},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-0362375e-d726-4b9e-ad8a-8b71e9ab2b12-13\nfc_af9a94a3-353e-9a3e-bc8f-1484bebced04_2","startedAtMs":"1787447385653","completedAtMs":"1787447386263"},"model_call_id":"55bd136e-e714-4a8d-bf22-33ab4486a9a4-4-8en9","session_id":"9a845f2e-de95-46d5-9fa0-61fc2c5131af","timestamp_ms":1787447386596}
