ndes=show('MARATHON-13')['design']\n# print sections mentioning message.created or unread or head_seq\nidx=des.find('last_read')\nprint(des[max(0,idx-400):idx+800] if idx>=0 else 'no last_read')\nprint('---')\nidx=des.find('## Interface')\nprint(des[idx:idx+3500])\nPY","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"he **same** `append_channel_event` + message insert path so IRC and HTTP share one dense seq. M15 consumes this contract; M13 does not implement IRC.\n\n### Seam: MARATHON-13 → MARATHON-17 (SPA)\n\nWire protocol above is normative for the SPA realtime client. M17 owns UI reconnect UX and when to subscribe (active channel + maybe sidebar). M13 does **not** modify `static/js/*`.\n\n### Seam: MARATHON-11 `last_read_seq`\n\n`channel_read_state.last_read_seq` refers to this same dense per-channel seq. M11 must treat head/read cursors as these event seqs (not message ids). M13 does not implement read APIs.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Migration **v6** (additive, backward compatible)\n\nNext version after M8’s v5. Do **not** renumber prior migrations.\n\n#### `channel_seq`\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS channel_seq (\n  channel_id TEXT NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,\n  head_seq INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0\n    CHECK (head_seq >= 0),\n  FOREIGN KEY (channel_id) REFERENCES channels(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\n);\n```\n\n- Row created lazily on first event for a channel (or optionally on channel create with `head_seq=0`).\n- Allocate: in a transaction, `INSERT … head_seq=1` on miss, else `UPDATE channel_seq SET head_seq = head_seq \n---\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Shared: durable channel frame envelope\n\nEvery durable per-channel frame **must** include:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"<event-type>\",\n  \"seq\": 42,\n  \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\"\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Rules |\n|-------|--------|\n| `type` | string; one of the durable types below |\n| `seq` | integer ≥ 1; dense per `channel_id` |\n| `channel_id` | string; never null on durable frames |\n| Extra fields | Per type; nested REST objects keep **exact** REST key sets (no `seq` inside nested objects) |\n\n**Non-durable / global:**\n\n```json\n{ \"type\": \"user.updated\", \"user\": { /* UserObj */ } }\n```\n\nNo `channel_id`, no `seq`.\n\n### Durable event types (normative)\n\n| `type` | Extra fields | Emitted when (actual state change only) |\n|--------|--------------|------------------------------------------|\n| `message.created` | `message`: `MessageObj` | Successful message create (top-level or reply) |\n| `message.updated` | `message`: `MessageObj` | Successful edit |\n| `message.deleted` | `message_id`: string | Successful soft-delete |\n| `reaction.changed` | `message_id`, `reactions`: `ReactionObj[]` | Successful add/remove reaction (full aggregate, same as REST) |\n| `membership.joined` | `user`: `UserObj` | Channel membership row **inserted** (join, create-channel creator, DM ensure-membership that inserts) |\n| `membership.left` | `user_id`: string | Channel membership row **deleted** (leave) |\n| `channel.created` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Channel row created (workspace create-channel, DM create) |\n| `channel.updated` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Topic PATCH that changes stored topic |\n| `channel.archived` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Archive transition false→true |\n| `channel.unarchived` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Unarchive true→false |\n| `channel.pin_added` | `message_id`, `pinned_by`, `pinned_at` | New pin row inserted (not idempotent no-op) |\n| `channel.pin_removed` | `message_id` | Pin row deleted (not idempotent no-op) |\n\nIdempotent HTTP no-ops (**must not** allocate seq / **must not** emit): join when already member; leave when not member; reaction already present/absent; pin already pinned; archive when already archived; topic PATCH with identical topic; profile PATCH with no field changes.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ WebSocket `GET /api/ws?token=<raw-bearer>`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client (SPA M17 / tools)** | Open `ws://127.0.0.1:800x/api/ws?token=<token>` (or `wss` if ever TLS). On open, `subscribe` each active channel; store last `seq` per channel; on reconnect `resume` with `since_seq`. While connecting/reconnecting: keep last REST snapshot; show reconnecting affordance (M17). Do not invent REST `seq`. |\n| **Server** | Validate `token` **before** treating the socket as authenticated; maintain per-connection subscription set; enforce channel read authz on subscribe/resume; deliver frames; never crash the process on client disconnect. |\n\n**Handshake / auth**\n\n- Missing/empty/whitespace `token`, unknown token, or deleted user → **reject** the WebSocket with HTTP **401** during upgrade when the framework allows; otherwise `accept` then immediately close with code **4401** and reason `unauthorized`. Do not send application frames.\n- Query param name is exactly **`token`** (not `access_token`). Extra query params ignored.\n- Same token must work on any node (shared `auth_tokens` — already true).\n\n**Wire encoding:** one JSON object per WebSocket text message. Binary frames ignored (no error). Unknown client `type` → serve\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T01:10:08.570Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":129,"interleavedOutput":"time=2026-08-23T01:10:08.570Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\nhe **same** `append_channel_event` + message insert path so IRC and HTTP share one dense seq. M15 consumes this contract; M13 does not implement IRC.\n\n### Seam: MARATHON-13 → MARATHON-17 (SPA)\n\nWire protocol above is normative for the SPA realtime client. M17 owns UI reconnect UX and when to subscribe (active channel + maybe sidebar). M13 does **not** modify `static/js/*`.\n\n### Seam: MARATHON-11 `last_read_seq`\n\n`channel_read_state.last_read_seq` refers to this same dense per-channel seq. M11 must treat head/read cursors as these event seqs (not message ids). M13 does not implement read APIs.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Migration **v6** (additive, backward compatible)\n\nNext version after M8’s v5. Do **not** renumber prior migrations.\n\n#### `channel_seq`\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS channel_seq (\n  channel_id TEXT NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,\n  head_seq INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0\n    CHECK (head_seq >= 0),\n  FOREIGN KEY (channel_id) REFERENCES channels(id) ON DELETE CASCADE\n);\n```\n\n- Row created lazily on first event for a channel (or optionally on channel create with `head_seq=0`).\n- Allocate: in a transaction, `INSERT … head_seq=1` on miss, else `UPDATE channel_seq SET head_seq = head_seq \n---\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Shared: durable channel frame envelope\n\nEvery durable per-channel frame **must** include:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"<event-type>\",\n  \"seq\": 42,\n  \"channel_id\": \"<uuid>\"\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Rules |\n|-------|--------|\n| `type` | string; one of the durable types below |\n| `seq` | integer ≥ 1; dense per `channel_id` |\n| `channel_id` | string; never null on durable frames |\n| Extra fields | Per type; nested REST objects keep **exact** REST key sets (no `seq` inside nested objects) |\n\n**Non-durable / global:**\n\n```json\n{ \"type\": \"user.updated\", \"user\": { /* UserObj */ } }\n```\n\nNo `channel_id`, no `seq`.\n\n### Durable event types (normative)\n\n| `type` | Extra fields | Emitted when (actual state change only) |\n|--------|--------------|------------------------------------------|\n| `message.created` | `message`: `MessageObj` | Successful message create (top-level or reply) |\n| `message.updated` | `message`: `MessageObj` | Successful edit |\n| `message.deleted` | `message_id`: string | Successful soft-delete |\n| `reaction.changed` | `message_id`, `reactions`: `ReactionObj[]` | Successful add/remove reaction (full aggregate, same as REST) |\n| `membership.joined` | `user`: `UserObj` | Channel membership row **inserted** (join, create-channel creator, DM ensure-membership that inserts) |\n| `membership.left` | `user_id`: string | Channel membership row **deleted** (leave) |\n| `channel.created` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Channel row created (workspace create-channel, DM create) |\n| `channel.updated` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Topic PATCH that changes stored topic |\n| `channel.archived` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Archive transition false→true |\n| `channel.unarchived` | `channel`: `ChannelObj` | Unarchive true→false |\n| `channel.pin_added` | `message_id`, `pinned_by`, `pinned_at` | New pin row inserted (not idempotent no-op) |\n| `channel.pin_removed` | `message_id` | Pin row deleted (not idempotent no-op) |\n\nIdempotent HTTP no-ops (**must not** allocate seq / **must not** emit): join when already member; leave when not member; reaction already present/absent; pin already pinned; archive when already archived; topic PATCH with identical topic; profile PATCH with no field changes.\n\n### Seam: Client ↔ WebSocket `GET /api/ws?token=<raw-bearer>`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client (SPA M17 / tools)** | Open `ws://127.0.0.1:800x/api/ws?token=<token>` (or `wss` if ever TLS). On open, `subscribe` each active channel; store last `seq` per channel; on reconnect `resume` with `since_seq`. While connecting/reconnecting: keep last REST snapshot; show reconnecting affordance (M17). Do not invent REST `seq`. |\n| **Server** | Validate `token` **before** treating the socket as authenticated; maintain per-connection subscription set; enforce channel read authz on subscribe/resume; deliver frames; never crash the process on client disconnect. |\n\n**Handshake / auth**\n\n- Missing/empty/whitespace `token`, unknown token, or deleted user → **reject** the WebSocket with HTTP **401** during upgrade when the framework allows; otherwise `accept` then immediately close with code **4401** and reason `unauthorized`. Do not send application frames.\n- Query param name is exactly **`token`** (not `access_token`). Extra query params ignored.\n- Same token must work on any node (shared `auth_tokens` — already true).\n\n**Wire encoding:** one JSON object per WebSocket text message. Binary frames ignored (no error). Unknown client `type` → serve\n","localExecutionTimeMs":50},"isBackground":false},"description":"Extract M13 seq/read contract details"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-9641ebc8-e199-4644-aeae-12357ca572a5-24\nfc_c2a2dcb8-54bc-9a59-a202-41bd064447ec_3","startedAtMs":"1787447408492","completedAtMs":"1787447408621"},"model_call_id":"55bd136e-e714-4a8d-bf22-33ab4486a9a4-6-gn6z","session_id":"9a845f2e-de95-46d5-9fa0-61fc2c5131af","timestamp_ms":1787447408647}
