sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"title:\", d.get(\"title\")); print(\"status:\", d.get(\"status\")); print(\"labels:\", d.get(\"labels\")); print(\"has_design:\", d.get(\"has_design\")); notes=d.get(\"notes\") or \"\"; print(\"NOTES:\\n\", notes[:3000] if notes else \"(none)\"); design=d.get(\"design\") or \"\"; print(\"DESIGN_LEN:\", len(design)); print(design[:500] if design else \"(no design inline)\")'"}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Fetch key sibling task designs/notes","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"8d1f97e9-e376-440d-a791-e2992491ec56","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"for id in MARATHON-16 MARATHON-8 MARATHON-7 MARATHON-5 MARATHON-13 MARATHON-11 MARATHON-18 MARATHON-9; do echo \"===== $id =====\"; loom data show $id --output json | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"title:\", d.get(\"title\")); print(\"status:\", d.get(\"status\")); print(\"labels:\", d.get(\"labels\")); print(\"has_design:\", d.get(\"has_design\")); notes=d.get(\"notes\") or \"\"; print(\"NOTES:\\n\", notes[:3000] if notes else \"(none)\"); design=d.get(\"design\") or \"\"; print(\"DESIGN_LEN:\", len(design)); print(design[:500] if design else \"(no design inline)\")'; done","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"===== MARATHON-16 =====\ntitle: SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\nstatus: closed\nlabels: ['frontend']\nhas_design: True\nNOTES:\n IMPL: Zero-build SPA at GET / (static/). Token write huddle.token; read fallbacks huddle_token/token. Workspace restore via huddle.workspaceSlug across logout. Join form POSTs /api/workspaces/{slug}/join (server still MARATHON-7). Verified via pytest + Playwright at 1280x900 (register/login/create/logout/restore; thread panel hidden).\nDESIGN_LEN: 23433\n# MARATHON-16 — SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\n\n## Summary\n\nReplace the stub `GET /` HTML with a zero-build Huddle SPA served identically from every HTTP node. The SPA owns browser session lifecycle (register → auto-login, login, logout), durable bearer storage under `localStorage` key `huddle.token` (with documented read fallbacks), restoration of the last workspace after logout/login, and the three-pane workspace shell (coloured sidebar + main message pane + on-demand thread panel) \n===== MARATHON-8 =====\ntitle: Messages, threads, reactions REST API\nstatus: closed\nlabels: ['backend']\nhas_design: True\nNOTES:\n IMPL: Messages/threads/reactions REST shipped. Schema is migration v5 (design text said v4; v4 already used by MARATHON-12 groups/invitations). Additive only — preserved v3 messages. file_ids non-empty → 400 until MARATHON-10; @username mentions only; slash bodies stored literally. Unit tests green (151 excl. live/cluster port-bound); port 8000 held by another agent so live cluster pytest left unrun here — cluster read-after-write covered via dual TestClient sharing sqlite.\nDESIGN_LEN: 28212\n# MARATHON-8 — Messages, threads, reactions REST API\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task completes the core chat write/read path for Huddle on top of MARATHON-7 channels and the minimal `messages` / pin embed already shipped: authenticated channel members can post top-level messages and one-level thread replies, list channel history (newest-first, cursor pagination) and thread replies (oldest-first), edit their own messages, soft-delete as author or workspace owner, and add/remove emoji reactions. It locks t\n===== MARATHON-7 =====\ntitle: Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, pins\nstatus: closed\nlabels: ['backend']\nhas_design: True\nNOTES:\n Shipped channels create/join/leave/topic/archive + workspace join + pins. Migration v3 messages+channel_pins; assert_channel_writable → 423 archived for M8. Tests: test_channels.py + test_pins.py; full suite 175 passed. Cluster two-app shared data_dir covered.\nDESIGN_LEN: 29753\n# MARATHON-7 — Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, pins\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task completes channel lifecycle for Huddle on top of the workspace tenancy shipped in MARATHON-5/6: authenticated callers can create public/private channels under a workspace slug, join and leave channels (with open-workspace auto-onboard and invite_only/guest/private gates), list channel members as `UserObj`, patch topic, archive/unarchive (owner-only), and pin/unpin messages. It also implements the SPA-locked\n===== MARATHON-5 =====\ntitle: Workspaces: create, list, detail, auto #general\nstatus: closed\nlabels: ['backend']\nhas_design: True\nNOTES:\n Shipped workspaces create/list/detail per design. Migration v2 + routes. read_state uses full ReadStateEntry {channel_id,last_read_seq,unread_count,mention_count}; include_archived accepts 1 and case-insensitive true. errors.py already broadened by MARATHON-4. Tests: tests/test_workspaces.py; full unit suite green; cluster verified create:8000 list:8001 detail:8002.\nDESIGN_LEN: 28664\n# MARATHON-5 — Workspaces: create, list, detail, auto #general\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the workspace tenancy root for Huddle: authenticated callers can create a workspace (unique kebab `slug`, display `name`, creator as `owner`, default `join_mode=open`), which atomically provisions the public `#general` channel and membership rows; list workspaces they own or belong to; and load a workspace by slug with the visible channel list plus embedded `read_state`. It locks `WorkspaceObj`, the initia\n===== MARATHON-13 =====\ntitle: WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\nstatus: review\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\nhas_design: True\nNOTES:\n Design complete for WS subscribe/resume + dense channel seq. Key decisions: SQLite channel_seq/channel_events (v6) as SoT; seq allocated in same txn as mutation; /api/ws?token=; subscribe=live only, resume=replay or resume.gap; user.updated global no seq; Redis fan-out deferred to MARATHON-14 (local hub + catch-up on any node via resume). Label remains backend for implementer after architect approval.\nDESIGN_LEN: 27570\n# MARATHON-13 — WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the real-time seam for Huddle: an authenticated WebSocket at `GET /api/ws?token=…`, client `subscribe` / `resume` control frames, and a **dense per-channel `seq`** assigned in shared SQLite so every durable channel mutation (messages including thread replies, reactions, membership, channel mutations, pins) gets a gap-free monotonic frame `{type, seq, channel_id, …}`. Profile changes keep the existing cha\n===== MARATHON-11 =====\ntitle: Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\nstatus: review\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\nhas_design: True\nNOTES:\n Design complete for search, slash commands, advanced mentions, and read_state. Grounded in MARATHON-5 ReadStateEntry, MARATHON-7 topic/archive authz, MARATHON-8 MessageObj + composer POST, MARATHON-12 group handles, MARATHON-13 last_read_seq=dense event seq (soft dep for mid-cursor recompute). No new migration (avoids v6 clash). Label remains backend for implementer after architect approval.\nDESIGN_LEN: 27763\n# MARATHON-11 — Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task completes the discovery and attention seams for Huddle on top of MARATHON-5/7/8/12: authenticated workspace members can full-text search messages they can see (`GET /api/search`), post slash commands through the existing message composer path (`POST /api/channels/{id}/messages`) with message-producing transforms (`/me`, `/shrug`, `//…` escape) and side-effect commands that return `message: null` (`/topic`, `/invi\n===== MARATHON-18 =====\ntitle: SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\nstatus: open\nlabels: ['frontend']\nhas_design: True\nNOTES:\n FEEDBACK attempt=1: critic requested changes; see CRITIC comment\nDESIGN_LEN: 28511\n# MARATHON-18 — SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the Huddle SPA settings surface on top of the MARATHON-16 shell: a **workspace settings modal** (tabs General / Members / Invitations) and a **channel settings modal** (members list/add, topic, archive/unarchive). It wires those UIs to the already-shipped REST seams from MARATHON-6/7/12 (`PATCH` workspace, members/roles/transfer, invitations create/list/revoke/accept, channel members/topic/archive) and locks the e\n===== MARATHON-9 =====\ntitle: DMs: get-or-create DM channel\nstatus: closed\nlabels: ['backend']\nhas_design: True\nNOTES:\n Implemented POST /api/dms get-or-create: deterministic dm- name hash (no migration); is_dm+is_private; ensure both memberships; list predicate hides DMs from non-members; DM authz member-only (no owner bypass) on members/PATCH; pins/messages already member-only. Tests: tests/test_dms.py (12). Full suite 204 passed. Live boundary: A→B and B→A same channel_id on :8000.\nDESIGN_LEN: 18939\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds authenticated **get-or-create** for 1:1 direct-message channels: `POST /api/dms` resolves a workspace-scoped DM between the caller and a peer `user_id`, returning the same `channel_id` for both directions and on every repeat call. The channel is persisted as a normal `channels` row with `is_dm=true` (and `is_private=true` for visibility), both users in `channel_members`, so existing channel/message authz (MARATHON-7/8) and the SPA `dms-list` split (MARATHON-16) work wi\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T01:14:52.174Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:14:52.213Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:14:52.238Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:14:52.268Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n