e-channel-modal|emoji-picker|message-input|channel-topic|empty-channel'"},{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/designs"},{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1"}],"fullText":"rg -n 'create-channel-modal|emoji-picker|message-input|channel-topic|empty-channel' /tmp/designs /work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-40"}],"fullText":"head -40"},{"name":"find","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws"},{"type":"word","value":"-name"},{"type":"raw_string","value":"'*hooks*'"}],"fullText":"find /work/ws -name '*hooks*'"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-30"}],"fullText":"head -30"},{"name":"rg","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-n"},{"type":"raw_string","value":"'create-channel-modal'"},{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws/worktrees/app"},{"type":"word","value":"--glob"},{"type":"raw_string","value":"'!**/.venv/**'"},{"type":"word","value":"--glob"},{"type":"raw_string","value":"'!**/diff.patch'"}],"fullText":"rg -n 'create-channel-modal' /work/ws/worktrees/app --glob '!**/.venv/**' --glob '!**/diff.patch'"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-20"}],"fullText":"head -20"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"comment"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-17"},{"type":"word","value":"--help"}],"fullText":"loom data comment MARATHON-17 --help"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-5"}],"fullText":"head -5"},{"name":"python3","args":[],"fullText":"python3"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/dev/null"},{"operator":">&","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"number","targetText":"1"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"python3"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Find testid hooks and task comments","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"8d1f97e9-e376-440d-a791-e2992491ec56","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"description":"Find testid hooks and task comments"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-74d38cd0-8f84-4ab9-8681-55e7f39030bc-30\nfc_e8806530-d7a4-9e9f-a2d5-14f5ad9328e6_1","startedAtMs":"1787447736883"},"model_call_id":"03dd848d-d7bd-4877-bfbf-ce6458bc28c6-10-lppn","session_id":"8d1f97e9-e376-440d-a791-e2992491ec56","timestamp_ms":1787447736912}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-74d38cd0-8f84-4ab9-8681-55e7f39030bc-29\nfc_e8806530-d7a4-9e9f-a2d5-14f5ad9328e6_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/designs/MARATHON-18.md","offset":1,"limit":250},"result":{"success":{"content":"# MARATHON-18 — SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the Huddle SPA settings surface on top of the MARATHON-16 shell: a **workspace settings modal** (tabs General / Members / Invitations) and a **channel settings modal** (members list/add, topic, archive/unarchive). It wires those UIs to the already-shipped REST seams from MARATHON-6/7/12 (`PATCH` workspace, members/roles/transfer, invitations create/list/revoke/accept, channel members/topic/archive) and locks the epic’s stable DOM ids plus `settings-*` / `invitation-*` / role / channel-member `data-testid`s so CUA/Playwright can drive admin flows at 1280×900. It also specifies the missing **channel add-member** REST seam that MARATHON-7 deferred, because the channel-settings “add” control cannot work against join alone for private channels.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Delivery | Extend the **zero-build vanilla SPA** (`static/` ES modules) — same stack as MARATHON-16; no bundler |\n| Module split | New `static/js/settings_ui.js` owns both modals; `shell.js` exposes open triggers + active workspace/channel; reuse `api.js` / `storage.js` |\n| Modal pattern | Match `auth-modal`: overlay + panel, `hidden` attribute, `role=\"dialog\"`, Escape/close dismiss; **one settings modal open at a time** |\n| Workspace entry | `data-testid=\"workspace-settings-btn\"` in `workspace-header` (visible whenever shell shows a workspace) |\n| Channel entry | Selecting a non-DM channel in `channel-list` sets active channel; `data-testid=\"channel-settings-btn\"` in message-pane header chrome (or beside channel list) opens channel settings for that id — **does not** require MARATHON-17 message composer |\n| Tabs | Workspace modal: exactly three tabs — `general`, `members`, `invitations`; only one panel visible |\n| Authz UX | Client **hides/disables** privileged controls from cached caller role; server remains SoT (403/404 still shown as `error.message`) |\n| Invitation redeem | Onboarding gains an **accept-by-code** form (M12 assigned redeem UX to this task); settings tab is create/list/revoke only |\n| Channel add-member | New backend seam `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (this design owns the contract); frontend labeled implementer may land the thin route or a tiny backend follow-up must land first — see Sequencing |\n| Selectors | Exact strings below; prefer `data-testid`; required **DOM ids**: `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic requires settings + invitations in the SPA with stable selectors; M16 explicitly deferred settings modals here.\n- Backend contracts for name/join_mode, roles, invitations, topic, archive, channel member list are closed (M6/7/12); inventing alternate envelopes would break graders and sibling designs.\n- M7’s neighborhood note already flagged `channel-add-member-*` without REST — shipping UI without an add seam leaves private-channel “add” untestable.\n- Keeping vanilla modules preserves `start.sh` / no-Node ops.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Fold settings into MARATHON-17 message chrome only | Blocks settings QA until messages land; task is independent with `frontend` label |\n| “Add member” = tell user to `POST .../join` | Fails for private channels (403 without membership); hooks expect add controls |\n| Profile PATCH inside General tab | Task tabs are name/join_mode/members/invitations only; profile is a different surface |\n| Groups CRUD UI | MARATHON-12 groups API exists but is not in this task description |\n| React settings app | Diverges from M16 zero-build convention |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nChannel add-member needs a **small backend POST** that did not ship in M7. This design locks that seam so SPA and server can be implemented in parallel; if the implementer is frontend-only, the lead should keep `frontend` and optionally add a short backend subtask — **do not** fake add via SQL in the browser.\n\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n\nFrom **MARATHON-16**: vanilla SPA; `api()` + bearer; `{error:{code,message}}`; visible form errors; `hidden` for unused chrome; hash `#/w/{slug}`; token keys unchanged.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-5/6**: `WorkspaceObj` keys `{id,slug,name,owner_id,join_mode}`; `join_mode` ∈ {`open`,`invite_only`}; `MemberObj` `{user_id,role,username,display_name}`; roles `owner|admin|member|guest`; non-member → 404; privilege → 403; PATCH workspace name/join_mode; PATCH member role matrix; `POST .../transfer_ownership`.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj` keys; `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` → `{members: UserObj[]}`; `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}`; `POST .../archive` / `.../unarchive` owner-only; archived topic writes → **423** `archived`; leave/join exist but settings “add” is not join.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-12**: `InvitationObj`; create/list/revoke/accept envelopes; invite_only join still 403 without accept.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-3/4**: `UserObj` keys on channel members list; bearer auth.\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\n\nAll names are **`data-testid` values** unless noted as **DOM `id`**. Elements must exist in the DOM when the corresponding UI is shown (not only as JS string constants). Product “frontend hooks” are not checked into this repo; the table below is **normative** for this task and matches the task wording (`settings-*`, `invitation-*`, role/channel-member names from sibling designs).\n\n#### Required DOM ids\n\n| `id` | Element |\n|------|---------|\n| `workspace-settings-modal` | Workspace settings overlay/dialog root |\n| `channel-settings-modal` | Channel settings overlay/dialog root |\n| `create-invitation-form` | Form that creates a workspace invitation |\n\nAlso set matching `data-testid` equal to the id string for the three roots/forms above (so either selector style works).\n\n#### Open / chrome\n\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\n|---------------|--------------|------|\n| `workspace-settings-btn` | Shell with current workspace | Opens workspace settings modal |\n| `channel-settings-btn` | Shell with an active non-DM channel | Opens channel settings for that channel |\n| `workspace-settings-close` | Workspace modal open | Closes workspace modal |\n| `channel-settings-close` | Channel modal open | Closes channel modal |\n\n#### Workspace settings — tabs & general\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `settings-tab-general` | Selects General tab |\n| `settings-tab-members` | Selects Members tab |\n| `settings-tab-invitations` | Selects Invitations tab |\n| `settings-panel-general` | General panel region |\n| `settings-panel-members` | Members panel region |\n| `settings-panel-invitations` | Invitations panel region |\n| `settings-name` | Workspace display name `<input>` |\n| `settings-join-mode` | `<select>` or radio group; values `open` \\| `invite_only` |\n| `settings-general-save` | Submit/save general settings |\n| `settings-general-error` | Visible error text for general save failures |\n| `settings-general-success` | Optional brief success indicator (may be aria-live); not required if save is silently successful and fields reflect server |\n\n**Negative:** Member/guest must **not** successfully persist general changes; controls may be disabled **or** save shows `settings-general-error` with server `error.message` (403).\n\n#### Workspace settings — members\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `settings-members-list` | Container for member rows |\n| `settings-member-row` | One row per `MemberObj` (may appear multiple times) |\n| `role-badge` | Read-only role label on a row (always present) |\n| `role-select` | `<select>` to change role when actor may edit that row; **absent or `disabled`** when actor cannot |\n| `settings-members-error` | Visible error for list/PATCH failures |\n| `settings-members-loading` | Optional loading marker while `GET .../members` in flight |\n| `settings-transfer-owner` | Owner-only control to transfer ownership (confirm + target admin) |\n| `settings-transfer-owner-select` | Admin target picker |\n| `settings-transfer-owner-submit` | Confirm transfer |\n| `settings-transfer-error` | Transfer error text |\n\nEach `settings-member-row` **must** expose `data-user-id=\"{user_id}\"`.\n\n`role-select` options: `admin`, `member`, `guest` only (never `owner` — ownership uses transfer).\n\n#### Workspace settings — invitations\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `create-invitation-form` | Same as DOM id; create form |\n| `invitation-max-uses` | Optional number input (default server 1 if empty) |\n| `invitation-expires-seconds` | Optional expiry seconds input |\n| `invitation-username` | Optional targeted username |\n| `invitation-create-submit` | Create submit control |\n| `invitation-create-error` | Visible create error |\n| `invitation-list` | Active invitations list container |\n| `invitation-row` | One row per active invitation |\n| `invitation-code` | Displays `InvitationObj.code` (copyable text) |\n| `invitation-revoke` | Revoke control on a row |\n| `invitation-list-error` | List/revoke error |\n\nEach `invitation-row` **must** expose `data-invitation-code=\"{code}\"` (and/or `data-invitation-id`).\n\nNon-admin: invitations tab may show a short “Admins only” empty state; create form and list fetch must **not** be required to succeed for members (hide form **or** show 403 in `invitation-list-error` without crashing).\n\n#### Onboarding — accept invitation (redeem)\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `invitation-accept-form` | Onboarding form (sibling to join-by-slug) |\n| `invitation-accept-code` | Code input |\n| `invitation-accept-submit` | Submit |\n| `invitation-accept-error` | Visible error |\n\n#### Channel settings\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `channel-settings-modal` | Modal root (also DOM id) |\n| `settings-topic` | Topic `<input>` / textarea |\n| `settings-topic-save` | Save topic |\n| `settings-topic-error` | Topic error (incl. 423 archived) |\n| `settings-archive` | Archive button (owner) |\n| `settings-unarchive` | Unarchive button (owner) |\n| `settings-archive-error` | Archive/unarchive error |\n| `channel-members-list` | Channel members container |\n| `channel-member-row` | One row per `UserObj` |\n| `channel-add-member-input` | Username or user id input for add |\n| `channel-add-member-submit` | Add submit |\n| `channel-add-member-error` | Add error |\n| `channel-members-error` | List error |\n\nEach `channel-member-row` **must** expose `data-user-id=\"{id}\"` (UserObj `id`).\n\nArchive vs unarchive: show the action that matches current `is_archived` (one primary control is enough; the other may stay in DOM but `hidden`).\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET/PATCH /api/workspaces/{slug}` (General tab)\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On open: seed `settings-name` / `settings-join-mode` from in-memory `WorkspaceObj`. Save → `PATCH` body subset `{name?, join_mode?}`. Disable `settings-general-save` while in flight. On **200**: replace cached workspace; refresh `workspace-header`. On **400/403**: show `error.message` in `settings-general-error`. On **401**: logout (M16). On **404**: close modal, leave workspace. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-6). |\n\n**Slow:** keep prior field values; do not clear the form.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}/members` + `PATCH .../members/{user_id}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On Members tab select / modal open: `GET` members. While slow: show `settings-members-loading` or keep prior rows. On **200**: render rows ordered as server returns; every row has `role-badge`; editable rows get `role-select` preselected to current role. On change of `role-select`: `PATCH` `{role}` immediately (or on explicit apply — **prefer immediate**). On **403/400**: revert select to last known role; show `settings-members-error`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-6 matrix). |\n\n**Who sees `role-select`:**\n\n| Actor role | Target | UI |\n|------------|--------|-----|\n| owner | admin/member/guest | `role-select` enabled |\n| owner | owner (self) | badge only |\n| admin | member/guest | `role-select` enabled |\n| admin | admin/owner | badge only |\n| member/guest | anyone | badge only |\n\nCaller role: derive from members list (`user_id === session user`) or from detail if already known.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/transfer_ownership`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Visible only if caller is workspace owner. Body `{new_owner_id}` from admin-only select. Confirm (browser `confirm` OK). On **200**: refresh workspace + members. On **400/403**: `settings-transfer-error`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-6). |\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ invitations (create / list / revoke / accept)\n\n#### Create — `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations` → **201** `{invitation}`\n\nClient body (omit empty optionals):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"expires_in_seconds\": 86400,\n  \"max_uses\": 5,\n  \"invited_username\": \"ada\"\n}\n```\n\nDisable submit while in flight; on success prepend/refresh list and show `invitation-code` on the new row; on 400/403 show `invitation-create-error`.\n\n#### List — `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations` → **200** `{invitations:[InvitationObj]}`\n\nLoad when Invitations tab opens (admin). On 403 show admin-only message.\n\n#### Revoke — `DELETE /api/invitations/{code}` → **200** `{revoked:true}`\n\nRemove row on success; on 404 refresh list.\n\n#### Accept — `POST /api/invitations/{code}/accept` → **200** `{workspace, channels?, read_state?}`\n\nFrom onboarding form: on success call existing `enterWorkspace` path (persist slug, show shell) using returned payload (fetch detail if channels omitted). On 403/404 show `invitation-accept-error`.\n\n**Server:** Unchanged (MARATHON-12).\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ channel topic / archive / members list\n\n| API | Client behavior |\n|-----|-----------------|\n| `GET /api/channels/{id}/members` | Fill `channel-members-list`; slow → keep prior / empty with loading |\n| `PATCH /api/channels/{id}` `{topic}` | Save from `settings-topic`; **423** → message in `settings-topic-error` and disable further topic edits until unarchived |","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":490,"fileSize":28740,"path":"/tmp/designs/MARATHON-18.md","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":250},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-74d38cd0-8f84-4ab9-8681-55e7f39030bc-29\nfc_e8806530-d7a4-9e9f-a2d5-14f5ad9328e6_0","startedAtMs":"1787447731926","completedAtMs":"1787447736925"},"model_call_id":"03dd848d-d7bd-4877-bfbf-ce6458bc28c6-10-lppn","session_id":"8d1f97e9-e376-440d-a791-e2992491ec56","timestamp_ms":1787447736949}
