{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-ab77b936-3762-4119-896b-d66be9dd4115-61\nfc_22680d88-c103-90ee-8f32-e3e02dd0e8ff_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cat > /tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n# MARATHON-17 — SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\n\n## Summary\n\nFill the MARATHON-16 workspace shell with the core chat UX: channel list selection and create-channel modal (duplicate-name validation, `#`-prefixed display names, `data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name` on rows), channel header (name + topic) with non-blank empty-channel copy, message history with composer (post / hover-toolbar edit+delete, edited indicator, empty-body validation, hard-reload survival via REST), message rows (avatar + author + human-readable timestamp + body), right-hand thread panel that bumps reply counts, and reactions via an in-DOM emoji-picker grid (never `prompt()`) with count badges. This task is **frontend-only** against already-shipped MARATHON-7/8 REST; it locks the epic’s `channel-*` / `message-*` / `thread-*` / `reaction-*` / `emoji-*` / `create-channel-modal` selector contract so CUA/Playwright can drive chat at 1280×900.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Delivery | Extend the **zero-build vanilla SPA** (`static/` ES modules) — same stack as MARATHON-16; no bundler |\n| Module split | New `static/js/chat_ui.js` owns channel switch, create modal, message pane, thread panel, reactions; `shell.js` exposes active workspace/channel + list refresh hooks; reuse `api.js` / `storage.js` |\n| Data path | **REST only** for this task (list/post/patch/delete/replies/reactions). No WebSocket live fan-out (MARATHON-13). After each successful mutation, update local DOM from the response envelope; on channel select, `GET` history |\n| Channel create | Modal `create-channel-modal` → `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels`; append sidebar row on 201; 409 → inline duplicate-name error |\n| Channel switch | Click sidebar row → set `activeChannel`, render header + load messages; keep thread panel closed unless opened on a message |\n| Empty states | Distinct non-blank copy for (a) no channel selected, (b) channel selected with zero messages |\n| Message chrome | Hover toolbar on own rows for edit/delete; react + reply available on all visible rows the caller can write |\n| Reactions | Fixed emoji **grid** in a popover (`emoji-picker`); toggle via POST/DELETE; badges show emoji + count |\n| Threads | Open `thread-panel` for a top-level parent; list replies oldest-first; composer posts with `parent_id`; bump parent `reply_count` UI |\n| Selectors | Exact `data-testid` strings below; required DOM **id** `create-channel-modal`; keep M16 shell testids intact |\n| M18 coexistence | Message-pane header includes `channel-settings-btn` mount (visible when non-DM active). Click dispatches `huddle:open-channel-settings` CustomEvent (detail `{channelId}`) or calls optional `ctx.openChannelSettings?.(id)` — M18 wires the handler; M17 must not open settings itself |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic + task require chat UX with stable selectors; M16 explicitly deferred composer/threads/reactions/create-channel here; M7/M8 APIs are closed.\n- REST-only avoids coupling to MARATHON-13 (still in review) while still meeting “survive hard reload” (SQLite-backed messages reload on GET).\n- Vanilla modules preserve `start.sh` / no-Node ops and match M16/M18.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Wait for WebSocket (M13) before SPA chat | Blocks P1 UX; REST already durable; live sync can layer later |\n| `window.prompt()` for emoji | Explicitly forbidden by task; graders look for grid picker |\n| Nested reply-to-reply UI | Server rejects deep `parent_id` (M8); one-level panel only |\n| Auto-select `#general` on workspace enter | Acceptable enhancement, but not required; placeholder “Select a channel” already in M16 — **prefer auto-select first non-DM channel (usually general)** for CUA speed; document as required behavior |\n| React/Vite chat island | Diverges from M16 zero-build convention |\n| Invent new message envelopes | Would break M8 graders and parallel agents |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nWithout M13, other users’ messages appear only after **manual channel re-select or soft refresh** (re-GET). Hard reload of the page restores history from REST. That is acceptable for this task’s acceptance bar; live fan-out is a follow-up when M13 ships.\n\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n\nFrom **MARATHON-16**: vanilla SPA; `api()` + bearer; `{error:{code,message}}`; `hidden` for unused chrome; hash `#/w/{slug}`; token keys `huddle.token` (+fallbacks); channel rows already expose `data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name`; `#` prefix display for non-DM; `thread-panel` starts hidden.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj` keys `{id,workspace_id,name,is_private,is_dm,topic,is_archived}`; create `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` body `{name, is_private?, topic?}`; name regex `^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`; **409** `conflict` on duplicate name; guests cannot create; only owner/admin create private.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-8**: `MessageObj` keys exactly  \n`{id, channel_id, author_id, author, body, parent_id, reply_count, created_at, edited_at, files, reactions, mentions}`  \n(no `seq`); `ReactionObj` `{emoji, count, user_ids}`; POST/GET channel messages; PATCH/DELETE message; GET replies; POST/DELETE reactions; empty body → **400**; archived writes → **423**; list newest-first top-level only; replies oldest-first.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-18** (sibling design): shared `activeChannel`; `channel-settings-btn` in message-pane header; settings must not require composer — M17 provides header chrome + event hook.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-3/4**: nested `author` is `UserObj` (`id, username, display_name, timezone, avatar_url, status_text, status_emoji`).\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\n\nProduct “frontend hooks” are not checked into this repo; the tables below are **normative** for this task. All names are **`data-testid` values** unless marked as DOM `id`. Elements must exist in the DOM when the corresponding UI is shown (not only as JS string constants). Prefer exactly these strings — no prefixes.\n\n#### Required DOM id\n\n| `id` | Element |\n|------|---------|\n| `create-channel-modal` | Create-channel overlay/dialog root |\n\nAlso set `data-testid=\"create-channel-modal\"` on the same node (either selector style works).\n\n#### Channels — list / create / header\n\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\n|---------------|--------------|------|\n| `channel-list` | Shell (M16) | Non-DM channel container (unchanged) |\n| `dms-list` | Shell (M16) | DM container (unchanged); switching DMs uses same message pane |\n| `channel-create-btn` | Shell with workspace | Opens create-channel modal |\n| `create-channel-modal` | Modal open (and present in DOM when closed+hidden) | Dialog root |\n| `create-channel-name` | Modal | Name `<input>` (kebab, no `#`) |\n| `create-channel-private` | Modal | Optional checkbox/toggle for `is_private` |\n| `create-channel-topic` | Modal | Optional topic input |\n| `create-channel-submit` | Modal | Submit |\n| `create-channel-error` | Modal | Visible validation / 409 / 403 text |\n| `create-channel-close` | Modal | Dismiss |\n| `channel-header` | Channel selected | Message-pane header chrome |\n| `channel-name` | Channel selected | Display name with `#` for non-DM (or DM peer label) |\n| `channel-topic` | Channel selected | Topic text (may be empty string rendered as muted “No topic” — still non-blank node text) |\n| `channel-settings-btn` | Non-DM channel selected | Settings entry for M18 (see coexistence) |\n| `empty-channel` | Selected channel with **zero** messages | Non-blank empty copy (e.g. “No messages yet”) |\n| `message-pane-placeholder` | Shell with **no** channel selected | Non-blank “Select a channel” (may reuse M16 placeholder; give it this testid) |\n\nEach channel row button **must** keep `data-channel-id=\"{id}\"` and `data-channel-name=\"{name}\"` (name **without** `#`). Active row: add class `is-active` (or `aria-current=\"true\"`).\n\n**Negative:** Display must **not** store `#` inside `data-channel-name` or create-channel payload `name`.\n\n#### Messages — list / composer / row / toolbar\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `message-pane` | Main pane (M16; unchanged id) |\n| `message-list` | Scrollable list of top-level messages |\n| `message-item` | One top-level message row (repeatable) |\n| `message-avatar` | Avatar image or initials element |\n| `message-author` | Author display name (fallback username) |\n| `message-timestamp` | Human-readable time |\n| `message-body` | Message text body |\n| `message-edited` | Visible only when `edited_at != null` (e.g. “Edited”) |\n| `message-toolbar` | Hover/focus toolbar on a row |\n| `message-edit-btn` | Start inline edit (author only) |\n| `message-delete-btn` | Delete (author or workspace owner — hide if neither) |\n| `message-reply-btn` | Open thread panel for this message |\n| `message-react-btn` | Open emoji picker for this message |\n| `message-edit-input` | Inline edit textarea/input when editing |\n| `message-edit-save` | Save edit |\n| `message-edit-cancel` | Cancel edit |\n| `message-composer` | Composer region for channel (top-level) |\n| `message-input` | Composer textarea/input |\n| `message-submit` | Post button |\n| `message-error` | Visible empty-body / 400 / 423 / network error |\n\nEach `message-item` **must** expose `data-message-id=\"{id}\"`.\n\n#### Threads\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `thread-panel` | Right panel (M16; unhide when open) |\n| `thread-header` | Panel header (parent preview / title) |\n| `thread-close` | Close panel |\n| `thread-reply-count` | Shows `N replies` (or `N reply`) from parent `reply_count` |\n| `thread-list` | Reply list container |\n| `thread-item` | One reply row (same inner author/body/timestamp pattern; may reuse `message-*` child testids) |\n| `thread-composer` | Reply composer |\n| `thread-input` | Reply input |\n| `thread-submit` | Post reply |\n| `thread-error` | Reply validation / API error |\n\nEach `thread-item` **must** expose `data-message-id=\"{id}\"`.\n\n#### Reactions / emoji\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `reaction-list` | Container of reaction badges on a message |\n| `reaction-badge` | One emoji+count badge (repeatable) |\n| `emoji-picker` | Grid popover/panel (never `prompt`) |\n| `emoji-option` | Clickable emoji cell in the grid (repeatable) |\n\nEach `reaction-badge` **must** expose `data-emoji=\"{emoji}\"` (exact server string).  \nEach `emoji-option` **must** expose `data-emoji=\"{emoji}\"`.\n\n**Negative:** Must **not** call `window.prompt`, `window.confirm` for emoji choice (confirm OK for delete).\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Bearer; body `{name, is_private?: bool, topic?: string}`. Client trims name; strips a leading `#` if the user typed one before send; validates non-empty locally. Disable submit in flight. **201** `{channel}` → append to `channel-list`, close modal, select new channel. **409** → show server `error.message` (or “Channel name already taken”) in `create-channel-error`. **400** → show validation message. **403** → permission error. **401** → M16 logout. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-7). |\n\n**Slow:** keep modal open; do not clear fields.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages?limit=&before=`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On channel select: GET with default limit (omit or `limit=50`). Render **newest-first from server** in `message-list` such that the **latest message is visually nearest the composer** (typical chat: reverse flex / scroll-to-bottom — implementer choice, but latest must be visible without hunting). While slow: show prior list or a non-blocking loading state; do not blank the header. **200** `{messages}` → replace list; if empty show `empty-channel`. **403/404** → show `message-error` and clear list. **401** → logout. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-8). Top-level only, non-deleted, newest-first. |\n\n**Pagination:** Initial page only is required for acceptance. Optional “Load older” using `before={oldest_id}` is nice-to-have, not required.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Top-level: body `{body}` from `message-input` (trim). Empty/whitespace → **do not** call API; show `message-error` (“Message cannot be empty”). Disable submit in flight. **201** `{message}` → append/prepend into list per display order; clear input; hide `empty-channel`. Thread reply: same with `{body, parent_id}`; append to `thread-list`; increment visible parent `reply_count` / `thread-reply-count`. **400** → show server message. **423** → archived lock copy in `message-error` / `thread-error`. **403** → not a member. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-8). |\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `PATCH /api/messages/{id}` / `DELETE /api/messages/{id}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client PATCH** | Author only controls. Body `{body}`; empty → local validation same as post. **200** → replace row body; show `message-edited` from `edited_at`. **409** → remove row / treat deleted. **403** → hide edit. |\n| **Client DELETE** | Confirm via `window.confirm` OK. Author or workspace owner (client may approximate: show delete if `author_id === me` OR caller is workspace owner from cached workspace `owner_id`). **200** `{deleted:true}` → remove row from list/thread; if parent deleted while thread open, close thread. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-8). |\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/messages/{parent_id}/replies`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On open thread: GET replies; render oldest-first in `thread-list`. Header shows parent body + `thread-reply-count`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged. Envelope key is **`replies`** (not `messages`). |\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ reactions\n\n#### `POST /api/messages/{id}/reactions` `{ \"emoji\": \"👍\" }` → `200 { \"reactions\": [ReactionObj] }`\n\n#### `DELETE /api/messages/{id}/reactions/{emoji}` → `200 { \"reactions\": [...] }`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Opening `emoji-picker` from `message-react-btn` shows a **fixed grid** of at least **8** emoji options (normative starter set: 👍 ❤️ 😂 😮 😢 🎉 ✅ 👀). Choosing an option POSTs that emoji. Clicking an existing `reaction-badge` where `user_ids` contains me → DELETE; else → POST. Replace `reaction-list` from response. Encode emoji in DELETE URL path (`encodeURIComponent`). Never use `prompt()`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (idempotent). |\n\n**Slow:** keep prior badges; disable picker options in flight for that message.\n\n---\n\n### HTTP client rules\n\nReuse MARATHON-16 `api()`: JSON, bearer, timeout, envelope parse, 401 → `onUnauthorized`. Do not invent cookies or alternate base URLs.\n\n### Ownership at the FE/BE seam\n\n| Behavior | Owner |\n|----------|-------|\n| Channel name uniqueness, kebab validation, topic max | **Server** (client may pre-check kebab + local duplicate for UX) |\n| Empty message body | **Both**: client blocks empty; server still 400 if bypassed |\n| Soft-delete visibility | **Server** omits from GET; client removes on DELETE 200 |\n| Reaction aggregation | **Server** returns full `reactions` array; client only renders |\n| Human-readable timestamps | **Client** (`Intl.DateTimeFormat` or equivalent from `created_at` UTC Z) |\n| Avatar URL missing | **Client** shows initials from `display_name` or `username` |\n| Live multi-tab / multi-user sync | **Out of scope** (M13) |\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Browser / in-memory (no SQLite migration)\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `activeChannel` | `ChannelObj \\| null` | Shared with M18 |\n| `messagesByChannelId` | `Map<id, MessageObj[]>` | Optional cache; invalidate on select or always refetch |\n| `openThreadParentId` | `string \\| null` | When thread panel open |\n| `emojiPickerMessageId` | `string \\| null` | Which message owns open picker |\n\n### Server schema\n\n**No schema changes.** Consume M7 `ChannelObj` and M8 `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` as shipped.\n\n### Entity shapes (normative for SPA)\n\n```json\n// ChannelObj (unchanged)\n{ \"id\": \"…\", \"workspace_id\": \"…\", \"name\": \"eng\", \"is_private\": false, \"is_dm\": false, \"topic\": \"Ship week\", \"is_archived\": false }\n\n// MessageObj (unchanged keys)\n{\n  \"id\": \"…\",\n  \"channel_id\": \"…\",\n  \"author_id\": \"…\",\n  \"author\": { \"id\": \"…\", \"username\": \"ada\", \"display_name\": \"Ada\", \"timezone\": null, \"avatar_url\": null, \"status_text\": null, \"status_emoji\": null },\n  \"body\": \"hello\",\n  \"parent_id\": null,\n  \"reply_count\": 0,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"edited_at\": null,\n  \"files\": [],\n  \"reactions\": [{ \"emoji\": \"👍\", \"count\": 1, \"user_ids\": [\"…\"] }],\n  \"mentions\": []\n}\n```\n\n**Backward compatible:** additive UI only; no API version bump.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/js/chat_ui.js` | Channel select handler integration API, create-channel modal controller, message list/composer/edit/delete, thread panel, emoji picker + reaction badges; export `initChatUi(ctx)` |\n| `tests/test_spa_chat.py` | TestClient: HTML contains required chat testids / `create-channel-modal` id; static JS references key API paths (`/messages`, `/reactions`, `/channels`); assert source does **not** contain `window.prompt` for emoji |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/index.html` | Create-channel modal markup; message-pane header + list + composer slots; thread-panel structure (close, list, composer); emoji-picker container (can be single reused popover); all required testids |\n| `static/css/app.css` | Header, message rows, hover toolbar, empty states, thread panel layout, emoji grid, reaction badges — fit **1280×900**; preserve sidebar colour language from M16 |\n| `static/js/shell.js` | Wire channel row clicks to `setActiveChannel`; expose `getWorkspace`, `getActiveChannel`, `setActiveChannel`, `getChannels`, `refreshChannels` / re-render list helpers; mount `channel-create-btn`; on workspace show, **auto-select** first non-DM channel if none active; keep `data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name`; `#` prefix display |\n| `static/js/app.js` | `initChatUi({ getToken, getUser, shell, onUnauthorized })` after shell init |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | Keep existing required testids green; do not remove M16 selectors |\n\n### Do not modify\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/messages/**`, `server/channels/**`, `server/workspaces/**` | Contracts already ship; SPA consumes |\n| `server/db.py` / migrations | No schema change |\n| `start.sh` | No build step |\n| Settings modals / invitation UI | MARATHON-18 |\n| WebSocket client | MARATHON-13 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order within this task\n\n1. HTML slots + CSS + testids (unblocks selector tests).\n2. Channel select + header + empty states + auto-select general.\n3. Create-channel modal → POST create → sidebar append.\n4. Message list GET + composer POST + empty validation.\n5. Hover toolbar edit/delete + edited indicator.\n6. Thread panel open/close + replies GET/POST + reply_count bump.\n7. Emoji picker + reaction badges toggle.\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Fully parallel with MARATHON-18 **if** both respect shared `activeChannel` + header `channel-settings-btn` / CustomEvent contract.\n- Independent of MARATHON-13/14/15; no live sync required.\n- Blocked only on closed M16 shell + M7/M8 APIs (already closed).\n\n### Seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumer |\n|----------|----------|\n| Chat `data-testid` set + `create-channel-modal` | QA / CUA |\n| `initChatUi` / active channel selection | MARATHON-18 settings button enablement |\n| `huddle:open-channel-settings` event (or ctx callback) | MARATHON-18 |\n| REST consumption of M7 create + M8 messages/reactions | Implementer |\n\n### Seams owned elsewhere\n\n| Contract | Owner |\n|----------|-------|\n| `ChannelObj` / create channel API | MARATHON-7 |\n| `MessageObj` / reactions API | MARATHON-8 |\n| Auth token + shell layout | MARATHON-16 |\n| Workspace/channel settings modals | MARATHON-18 |\n| WS resume / dense seq live updates | MARATHON-13 |\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not create unless lead asks)\n\n- Wire chat UI to MARATHON-13 WS events for live append/patch without refresh.\n- Infinite scroll / jump-to-date.\n- Slash-command autocomplete UI (MARATHON-11 server).\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| Workspace/channel settings modals | `settings_ui.js`, M18 testids | MARATHON-18 |\n| WebSocket subscribe/resume | `/api/ws` | MARATHON-13 |\n| File attach in composer | `file_ids`, MARATHON-10 | Non-empty file_ids still 400 |\n| Search / slash / read receipts UI | MARATHON-11 | Different task |\n| Pins UI | pin routes exist | Not in this task description |\n| DM create UX | MARATHON-9 API exists; list already split — creating new DMs not required here |\n| IRC | MARATHON-15 | Unrelated |\n| Changing REST envelopes / schema | `server/**` | Frontend-only |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `static/index.html`, `shell.js`, `app.js`, `app.css` | **In scope** — extend |\n| `static/js/api.js`, `storage.js`, `auth_ui.js` | **Reuse** — no contract change |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | **Keep green**; chat selectors in new test file |\n| `server/messages/**`, `server/channels/**`, create channel route | **Consume only** |\n| `tests/test_messages.py`, `test_channels.py` | **Out of scope** to rewrite; must stay green |\n| Grep `create-channel` / `emoji-picker` / `message-composer` in `static/` | No hits yet — greenfield UI |\n| Frontend-dev M18 WIP adding `channel-settings-btn` / message-pane header | **Coordinate** via shared header testids; do not delete settings hooks if already merged |\n| M16 placeholder “Select a channel” | **Replace/retag** as `message-pane-placeholder` / `empty-channel` per states |\n| M8 `prompt` mention in older notes | N/A — SPA must use grid |\n\nIf nothing else: neighborhood scan found M18 settings WIP and M13 WS as siblings — both explicitly out of scope above.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Case | Expected behavior |\n|------|-------------------|\n| Create name `Eng` / `eng_ops` / `e` / empty | Client and/or server **400**; show `create-channel-error` |\n| Create duplicate `general` | **409**; visible duplicate-name error; modal stays open |\n| User types `#eng` in create field | Strip `#` before POST; send `eng` |\n| Select archived channel | Allow **read** history; composer disabled + `message-error` explains archived (POST would 423) |\n| Empty message submit | No API call; `message-error` visible |\n| Edit then empty save | Same local validation; no PATCH |\n| Delete message with open thread | Close thread if parent deleted; if reply deleted, remove from thread-list and decrement count |\n| Reaction on deleted message | **409** → refresh/remove row |\n| Non-member viewing public channel | GET may succeed (M8 public read); POST → **403** → show error; hide composer if known non-member (optional: try and surface error) |\n| Guest creating channel | **403** in `create-channel-error` |\n| Hard reload after posts | Token restores workspace (M16); auto-select channel; GET messages shows prior posts |\n| `avatar_url` null | Initials avatar; `message-avatar` still present |\n| `display_name` null/empty | Show `username` in `message-author` |\n| Timestamp | Parse `created_at` as UTC; display local human-readable (date + time or relative); full ISO may be `title` tooltip |\n| Thread on message with `reply_count=0` | Panel still opens; empty `thread-list` + composer |\n| Emoji picker open + click outside / Escape | Close picker |\n| Double-click channel | Idempotent re-select; avoid duplicate in-flight GETs (abort or ignore stale) |\n| Network timeout | `api()` timeout → show `message-error` / modal error with failure text; keep prior data |\n| `window.prompt` | **Must not** be used for emoji or channel name |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Authenticated workspace shell lists channels with `#` prefix for non-DM; each row has `data-channel-id` and `data-channel-name` (no `#` in data attribute).\n2. Clicking a channel shows `channel-header` with `channel-name` and `channel-topic`; message pane leaves the generic “Select a channel” state.\n3. Empty channel shows non-blank `empty-channel` copy (not a white void).\n4. `channel-create-btn` opens `create-channel-modal`; valid create calls `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` and adds the channel to `channel-list`; selecting it works.\n5. Duplicate channel name shows visible error in `create-channel-error` and does **not** add a duplicate row.\n6. Composer posts via `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages`; new message appears as `message-item` with avatar, author, human-readable timestamp, and body.\n7. Empty composer submit shows `message-error` and does **not** create a server message.\n8. Hover/focus toolbar allows author to edit; after save, `message-edited` is visible and body updates; hard reload + re-open channel still shows edited body from server.\n9. Author (or owner) can delete via toolbar; message disappears from the list.\n10. `message-reply-btn` opens `thread-panel` (unhidden); replies load; posting a reply increments `thread-reply-count` / parent reply affordance.\n11. `message-react-btn` opens `emoji-picker` grid with `emoji-option` cells; choosing one creates a `reaction-badge` with count; clicking badge toggles caller’s reaction; **no** `prompt()`.\n12. Required testids in the tables above are present when their UI state is visible; `create-channel-modal` exists as a DOM id.\n13. **Negative:** must **not** require MARATHON-13 WS for the above; must **not** break M16 auth/shell testids; must **not** implement settings modals (M18); must **not** send `#` in channel `name` field; must **not** use `{messages}` as the replies envelope key when calling the API.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated\n\n- Extend/add `tests/test_spa_chat.py` (TestClient):\n  - `GET /` HTML includes `create-channel-modal`, `channel-create-btn`, `message-list`, `message-composer`, `message-input`, `thread-close`, `emoji-picker` (picker may be `hidden`).\n  - `/static/js/chat_ui.js` returns 200 and references `/messages` and `/reactions`.\n  - Source of chat module does not contain `prompt(` for emoji flows.\n- Existing `tests/test_spa_shell.py`, `test_messages.py`, `test_channels.py` remain green.\n\n### Manual / Playwright at 1280×900\n\n1. Register → create workspace → confirm `#general` auto-selected or selectable; header shows name/topic.\n2. Post three messages; reload page; return to channel; all three still present with authors/timestamps.\n3. Edit one message; see edited indicator; reload; persists.\n4. Delete one message; gone after reload.\n5. Open thread; reply; badge/count bumps; close panel.\n6. Add 👍 via emoji grid; count 1; click badge to remove.\n7. Create channel `eng`; appears as `#eng`; create `eng` again → error.\n8. Submit empty message → error; no new row.\n9. Confirm no native prompt dialogs during reaction flow.\n\n### Done when\n\nAcceptance criteria 1–13 hold on a single HTTP node with shared SQLite; suite green; design selectors stable for CUA.\nDESIGN_EOF\nwc -c /tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md\n","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-ab77b936-3762-4119-896b-d66be9dd4115-61\nfc_22680d88-c103-90ee-8f32-e3e02dd0e8ff_0","simpleCommands":["cat","wc"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cat","args":[],"fullText":"cat"},{"name":"wc","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md"}],"fullText":"wc -c /tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":false,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"cat"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Write MARATHON-17 design markdown file","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"8d1f97e9-e376-440d-a791-e2992491ec56","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"description":"Write MARATHON-17 design markdown file"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-ab77b936-3762-4119-896b-d66be9dd4115-61\nfc_22680d88-c103-90ee-8f32-e3e02dd0e8ff_0","startedAtMs":"1787447982494"},"model_call_id":"03dd848d-d7bd-4877-bfbf-ce6458bc28c6-18-tz0i","session_id":"8d1f97e9-e376-440d-a791-e2992491ec56","timestamp_ms":1787447982527}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-ab77b936-3762-4119-896b-d66be9dd4115-61\nfc_22680d88-c103-90ee-8f32-e3e02dd0e8ff_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cat > /tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n# MARATHON-17 — SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\n\n## Summary\n\nFill the MARATHON-16 workspace shell with the core chat UX: channel list selection and create-channel modal (duplicate-name validation, `#`-prefixed display names, `data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name` on rows), channel header (name + topic) with non-blank empty-channel copy, message history with composer (post / hover-toolbar edit+delete, edited indicator, empty-body validation, hard-reload survival via REST), message rows (avatar + author + human-readable timestamp + body), right-hand thread panel that bumps reply counts, and reactions via an in-DOM emoji-picker grid (never `prompt()`) with count badges. This task is **frontend-only** against already-shipped MARATHON-7/8 REST; it locks the epic’s `channel-*` / `message-*` / `thread-*` / `reaction-*` / `emoji-*` / `create-channel-modal` selector contract so CUA/Playwright can drive chat at 1280×900.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Delivery | Extend the **zero-build vanilla SPA** (`static/` ES modules) — same stack as MARATHON-16; no bundler |\n| Module split | New `static/js/chat_ui.js` owns channel switch, create modal, message pane, thread panel, reactions; `shell.js` exposes active workspace/channel + list refresh hooks; reuse `api.js` / `storage.js` |\n| Data path | **REST only** for this task (list/post/patch/delete/replies/reactions). No WebSocket live fan-out (MARATHON-13). After each successful mutation, update local DOM from the response envelope; on channel select, `GET` history |\n| Channel create | Modal `create-channel-modal` → `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels`; append sidebar row on 201; 409 → inline duplicate-name error |\n| Channel switch | Click sidebar row → set `activeChannel`, render header + load messages; keep thread panel closed unless opened on a message |\n| Empty states | Distinct non-blank copy for (a) no channel selected, (b) channel selected with zero messages |\n| Message chrome | Hover toolbar on own rows for edit/delete; react + reply available on all visible rows the caller can write |\n| Reactions | Fixed emoji **grid** in a popover (`emoji-picker`); toggle via POST/DELETE; badges show emoji + count |\n| Threads | Open `thread-panel` for a top-level parent; list replies oldest-first; composer posts with `parent_id`; bump parent `reply_count` UI |\n| Selectors | Exact `data-testid` strings below; required DOM **id** `create-channel-modal`; keep M16 shell testids intact |\n| M18 coexistence | Message-pane header includes `channel-settings-btn` mount (visible when non-DM active). Click dispatches `huddle:open-channel-settings` CustomEvent (detail `{channelId}`) or calls optional `ctx.openChannelSettings?.(id)` — M18 wires the handler; M17 must not open settings itself |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic + task require chat UX with stable selectors; M16 explicitly deferred composer/threads/reactions/create-channel here; M7/M8 APIs are closed.\n- REST-only avoids coupling to MARATHON-13 (still in review) while still meeting “survive hard reload” (SQLite-backed messages reload on GET).\n- Vanilla modules preserve `start.sh` / no-Node ops and match M16/M18.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Wait for WebSocket (M13) before SPA chat | Blocks P1 UX; REST already durable; live sync can layer later |\n| `window.prompt()` for emoji | Explicitly forbidden by task; graders look for grid picker |\n| Nested reply-to-reply UI | Server rejects deep `parent_id` (M8); one-level panel only |\n| Auto-select `#general` on workspace enter | Acceptable enhancement, but not required; placeholder “Select a channel” already in M16 — **prefer auto-select first non-DM channel (usually general)** for CUA speed; document as required behavior |\n| React/Vite chat island | Diverges from M16 zero-build convention |\n| Invent new message envelopes | Would break M8 graders and parallel agents |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nWithout M13, other users’ messages appear only after **manual channel re-select or soft refresh** (re-GET). Hard reload of the page restores history from REST. That is acceptable for this task’s acceptance bar; live fan-out is a follow-up when M13 ships.\n\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n\nFrom **MARATHON-16**: vanilla SPA; `api()` + bearer; `{error:{code,message}}`; `hidden` for unused chrome; hash `#/w/{slug}`; token keys `huddle.token` (+fallbacks); channel rows already expose `data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name`; `#` prefix display for non-DM; `thread-panel` starts hidden.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj` keys `{id,workspace_id,name,is_private,is_dm,topic,is_archived}`; create `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` body `{name, is_private?, topic?}`; name regex `^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`; **409** `conflict` on duplicate name; guests cannot create; only owner/admin create private.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-8**: `MessageObj` keys exactly  \n`{id, channel_id, author_id, author, body, parent_id, reply_count, created_at, edited_at, files, reactions, mentions}`  \n(no `seq`); `ReactionObj` `{emoji, count, user_ids}`; POST/GET channel messages; PATCH/DELETE message; GET replies; POST/DELETE reactions; empty body → **400**; archived writes → **423**; list newest-first top-level only; replies oldest-first.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-18** (sibling design): shared `activeChannel`; `channel-settings-btn` in message-pane header; settings must not require composer — M17 provides header chrome + event hook.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-3/4**: nested `author` is `UserObj` (`id, username, display_name, timezone, avatar_url, status_text, status_emoji`).\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\n\nProduct “frontend hooks” are not checked into this repo; the tables below are **normative** for this task. All names are **`data-testid` values** unless marked as DOM `id`. Elements must exist in the DOM when the corresponding UI is shown (not only as JS string constants). Prefer exactly these strings — no prefixes.\n\n#### Required DOM id\n\n| `id` | Element |\n|------|---------|\n| `create-channel-modal` | Create-channel overlay/dialog root |\n\nAlso set `data-testid=\"create-channel-modal\"` on the same node (either selector style works).\n\n#### Channels — list / create / header\n\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\n|---------------|--------------|------|\n| `channel-list` | Shell (M16) | Non-DM channel container (unchanged) |\n| `dms-list` | Shell (M16) | DM container (unchanged); switching DMs uses same message pane |\n| `channel-create-btn` | Shell with workspace | Opens create-channel modal |\n| `create-channel-modal` | Modal open (and present in DOM when closed+hidden) | Dialog root |\n| `create-channel-name` | Modal | Name `<input>` (kebab, no `#`) |\n| `create-channel-private` | Modal | Optional checkbox/toggle for `is_private` |\n| `create-channel-topic` | Modal | Optional topic input |\n| `create-channel-submit` | Modal | Submit |\n| `create-channel-error` | Modal | Visible validation / 409 / 403 text |\n| `create-channel-close` | Modal | Dismiss |\n| `channel-header` | Channel selected | Message-pane header chrome |\n| `channel-name` | Channel selected | Display name with `#` for non-DM (or DM peer label) |\n| `channel-topic` | Channel selected | Topic text (may be empty string rendered as muted “No topic” — still non-blank node text) |\n| `channel-settings-btn` | Non-DM channel selected | Settings entry for M18 (see coexistence) |\n| `empty-channel` | Selected channel with **zero** messages | Non-blank empty copy (e.g. “No messages yet”) |\n| `message-pane-placeholder` | Shell with **no** channel selected | Non-blank “Select a channel” (may reuse M16 placeholder; give it this testid) |\n\nEach channel row button **must** keep `data-channel-id=\"{id}\"` and `data-channel-name=\"{name}\"` (name **without** `#`). Active row: add class `is-active` (or `aria-current=\"true\"`).\n\n**Negative:** Display must **not** store `#` inside `data-channel-name` or create-channel payload `name`.\n\n#### Messages — list / composer / row / toolbar\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `message-pane` | Main pane (M16; unchanged id) |\n| `message-list` | Scrollable list of top-level messages |\n| `message-item` | One top-level message row (repeatable) |\n| `message-avatar` | Avatar image or initials element |\n| `message-author` | Author display name (fallback username) |\n| `message-timestamp` | Human-readable time |\n| `message-body` | Message text body |\n| `message-edited` | Visible only when `edited_at != null` (e.g. “Edited”) |\n| `message-toolbar` | Hover/focus toolbar on a row |\n| `message-edit-btn` | Start inline edit (author only) |\n| `message-delete-btn` | Delete (author or workspace owner — hide if neither) |\n| `message-reply-btn` | Open thread panel for this message |\n| `message-react-btn` | Open emoji picker for this message |\n| `message-edit-input` | Inline edit textarea/input when editing |\n| `message-edit-save` | Save edit |\n| `message-edit-cancel` | Cancel edit |\n| `message-composer` | Composer region for channel (top-level) |\n| `message-input` | Composer textarea/input |\n| `message-submit` | Post button |\n| `message-error` | Visible empty-body / 400 / 423 / network error |\n\nEach `message-item` **must** expose `data-message-id=\"{id}\"`.\n\n#### Threads\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `thread-panel` | Right panel (M16; unhide when open) |\n| `thread-header` | Panel header (parent preview / title) |\n| `thread-close` | Close panel |\n| `thread-reply-count` | Shows `N replies` (or `N reply`) from parent `reply_count` |\n| `thread-list` | Reply list container |\n| `thread-item` | One reply row (same inner author/body/timestamp pattern; may reuse `message-*` child testids) |\n| `thread-composer` | Reply composer |\n| `thread-input` | Reply input |\n| `thread-submit` | Post reply |\n| `thread-error` | Reply validation / API error |\n\nEach `thread-item` **must** expose `data-message-id=\"{id}\"`.\n\n#### Reactions / emoji\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `reaction-list` | Container of reaction badges on a message |\n| `reaction-badge` | One emoji+count badge (repeatable) |\n| `emoji-picker` | Grid popover/panel (never `prompt`) |\n| `emoji-option` | Clickable emoji cell in the grid (repeatable) |\n\nEach `reaction-badge` **must** expose `data-emoji=\"{emoji}\"` (exact server string).  \nEach `emoji-option` **must** expose `data-emoji=\"{emoji}\"`.\n\n**Negative:** Must **not** call `window.prompt`, `window.confirm` for emoji choice (confirm OK for delete).\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Bearer; body `{name, is_private?: bool, topic?: string}`. Client trims name; strips a leading `#` if the user typed one before send; validates non-empty locally. Disable submit in flight. **201** `{channel}` → append to `channel-list`, close modal, select new channel. **409** → show server `error.message` (or “Channel name already taken”) in `create-channel-error`. **400** → show validation message. **403** → permission error. **401** → M16 logout. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-7). |\n\n**Slow:** keep modal open; do not clear fields.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages?limit=&before=`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On channel select: GET with default limit (omit or `limit=50`). Render **newest-first from server** in `message-list` such that the **latest message is visually nearest the composer** (typical chat: reverse flex / scroll-to-bottom — implementer choice, but latest must be visible without hunting). While slow: show prior list or a non-blocking loading state; do not blank the header. **200** `{messages}` → replace list; if empty show `empty-channel`. **403/404** → show `message-error` and clear list. **401** → logout. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-8). Top-level only, non-deleted, newest-first. |\n\n**Pagination:** Initial page only is required for acceptance. Optional “Load older” using `before={oldest_id}` is nice-to-have, not required.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Top-level: body `{body}` from `message-input` (trim). Empty/whitespace → **do not** call API; show `message-error` (“Message cannot be empty”). Disable submit in flight. **201** `{message}` → append/prepend into list per display order; clear input; hide `empty-channel`. Thread reply: same with `{body, parent_id}`; append to `thread-list`; increment visible parent `reply_count` / `thread-reply-count`. **400** → show server message. **423** → archived lock copy in `message-error` / `thread-error`. **403** → not a member. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-8). |\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `PATCH /api/messages/{id}` / `DELETE /api/messages/{id}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client PATCH** | Author only controls. Body `{body}`; empty → local validation same as post. **200** → replace row body; show `message-edited` from `edited_at`. **409** → remove row / treat deleted. **403** → hide edit. |\n| **Client DELETE** | Confirm via `window.confirm` OK. Author or workspace owner (client may approximate: show delete if `author_id === me` OR caller is workspace owner from cached workspace `owner_id`). **200** `{deleted:true}` → remove row from list/thread; if parent deleted while thread open, close thread. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-8). |\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/messages/{parent_id}/replies`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On open thread: GET replies; render oldest-first in `thread-list`. Header shows parent body + `thread-reply-count`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged. Envelope key is **`replies`** (not `messages`). |\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ reactions\n\n#### `POST /api/messages/{id}/reactions` `{ \"emoji\": \"👍\" }` → `200 { \"reactions\": [ReactionObj] }`\n\n#### `DELETE /api/messages/{id}/reactions/{emoji}` → `200 { \"reactions\": [...] }`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Opening `emoji-picker` from `message-react-btn` shows a **fixed grid** of at least **8** emoji options (normative starter set: 👍 ❤️ 😂 😮 😢 🎉 ✅ 👀). Choosing an option POSTs that emoji. Clicking an existing `reaction-badge` where `user_ids` contains me → DELETE; else → POST. Replace `reaction-list` from response. Encode emoji in DELETE URL path (`encodeURIComponent`). Never use `prompt()`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (idempotent). |\n\n**Slow:** keep prior badges; disable picker options in flight for that message.\n\n---\n\n### HTTP client rules\n\nReuse MARATHON-16 `api()`: JSON, bearer, timeout, envelope parse, 401 → `onUnauthorized`. Do not invent cookies or alternate base URLs.\n\n### Ownership at the FE/BE seam\n\n| Behavior | Owner |\n|----------|-------|\n| Channel name uniqueness, kebab validation, topic max | **Server** (client may pre-check kebab + local duplicate for UX) |\n| Empty message body | **Both**: client blocks empty; server still 400 if bypassed |\n| Soft-delete visibility | **Server** omits from GET; client removes on DELETE 200 |\n| Reaction aggregation | **Server** returns full `reactions` array; client only renders |\n| Human-readable timestamps | **Client** (`Intl.DateTimeFormat` or equivalent from `created_at` UTC Z) |\n| Avatar URL missing | **Client** shows initials from `display_name` or `username` |\n| Live multi-tab / multi-user sync | **Out of scope** (M13) |\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Browser / in-memory (no SQLite migration)\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `activeChannel` | `ChannelObj \\| null` | Shared with M18 |\n| `messagesByChannelId` | `Map<id, MessageObj[]>` | Optional cache; invalidate on select or always refetch |\n| `openThreadParentId` | `string \\| null` | When thread panel open |\n| `emojiPickerMessageId` | `string \\| null` | Which message owns open picker |\n\n### Server schema\n\n**No schema changes.** Consume M7 `ChannelObj` and M8 `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` as shipped.\n\n### Entity shapes (normative for SPA)\n\n```json\n// ChannelObj (unchanged)\n{ \"id\": \"…\", \"workspace_id\": \"…\", \"name\": \"eng\", \"is_private\": false, \"is_dm\": false, \"topic\": \"Ship week\", \"is_archived\": false }\n\n// MessageObj (unchanged keys)\n{\n  \"id\": \"…\",\n  \"channel_id\": \"…\",\n  \"author_id\": \"…\",\n  \"author\": { \"id\": \"…\", \"username\": \"ada\", \"display_name\": \"Ada\", \"timezone\": null, \"avatar_url\": null, \"status_text\": null, \"status_emoji\": null },\n  \"body\": \"hello\",\n  \"parent_id\": null,\n  \"reply_count\": 0,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"edited_at\": null,\n  \"files\": [],\n  \"reactions\": [{ \"emoji\": \"👍\", \"count\": 1, \"user_ids\": [\"…\"] }],\n  \"mentions\": []\n}\n```\n\n**Backward compatible:** additive UI only; no API version bump.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/js/chat_ui.js` | Channel select handler integration API, create-channel modal controller, message list/composer/edit/delete, thread panel, emoji picker + reaction badges; export `initChatUi(ctx)` |\n| `tests/test_spa_chat.py` | TestClient: HTML contains required chat testids / `create-channel-modal` id; static JS references key API paths (`/messages`, `/reactions`, `/channels`); assert source does **not** contain `window.prompt` for emoji |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/index.html` | Create-channel modal markup; message-pane header + list + composer slots; thread-panel structure (close, list, composer); emoji-picker container (can be single reused popover); all required testids |\n| `static/css/app.css` | Header, message rows, hover toolbar, empty states, thread panel layout, emoji grid, reaction badges — fit **1280×900**; preserve sidebar colour language from M16 |\n| `static/js/shell.js` | Wire channel row clicks to `setActiveChannel`; expose `getWorkspace`, `getActiveChannel`, `setActiveChannel`, `getChannels`, `refreshChannels` / re-render list helpers; mount `channel-create-btn`; on workspace show, **auto-select** first non-DM channel if none active; keep `data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name`; `#` prefix display |\n| `static/js/app.js` | `initChatUi({ getToken, getUser, shell, onUnauthorized })` after shell init |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | Keep existing required testids green; do not remove M16 selectors |\n\n### Do not modify\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/messages/**`, `server/channels/**`, `server/workspaces/**` | Contracts already ship; SPA consumes |\n| `server/db.py` / migrations | No schema change |\n| `start.sh` | No build step |\n| Settings modals / invitation UI | MARATHON-18 |\n| WebSocket client | MARATHON-13 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order within this task\n\n1. HTML slots + CSS + testids (unblocks selector tests).\n2. Channel select + header + empty states + auto-select general.\n3. Create-channel modal → POST create → sidebar append.\n4. Message list GET + composer POST + empty validation.\n5. Hover toolbar edit/delete + edited indicator.\n6. Thread panel open/close + replies GET/POST + reply_count bump.\n7. Emoji picker + reaction badges toggle.\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Fully parallel with MARATHON-18 **if** both respect shared `activeChannel` + header `channel-settings-btn` / CustomEvent contract.\n- Independent of MARATHON-13/14/15; no live sync required.\n- Blocked only on closed M16 shell + M7/M8 APIs (already closed).\n\n### Seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumer |\n|----------|----------|\n| Chat `data-testid` set + `create-channel-modal` | QA / CUA |\n| `initChatUi` / active channel selection | MARATHON-18 settings button enablement |\n| `huddle:open-channel-settings` event (or ctx callback) | MARATHON-18 |\n| REST consumption of M7 create + M8 messages/reactions | Implementer |\n\n### Seams owned elsewhere\n\n| Contract | Owner |\n|----------|-------|\n| `ChannelObj` / create channel API | MARATHON-7 |\n| `MessageObj` / reactions API | MARATHON-8 |\n| Auth token + shell layout | MARATHON-16 |\n| Workspace/channel settings modals | MARATHON-18 |\n| WS resume / dense seq live updates | MARATHON-13 |\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not create unless lead asks)\n\n- Wire chat UI to MARATHON-13 WS events for live append/patch without refresh.\n- Infinite scroll / jump-to-date.\n- Slash-command autocomplete UI (MARATHON-11 server).\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| Workspace/channel settings modals | `settings_ui.js`, M18 testids | MARATHON-18 |\n| WebSocket subscribe/resume | `/api/ws` | MARATHON-13 |\n| File attach in composer | `file_ids`, MARATHON-10 | Non-empty file_ids still 400 |\n| Search / slash / read receipts UI | MARATHON-11 | Different task |\n| Pins UI | pin routes exist | Not in this task description |\n| DM create UX | MARATHON-9 API exists; list already split — creating new DMs not required here |\n| IRC | MARATHON-15 | Unrelated |\n| Changing REST envelopes / schema | `server/**` | Frontend-only |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `static/index.html`, `shell.js`, `app.js`, `app.css` | **In scope** — extend |\n| `static/js/api.js`, `storage.js`, `auth_ui.js` | **Reuse** — no contract change |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | **Keep green**; chat selectors in new test file |\n| `server/messages/**`, `server/channels/**`, create channel route | **Consume only** |\n| `tests/test_messages.py`, `test_channels.py` | **Out of scope** to rewrite; must stay green |\n| Grep `create-channel` / `emoji-picker` / `message-composer` in `static/` | No hits yet — greenfield UI |\n| Frontend-dev M18 WIP adding `channel-settings-btn` / message-pane header | **Coordinate** via shared header testids; do not delete settings hooks if already merged |\n| M16 placeholder “Select a channel” | **Replace/retag** as `message-pane-placeholder` / `empty-channel` per states |\n| M8 `prompt` mention in older notes | N/A — SPA must use grid |\n\nIf nothing else: neighborhood scan found M18 settings WIP and M13 WS as siblings — both explicitly out of scope above.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Case | Expected behavior |\n|------|-------------------|\n| Create name `Eng` / `eng_ops` / `e` / empty | Client and/or server **400**; show `create-channel-error` |\n| Create duplicate `general` | **409**; visible duplicate-name error; modal stays open |\n| User types `#eng` in create field | Strip `#` before POST; send `eng` |\n| Select archived channel | Allow **read** history; composer disabled + `message-error` explains archived (POST would 423) |\n| Empty message submit | No API call; `message-error` visible |\n| Edit then empty save | Same local validation; no PATCH |\n| Delete message with open thread | Close thread if parent deleted; if reply deleted, remove from thread-list and decrement count |\n| Reaction on deleted message | **409** → refresh/remove row |\n| Non-member viewing public channel | GET may succeed (M8 public read); POST → **403** → show error; hide composer if known non-member (optional: try and surface error) |\n| Guest creating channel | **403** in `create-channel-error` |\n| Hard reload after posts | Token restores workspace (M16); auto-select channel; GET messages shows prior posts |\n| `avatar_url` null | Initials avatar; `message-avatar` still present |\n| `display_name` null/empty | Show `username` in `message-author` |\n| Timestamp | Parse `created_at` as UTC; display local human-readable (date + time or relative); full ISO may be `title` tooltip |\n| Thread on message with `reply_count=0` | Panel still opens; empty `thread-list` + composer |\n| Emoji picker open + click outside / Escape | Close picker |\n| Double-click channel | Idempotent re-select; avoid duplicate in-flight GETs (abort or ignore stale) |\n| Network timeout | `api()` timeout → show `message-error` / modal error with failure text; keep prior data |\n| `window.prompt` | **Must not** be used for emoji or channel name |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Authenticated workspace shell lists channels with `#` prefix for non-DM; each row has `data-channel-id` and `data-channel-name` (no `#` in data attribute).\n2. Clicking a channel shows `channel-header` with `channel-name` and `channel-topic`; message pane leaves the generic “Select a channel” state.\n3. Empty channel shows non-blank `empty-channel` copy (not a white void).\n4. `channel-create-btn` opens `create-channel-modal`; valid create calls `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` and adds the channel to `channel-list`; selecting it works.\n5. Duplicate channel name shows visible error in `create-channel-error` and does **not** add a duplicate row.\n6. Composer posts via `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages`; new message appears as `message-item` with avatar, author, human-readable timestamp, and body.\n7. Empty composer submit shows `message-error` and does **not** create a server message.\n8. Hover/focus toolbar allows author to edit; after save, `message-edited` is visible and body updates; hard reload + re-open channel still shows edited body from server.\n9. Author (or owner) can delete via toolbar; message disappears from the list.\n10. `message-reply-btn` opens `thread-panel` (unhidden); replies load; posting a reply increments `thread-reply-count` / parent reply affordance.\n11. `message-react-btn` opens `emoji-picker` grid with `emoji-option` cells; choosing one creates a `reaction-badge` with count; clicking badge toggles caller’s reaction; **no** `prompt()`.\n12. Required testids in the tables above are present when their UI state is visible; `create-channel-modal` exists as a DOM id.\n13. **Negative:** must **not** require MARATHON-13 WS for the above; must **not** break M16 auth/shell testids; must **not** implement settings modals (M18); must **not** send `#` in channel `name` field; must **not** use `{messages}` as the replies envelope key when calling the API.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated\n\n- Extend/add `tests/test_spa_chat.py` (TestClient):\n  - `GET /` HTML includes `create-channel-modal`, `channel-create-btn`, `message-list`, `message-composer`, `message-input`, `thread-close`, `emoji-picker` (picker may be `hidden`).\n  - `/static/js/chat_ui.js` returns 200 and references `/messages` and `/reactions`.\n  - Source of chat module does not contain `prompt(` for emoji flows.\n- Existing `tests/test_spa_shell.py`, `test_messages.py`, `test_channels.py` remain green.\n\n### Manual / Playwright at 1280×900\n\n1. Register → create workspace → confirm `#general` auto-selected or selectable; header shows name/topic.\n2. Post three messages; reload page; return to channel; all three still present with authors/timestamps.\n3. Edit one message; see edited indicator; reload; persists.\n4. Delete one message; gone after reload.\n5. Open thread; reply; badge/count bumps; close panel.\n6. Add 👍 via emoji grid; count 1; click badge to remove.\n7. Create channel `eng`; appears as `#eng`; create `eng` again → error.\n8. Submit empty message → error; no new row.\n9. Confirm no native prompt dialogs during reaction flow.\n\n### Done when\n\nAcceptance criteria 1–13 hold on a single HTTP node with shared SQLite; suite green; design selectors stable for CUA.\nDESIGN_EOF\nwc -c /tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md\n","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-ab77b936-3762-4119-896b-d66be9dd4115-61\nfc_22680d88-c103-90ee-8f32-e3e02dd0e8ff_0","simpleCommands":["cat","wc"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cat","args":[],"fullText":"cat"},{"name":"wc","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md"}],"fullText":"wc -c /tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":false,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"cat"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Write MARATHON-17 design markdown file","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"8d1f97e9-e376-440d-a791-e2992491ec56","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"cat > /tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n# MARATHON-17 — SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\n\n## Summary\n\nFill the MARATHON-16 workspace shell with the core chat UX: channel list selection and create-channel modal (duplicate-name validation, `#`-prefixed display names, `data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name` on rows), channel header (name + topic) with non-blank empty-channel copy, message history with composer (post / hover-toolbar edit+delete, edited indicator, empty-body validation, hard-reload survival via REST), message rows (avatar + author + human-readable timestamp + body), right-hand thread panel that bumps reply counts, and reactions via an in-DOM emoji-picker grid (never `prompt()`) with count badges. This task is **frontend-only** against already-shipped MARATHON-7/8 REST; it locks the epic’s `channel-*` / `message-*` / `thread-*` / `reaction-*` / `emoji-*` / `create-channel-modal` selector contract so CUA/Playwright can drive chat at 1280×900.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Delivery | Extend the **zero-build vanilla SPA** (`static/` ES modules) — same stack as MARATHON-16; no bundler |\n| Module split | New `static/js/chat_ui.js` owns channel switch, create modal, message pane, thread panel, reactions; `shell.js` exposes active workspace/channel + list refresh hooks; reuse `api.js` / `storage.js` |\n| Data path | **REST only** for this task (list/post/patch/delete/replies/reactions). No WebSocket live fan-out (MARATHON-13). After each successful mutation, update local DOM from the response envelope; on channel select, `GET` history |\n| Channel create | Modal `create-channel-modal` → `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels`; append sidebar row on 201; 409 → inline duplicate-name error |\n| Channel switch | Click sidebar row → set `activeChannel`, render header + load messages; keep thread panel closed unless opened on a message |\n| Empty states | Distinct non-blank copy for (a) no channel selected, (b) channel selected with zero messages |\n| Message chrome | Hover toolbar on own rows for edit/delete; react + reply available on all visible rows the caller can write |\n| Reactions | Fixed emoji **grid** in a popover (`emoji-picker`); toggle via POST/DELETE; badges show emoji + count |\n| Threads | Open `thread-panel` for a top-level parent; list replies oldest-first; composer posts with `parent_id`; bump parent `reply_count` UI |\n| Selectors | Exact `data-testid` strings below; required DOM **id** `create-channel-modal`; keep M16 shell testids intact |\n| M18 coexistence | Message-pane header includes `channel-settings-btn` mount (visible when non-DM active). Click dispatches `huddle:open-channel-settings` CustomEvent (detail `{channelId}`) or calls optional `ctx.openChannelSettings?.(id)` — M18 wires the handler; M17 must not open settings itself |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic + task require chat UX with stable selectors; M16 explicitly deferred composer/threads/reactions/create-channel here; M7/M8 APIs are closed.\n- REST-only avoids coupling to MARATHON-13 (still in review) while still meeting “survive hard reload” (SQLite-backed messages reload on GET).\n- Vanilla modules preserve `start.sh` / no-Node ops and match M16/M18.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Wait for WebSocket (M13) before SPA chat | Blocks P1 UX; REST already durable; live sync can layer later |\n| `window.prompt()` for emoji | Explicitly forbidden by task; graders look for grid picker |\n| Nested reply-to-reply UI | Server rejects deep `parent_id` (M8); one-level panel only |\n| Auto-select `#general` on workspace enter | Acceptable enhancement, but not required; placeholder “Select a channel” already in M16 — **prefer auto-select first non-DM channel (usually general)** for CUA speed; document as required behavior |\n| React/Vite chat island | Diverges from M16 zero-build convention |\n| Invent new message envelopes | Would break M8 graders and parallel agents |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nWithout M13, other users’ messages appear only after **manual channel re-select or soft refresh** (re-GET). Hard reload of the page restores history from REST. That is acceptable for this task’s acceptance bar; live fan-out is a follow-up when M13 ships.\n\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\n\nFrom **MARATHON-16**: vanilla SPA; `api()` + bearer; `{error:{code,message}}`; `hidden` for unused chrome; hash `#/w/{slug}`; token keys `huddle.token` (+fallbacks); channel rows already expose `data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name`; `#` prefix display for non-DM; `thread-panel` starts hidden.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-7**: `ChannelObj` keys `{id,workspace_id,name,is_private,is_dm,topic,is_archived}`; create `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` body `{name, is_private?, topic?}`; name regex `^[a-z0-9-]{2,32}$`; **409** `conflict` on duplicate name; guests cannot create; only owner/admin create private.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-8**: `MessageObj` keys exactly  \n`{id, channel_id, author_id, author, body, parent_id, reply_count, created_at, edited_at, files, reactions, mentions}`  \n(no `seq`); `ReactionObj` `{emoji, count, user_ids}`; POST/GET channel messages; PATCH/DELETE message; GET replies; POST/DELETE reactions; empty body → **400**; archived writes → **423**; list newest-first top-level only; replies oldest-first.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-18** (sibling design): shared `activeChannel`; `channel-settings-btn` in message-pane header; settings must not require composer — M17 provides header chrome + event hook.\n\nFrom **MARATHON-3/4**: nested `author` is `UserObj` (`id, username, display_name, timezone, avatar_url, status_text, status_emoji`).\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\n\nProduct “frontend hooks” are not checked into this repo; the tables below are **normative** for this task. All names are **`data-testid` values** unless marked as DOM `id`. Elements must exist in the DOM when the corresponding UI is shown (not only as JS string constants). Prefer exactly these strings — no prefixes.\n\n#### Required DOM id\n\n| `id` | Element |\n|------|---------|\n| `create-channel-modal` | Create-channel overlay/dialog root |\n\nAlso set `data-testid=\"create-channel-modal\"` on the same node (either selector style works).\n\n#### Channels — list / create / header\n\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\n|---------------|--------------|------|\n| `channel-list` | Shell (M16) | Non-DM channel container (unchanged) |\n| `dms-list` | Shell (M16) | DM container (unchanged); switching DMs uses same message pane |\n| `channel-create-btn` | Shell with workspace | Opens create-channel modal |\n| `create-channel-modal` | Modal open (and present in DOM when closed+hidden) | Dialog root |\n| `create-channel-name` | Modal | Name `<input>` (kebab, no `#`) |\n| `create-channel-private` | Modal | Optional checkbox/toggle for `is_private` |\n| `create-channel-topic` | Modal | Optional topic input |\n| `create-channel-submit` | Modal | Submit |\n| `create-channel-error` | Modal | Visible validation / 409 / 403 text |\n| `create-channel-close` | Modal | Dismiss |\n| `channel-header` | Channel selected | Message-pane header chrome |\n| `channel-name` | Channel selected | Display name with `#` for non-DM (or DM peer label) |\n| `channel-topic` | Channel selected | Topic text (may be empty string rendered as muted “No topic” — still non-blank node text) |\n| `channel-settings-btn` | Non-DM channel selected | Settings entry for M18 (see coexistence) |\n| `empty-channel` | Selected channel with **zero** messages | Non-blank empty copy (e.g. “No messages yet”) |\n| `message-pane-placeholder` | Shell with **no** channel selected | Non-blank “Select a channel” (may reuse M16 placeholder; give it this testid) |\n\nEach channel row button **must** keep `data-channel-id=\"{id}\"` and `data-channel-name=\"{name}\"` (name **without** `#`). Active row: add class `is-active` (or `aria-current=\"true\"`).\n\n**Negative:** Display must **not** store `#` inside `data-channel-name` or create-channel payload `name`.\n\n#### Messages — list / composer / row / toolbar\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `message-pane` | Main pane (M16; unchanged id) |\n| `message-list` | Scrollable list of top-level messages |\n| `message-item` | One top-level message row (repeatable) |\n| `message-avatar` | Avatar image or initials element |\n| `message-author` | Author display name (fallback username) |\n| `message-timestamp` | Human-readable time |\n| `message-body` | Message text body |\n| `message-edited` | Visible only when `edited_at != null` (e.g. “Edited”) |\n| `message-toolbar` | Hover/focus toolbar on a row |\n| `message-edit-btn` | Start inline edit (author only) |\n| `message-delete-btn` | Delete (author or workspace owner — hide if neither) |\n| `message-reply-btn` | Open thread panel for this message |\n| `message-react-btn` | Open emoji picker for this message |\n| `message-edit-input` | Inline edit textarea/input when editing |\n| `message-edit-save` | Save edit |\n| `message-edit-cancel` | Cancel edit |\n| `message-composer` | Composer region for channel (top-level) |\n| `message-input` | Composer textarea/input |\n| `message-submit` | Post button |\n| `message-error` | Visible empty-body / 400 / 423 / network error |\n\nEach `message-item` **must** expose `data-message-id=\"{id}\"`.\n\n#### Threads\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `thread-panel` | Right panel (M16; unhide when open) |\n| `thread-header` | Panel header (parent preview / title) |\n| `thread-close` | Close panel |\n| `thread-reply-count` | Shows `N replies` (or `N reply`) from parent `reply_count` |\n| `thread-list` | Reply list container |\n| `thread-item` | One reply row (same inner author/body/timestamp pattern; may reuse `message-*` child testids) |\n| `thread-composer` | Reply composer |\n| `thread-input` | Reply input |\n| `thread-submit` | Post reply |\n| `thread-error` | Reply validation / API error |\n\nEach `thread-item` **must** expose `data-message-id=\"{id}\"`.\n\n#### Reactions / emoji\n\n| `data-testid` | Role |\n|---------------|------|\n| `reaction-list` | Container of reaction badges on a message |\n| `reaction-badge` | One emoji+count badge (repeatable) |\n| `emoji-picker` | Grid popover/panel (never `prompt`) |\n| `emoji-option` | Clickable emoji cell in the grid (repeatable) |\n\nEach `reaction-badge` **must** expose `data-emoji=\"{emoji}\"` (exact server string).  \nEach `emoji-option` **must** expose `data-emoji=\"{emoji}\"`.\n\n**Negative:** Must **not** call `window.prompt`, `window.confirm` for emoji choice (confirm OK for delete).\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Bearer; body `{name, is_private?: bool, topic?: string}`. Client trims name; strips a leading `#` if the user typed one before send; validates non-empty locally. Disable submit in flight. **201** `{channel}` → append to `channel-list`, close modal, select new channel. **409** → show server `error.message` (or “Channel name already taken”) in `create-channel-error`. **400** → show validation message. **403** → permission error. **401** → M16 logout. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-7). |\n\n**Slow:** keep modal open; do not clear fields.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages?limit=&before=`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On channel select: GET with default limit (omit or `limit=50`). Render **newest-first from server** in `message-list` such that the **latest message is visually nearest the composer** (typical chat: reverse flex / scroll-to-bottom — implementer choice, but latest must be visible without hunting). While slow: show prior list or a non-blocking loading state; do not blank the header. **200** `{messages}` → replace list; if empty show `empty-channel`. **403/404** → show `message-error` and clear list. **401** → logout. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-8). Top-level only, non-deleted, newest-first. |\n\n**Pagination:** Initial page only is required for acceptance. Optional “Load older” using `before={oldest_id}` is nice-to-have, not required.\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/messages`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Top-level: body `{body}` from `message-input` (trim). Empty/whitespace → **do not** call API; show `message-error` (“Message cannot be empty”). Disable submit in flight. **201** `{message}` → append/prepend into list per display order; clear input; hide `empty-channel`. Thread reply: same with `{body, parent_id}`; append to `thread-list`; increment visible parent `reply_count` / `thread-reply-count`. **400** → show server message. **423** → archived lock copy in `message-error` / `thread-error`. **403** → not a member. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-8). |\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `PATCH /api/messages/{id}` / `DELETE /api/messages/{id}`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client PATCH** | Author only controls. Body `{body}`; empty → local validation same as post. **200** → replace row body; show `message-edited` from `edited_at`. **409** → remove row / treat deleted. **403** → hide edit. |\n| **Client DELETE** | Confirm via `window.confirm` OK. Author or workspace owner (client may approximate: show delete if `author_id === me` OR caller is workspace owner from cached workspace `owner_id`). **200** `{deleted:true}` → remove row from list/thread; if parent deleted while thread open, close thread. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-8). |\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/messages/{parent_id}/replies`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | On open thread: GET replies; render oldest-first in `thread-list`. Header shows parent body + `thread-reply-count`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged. Envelope key is **`replies`** (not `messages`). |\n\n---\n\n### Seam: SPA ↔ reactions\n\n#### `POST /api/messages/{id}/reactions` `{ \"emoji\": \"👍\" }` → `200 { \"reactions\": [ReactionObj] }`\n\n#### `DELETE /api/messages/{id}/reactions/{emoji}` → `200 { \"reactions\": [...] }`\n\n| Side | Responsibility |\n|------|----------------|\n| **Client** | Opening `emoji-picker` from `message-react-btn` shows a **fixed grid** of at least **8** emoji options (normative starter set: 👍 ❤️ 😂 😮 😢 🎉 ✅ 👀). Choosing an option POSTs that emoji. Clicking an existing `reaction-badge` where `user_ids` contains me → DELETE; else → POST. Replace `reaction-list` from response. Encode emoji in DELETE URL path (`encodeURIComponent`). Never use `prompt()`. |\n| **Server** | Unchanged (idempotent). |\n\n**Slow:** keep prior badges; disable picker options in flight for that message.\n\n---\n\n### HTTP client rules\n\nReuse MARATHON-16 `api()`: JSON, bearer, timeout, envelope parse, 401 → `onUnauthorized`. Do not invent cookies or alternate base URLs.\n\n### Ownership at the FE/BE seam\n\n| Behavior | Owner |\n|----------|-------|\n| Channel name uniqueness, kebab validation, topic max | **Server** (client may pre-check kebab + local duplicate for UX) |\n| Empty message body | **Both**: client blocks empty; server still 400 if bypassed |\n| Soft-delete visibility | **Server** omits from GET; client removes on DELETE 200 |\n| Reaction aggregation | **Server** returns full `reactions` array; client only renders |\n| Human-readable timestamps | **Client** (`Intl.DateTimeFormat` or equivalent from `created_at` UTC Z) |\n| Avatar URL missing | **Client** shows initials from `display_name` or `username` |\n| Live multi-tab / multi-user sync | **Out of scope** (M13) |\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Browser / in-memory (no SQLite migration)\n\n| Field | Type | Notes |\n|-------|------|-------|\n| `activeChannel` | `ChannelObj \\| null` | Shared with M18 |\n| `messagesByChannelId` | `Map<id, MessageObj[]>` | Optional cache; invalidate on select or always refetch |\n| `openThreadParentId` | `string \\| null` | When thread panel open |\n| `emojiPickerMessageId` | `string \\| null` | Which message owns open picker |\n\n### Server schema\n\n**No schema changes.** Consume M7 `ChannelObj` and M8 `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` as shipped.\n\n### Entity shapes (normative for SPA)\n\n```json\n// ChannelObj (unchanged)\n{ \"id\": \"…\", \"workspace_id\": \"…\", \"name\": \"eng\", \"is_private\": false, \"is_dm\": false, \"topic\": \"Ship week\", \"is_archived\": false }\n\n// MessageObj (unchanged keys)\n{\n  \"id\": \"…\",\n  \"channel_id\": \"…\",\n  \"author_id\": \"…\",\n  \"author\": { \"id\": \"…\", \"username\": \"ada\", \"display_name\": \"Ada\", \"timezone\": null, \"avatar_url\": null, \"status_text\": null, \"status_emoji\": null },\n  \"body\": \"hello\",\n  \"parent_id\": null,\n  \"reply_count\": 0,\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"edited_at\": null,\n  \"files\": [],\n  \"reactions\": [{ \"emoji\": \"👍\", \"count\": 1, \"user_ids\": [\"…\"] }],\n  \"mentions\": []\n}\n```\n\n**Backward compatible:** additive UI only; no API version bump.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/js/chat_ui.js` | Channel select handler integration API, create-channel modal controller, message list/composer/edit/delete, thread panel, emoji picker + reaction badges; export `initChatUi(ctx)` |\n| `tests/test_spa_chat.py` | TestClient: HTML contains required chat testids / `create-channel-modal` id; static JS references key API paths (`/messages`, `/reactions`, `/channels`); assert source does **not** contain `window.prompt` for emoji |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `static/index.html` | Create-channel modal markup; message-pane header + list + composer slots; thread-panel structure (close, list, composer); emoji-picker container (can be single reused popover); all required testids |\n| `static/css/app.css` | Header, message rows, hover toolbar, empty states, thread panel layout, emoji grid, reaction badges — fit **1280×900**; preserve sidebar colour language from M16 |\n| `static/js/shell.js` | Wire channel row clicks to `setActiveChannel`; expose `getWorkspace`, `getActiveChannel`, `setActiveChannel`, `getChannels`, `refreshChannels` / re-render list helpers; mount `channel-create-btn`; on workspace show, **auto-select** first non-DM channel if none active; keep `data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name`; `#` prefix display |\n| `static/js/app.js` | `initChatUi({ getToken, getUser, shell, onUnauthorized })` after shell init |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | Keep existing required testids green; do not remove M16 selectors |\n\n### Do not modify\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/messages/**`, `server/channels/**`, `server/workspaces/**` | Contracts already ship; SPA consumes |\n| `server/db.py` / migrations | No schema change |\n| `start.sh` | No build step |\n| Settings modals / invitation UI | MARATHON-18 |\n| WebSocket client | MARATHON-13 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Build order within this task\n\n1. HTML slots + CSS + testids (unblocks selector tests).\n2. Channel select + header + empty states + auto-select general.\n3. Create-channel modal → POST create → sidebar append.\n4. Message list GET + composer POST + empty validation.\n5. Hover toolbar edit/delete + edited indicator.\n6. Thread panel open/close + replies GET/POST + reply_count bump.\n7. Emoji picker + reaction badges toggle.\n\n### Parallelism\n\n- Fully parallel with MARATHON-18 **if** both respect shared `activeChannel` + header `channel-settings-btn` / CustomEvent contract.\n- Independent of MARATHON-13/14/15; no live sync required.\n- Blocked only on closed M16 shell + M7/M8 APIs (already closed).\n\n### Seams this task owns\n\n| Contract | Consumer |\n|----------|----------|\n| Chat `data-testid` set + `create-channel-modal` | QA / CUA |\n| `initChatUi` / active channel selection | MARATHON-18 settings button enablement |\n| `huddle:open-channel-settings` event (or ctx callback) | MARATHON-18 |\n| REST consumption of M7 create + M8 messages/reactions | Implementer |\n\n### Seams owned elsewhere\n\n| Contract | Owner |\n|----------|-------|\n| `ChannelObj` / create channel API | MARATHON-7 |\n| `MessageObj` / reactions API | MARATHON-8 |\n| Auth token + shell layout | MARATHON-16 |\n| Workspace/channel settings modals | MARATHON-18 |\n| WS resume / dense seq live updates | MARATHON-13 |\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not create unless lead asks)\n\n- Wire chat UI to MARATHON-13 WS events for live append/patch without refresh.\n- Infinite scroll / jump-to-date.\n- Slash-command autocomplete UI (MARATHON-11 server).\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\n| Item | File / pattern | Why excluded |\n|------|----------------|--------------|\n| Workspace/channel settings modals | `settings_ui.js`, M18 testids | MARATHON-18 |\n| WebSocket subscribe/resume | `/api/ws` | MARATHON-13 |\n| File attach in composer | `file_ids`, MARATHON-10 | Non-empty file_ids still 400 |\n| Search / slash / read receipts UI | MARATHON-11 | Different task |\n| Pins UI | pin routes exist | Not in this task description |\n| DM create UX | MARATHON-9 API exists; list already split — creating new DMs not required here |\n| IRC | MARATHON-15 | Unrelated |\n| Changing REST envelopes / schema | `server/**` | Frontend-only |\n\n**Neighborhood scan account:**\n\n| Hit | Disposition |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `static/index.html`, `shell.js`, `app.js`, `app.css` | **In scope** — extend |\n| `static/js/api.js`, `storage.js`, `auth_ui.js` | **Reuse** — no contract change |\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` | **Keep green**; chat selectors in new test file |\n| `server/messages/**`, `server/channels/**`, create channel route | **Consume only** |\n| `tests/test_messages.py`, `test_channels.py` | **Out of scope** to rewrite; must stay green |\n| Grep `create-channel` / `emoji-picker` / `message-composer` in `static/` | No hits yet — greenfield UI |\n| Frontend-dev M18 WIP adding `channel-settings-btn` / message-pane header | **Coordinate** via shared header testids; do not delete settings hooks if already merged |\n| M16 placeholder “Select a channel” | **Replace/retag** as `message-pane-placeholder` / `empty-channel` per states |\n| M8 `prompt` mention in older notes | N/A — SPA must use grid |\n\nIf nothing else: neighborhood scan found M18 settings WIP and M13 WS as siblings — both explicitly out of scope above.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Case | Expected behavior |\n|------|-------------------|\n| Create name `Eng` / `eng_ops` / `e` / empty | Client and/or server **400**; show `create-channel-error` |\n| Create duplicate `general` | **409**; visible duplicate-name error; modal stays open |\n| User types `#eng` in create field | Strip `#` before POST; send `eng` |\n| Select archived channel | Allow **read** history; composer disabled + `message-error` explains archived (POST would 423) |\n| Empty message submit | No API call; `message-error` visible |\n| Edit then empty save | Same local validation; no PATCH |\n| Delete message with open thread | Close thread if parent deleted; if reply deleted, remove from thread-list and decrement count |\n| Reaction on deleted message | **409** → refresh/remove row |\n| Non-member viewing public channel | GET may succeed (M8 public read); POST → **403** → show error; hide composer if known non-member (optional: try and surface error) |\n| Guest creating channel | **403** in `create-channel-error` |\n| Hard reload after posts | Token restores workspace (M16); auto-select channel; GET messages shows prior posts |\n| `avatar_url` null | Initials avatar; `message-avatar` still present |\n| `display_name` null/empty | Show `username` in `message-author` |\n| Timestamp | Parse `created_at` as UTC; display local human-readable (date + time or relative); full ISO may be `title` tooltip |\n| Thread on message with `reply_count=0` | Panel still opens; empty `thread-list` + composer |\n| Emoji picker open + click outside / Escape | Close picker |\n| Double-click channel | Idempotent re-select; avoid duplicate in-flight GETs (abort or ignore stale) |\n| Network timeout | `api()` timeout → show `message-error` / modal error with failure text; keep prior data |\n| `window.prompt` | **Must not** be used for emoji or channel name |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Authenticated workspace shell lists channels with `#` prefix for non-DM; each row has `data-channel-id` and `data-channel-name` (no `#` in data attribute).\n2. Clicking a channel shows `channel-header` with `channel-name` and `channel-topic`; message pane leaves the generic “Select a channel” state.\n3. Empty channel shows non-blank `empty-channel` copy (not a white void).\n4. `channel-create-btn` opens `create-channel-modal`; valid create calls `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels` and adds the channel to `channel-list`; selecting it works.\n5. Duplicate channel name shows visible error in `create-channel-error` and does **not** add a duplicate row.\n6. Composer posts via `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages`; new message appears as `message-item` with avatar, author, human-readable timestamp, and body.\n7. Empty composer submit shows `message-error` and does **not** create a server message.\n8. Hover/focus toolbar allows author to edit; after save, `message-edited` is visible and body updates; hard reload + re-open channel still shows edited body from server.\n9. Author (or owner) can delete via toolbar; message disappears from the list.\n10. `message-reply-btn` opens `thread-panel` (unhidden); replies load; posting a reply increments `thread-reply-count` / parent reply affordance.\n11. `message-react-btn` opens `emoji-picker` grid with `emoji-option` cells; choosing one creates a `reaction-badge` with count; clicking badge toggles caller’s reaction; **no** `prompt()`.\n12. Required testids in the tables above are present when their UI state is visible; `create-channel-modal` exists as a DOM id.\n13. **Negative:** must **not** require MARATHON-13 WS for the above; must **not** break M16 auth/shell testids; must **not** implement settings modals (M18); must **not** send `#` in channel `name` field; must **not** use `{messages}` as the replies envelope key when calling the API.\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Automated\n\n- Extend/add `tests/test_spa_chat.py` (TestClient):\n  - `GET /` HTML includes `create-channel-modal`, `channel-create-btn`, `message-list`, `message-composer`, `message-input`, `thread-close`, `emoji-picker` (picker may be `hidden`).\n  - `/static/js/chat_ui.js` returns 200 and references `/messages` and `/reactions`.\n  - Source of chat module does not contain `prompt(` for emoji flows.\n- Existing `tests/test_spa_shell.py`, `test_messages.py`, `test_channels.py` remain green.\n\n### Manual / Playwright at 1280×900\n\n1. Register → create workspace → confirm `#general` auto-selected or selectable; header shows name/topic.\n2. Post three messages; reload page; return to channel; all three still present with authors/timestamps.\n3. Edit one message; see edited indicator; reload; persists.\n4. Delete one message; gone after reload.\n5. Open thread; reply; badge/count bumps; close panel.\n6. Add 👍 via emoji grid; count 1; click badge to remove.\n7. Create channel `eng`; appears as `#eng`; create `eng` again → error.\n8. Submit empty message → error; no new row.\n9. Confirm no native prompt dialogs during reaction flow.\n\n### Done when\n\nAcceptance criteria 1–13 hold on a single HTTP node with shared SQLite; suite green; design selectors stable for CUA.\nDESIGN_EOF\nwc -c /tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md\n","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"27426 /tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md\n","stderr":"","executionTime":623,"interleavedOutput":"27426 /tmp/designs/MARATHON-17.md\n","localExecutionTimeMs":29},"isBackground":false},"description":"Write MARATHON-17 design markdown file"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-ab77b936-3762-4119-896b-d66be9dd4115-61\nfc_22680d88-c103-90ee-8f32-e3e02dd0e8ff_0","startedAtMs":"1787447982494","completedAtMs":"1787447983117"},"model_call_id":"03dd848d-d7bd-4877-bfbf-ce6458bc28c6-18-tz0i","session_id":"8d1f97e9-e376-440d-a791-e2992491ec56","timestamp_ms":1787447983150}
