{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-d26bd77c-0242-41d1-a87d-8009a8007904-8\nfc_e94b603a-f8ca-9705-9ec8-9532de70fe7c_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"loom data update --help; loom data show --help 2>&1 | head -80; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\n# Get full JSON for epic and a few key siblings with designs\nfor tid in [\"MARATHON-1\",\"MARATHON-8\",\"MARATHON-3\",\"MARATHON-11\",\"MARATHON-17\",\"MARATHON-13\"]:\n    out=subprocess.check_output([\"loom\",\"data\",\"show\",tid,\"--output\",\"json\"])\n    d=json.loads(out)\n    print(\"====\", tid, \"====\")\n    for k in [\"notes\",\"design\",\"description\",\"labels\",\"status\",\"has_design\",\"design_format\"]:\n        v=d.get(k)\n        if v is None: continue\n        s=str(v)\n        print(f\"{k}: len={len(s)}\")\n        if k in (\"notes\",\"design\") and s:\n            print(s[:3000])\n            if len(s)>3000: print(\"...[truncated]...\")\nPY","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-d26bd77c-0242-41d1-a87d-8009a8007904-8\nfc_e94b603a-f8ca-9705-9ec8-9532de70fe7c_0","simpleCommands":["loom","loom","head","python3"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"update"},{"type":"word","value":"--help"}],"fullText":"loom data update --help"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"--help"}],"fullText":"loom data show --help"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-80"}],"fullText":"head -80"},{"name":"python3","args":[],"fullText":"python3"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">&","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"number","targetText":"1"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"python3"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Inspect epic/sibling design fields","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"27ef4deb-7d8c-45c3-96ef-6099aabacf08","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"loom data update --help; loom data show --help 2>&1 | head -80; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\n# Get full JSON for epic and a few key siblings with designs\nfor tid in [\"MARATHON-1\",\"MARATHON-8\",\"MARATHON-3\",\"MARATHON-11\",\"MARATHON-17\",\"MARATHON-13\"]:\n    out=subprocess.check_output([\"loom\",\"data\",\"show\",tid,\"--output\",\"json\"])\n    d=json.loads(out)\n    print(\"====\", tid, \"====\")\n    for k in [\"notes\",\"design\",\"description\",\"labels\",\"status\",\"has_design\",\"design_format\"]:\n        v=d.get(k)\n        if v is None: continue\n        s=str(v)\n        print(f\"{k}: len={len(s)}\")\n        if k in (\"notes\",\"design\") and s:\n            print(s[:3000])\n            if len(s)>3000: print(\"...[truncated]...\")\nPY","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"Update issue fields\n\nUsage:\n  loom data update <issue-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --add-label stringArray           Add label (repeatable); other labels are preserved\n      --assignee string                 Set assignee\n      --depends-on stringArray          Add dependency on issue ID (repeatable)\n      --description string              Set description\n      --description-from-file string    Read description from file (use - for stdin)\n      --design string                   Set design\n      --design-format string            Set design format (markdown or html)\n  -h, --help                            help for update\n      --notes string                    Set notes\n      --priority int                    Set priority\n      --remove-depends-on stringArray   Remove dependency on issue ID (repeatable)\n      --remove-label stringArray        Remove label (repeatable); other labels are preserved\n      --status string                   Set status\n      --title string                    Set title\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n  -o, --output string       Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string       Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\nShow a single issue by ID (HTTP)\n\nUsage:\n  loom data show <issue-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for show\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n  -o, --output string       Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string       Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\n==== MARATHON-1 ====\ndescription: len=873\nstatus: len=4\nhas_design: len=5\n==== MARATHON-8 ====\nnotes: len=478\nIMPL: Messages/threads/reactions REST shipped. Schema is migration v5 (design text said v4; v4 already used by MARATHON-12 groups/invitations). Additive only — preserved v3 messages. file_ids non-empty → 400 until MARATHON-10; @username mentions only; slash bodies stored literally. Unit tests green (151 excl. live/cluster port-bound); port 8000 held by another agent so live cluster pytest left unrun here — cluster read-after-write covered via dual TestClient sharing sqlite.\ndesign: len=28212\n# MARATHON-8 — Messages, threads, reactions REST API\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task completes the core chat write/read path for Huddle on top of MARATHON-7 channels and the minimal `messages` / pin embed already shipped: authenticated channel members can post top-level messages and one-level thread replies, list channel history (newest-first, cursor pagination) and thread replies (oldest-first), edit their own messages, soft-delete as author or workspace owner, and add/remove emoji reactions. It locks the REST `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` contracts the SPA (MARATHON-17) and downstream search/WS tasks consume, extends schema with reaction (and optional attachment join) tables while **preserving** the v3 `messages` table and pin routes, and leaves slash-command interception, full mention forms, file upload ownership, and dense `seq` fan-out to their owning tasks.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite SoT; **migration version 4** additive: `message_reactions`, optional `message_files`, optional `messages.blocks_json`; **do not** drop/recreate v3 `messages` |\n| Route layout | Channel-scoped on `server/channels/routes.py`: `POST`/`GET /api/channels/{id}/messages`. Message-scoped on existing `server/messages/routes.py`: `PATCH`/`DELETE /{id}`, `GET /{parent_id}/replies`, `POST`/`DELETE .../reactions`, keep existing pin routes |\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all endpoints require Bearer |\n| `MessageObj` | **Same key set as MARATHON-7** (`MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`); enrich `reply_count`, `files`, `reactions`, `mentions` for real data; **no `seq`** on REST objects (product: seq lives on WS frames — MARATHON-13) |\n| Soft delete | Set `deleted_at`; **exclude** deleted rows from channel history and reply lists; DELETE idempotent; PATCH / react on deleted → **409** `conflict` |\n| Archived writes | Reuse `server.channels.store.assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived` for POST message, PATCH, DELETE (mutating), POST/DELETE reaction (same as pin) |\n| Membership for writes | Same as pin mutate: caller must be **channel member**; workspace owner without membership → **403** |\n| Membership for reads | Same as GET pins: public → workspace member else 404; private/DM → channel member else 403 (non-member workspace) / 404 (stranger) |\n| Threads | Single level only: `parent_id` must reference a **top-level** (`parent_id IS NULL`), same-channel, non-deleted message |\n| Reactions | Table unique on `(message_id, user_id, emoji)`; aggregate to `[{emoji, count, user_ids}]`; POST/DELETE idempotent |\n| `file_ids` / `blocks` | Accept on POST for product shape; `blocks` persisted as JSON text (not exposed on `MessageObj` keys); `file_ids` validated against files when present — **non-empty `file_ids` → 400** until MARATHON-10 provides attachable `files` rows (seam documented) |\n| Mentions (this task) | Resolve `@username` only (word-boundary, no mid-word, no self, dedupe, must be workspace member); `@channel`/`@her\n...[truncated]...\ndescription: len=469\nlabels: len=11\nstatus: len=6\nhas_design: len=4\ndesign_format: len=8\n==== MARATHON-3 ====\nnotes: len=335\nAuth API implemented: POST /api/auth/register|login, GET /api/auth/me; SQLite users+auth_tokens (migration v1); scrypt passwords; SHA-256 bearer tokens; error envelope; get_current_user dependency. Tests: tests/test_auth.py (33 suite total green). Cluster verified token across :8000/:8001/:8002. Logout/revoke out of scope per design.\ndesign: len=20666\n# MARATHON-3 — Auth API: register, login, me, bearer tokens\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the first product API surface for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, backed by durable users and bearer tokens in the shared SQLite database so any of the three HTTP nodes accepts the same credential. It locks the canonical `UserObj` JSON shape (consumed by Profiles, Workspaces, and the SPA), the error envelope convention for all later REST routes, and a reusable FastAPI auth dependency that every authenticated endpoint will import.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Durable auth store | **SQLite** at `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` (shared by all nodes) — tables `users` + `auth_tokens` |\n| Token transport | Opaque bearer string in `Authorization: Bearer <token>` |\n| Token persistence | Store **SHA-256 hex** of the token; return plaintext only in register/login responses |\n| Password storage | **stdlib `hashlib.scrypt`** (salt per user); never store plaintext |\n| User / token ids | Stable strings: **UUID4** hex/`str` for `users.id`; tokens identified by hash (no separate public token id) |\n| Route layout | FastAPI `APIRouter` in `server/auth/routes.py` mounted from `server/app.py` under `/api/auth` |\n| Auth dependency | `server/auth/deps.py::get_current_user` for `/me` and for MARATHON-4+ |\n| Schema evolution | Extend MARATHON-2 `schema_migrations`: apply version **1** (users + auth_tokens) idempotently on node lifespan |\n\n### Why\n\n- MARATHON-2 fixed SQLite as SoT and Redis as ephemeral fan-out only. Storing tokens in Redis would break “any node accepts the same token” after Redis `SIGKILL` and contradicts MARATHON-14. Shared SQLite is the only persistence already wired on every node.\n- Opaque bearer tokens match the epic (“REST + bearer auth”) and the SPA task (`localStorage` `huddle.token`) without JWT clock skew or shared signing secrets across processes.\n- Hashing stored tokens limits damage from a DB file read while still allowing constant-time lookup by hashing the presented bearer.\n- `scrypt` via stdlib avoids new native deps (bcrypt/argon2 wheels) on cold `pip install` in `start.sh`.\n- Establishing `UserObj` and the `{ \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\" } }` envelope here prevents Profiles/SPA from inventing competing shapes (MARATHON-2 deferred error envelopes to Auth).\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| JWT / signed tokens | Needs shared secret rotation; harder to revoke; not required by contract |\n| Redis session keys | Not durable across Redis death; wrong SoT |\n| Per-node in-memory tokens | Violates “cluster-wide / any node accepts the same token” |\n| `passlib` / `bcrypt` | Extra dependency; stdlib scrypt is enough for this harness |\n| Email as login identifier | Explicitly forbidden by task |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nMultiple live tokens per user (each register/login mints a new row) simplifies SPA “l\n...[truncated]...\ndescription: len=365\nlabels: len=11\nstatus: len=6\nhas_design: len=4\ndesign_format: len=8\n==== MARATHON-11 ====\nnotes: len=394\nDesign complete for search, slash commands, advanced mentions, and read_state. Grounded in MARATHON-5 ReadStateEntry, MARATHON-7 topic/archive authz, MARATHON-8 MessageObj + composer POST, MARATHON-12 group handles, MARATHON-13 last_read_seq=dense event seq (soft dep for mid-cursor recompute). No new migration (avoids v6 clash). Label remains backend for implementer after architect approval.\ndesign: len=27763\n# MARATHON-11 — Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task completes the discovery and attention seams for Huddle on top of MARATHON-5/7/8/12: authenticated workspace members can full-text search messages they can see (`GET /api/search`), post slash commands through the existing message composer path (`POST /api/channels/{id}/messages`) with message-producing transforms (`/me`, `/shrug`, `//…` escape) and side-effect commands that return `message: null` (`/topic`, `/invite`, `/archive`, `/unarchive`), resolve advanced mentions (`@username`, `@group-handle`, `@channel`, `@here`) into the existing `MessageObj.mentions` user-id array without self-inclusion, and read/advance per-channel `read_state` via `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` using the same `ReadStateEntry` shape already embedded on workspace detail. It does not build SPA search UI, WS badge push, file-content search, or IRC command bridging.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Search route | New package `server/search/` with `GET /api/search?q=&workspace_id=&limit=` mounted from `server/app.py` |\n| Search SoT | Shared SQLite; **case-insensitive substring** match on non-deleted `messages.body` (`LIKE` + `LOWER`); no FTS migration in this task |\n| Slash interception | **Before** `create_message` inside `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages` (and only there — not on PATCH). Parser in `server/messages/slash.py` |\n| Slash escape | Body starting with `//` → strip **one** leading `/`, treat remainder as normal message body (literal slash text) |\n| Side-effect response | Always HTTP **201** with `message: null` plus `channel` and/or `invited_user` as applicable; never insert a message row |\n| Mentions | Extend `resolve_mentions` in `server/messages/store.py`; keep `mentions: string[]` of user ids on `MessageObj` (no new JSON keys) |\n| `@channel` / `@here` | Reserved tokens; never resolved as usernames even if such users exist |\n| Username vs group collision | Same handle string: **username (workspace member) wins**; else expand `user_groups.handle` in that workspace |\n| `@here` without presence | Expand to channel members who currently hold ≥1 `auth_tokens` row (session proxy for “online”); exclude author. If empty set after exclude, mentions gain nothing from `@here` alone |\n| Read APIs | `GET` + `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/read` on `server/channels/routes.py` |\n| `last_read_seq` meaning | Dense per-channel **event seq** from MARATHON-13 (`channel_seq.head_seq` / `channel_events.seq`), **not** message UUID. Cursor **never decreases** |\n| Unread / mention counters | Maintain incrementally on message create; **recompute** on POST read when `channel_events` exists; if M13 tables absent, POST that advances cursor **zeros** both counts (mark-read) |\n| Schema | **No new migration** required (`channel_read_state` already v2). Do **not** claim v6 (owned by MARATHON-13) |\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all endpoints Bearer-requir\n...[truncated]...\ndescription: len=456\nlabels: len=24\nstatus: len=6\nhas_design: len=4\ndesign_format: len=8\n==== MARATHON-17 ====\nnotes: len=386\nDESIGN: SPA chat UX for channels/messages/threads/reactions on M16 shell + M7/M8 REST. Zero-build chat_ui.js; REST-only (no WS/M13); normative channel-*/message-*/thread-*/reaction-*/emoji-* testids + create-channel-modal; emoji grid not prompt(); coexist with M18 via channel-settings-btn + huddle:open-channel-settings. Label remains frontend for implementer after architect approval.\ndesign: len=27259\n# MARATHON-17 — SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\n\n## Summary\n\nFill the MARATHON-16 workspace shell with the core chat UX: channel list selection and create-channel modal (duplicate-name validation, `#`-prefixed display names, `data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name` on rows), channel header (name + topic) with non-blank empty-channel copy, message history with composer (post / hover-toolbar edit+delete, edited indicator, empty-body validation, hard-reload survival via REST), message rows (avatar + author + human-readable timestamp + body), right-hand thread panel that bumps reply counts, and reactions via an in-DOM emoji-picker grid (never `prompt()`) with count badges. This task is **frontend-only** against already-shipped MARATHON-7/8 REST; it locks the epic’s `channel-*` / `message-*` / `thread-*` / `reaction-*` / `emoji-*` / `create-channel-modal` selector contract so CUA/Playwright can drive chat at 1280×900.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Delivery | Extend the **zero-build vanilla SPA** (`static/` ES modules) — same stack as MARATHON-16; no bundler |\n| Module split | New `static/js/chat_ui.js` owns channel switch, create modal, message pane, thread panel, reactions; `shell.js` exposes active workspace/channel + list refresh hooks; reuse `api.js` / `storage.js` |\n| Data path | **REST only** for this task (list/post/patch/delete/replies/reactions). No WebSocket live fan-out (MARATHON-13). After each successful mutation, update local DOM from the response envelope; on channel select, `GET` history |\n| Channel create | Modal `create-channel-modal` → `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels`; append sidebar row on 201; 409 → inline duplicate-name error |\n| Channel switch | Click sidebar row → set `activeChannel`, render header + load messages; keep thread panel closed unless opened on a message |\n| Empty states | Distinct non-blank copy for (a) no channel selected, (b) channel selected with zero messages |\n| Message chrome | Hover toolbar on own rows for edit/delete; react + reply available on all visible rows the caller can write |\n| Reactions | Fixed emoji **grid** in a popover (`emoji-picker`); toggle via POST/DELETE; badges show emoji + count |\n| Threads | Open `thread-panel` for a top-level parent; list replies oldest-first; composer posts with `parent_id`; bump parent `reply_count` UI |\n| Selectors | Exact `data-testid` strings below; required DOM **id** `create-channel-modal`; keep M16 shell testids intact |\n| M18 coexistence | Message-pane header includes `channel-settings-btn` mount (visible when non-DM active). Click dispatches `huddle:open-channel-settings` CustomEvent (detail `{channelId}`) or calls optional `ctx.openChannelSettings?.(id)` — M18 wires the handler; M17 must not open settings itself |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic + task require chat UX with stable selectors; M16 explicitly deferred composer/threads/reactions/create-channel here; M7/M8 APIs are closed.\n- REST-only avoids coup\n...[truncated]...\ndescription: len=572\nlabels: len=25\nstatus: len=6\nhas_design: len=4\ndesign_format: len=8\n==== MARATHON-13 ====\nnotes: len=404\nDesign complete for WS subscribe/resume + dense channel seq. Key decisions: SQLite channel_seq/channel_events (v6) as SoT; seq allocated in same txn as mutation; /api/ws?token=; subscribe=live only, resume=replay or resume.gap; user.updated global no seq; Redis fan-out deferred to MARATHON-14 (local hub + catch-up on any node via resume). Label remains backend for implementer after architect approval.\ndesign: len=27570\n# MARATHON-13 — WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the real-time seam for Huddle: an authenticated WebSocket at `GET /api/ws?token=…`, client `subscribe` / `resume` control frames, and a **dense per-channel `seq`** assigned in shared SQLite so every durable channel mutation (messages including thread replies, reactions, membership, channel mutations, pins) gets a gap-free monotonic frame `{type, seq, channel_id, …}`. Profile changes keep the existing channel-less `user.updated` shape (no `seq`). Same `seq` / event rows are visible from every HTTP node via the shared DB; **live cross-node push** remains MARATHON-14 (this task delivers live frames to connections on the writing node and makes catch-up via `resume` work on any node).\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Seq SoT | **Shared SQLite** counters + durable `channel_events` log (not Redis). Allocation is in the **same transaction** as the HTTP mutation so rollbacks never burn a seq. |\n| Dense rule | Per `channel_id`, `seq` starts at **0** (empty) and first durable event is **1**, then `+1` per committed durable event. No gaps, no duplicates, no reuse. |\n| WS transport | FastAPI/Starlette WebSocket on **`/api/ws`**, auth via query `token` (raw bearer, same value as `Authorization: Bearer`). |\n| Control protocol | Client JSON: `subscribe`, `resume` (with `since_seq`). Server JSON: `subscribed`, `resumed`, `resume.gap`, plus durable/live event frames and `user.updated`. |\n| History vs live | `subscribe` = watch from **now** (ack `head_seq`, no backlog). `resume` = authorize + **replay** `(since_seq+1)…head` then live, or `resume.gap` if `since_seq` is older than the retained tail. Channel history UI still uses REST (MARATHON-8). |\n| Retention | Keep the last **`CHANNEL_EVENT_RETAIN = 10_000`** events per channel (constant in code). After append, prune `seq < head_seq - RETAIN + 1`. Tail = minimum retained `seq` (or `1` if none pruned yet / empty head). |\n| Local delivery | Process-local **connection hub** on each node. `emit` records to SQLite; **after commit** `deliver(frame)` fans to local WS subscribers. Redis publish is a **no-op stub hook** owned by MARATHON-14. |\n| Cross-node live | **Out of scope** (MARATHON-14). Reconnect-to-other-node **replay** works in this task because resume reads SQLite. |\n| REST objects | **Do not** add `seq` to `MessageObj` / `ChannelObj` / `UserObj` (MARATHON-8/4 locks). |\n| Thread replies | Same frame type `message.created`; “reply” is `message.parent_id != null` inside the nested `MessageObj` (no separate `reply.*` type). |\n| Publish call sites | Refactor existing post-commit `publish_*` so **seq append happens inside the open write transaction**; hub deliver stays post-commit and must not raise. |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic + MARATHON-2 forbid Redis as SoT (Redis `SIGKILL` must not break dense seq). Shared SQLite is already the cluster SoT.\n- MARATHON-8/4 already froze event *shapes*\n...[truncated]...\ndescription: len=499\nlabels: len=24\nstatus: len=6\nhas_design: len=4\ndesign_format: len=8\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-23T01:22:25.491Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:22:25.535Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:22:25.550Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:22:25.563Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:22:25.578Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:22:25.593Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n","executionTime":243,"interleavedOutput":"Update issue fields\n\nUsage:\n  loom data update <issue-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --add-label stringArray           Add label (repeatable); other labels are preserved\n      --assignee string                 Set assignee\n      --depends-on stringArray          Add dependency on issue ID (repeatable)\n      --description string              Set description\n      --description-from-file string    Read description from file (use - for stdin)\n      --design string                   Set design\n      --design-format string            Set design format (markdown or html)\n  -h, --help                            help for update\n      --notes string                    Set notes\n      --priority int                    Set priority\n      --remove-depends-on stringArray   Remove dependency on issue ID (repeatable)\n      --remove-label stringArray        Remove label (repeatable); other labels are preserved\n      --status string                   Set status\n      --title string                    Set title\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n  -o, --output string       Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string       Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\nShow a single issue by ID (HTTP)\n\nUsage:\n  loom data show <issue-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for show\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n  -o, --output string       Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string       Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\ntime=2026-08-23T01:22:25.491Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:22:25.535Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:22:25.550Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:22:25.563Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n==== MARATHON-1 ====\ndescription: len=873\nstatus: len=4\nhas_design: len=5\n==== MARATHON-8 ====\nnotes: len=478\nIMPL: Messages/threads/reactions REST shipped. Schema is migration v5 (design text said v4; v4 already used by MARATHON-12 groups/invitations). Additive only — preserved v3 messages. file_ids non-empty → 400 until MARATHON-10; @username mentions only; slash bodies stored literally. Unit tests green (151 excl. live/cluster port-bound); port 8000 held by another agent so live cluster pytest left unrun here — cluster read-after-write covered via dual TestClient sharing sqlite.\ndesign: len=28212\n# MARATHON-8 — Messages, threads, reactions REST API\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task completes the core chat write/read path for Huddle on top of MARATHON-7 channels and the minimal `messages` / pin embed already shipped: authenticated channel members can post top-level messages and one-level thread replies, list channel history (newest-first, cursor pagination) and thread replies (oldest-first), edit their own messages, soft-delete as author or workspace owner, and add/remove emoji reactions. It locks the REST `MessageObj` / `ReactionObj` contracts the SPA (MARATHON-17) and downstream search/WS tasks consume, extends schema with reaction (and optional attachment join) tables while **preserving** the v3 `messages` table and pin routes, and leaves slash-command interception, full mention forms, file upload ownership, and dense `seq` fan-out to their owning tasks.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite SoT; **migration version 4** additive: `message_reactions`, optional `message_files`, optional `messages.blocks_json`; **do not** drop/recreate v3 `messages` |\n| Route layout | Channel-scoped on `server/channels/routes.py`: `POST`/`GET /api/channels/{id}/messages`. Message-scoped on existing `server/messages/routes.py`: `PATCH`/`DELETE /{id}`, `GET /{parent_id}/replies`, `POST`/`DELETE .../reactions`, keep existing pin routes |\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all endpoints require Bearer |\n| `MessageObj` | **Same key set as MARATHON-7** (`MESSAGE_OBJ_KEYS`); enrich `reply_count`, `files`, `reactions`, `mentions` for real data; **no `seq`** on REST objects (product: seq lives on WS frames — MARATHON-13) |\n| Soft delete | Set `deleted_at`; **exclude** deleted rows from channel history and reply lists; DELETE idempotent; PATCH / react on deleted → **409** `conflict` |\n| Archived writes | Reuse `server.channels.store.assert_channel_writable` → **423** `archived` for POST message, PATCH, DELETE (mutating), POST/DELETE reaction (same as pin) |\n| Membership for writes | Same as pin mutate: caller must be **channel member**; workspace owner without membership → **403** |\n| Membership for reads | Same as GET pins: public → workspace member else 404; private/DM → channel member else 403 (non-member workspace) / 404 (stranger) |\n| Threads | Single level only: `parent_id` must reference a **top-level** (`parent_id IS NULL`), same-channel, non-deleted message |\n| Reactions | Table unique on `(message_id, user_id, emoji)`; aggregate to `[{emoji, count, user_ids}]`; POST/DELETE idempotent |\n| `file_ids` / `blocks` | Accept on POST for product shape; `blocks` persisted as JSON text (not exposed on `MessageObj` keys); `file_ids` validated against files when present — **non-empty `file_ids` → 400** until MARATHON-10 provides attachable `files` rows (seam documented) |\n| Mentions (this task) | Resolve `@username` only (word-boundary, no mid-word, no self, dedupe, must be workspace member); `@channel`/`@her\n...[truncated]...\ndescription: len=469\nlabels: len=11\nstatus: len=6\nhas_design: len=4\ndesign_format: len=8\n==== MARATHON-3 ====\nnotes: len=335\nAuth API implemented: POST /api/auth/register|login, GET /api/auth/me; SQLite users+auth_tokens (migration v1); scrypt passwords; SHA-256 bearer tokens; error envelope; get_current_user dependency. Tests: tests/test_auth.py (33 suite total green). Cluster verified token across :8000/:8001/:8002. Logout/revoke out of scope per design.\ndesign: len=20666\n# MARATHON-3 — Auth API: register, login, me, bearer tokens\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the first product API surface for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, backed by durable users and bearer tokens in the shared SQLite database so any of the three HTTP nodes accepts the same credential. It locks the canonical `UserObj` JSON shape (consumed by Profiles, Workspaces, and the SPA), the error envelope convention for all later REST routes, and a reusable FastAPI auth dependency that every authenticated endpoint will import.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Durable auth store | **SQLite** at `/app/data/huddle.sqlite` (shared by all nodes) — tables `users` + `auth_tokens` |\n| Token transport | Opaque bearer string in `Authorization: Bearer <token>` |\n| Token persistence | Store **SHA-256 hex** of the token; return plaintext only in register/login responses |\n| Password storage | **stdlib `hashlib.scrypt`** (salt per user); never store plaintext |\n| User / token ids | Stable strings: **UUID4** hex/`str` for `users.id`; tokens identified by hash (no separate public token id) |\n| Route layout | FastAPI `APIRouter` in `server/auth/routes.py` mounted from `server/app.py` under `/api/auth` |\n| Auth dependency | `server/auth/deps.py::get_current_user` for `/me` and for MARATHON-4+ |\n| Schema evolution | Extend MARATHON-2 `schema_migrations`: apply version **1** (users + auth_tokens) idempotently on node lifespan |\n\n### Why\n\n- MARATHON-2 fixed SQLite as SoT and Redis as ephemeral fan-out only. Storing tokens in Redis would break “any node accepts the same token” after Redis `SIGKILL` and contradicts MARATHON-14. Shared SQLite is the only persistence already wired on every node.\n- Opaque bearer tokens match the epic (“REST + bearer auth”) and the SPA task (`localStorage` `huddle.token`) without JWT clock skew or shared signing secrets across processes.\n- Hashing stored tokens limits damage from a DB file read while still allowing constant-time lookup by hashing the presented bearer.\n- `scrypt` via stdlib avoids new native deps (bcrypt/argon2 wheels) on cold `pip install` in `start.sh`.\n- Establishing `UserObj` and the `{ \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\" } }` envelope here prevents Profiles/SPA from inventing competing shapes (MARATHON-2 deferred error envelopes to Auth).\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| JWT / signed tokens | Needs shared secret rotation; harder to revoke; not required by contract |\n| Redis session keys | Not durable across Redis death; wrong SoT |\n| Per-node in-memory tokens | Violates “cluster-wide / any node accepts the same token” |\n| `passlib` / `bcrypt` | Extra dependency; stdlib scrypt is enough for this harness |\n| Email as login identifier | Explicitly forbidden by task |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nMultiple live tokens per user (each register/login mints a new row) simplifies SPA “l\n...[truncated]...\ndescription: len=365\nlabels: len=11\nstatus: len=6\nhas_design: len=4\ndesign_format: len=8\n==== MARATHON-11 ====\nnotes: len=394\nDesign complete for search, slash commands, advanced mentions, and read_state. Grounded in MARATHON-5 ReadStateEntry, MARATHON-7 topic/archive authz, MARATHON-8 MessageObj + composer POST, MARATHON-12 group handles, MARATHON-13 last_read_seq=dense event seq (soft dep for mid-cursor recompute). No new migration (avoids v6 clash). Label remains backend for implementer after architect approval.\ndesign: len=27763\n# MARATHON-11 — Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task completes the discovery and attention seams for Huddle on top of MARATHON-5/7/8/12: authenticated workspace members can full-text search messages they can see (`GET /api/search`), post slash commands through the existing message composer path (`POST /api/channels/{id}/messages`) with message-producing transforms (`/me`, `/shrug`, `//…` escape) and side-effect commands that return `message: null` (`/topic`, `/invite`, `/archive`, `/unarchive`), resolve advanced mentions (`@username`, `@group-handle`, `@channel`, `@here`) into the existing `MessageObj.mentions` user-id array without self-inclusion, and read/advance per-channel `read_state` via `GET/POST /api/channels/{id}/read` using the same `ReadStateEntry` shape already embedded on workspace detail. It does not build SPA search UI, WS badge push, file-content search, or IRC command bridging.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Search route | New package `server/search/` with `GET /api/search?q=&workspace_id=&limit=` mounted from `server/app.py` |\n| Search SoT | Shared SQLite; **case-insensitive substring** match on non-deleted `messages.body` (`LIKE` + `LOWER`); no FTS migration in this task |\n| Slash interception | **Before** `create_message` inside `POST /api/channels/{id}/messages` (and only there — not on PATCH). Parser in `server/messages/slash.py` |\n| Slash escape | Body starting with `//` → strip **one** leading `/`, treat remainder as normal message body (literal slash text) |\n| Side-effect response | Always HTTP **201** with `message: null` plus `channel` and/or `invited_user` as applicable; never insert a message row |\n| Mentions | Extend `resolve_mentions` in `server/messages/store.py`; keep `mentions: string[]` of user ids on `MessageObj` (no new JSON keys) |\n| `@channel` / `@here` | Reserved tokens; never resolved as usernames even if such users exist |\n| Username vs group collision | Same handle string: **username (workspace member) wins**; else expand `user_groups.handle` in that workspace |\n| `@here` without presence | Expand to channel members who currently hold ≥1 `auth_tokens` row (session proxy for “online”); exclude author. If empty set after exclude, mentions gain nothing from `@here` alone |\n| Read APIs | `GET` + `POST /api/channels/{channel_id}/read` on `server/channels/routes.py` |\n| `last_read_seq` meaning | Dense per-channel **event seq** from MARATHON-13 (`channel_seq.head_seq` / `channel_events.seq`), **not** message UUID. Cursor **never decreases** |\n| Unread / mention counters | Maintain incrementally on message create; **recompute** on POST read when `channel_events` exists; if M13 tables absent, POST that advances cursor **zeros** both counts (mark-read) |\n| Schema | **No new migration** required (`channel_read_state` already v2). Do **not** claim v6 (owned by MARATHON-13) |\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all endpoints Bearer-requirtime=2026-08-23T01:22:25.578Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\ntime=2026-08-23T01:22:25.593Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n\n...[truncated]...\ndescription: len=456\nlabels: len=24\nstatus: len=6\nhas_design: len=4\ndesign_format: len=8\n==== MARATHON-17 ====\nnotes: len=386\nDESIGN: SPA chat UX for channels/messages/threads/reactions on M16 shell + M7/M8 REST. Zero-build chat_ui.js; REST-only (no WS/M13); normative channel-*/message-*/thread-*/reaction-*/emoji-* testids + create-channel-modal; emoji grid not prompt(); coexist with M18 via channel-settings-btn + huddle:open-channel-settings. Label remains frontend for implementer after architect approval.\ndesign: len=27259\n# MARATHON-17 — SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\n\n## Summary\n\nFill the MARATHON-16 workspace shell with the core chat UX: channel list selection and create-channel modal (duplicate-name validation, `#`-prefixed display names, `data-channel-id` / `data-channel-name` on rows), channel header (name + topic) with non-blank empty-channel copy, message history with composer (post / hover-toolbar edit+delete, edited indicator, empty-body validation, hard-reload survival via REST), message rows (avatar + author + human-readable timestamp + body), right-hand thread panel that bumps reply counts, and reactions via an in-DOM emoji-picker grid (never `prompt()`) with count badges. This task is **frontend-only** against already-shipped MARATHON-7/8 REST; it locks the epic’s `channel-*` / `message-*` / `thread-*` / `reaction-*` / `emoji-*` / `create-channel-modal` selector contract so CUA/Playwright can drive chat at 1280×900.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Delivery | Extend the **zero-build vanilla SPA** (`static/` ES modules) — same stack as MARATHON-16; no bundler |\n| Module split | New `static/js/chat_ui.js` owns channel switch, create modal, message pane, thread panel, reactions; `shell.js` exposes active workspace/channel + list refresh hooks; reuse `api.js` / `storage.js` |\n| Data path | **REST only** for this task (list/post/patch/delete/replies/reactions). No WebSocket live fan-out (MARATHON-13). After each successful mutation, update local DOM from the response envelope; on channel select, `GET` history |\n| Channel create | Modal `create-channel-modal` → `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/channels`; append sidebar row on 201; 409 → inline duplicate-name error |\n| Channel switch | Click sidebar row → set `activeChannel`, render header + load messages; keep thread panel closed unless opened on a message |\n| Empty states | Distinct non-blank copy for (a) no channel selected, (b) channel selected with zero messages |\n| Message chrome | Hover toolbar on own rows for edit/delete; react + reply available on all visible rows the caller can write |\n| Reactions | Fixed emoji **grid** in a popover (`emoji-picker`); toggle via POST/DELETE; badges show emoji + count |\n| Threads | Open `thread-panel` for a top-level parent; list replies oldest-first; composer posts with `parent_id`; bump parent `reply_count` UI |\n| Selectors | Exact `data-testid` strings below; required DOM **id** `create-channel-modal`; keep M16 shell testids intact |\n| M18 coexistence | Message-pane header includes `channel-settings-btn` mount (visible when non-DM active). Click dispatches `huddle:open-channel-settings` CustomEvent (detail `{channelId}`) or calls optional `ctx.openChannelSettings?.(id)` — M18 wires the handler; M17 must not open settings itself |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic + task require chat UX with stable selectors; M16 explicitly deferred composer/threads/reactions/create-channel here; M7/M8 APIs are closed.\n- REST-only avoids coup\n...[truncated]...\ndescription: len=572\nlabels: len=25\nstatus: len=6\nhas_design: len=4\ndesign_format: len=8\n==== MARATHON-13 ====\nnotes: len=404\nDesign complete for WS subscribe/resume + dense channel seq. Key decisions: SQLite channel_seq/channel_events (v6) as SoT; seq allocated in same txn as mutation; /api/ws?token=; subscribe=live only, resume=replay or resume.gap; user.updated global no seq; Redis fan-out deferred to MARATHON-14 (local hub + catch-up on any node via resume). Label remains backend for implementer after architect approval.\ndesign: len=27570\n# MARATHON-13 — WebSocket subscribe/resume and dense channel seq\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the real-time seam for Huddle: an authenticated WebSocket at `GET /api/ws?token=…`, client `subscribe` / `resume` control frames, and a **dense per-channel `seq`** assigned in shared SQLite so every durable channel mutation (messages including thread replies, reactions, membership, channel mutations, pins) gets a gap-free monotonic frame `{type, seq, channel_id, …}`. Profile changes keep the existing channel-less `user.updated` shape (no `seq`). Same `seq` / event rows are visible from every HTTP node via the shared DB; **live cross-node push** remains MARATHON-14 (this task delivers live frames to connections on the writing node and makes catch-up via `resume` work on any node).\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Seq SoT | **Shared SQLite** counters + durable `channel_events` log (not Redis). Allocation is in the **same transaction** as the HTTP mutation so rollbacks never burn a seq. |\n| Dense rule | Per `channel_id`, `seq` starts at **0** (empty) and first durable event is **1**, then `+1` per committed durable event. No gaps, no duplicates, no reuse. |\n| WS transport | FastAPI/Starlette WebSocket on **`/api/ws`**, auth via query `token` (raw bearer, same value as `Authorization: Bearer`). |\n| Control protocol | Client JSON: `subscribe`, `resume` (with `since_seq`). Server JSON: `subscribed`, `resumed`, `resume.gap`, plus durable/live event frames and `user.updated`. |\n| History vs live | `subscribe` = watch from **now** (ack `head_seq`, no backlog). `resume` = authorize + **replay** `(since_seq+1)…head` then live, or `resume.gap` if `since_seq` is older than the retained tail. Channel history UI still uses REST (MARATHON-8). |\n| Retention | Keep the last **`CHANNEL_EVENT_RETAIN = 10_000`** events per channel (constant in code). After append, prune `seq < head_seq - RETAIN + 1`. Tail = minimum retained `seq` (or `1` if none pruned yet / empty head). |\n| Local delivery